{"id": "8", "question": "what is the difference between tartate and succinate", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between tartate and succinate is their chemical derivation: succinate is derived from succinic acid while tartrate is derived from tartaric acid. Additionally, succinate is an extended-release drug that stays in the bloodstream for 24 hours, making it a once-per-day pill. On the other hand, tartrate is an immediate-release drug that does not stay in the bloodstream for 24 hours and needs to be taken at regular intervals. Another important difference is that succinate has a greater dehydrating effect and may cause side effects like constipation and dry mouth, whereas tartrate may cause diarrhea and sleep issues like insomnia or unusual dreams.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartrate is derived from the tartaric acid. Succinic acid is ethan-1,2-dicarboxylic acid. Succinate form of metoprolol is an extended release drug and it plays its role in the circulatory system for 24 hours. However, the tartrate form of metoprolol does not appear in the blood stream for 24 hours because metoprolol tartrate is an immediate-release drug.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartrate is derived from the tartaric acid. Succinic acid is ethan-1,2-dicarboxylic acid. Succinate form of metoprolol is an extended release drug and it plays its role in the circulatory system for 24 hours. However, the tartrate form of metoprolol does not appear in the blood stream for 24 hours because metoprolol tartrate is an immediate-release drug.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartrate is derived from the tartaric acid. Succinic acid is ethan-1,2-dicarboxylic acid. Succinate form of metoprolol is an extended release drug and it plays its role in the circulatory system for 24 hours. However, the tartrate form of metoprolol does not appear in the blood stream for 24 hours because metoprolol tartrate is an immediate-release drug.\", \"The key difference between tartarate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartarate is derived from the tartaric acid. Succinic acid is ethan-1,2-dicarboxylic acid.\", \"The key difference between tartate and succinate is the origin of the chemical substances used in the drug manufacturing process. Tartaric acid is used to produce tartrate, whereas succinic acid is used to produce succinate.\", \"The key difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from succinic acid and tartrate is derived from tartaric acid. Succinate form of metoprolol is an extended release drug and it plays its role in the circulatory system for 24 hours. However, the tartrate form of metoprolol does not appear in the blood stream for 24 hours because metoprolol tartrate is an immediate-release drug.\"]", "time_sec": 20.313, "generation_time_seconds": 19.4243, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6579, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 44815, 349, 323, 20038, 3277, 374, 429, 20038, 3277, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 20038, 92335, 13621, 323, 12183, 376, 349, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 44815, 277, 292, 13621, 13, 88179, 92335, 13621, 374, 8372, 276, 12, 16, 11, 17, 1737, 292, 277, 2011, 88, 415, 13621, 13, 88179, 3277, 1352, 315, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 374, 458, 11577, 4879, 5506, 323, 432, 11088, 1181, 3476, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 369, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 12183, 376, 349, 1352, 315, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 1558, 537, 4994, 304, 279, 6543, 4269, 369, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 1576, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 12183, 376, 349, 374, 458, 13922, 44724, 5506, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartrate is derived from the tartaric acid. Succinic acid is ethan-1,2-dicarboxylic acid. Succinate form of metoprolol is an extended release drug and it plays its role in the circulatory system for 24 hours. However, the tartrate form of metoprolol does not appear in the blood stream for 24 hours because metoprolol tartrate is an immediate-release drug.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5679352299223313, "g_worst_claim": 0.45356444517771405, "g_content": 2.8135417591441763, "g_traj_mean": 1.687809705734253}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1376, 6672, 1948, 44815, 277, 349, 323, 20038, 3277, 374, 429, 20038, 3277, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 20038, 92335, 13621, 323, 44815, 277, 349, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 44815, 277, 292, 13621, 13, 88179, 92335, 13621, 374, 8372, 276, 12, 16, 11, 17, 1737, 292, 277, 2011, 88, 415, 13621, 13, 151645], "pred": "The key difference between tartarate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartarate is derived from the tartaric acid. Succinic acid is ethan-1,2-dicarboxylic acid.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.490414010673307, "g_worst_claim": 0.701966815524631, "g_content": 2.101893742879232, "g_traj_mean": 1.266042709350586}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1376, 6672, 1948, 44815, 349, 323, 20038, 3277, 374, 279, 6238, 315, 279, 11483, 32055, 1483, 304, 279, 5506, 14919, 1882, 13, 77541, 277, 292, 13621, 374, 1483, 311, 8193, 12183, 376, 349, 11, 19853, 20038, 92335, 13621, 374, 1483, 311, 8193, 20038, 3277, 13, 151645], "pred": "The key difference between tartate and succinate is the origin of the chemical substances used in the drug manufacturing process. Tartaric acid is used to produce tartrate, whereas succinic acid is used to produce succinate.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8147602394635499, "g_worst_claim": 0.06071795658631758, "g_content": 1.682573838667436, "g_traj_mean": 1.0108410120010376}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1376, 6672, 1948, 44815, 349, 323, 20038, 3277, 374, 429, 20038, 3277, 374, 14257, 504, 20038, 92335, 13621, 323, 12183, 376, 349, 374, 14257, 504, 44815, 277, 292, 13621, 13, 88179, 3277, 1352, 315, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 374, 458, 11577, 4879, 5506, 323, 432, 11088, 1181, 3476, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 369, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 12183, 376, 349, 1352, 315, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 1558, 537, 4994, 304, 279, 6543, 4269, 369, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 1576, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 12183, 376, 349, 374, 458, 13922, 44724, 5506, 13, 151645], "pred": "The key difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from succinic acid and tartrate is derived from tartaric acid. Succinate form of metoprolol is an extended release drug and it plays its role in the circulatory system for 24 hours. However, the tartrate form of metoprolol does not appear in the blood stream for 24 hours because metoprolol tartrate is an immediate-release drug.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7428846121964956, "g_worst_claim": 1.1523486721900202, "g_content": 2.716753429836697, "g_traj_mean": 1.6741634607315063}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.77, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "16", "question": "wat is dna", "gt": "Based on the given passages, DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, with the base pairs forming the ladder's rungs and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces of the ladder. The order of the nitrogen bases in a DNA sequence forms genes, which provide the instructions for making proteins.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. The main role of DNA molecules is the long-term storage of information. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, and it can replicate, or make copies of itself.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. The main role of DNA molecules is the long-term storage of information. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, and it can replicate, or make copies of itself.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. The main role of DNA molecules is the long-term storage of information. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, and it can replicate, or make copies of itself.\", \"Based on the given passages, DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The nitrogen bases adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C) form the genetic code. DNA is a double helix structure with base pairs forming the rungs of a ladder-like structure, and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces. DNA's main role is the long-term storage of information, and it can replicate to make copies of itself.\", \"DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. The main role of DNA molecules is the long-term storage of information. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions or genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, with the base pairs forming the ladder's rungs and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces. DNA can replicate, or make copies of itself.\", \"Based on the given passages, DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone and can replicate, making copies of itself.\"]", "time_sec": 30.972, "generation_time_seconds": 29.7995, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1262, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 15552, 374, 264, 30384, 292, 13621, 429, 5610, 279, 18929, 11221, 1483, 304, 279, 4401, 323, 30201, 315, 678, 3881, 5382, 43204, 323, 1045, 40968, 13, 576, 1887, 3476, 315, 15552, 34615, 374, 279, 1293, 9663, 5819, 315, 1995, 13, 15552, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 34615, 2598, 30384, 354, 3341, 11, 1817, 8482, 264, 78006, 1874, 11, 264, 13163, 1874, 11, 323, 264, 46403, 2331, 13, 576, 3040, 4494, 315, 46403, 23092, 525, 99113, 482, 320, 32, 701, 270, 1600, 482, 320, 51, 701, 1675, 91256, 320, 38, 701, 323, 9503, 42581, 482, 320, 34, 568, 576, 1973, 315, 1493, 23092, 26569, 15552, 594, 11221, 11, 476, 18929, 2038, 11, 892, 10742, 7761, 1246, 311, 1281, 27796, 13, 15552, 374, 264, 1990, 11338, 941, 14122, 553, 2331, 13530, 12392, 311, 264, 13163, 62737, 92373, 55427, 11, 323, 432, 646, 45013, 11, 476, 1281, 10993, 315, 5086, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. The main role of DNA molecules is the long-term storage of information. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, and it can replicate, or make copies of itself.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9118348251447579, "g_worst_claim": 0.008901311350720269, "g_content": 1.5749815772561466, "g_traj_mean": 0.9509429931640625}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 15552, 11, 476, 409, 60163, 1897, 263, 22147, 292, 13621, 11, 374, 264, 30384, 292, 13621, 429, 5610, 279, 18929, 11221, 1483, 304, 279, 4401, 323, 30201, 315, 678, 3881, 5382, 43204, 323, 1045, 40968, 13, 1084, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 34615, 2598, 30384, 354, 3341, 11, 1817, 8482, 264, 78006, 1874, 11, 264, 13163, 1874, 11, 323, 264, 46403, 2331, 13, 576, 46403, 23092, 99113, 482, 320, 32, 701, 270, 1600, 482, 320, 51, 701, 1675, 91256, 320, 38, 701, 323, 9503, 42581, 482, 320, 34, 8, 1352, 279, 18929, 2038, 13, 15552, 374, 264, 1990, 11338, 941, 5944, 448, 2331, 13530, 29064, 279, 1598, 5857, 315, 264, 35765, 12681, 5944, 11, 323, 279, 13163, 323, 78006, 34615, 29064, 279, 12140, 3108, 46468, 13, 15552, 594, 1887, 3476, 374, 279, 1293, 9663, 5819, 315, 1995, 11, 323, 432, 646, 45013, 311, 1281, 10993, 315, 5086, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The nitrogen bases adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C) form the genetic code. DNA is a double helix structure with base pairs forming the rungs of a ladder-like structure, and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces. DNA's main role is the long-term storage of information, and it can replicate to make copies of itself.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7732557383923648, "g_worst_claim": 0.0340580509768592, "g_content": 1.2081101637620193, "g_traj_mean": 0.7893884778022766}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [55320, 11, 476, 409, 60163, 1897, 263, 22147, 292, 13621, 11, 374, 264, 30384, 292, 13621, 429, 5610, 279, 18929, 11221, 1483, 304, 279, 4401, 323, 30201, 315, 678, 3881, 5382, 43204, 323, 1045, 40968, 13, 576, 1887, 3476, 315, 15552, 34615, 374, 279, 1293, 9663, 5819, 315, 1995, 13, 15552, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 34615, 2598, 30384, 354, 3341, 11, 1817, 8482, 264, 78006, 1874, 11, 264, 13163, 1874, 11, 323, 264, 46403, 2331, 13, 576, 3040, 4494, 315, 46403, 23092, 525, 99113, 482, 320, 32, 701, 270, 1600, 482, 320, 51, 701, 1675, 91256, 320, 38, 701, 323, 9503, 42581, 482, 320, 34, 568, 576, 1973, 315, 1493, 23092, 26569, 15552, 594, 11221, 476, 18929, 2038, 11, 892, 10742, 7761, 1246, 311, 1281, 27796, 13, 15552, 374, 264, 1990, 11338, 941, 14122, 553, 2331, 13530, 12392, 311, 264, 13163, 62737, 92373, 55427, 11, 448, 279, 2331, 13530, 29064, 279, 35765, 594, 1598, 5857, 323, 279, 13163, 323, 78006, 34615, 29064, 279, 12140, 3108, 46468, 13, 15552, 646, 45013, 11, 476, 1281, 10993, 315, 5086, 13, 151645], "pred": "DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. The main role of DNA molecules is the long-term storage of information. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions or genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, with the base pairs forming the ladder's rungs and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces. DNA can replicate, or make copies of itself.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9283789621990388, "g_worst_claim": 0.011524030140468053, "g_content": 1.6868121955968156, "g_traj_mean": 1.0267155170440674}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 15552, 11, 476, 409, 60163, 1897, 263, 22147, 292, 13621, 11, 374, 264, 30384, 292, 13621, 429, 5610, 279, 18929, 11221, 1483, 304, 279, 4401, 323, 30201, 315, 678, 3881, 5382, 43204, 323, 1045, 40968, 13, 1084, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 34615, 2598, 30384, 354, 3341, 11, 1817, 8482, 264, 78006, 1874, 11, 264, 13163, 1874, 11, 323, 264, 46403, 2331, 13, 576, 3040, 4494, 315, 46403, 23092, 525, 99113, 482, 320, 32, 701, 270, 1600, 482, 320, 51, 701, 1675, 91256, 320, 38, 701, 323, 9503, 42581, 482, 320, 34, 568, 576, 1973, 315, 1493, 23092, 26569, 15552, 594, 11221, 11, 476, 18929, 2038, 13, 15552, 374, 264, 1990, 11338, 941, 14122, 553, 2331, 13530, 12392, 311, 264, 13163, 62737, 92373, 55427, 323, 646, 45013, 11, 3259, 10993, 315, 5086, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone and can replicate, making copies of itself.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7900238911578077, "g_worst_claim": 0.02106320219380515, "g_content": 1.5554059784987877, "g_traj_mean": 0.8639078140258789}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "20", "question": "how to grill a porterhouse", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not contain any information or instructions on how to grill a Porterhouse steak specifically. While they do provide general guidance on setting up a grill and preparing the grill grate, they do not offer any specific advice or steps for cooking a Porterhouse steak. Therefore, I cannot provide a response based on the given passages.", "pred": "1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\n2. Replace the grill grate.\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\n5. Heat the grill to high heat.\n6. Place the porterhouse on the grill, bone side down.\n7. Grill for approximately 5-7 minutes per side for medium-rare, or adjust according to desired doneness.\n8. Remove and let rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\n2. Replace the grill grate.\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\n5. Heat the grill to high heat.\n6. Place the porterhouse on the grill, bone side down.\n7. Grill for approximately 5-7 minutes per side for medium-rare, or adjust according to desired doneness.\n8. Remove and let rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\\n2. Replace the grill grate.\\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\", \"Based on the given passages, to grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\\n2. Replace the grill grate.\\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\\n5. Heat the grill to high heat.\\n6. Place the porterhouse on the grill, bone side down.\\n7. Grill for approximately 5-7 minutes per side for medium-rare, or adjust according to desired doneness.\\n8. Remove and let rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing and serving.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to grill a porterhouse:\\n\\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\\n2. Replace the grill grate.\\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\", \"Based on the given passages, to grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\\n2. Replace the grill grate.\\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\\n4. Keep the grill hot, clean, and lubricated. When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\"]", "time_sec": 23.845, "generation_time_seconds": 22.942, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8925, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 39058, 264, 87186, 7675, 11, 1795, 149