{"id": "22", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure the delivery of quality behavioral health services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and work towards improving the overall health and well-being of Virginians. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and host weekly Q&A sessions for providers to address their questions and issues.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia, a provider of behavioral health services, offers continuing education clock hours/credits through e-learning courses and hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Magellan of Virginia, a provider of behavioral health services, offers continuing education clock hours/credits through e-learning courses and hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia. They are selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians.\", \"Magellan of Virginia, a provider of behavioral health services, offers continuing education clock hours/credits through e-learning courses and hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays.\", \"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia provides the following services and information:\\n\\n1. Continuing education clock hours/credits: Magellan offers CE clock hours/credits for e-learning courses approved by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB).\\n\\n2. Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA): Magellan of Virginia was selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA).\\n\\n3. Behavioral health services: Magellan administers behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs.\\n\\n4. Provider Q&A Sessions: Magellan of Virginia hosts weekly calls each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. These calls are open to all providers to address their questions and issues.\", \"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia provides provider Q&A sessions on Fridays. These sessions are held each Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. and are open to all providers to address their questions and issues. The weekly calls continue until further notice. Magellan of Virginia ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to elevate the quality and satisfaction in healthcare delivery.\"]", "time_sec": 21.339, "generation_time_seconds": 20.633, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6908, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 374, 264, 9109, 315, 35595, 2820, 3516, 304, 12989, 13, 2379, 525, 4091, 553, 279, 12989, 5887, 315, 12939, 45765, 8307, 320, 8395, 1911, 8, 311, 8683, 438, 279, 71984, 6267, 8307, 28593, 320, 97151, 7778, 8, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 6879, 84786, 25351, 4271, 35595, 2820, 3516, 525, 12600, 311, 12989, 33029, 65366, 273, 288, 11, 69120, 448, 3613, 11, 12565, 11, 323, 38110, 311, 7269, 279, 8084, 2820, 323, 1632, 32751, 315, 11214, 5380, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia. They are selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4437050773037805, "g_worst_claim": 0.23042895396550497, "g_content": 2.16598234785364, "g_traj_mean": 1.3230969905853271}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 11, 264, 9109, 315, 35595, 2820, 3516, 11, 6081, 14354, 6731, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 1526, 384, 70756, 13980, 323, 18432, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 13, 151645], "pred": "Magellan of Virginia, a provider of behavioral health services, offers continuing education clock hours/credits through e-learning courses and hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7121085897324575, "g_worst_claim": 0.08468469551631383, "g_content": 3.7059371948242186, "g_traj_mean": 2.6131298542022705}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 279, 2701, 3516, 323, 1995, 1447, 16, 13, 81017, 6731, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 25, 6879, 84786, 6081, 26711, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 369, 384, 70756, 13980, 11792, 553, 279, 3693, 68969, 10024, 320, 88669, 8, 323, 279, 10024, 315, 9784, 5547, 71086, 320, 1911, 52868, 3593, 17, 13, 71984, 6267, 8307, 28593, 320, 97151, 7778, 1648, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 572, 4091, 553, 279, 12989, 5887, 315, 12939, 45765, 8307, 320, 8395, 1911, 8, 311, 8683, 438, 279, 71984, 6267, 8307, 28593, 320, 97151, 7778, 3593, 18, 13, 71984, 2820, 3516, 25, 6879, 84786, 3986, 9303, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 382, 19, 13