{"id": "24", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nMagellan of Virginia does offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses. According to passage 1, Magellan is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB).\n\nAdditionally, Magellan of Virginia has been selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. This is mentioned in passage 2.\n\nFinally, Magellan of Virginia offers a Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. for providers to address their questions and issues. This is mentioned in passage 3.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses, as approved by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Magellan also hosts provider Q&A sessions on Fridays to address questions and issues from all providers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses, as approved by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Magellan also hosts provider Q&A sessions on Fridays to address questions and issues from all providers.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia. They are selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians.\", \"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses, as approved by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Magellan also hosts provider Q&A sessions on Fridays to address questions and issues from all providers.\", \"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider that offers continuing education clock hours/credits through e-learning courses and is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Magellan of Virginia is also selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) and administers behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Additionally, Magellan of Virginia hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m.\", \"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is an organization that provides behavioral health services in Virginia for members enrolled in Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They are approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). They also host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m.\"]", "time_sec": 21.239, "generation_time_seconds": 20.5865, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6447, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 374, 264, 9109, 315, 35595, 2820, 3516, 304, 12989, 13, 2379, 525, 4091, 553, 279, 12989, 5887, 315, 12939, 45765, 8307, 320, 8395, 1911, 8, 311, 8683, 438, 279, 71984, 6267, 8307, 28593, 320, 97151, 7778, 8, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 6879, 84786, 25351, 4271, 35595, 2820, 3516, 525, 12600, 311, 12989, 33029, 65366, 273, 288, 11, 69120, 448, 3613, 11, 12565, 11, 323, 38110, 311, 7269, 279, 8084, 2820, 323, 1632, 32751, 315, 11214, 5380, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia. They are selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4437050773037805, "g_worst_claim": 0.23042895396550497, "g_content": 2.16598234785364, "g_traj_mean": 1.3230969905853271}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 2379, 3010, 14354, 6731, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 369, 862, 384, 70756, 13980, 11, 438, 11792, 553, 279, 3693, 68969, 10024, 320, 88669, 8, 323, 279, 10024, 315, 9784, 5547, 71086, 320, 1911, 52868, 568, 6879, 84786, 1083, 18432, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 311, 2621, 4755, 323, 4714, 504, 678, 12565, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses, as approved by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Magellan also hosts provider Q&A sessions on Fridays to address questions and issues from all providers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8524443041113083, "g_worst_claim": 0.23042895396550497, "g_content": 2.8292437962123325, "g_traj_mean": 1.9479533433914185}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 374, 264, 9109, 429, 6081, 14354, 6731, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 1526, 384, 70756, 13980, 323, 374, 11792, 311, 3010, 26711, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 553, 279, 3693, 68969, 10024, 320, 88669, 8, 323, 279, 10024, 315, 9784, 5547, 71086, 320, 1911, 52868, 568, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 374, 1083, 4091, 553, 279, 12989, 5887, 315, 12939, 45765, 8307, 320, 8395, 1911, 8, 311, 8683, 438, 279, 71984, 6267, 8307, 28593, 320, 97151, 7778, 8, 323, 3986, 9303, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 22406, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 18432, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 481, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider that offers continuing education clock hours/credits through e-learning courses and is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Magellan of Virginia is also selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) and administers behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Additionally, Magellan of Virginia hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2235284982787238, "g_worst_claim": 0.23042895396550497, "g_content": 2.39964248194839, "g_traj_mean": 1.5859861373901367}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 374, 458, 7321, 429, 5707, 35595, 2820, 3516, 304, 12989, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 2379, 525, 11792, 311, 3010, 26711, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 553, 279, 3693, 68969, 10024, 320, 88669, 8, 323, 279, 10024, 315, 9784, 5547, 71086, 320, 1911, 52868, 568, 2379, 1083, 3468, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 481, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is an organization that provides behavioral health services in Virginia for members enrolled in Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They are approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). They also host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.463495766371146, "g_worst_claim": 0.23042895396550497, "g_content": 2.6997440617258954, "g_traj_mean": 1.8264864683151245}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.02, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "26", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not mention anything about Magellan of Virginia's status as a provider or its relationship with other providers. Passage 1 discusses Magellan's ability to offer continuing education credits, while Passage 2 explains its role as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Passage 3 mentions a weekly call for providers to ask questions and address issues, but it does not provide information about Magellan's status as a provider. Therefore, I cannot answer the question based on the given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services. It was selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services. It was selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia. They are selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians.\", \"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services. Specifically, they administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses through the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Additionally, Magellan of Virginia hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. for all providers to address their questions and issues.\", \"Based on the given passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services. It was selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs.\", \"Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and partner with members, providers, and stakeholders to elevate the quality and satisfaction in healthcare delivery. Magellan of Virginia also hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.\"]", "time_sec": 19.441, "generation_time_seconds": 18.7154, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7153, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 374, 264, 9109, 315, 35595, 2820, 3516, 304, 12989, 13, 2379, 525, 4091, 553, 279, 12989, 5887, 315, 12939, 45765, 8307, 320, 8395, 1911, 8, 311, 8683, 438, 279, 71984, 6267, 8307, 28593, 320, 97151, 7778, 8, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 6879, 84786, 25351, 4271, 35595, 2820, 3516, 525, 12600, 311, 12989, 33029, 65366, 273, 288, 11, 69120, 448, 3613, 11, 12565, 11, 323, 3811