faction in healthcare delivery. Magellan of Virginia also hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8743740826592177, "g_worst_claim": 0.4868062337239583, "g_content": 2.9476903279622397, "g_traj_mean": 1.9688283205032349}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "27", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it.\n2. If it won't lock, open the door.\n3. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n4. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n5. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n6. Align the door stop with the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it was removed.\n7. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n8. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it.\n2. If it won't lock, open the door.\n3. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n4. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n5. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n6. Align the door stop with the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it was removed.\n7. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n8. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n5. Re-lace the door stop back on the jamb.\\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n7. Use this to align the door stop.\\n8. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n9. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it.\\n2. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n3. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n4. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n5. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n6. Align the door stop with the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it was removed.\\n7. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n8. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off.\\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.\"]", "time_sec": 32.288, "generation_time_seconds": 31.4741, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7756, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 18, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 24, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnis