767, 279, 13169, 11968, 14178, 13, 14561, 279, 13169, 11968, 13, 3197, 264, 6006, 56926, 2765, 1405, 2287, 11, 432, 748, 1576, 279, 56926, 3171, 1405, 5285, 448, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 13169, 11968, 13, 17688, 498, 646, 9355, 1490, 279, 5786, 44598, 13, 1416, 537, 11, 653, 279, 330, 33115, 29033, 1273, 1, 320, 10463, 220, 16, 568, 1416, 498, 1477, 429, 279, 56926, 18508, 279, 13169, 11968, 2238, 1550, 476, 2238, 3347, 11, 1281, 2704, 678, 279, 6006, 594, 75593, 44922, 525, 10296, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door and use the chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n2. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\n3. If the door still won't lock, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb. Tighten the hinges first. Enlarge the strike plate hole. Move the strike plate. When a door latch won’t catch, it’s because the latch doesn’t align with the hole in the strike plate. Sometimes you can clearly see the misalignment. If not, do the \"lipstick test\" (Photo 1). If you find that the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9630851345199938, "g_worst_claim": -0.10825970023870468, "g_content": 2.789159647623698, "g_traj_mean": 1.9346084594726562}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 18, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 279, 6006, 2936, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 49472, 279, 6006, 2936, 448, 279, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 624, 21, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 22, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 23, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on the door stop until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Align the door stop with the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n6. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n7. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n8. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7337439170632765, "g_worst_claim": 0.34354885419209796, "g_content": 2.4606179250797755, "g_traj_mean": 1.6642125844955444}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "31", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\n\n1. Check the door stop: According to passage 2, if the door won't lock, try tapping the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Then, place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.\n2. Adjust the latch hole: If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb, as suggested in passage 3. Before doing so, tighten the hinges first. Additionally, you may need to enlarge the strike plate hole and move the strike plate.\n\nIf the passages do not provide sufficient information to answer the question, the response would be: \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. Use this alignment to align the door stop.\n8. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n9. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. Use this alignment to align the door stop.\n8. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n9. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n7. Use this alignment to align the door stop.\\n8. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n9. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\\n9. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on.\\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it still won't lock, open the door. Using a chisel, tap the end under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it up until it comes loose, then remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Secure the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original position. This should align the door stop correctly. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. With the door stop aligned, the door should now shut and lock normally.\"]", "time_sec": 29.816, "generation_time_seconds": 29.0505, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7536, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 18, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 24, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8307889970895252, "g_worst_claim": 0.09454040726025899, "g_content": 2.4542844748195214, "g_traj_mean": 1.7495181560516357}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 18, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 5443, 419, 17189, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 23, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 24, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. Use this alignment to align the door stop.\n8. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n9. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7641593249045284, "g_worst_claim": 0.09454040726025899, "g_content": 2.2515043876540495, "g_traj_mean": 1.6712936162948608}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 18, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 24, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\n9. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on.\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8830688417738808, "g_worst_claim": 0.3140886263413863, "g_content": 2.456700510792918, "g_traj_mean": 1.7043228149414062}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1156, 9311, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2058, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 13, 12091, 264, 521, 65294, 11, 15239, 279, 835, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 323, 81279, 432, 705, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 11, 1221, 4057, 432, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 34502, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 11, 6243, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 2309, 13, 1096, 1265, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 12440, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 3085, 279, 6006, 2936, 26118, 11, 279, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it still won't lock, open the door. Using a chisel, tap the end under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it up until it comes loose, then remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Secure the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original position. This should align the door stop correctly. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. With the door stop aligned, the door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.470545389334943, "g_worst_claim": -0.22796733038766043, "g_content": 2.3632685734675483, "g_traj_mean": 1.6690216064453125}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "32", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a possible solution to fix a door that won't lock:\n\n1. Check if the door stops are properly aligned. If the door stops are not aligned, use a chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it up until it comes loose. Remove the door stop and use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb and set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n2. Check if the latch hole in the jamb is properly aligned with the strike plate. If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, tighten the hinges first. Then, enlarge the strike plate hole. Move the strike plate if necessary.\n\nIf these steps do not solve the problem, it may be necessary to seek further assistance from a professional locksmith or carpenter.", "pred": "This should allow the door to shut and lock normally. If the door latch still doesn't catch, you may need to align the latch with the hole in the strike plate and ensure that all the door's hinge screws are tightened.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "This should allow the door to shut and lock normally. If the door latch still doesn't catch, you may need to align the latch with the hole in the strike plate and ensure that all the door's hinge screws are tightened.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Close the door and attempt to lock it.\\n2. If the door won't lock, open it again.\\n3. Use a chisel to tap under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it up until it comes loose. Remove the door stop.\\n4. Repeat step 3 to remove the door stop on the top.\\n5. Use the chisel to remove the door stop.\\n6. Set the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n7. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\\n\\nThis should allow the door to shut and lock normally. If the door latch still doesn't catch, you may need to align the latch with the hole in the strike plate and ensure that all the door's hinge screws are tightened.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix a door that won't lock, you should:\\n\\n1. Close the door and try to lock it.\\n2. If the door won't lock, open the door.\\n3. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n4. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n5. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n6. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\\n7. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n8. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\\n9. Use this to align the door stop.\\n10. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n11. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fix a door that won't lock:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Use a chisel to tap the end under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove the door stop.\\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n7. Use the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off to align the door stop.\\n8. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n9. The door should now shut and lock normally.\"]", "time_sec": 33.853, "generation_time_seconds": 32.672, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1699, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 18, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 24, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off.\n8. Use this line to align the door stop.\n9. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n10. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8522178293259792, "g_worst_claim": 0.24231030543645224, "g_content": 2.4720420354529273, "g_traj_mean": 1.7602660655975342}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 13032, 279, 6006, 323, 4774, 311, 5296, 432, 624, 17, 13, 1416, 279, 6006, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 432, 1549, 624, 18, 13, 5443, 264, 521, 65294, 311, 15239, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 323, 81279, 432, 705, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 13, 10783, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 19, 13, 44801, 3019, 220, 18, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 1909, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 11, 5285, 287, 432, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 9666, 315, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 382, 1986, 1265, 2138, 279, 6006, 311, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 1416, 279, 6006, 56926, 2058, 3171, 944, 2287, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 5285, 279, 56926, 448, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 13169, 11968, 323, 5978, 429, 678, 279, 6006, 594, 75593, 44922, 525, 84720, 13, 151645], "pred": "This should allow the door to shut and lock normally. If the door latch still doesn't catch, you may need to align the latch with the hole in the strike plate and ensure that all the door's hinge screws are tightened.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.318472254441096, "g_worst_claim": 0.15826128919919333, "g_content": 1.9981207790144955, "g_traj_mean": 1.350137710571289}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 498, 1265, 1447, 16, 13, 13032, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 624, 17, 13, 1416, 279, 6006, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 18, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 5