6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 20, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 21, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 22, 13, 5443, 279, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 23, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 24, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Use a chisel to tap the end under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.\n3. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove the door stop.\n4. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\n5. Lace the door stop back on the jamb.\n6. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n7. Use the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off to align the door stop.\n8. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n9. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0204857871021003, "g_worst_claim": 0.3482782443364461, "g_content": 2.5198350564027443, "g_traj_mean": 1.7852712869644165}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 17.05, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "33", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "To cook pollock, first preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper and place them on the baking sheet. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes. If desired, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet and return fish to the oven to allow cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "pred": "Based on the given passages:\n1. Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return fish to the oven and allow cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages:\n1. Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return fish to the oven and allow cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the seasoned fillets in a preheated oven.\\n4. Bake until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n1. Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n5. Return fish to the oven and allow cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n5. After 15 minutes, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 22.634, "generation_time_seconds": 21.9821, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6351, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 20, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 8