{"id": "35", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "To cook pollock, first, preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Then, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Next, place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish flakes easily. If desired, you can also add cheese on top of the pollock fillets and bake for an additional 3 minutes to melt the cheese.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, the steps to cook pollock are:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the seasoned fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet, and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n4. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and are flaky, which will take about 15 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with cooking spray.\\n4. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 21.361, "generation_time_seconds": 20.5974, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7466, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 20, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9974508443765192, "g_worst_claim": 0.3281064033508301, "g_content": 1.4039999154897838, "g_traj_mean": 0.9481435418128967}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 7354, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 525, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 51514, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 525, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the steps to cook pollock are:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the seasoned fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.793324046976426, "g_worst_claim": 0.3281064033508301, "g_content": 1.2105224833768957, "g_traj_mean": 0.7589842081069946}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 11, 323, 6193, 1105, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 525, 1320, 28100, 11, 892, 686, 1896, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet, and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n4. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and are flaky, which will take about 15 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9623892720937021, "g_worst_claim": -0.06978392601013184, "g_content": 1.2195347872647373, "g_traj_mean": 0.8248440623283386}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 31293, 448, 17233, 22899, 624, 19, 13, 22735, 279, 1461, 9942, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 624, 20, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with cooking spray.\n4. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0640232566024077, "g_worst_claim": 0.08726902802785237, "g_content": 1.2763103728598737, "g_traj_mean": 0.8904454708099365}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.06, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "36", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook pollock:\n\nPassage 1:\n\n* Spray a baking sheet with butter-flavored cooking spray.\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Place the fillets on the baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n* Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 2:\n\n* Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Bake the fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n* Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n* Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on top of each fillet.\n* Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.\n\nTherefore, to cook pollock, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n2. Place the fillets on a baking sheet or in the oven.\n3. Cook the pollock until it flakes easily, either by baking it in the oven or on the stovetop.\n4. Add cheese to the pollock if desired and return it to the oven to melt the cheese.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet.\\n4. For additional flavor, layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes.\\n6. After baking, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n7. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which should take about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook pollock:\\n\\n1. Prepare the cooking surface: Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray.\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Arrange the pollock fillets on the prepared baking sheet.\\n4. Layer the pollock fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n5. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n6. Place the pollock fillets in the preheated oven.\\n7. Bake the pollock fillets until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n8. After the fish has cooked, turn off the oven.\\n9. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n10. Return the pollock fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, the steps to cook pollock are:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet.\\n4. Layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n6. Turn off the oven.\\n7. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n8. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 28.776, "generation_time_seconds": 27.8395, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9261, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 20, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9974508443765192, "g_worst_claim": 0.3281064033508301, "g_content": 1.4039999154897838, "g_traj_mean": 0.9481435418128967}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 1752, 5107, 17172, 11, 6193, 279, 1461, 9942, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 624, 20, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 892, 1265, 1896, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 4636, 27815, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 22, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 1265, 1896, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet.\n4. For additional flavor, layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes.\n6. After baking, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n7. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which should take about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9449759956169665, "g_worst_claim": -0.08260826766490936, "g_content": 1.269760805017808, "g_traj_mean": 0.8767337799072266}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 17233, 7329, 25, 60561, 264, 27815, 10834, 448, 14100, 87240, 17233, 22899, 624, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 40580, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 389, 279, 10030, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 22735, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 624, 20, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 21, 13, 10771, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 624, 22, 13, 52074, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 4636, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 24, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 16, 15, 13, 3411, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Prepare the cooking surface: Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray.\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Arrange the pollock fillets on the prepared baking sheet.\n4. Layer the pollock fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n5. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n6. Place the pollock fillets in the preheated oven.\n7. Bake the pollock fillets until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n8. After the fish has cooked, turn off the oven.\n9. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n10. Return the pollock fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0283341869170597, "g_worst_claim": 0.06561096148057417, "g_content": 1.2866191420444222, "g_traj_mean": 0.8584127426147461}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 7354, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 525, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 22735, 1105, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 624, 20, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 23, 13, 3411, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet.\n4. Layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n6. Turn off the oven.\n7. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n8. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.033920391626349, "g_worst_claim": -0.10965349525213242, "g_content": 1.435912101499496, "g_traj_mean": 0.8640990853309631}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "37", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook pollock:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) (Passage 2).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper (Passage 1 and 2).\n3. Place the pollock fillets on a baking sheet lined with butter-flavored cooking spray (Passage 1).\n4. Add onion, green pepper, and tomato slices to the baking sheet (Passage 1).\n5. Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily (Passage 1 and 2).\n6. To add cheesy flavor, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven for an additional 3 minutes (Passage 3).\n\nNote that Passage 3 does not provide any specific instructions for cooking the pollock, but rather suggests adding cheese to the existing dish.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Put the fillets in the preheated oven.\n4. Bake them until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n5. Turn the oven off.\n6. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n7. Return the fish to the oven.\n8. Allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Put the fillets in the preheated oven.\n4. Bake them until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n5. Turn the oven off.\n6. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n7. Return the fish to the oven.\n8. Allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet.\\n4. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices (optional).\\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n6. If desired, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n7. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Put the fillets in the preheated oven.\\n4. Bake them until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n5. Turn the oven off.\\n6. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n7. Return the fish to the oven.\\n8. Allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet.\\n4. For additional flavor, layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes.\\n6. After baking, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n7. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which should take about 3 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 26.943, "generation_time_seconds": 26.066, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8674, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 20, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9549485368206614, "g_worst_claim": 0.2581060727437337, "g_content": 1.3863121913029597, "g_traj_mean": 0.9407467246055603}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 22735, 279, 1461, 9942, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 320, 12807, 4292, 20, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 12685, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 22, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet.\n4. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices (optional).\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n6. If desired, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n7. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9544364250090964, "g_worst_claim": -0.03058812767267227, "g_content": 1.3487115713266227, "g_traj_mean": 0.9274953007698059}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 10224, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 1105, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 11999, 279, 23387, 1007, 624, 21, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 22, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 624, 23, 13, 26530, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Put the fillets in the preheated oven.\n4. Bake them until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n5. Turn the oven off.\n6. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n7. Return the fish to the oven.\n8. Allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0096884215312334, "g_worst_claim": 0.20624251365661622, "g_content": 1.2788447986949574, "g_traj_mean": 0.8836707472801208}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 1752, 5107, 17172, 11, 6193, 279, 1461, 9942, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 624, 20, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 892, 1265, 1896, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 4636, 27815, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 22, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 1265, 1896, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet.\n4. For additional flavor, layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes.\n6. After baking, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n7. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which should take about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.928240231615343, "g_worst_claim": -0.0644499808549881, "g_content": 1.256424398983226, "g_traj_mean": 0.8773548603057861}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "38", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook pollock:\n\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. You can also add sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes on top of the fillets. Bake for 15 minutes or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. If desired, top with cheese and return to the oven for an additional 3 minutes or until the cheese is melted.\n\nTherefore, the answer is not \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n5. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n6. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, taking about 3 more minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n5. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n6. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, taking about 3 more minutes.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook pollock:\\n\\n1. Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n5. Return fish to the oven and allow cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook pollock:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n5. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, taking about 3 more minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps: \\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). \\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. \\n3. Either place the pollock fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices as described in passage 1, or bake directly on a preheated baking sheet as mentioned in passage 3. \\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. \\n5. If desired, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven to allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 25.395, "generation_time_seconds": 24.4388, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9447, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 20, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9549485368206614, "g_worst_claim": 0.2581060727437337, "g_content": 1.3863121913029597, "g_traj_mean": 0.9407467246055603}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 304, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 23387, 1007, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 20, 13, 3411, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook pollock:\n\n1. Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake in preheated oven until fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n4. Turn oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n5. Return fish to the oven and allow cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3652667423897837, "g_worst_claim": 0.2581060727437337, "g_content": 1.6940932273864746, "g_traj_mean": 1.194156527519226}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 323, 6193, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 21, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 4633, 911, 220, 18, 803, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\n5. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n6. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, taking about 3 more minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0504596373849597, "g_worst_claim": 0.2759247620900472, "g_content": 1.487895402751985, "g_traj_mean": 0.9647019505500793}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 25, 715, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 568, 715, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 13, 715, 18, 13, 20988, 1992, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 323, 6193, 1105, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 438, 7481, 304, 21085, 220, 16, 11, 476, 22544, 5961, 389, 264, 855, 383, 657, 27815, 10834, 438, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 13, 715, 19, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 715, 20, 13, 1416, 12685, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 11, 323, 470, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 311, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook pollock, follow these steps: \n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). \n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. \n3. Either place the pollock fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices as described in passage 1, or bake directly on a preheated baking sheet as mentioned in passage 3. \n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes. \n5. If desired, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven to allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0158440063678353, "g_worst_claim": 0.16366084416707358, "g_content": 1.4644419695879962, "g_traj_mean": 0.9633809328079224}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.6, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "39", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you can run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior. You can then apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Afterward, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. You can mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water, dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. Some plastic may be extremely difficult to remove, in which case you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun and then peel it off. If not all plastic comes off, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "7. **Replace parts if necessary**: If not all the plastic can be removed, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. Consult a service technician if replacement is required.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "7. **Replace parts if necessary**: If not all the plastic can be removed, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. Consult a service technician if replacement is required.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n7. Soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and leave it on the element for 5 minutes.\\n8. Use this cloth to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element then wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth.\\n9. Remove any remaining nail polish remover residue with a cloth that has been dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap, then rinse the coils with water.\\n\\nIf heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun is necessary, the plastic may be difficult to remove and you may not be able to get all of it off. In such cases, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer, and it's recommended to call a service technician for repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n1. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n2. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n3. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n4. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\\n5. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you may need to heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once the plastic is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In this case, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Identify the type and location of the plastic**: Determine whether the plastic is on the exterior or interior of the dryer and its location (e.g., inside the drum, coils, or other parts).\\n\\n2. **Use a plastic scraper**: If the plastic is on the exterior, use a plastic scraper to gently remove it. Be careful not to damage the dryer's surface.\\n\\n3. **Apply nail polish remover**: For plastic on the interior, mix 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover with a clean cloth. Gently rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n\\n4. **Rinse with water**: After dissolving the plastic, rinse the area with a damp cloth to remove the nail polish remover.\\n\\n5. **Use a wet soapy cloth**: Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Rinse with a clean water-dipped cloth.\\n\\n6. **Final rinse**: Ensure all nail polish remover residue is removed by rinsing the area with a cloth that has been dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap.\\n\\n7. **Replace parts if necessary**: If not all the plastic can be removed, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. Consult a service technician if replacement is required.\"]", "time_sec": 45.55, "generation_time_seconds": 44.6889, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8493, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 23579, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 432, 374, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 498, 525, 11889, 311, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 311, 4583, 419, 943, 315, 12733, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.494807734196876, "g_worst_claim": 0.2691250244776408, "g_content": 1.9555065757349919, "g_traj_mean": 1.4489868879318237}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 7354, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 624, 21, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 22, 13, 2055, 585, 264, 27292, 304, 458, 64702, 603, 5980, 30995, 44029, 76248, 323, 5274, 432, 389, 279, 2392, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 419, 27292, 311, 44901, 279, 9664, 12188, 1007, 315, 279, 2392, 1221, 39094, 279, 70760, 448, 264, 4240, 11, 40269, 27292, 624, 24, 13, 10783, 894, 9664, 30995, 44029, 76248, 48132, 448, 264, 27292, 429, 702, 1012, 72207, 304, 264, 6291, 315, 8205, 3015, 323, 12000, 26785, 11, 1221, 73241, 279, 70760, 448, 3015, 382, 2679, 23579, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 374, 5871, 11, 279, 12188, 1231, 387, 5000, 311, 4057, 323, 498, 1231, 537, 387, 2952, 311, 633, 678, 315, 432, 1007, 13, 758, 1741, 5048, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 11, 323, 432, 594, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 369, 12733, 13, 151645], "pred": "If heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun is necessary, the plastic may be difficult to remove and you may not be able to get all of it off. In such cases, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer, and it's recommended to call a service technician for repair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.588536671846336, "g_worst_claim": 0.3692958354949951, "g_content": 2.0402805685139387, "g_traj_mean": 1.541925311088562}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 17, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 18, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 19, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 20, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 21, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 2679, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8628, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 279, 12188, 374, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 13, 4354, 11, 421, 498, 4157, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 758, 419, 1142, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 369, 12994, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n1. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n2. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n3. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n4. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n5. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you may need to heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once the plastic is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In this case, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3279228089170827, "g_worst_claim": 0.2691250244776408, "g_content": 1.6984918767755681, "g_traj_mean": 1.2812647819519043}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 28301, 1437, 279, 943, 323, 3728, 315, 279, 12188, 95518, 29901, 3425, 279, 12188, 374, 389, 279, 27263, 476, 14791, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 1181, 3728, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 4766, 279, 23196, 11, 70760, 11, 476, 1008, 5479, 3593, 17, 13, 3070, 10253, 264, 12188, 88034, 95518, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 389, 279, 27263, 11, 990, 264, 12188, 88034, 311, 29273, 4057, 432, 13, 2823, 16585, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 7329, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 28497, 30995, 44029, 76248, 95518, 1752, 12188, 389, 279, 14791, 11, 6514, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 448, 264, 4240, 27292, 13, 479, 4402, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 448, 3015, 95518, 4636, 13772, 19648, 279, 12188, 11, 73241, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 4057, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 10253, 264, 14401, 773, 9667, 27292, 95518, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 13, 57368, 325, 448, 264, 4240, 3015, 1737, 6450, 27292, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 19357, 73241, 95518, 29279, 678, 30995, 44029, 76248, 48132, 374, 6963, 553, 96039, 287, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 27292, 429, 702, 1012, 72207, 304, 264, 6291, 315, 8205, 3015, 323, 12000, 26785, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 23107, 5479, 421, 5871, 95518, 1416, 537, 678, 279, 12188, 646, 387, 6963, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 19960, 264, 2473, 53511, 421, 13723, 374, 2567, 13, 151645], "pred": "7. **Replace parts if necessary**: If not all the plastic can be removed, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. Consult a service technician if replacement is required.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8592690279353932, "g_worst_claim": -0.15721778571605682, "g_content": 1.1256082864632284, "g_traj_mean": 0.8463608026504517}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.75, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "40", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first, run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Then, scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior. Next, apply nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth and then mix liquid laundry soap with water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Finally, rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water.\n6. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water.\n6. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n\\nIf the plastic coat is especially difficult to remove, you might need to use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic, allowing it to peel off more easily. However, if the plastic doesn't come off completely, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. In such cases, it's recommended to call a service technician for a professional repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you should use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water, dip a clean cloth in the solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, you should:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water.\\n6. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\"]", "time_sec": 34.127, "generation_time_seconds": 33.3397, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7745, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 23579, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 432, 374, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 498, 525, 11889, 311, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 311, 4583, 419, 943, 315, 12733, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.494807734196876, "g_worst_claim": 0.2691250244776408, "g_content": 1.9555065757349919, "g_traj_mean": 1.4489868879318237}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 382, 2679, 279, 12188, 22875, 374, 5310, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 2578, 1184, 311, 990, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 311, 8628, 279, 12188, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 57112, 1007, 803, 6707, 13, 4354, 11, 421, 279, 12188, 3171, 944, 2525, 1007, 6587, 11, 24891, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 1231, 387, 5871, 13, 758, 1741, 5048, 11, 432, 594, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 369, 264, 6584, 12733, 13, 151645], "pred": "If the plastic coat is especially difficult to remove, you might need to use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic, allowing it to peel off more easily. However, if the plastic doesn't come off completely, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. In such cases, it's recommended to call a service technician for a professional repair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.36499286718853, "g_worst_claim": 0.2691250244776408, "g_content": 1.814393477006392, "g_traj_mean": 1.324241042137146}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 12188, 700, 315, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 498, 1265, 990, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 311, 57128, 279, 12188, 1007, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 11, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 279, 6291, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you should use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water, dip a clean cloth in the solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4400016062640932, "g_worst_claim": 0.3633033831914266, "g_content": 1.9460275584253772, "g_traj_mean": 1.4561262130737305}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 498, 1265, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 624, 21, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water.\n6. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5984180470215044, "g_worst_claim": 0.3633033831914266, "g_content": 1.934803263346354, "g_traj_mean": 1.4528645277023315}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 73.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "42", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. (Passage 1)\n2. Heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun to make it easier to peel off. Once heated, use a cloth to peel off the plastic. (Passage 2)\n3. Soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and use it to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element after leaving it on the element for 5 minutes. Then, wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth and remove any remaining residue with a cloth dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to remove plastic from the drum of a clothes dryer.", "pred": "If the plastic is difficult to remove, you may need to **heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun** until it becomes softened. Once heated, you might be able to peel off the plastic. If you are not able to remove all of the plastic, you might need to **replace the drum or the entire dryer**. If you decide to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "If the plastic is difficult to remove, you may need to **heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun** until it becomes softened. Once heated, you might be able to peel off the plastic. If you are not able to remove all of the plastic, you might need to **replace the drum or the entire dryer**. If you decide to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution. Rub the area again.\\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n\\nThese steps should help remove plastic from the dryer effectively.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n2. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic area to dissolve it.\\n3. Rinse the area with a damp cloth.\\n4. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water, dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\\n5. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n\\nIf heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun results in the plastic melting, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you decide to replace the drum, it's recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic**. This step is likely to help the plastic coat becomes more pliable, making it easier to remove.\\n\\n2. **Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper**. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior during this step.\\n\\n3. **Apply nail polish remover** (1 to 2 tsp) to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. This step will help loosen the plastic residue.\\n\\n4. **Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover**. This helps to remove any residue that was not fully dissolved.\\n\\n5. **Mix 1 tsp of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water**. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. This step can help further break down the plastic and make it easier to rinse.\\n\\n6. **Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water**. This final rinse helps to completely remove any remaining nail polish remover and other residues.\\n\\nIf the plastic is difficult to remove, you may need to **heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun** until it becomes softened. Once heated, you might be able to peel off the plastic. If you are not able to remove all of the plastic, you might need to **replace the drum or the entire dryer**. If you decide to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.\"]", "time_sec": 40.636, "generation_time_seconds": 39.7318, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8895, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 23579, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 432, 374, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 498, 525, 11889, 311, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 311, 4583, 419, 943, 315, 12733, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.479496664170526, "g_worst_claim": 0.32981576522191364, "g_content": 1.91561099939179, "g_traj_mean": 1.4323656558990479}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 624, 21, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 382, 9485, 7354, 1265, 1492, 4057, 12188, 504, 279, 46622, 13444, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps should help remove plastic from the dryer effectively.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4217804434560453, "g_worst_claim": -0.09251285791397094, "g_content": 1.777510480182927, "g_traj_mean": 1.383387804031372}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 179