{"id": "43", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to get plastic out of a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n4. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic is still difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun before attempting to scrape it off. However, if the plastic cannot be removed completely, it may be necessary to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n1. Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\n2. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n3. Rinse the area with a damp cloth.\n4. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water and dip a clean cloth in this solution. Rub the area again.\n5. Rinse the area with a cloth dipped in clean water.\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove and heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun does not help, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you decide to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete the repair.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n1. Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\n2. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n3. Rinse the area with a damp cloth.\n4. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water and dip a clean cloth in this solution. Rub the area again.\n5. Rinse the area with a cloth dipped in clean water.\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove and heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun does not help, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you decide to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete the repair.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\\n7. Rinse the area well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n8. If the plastic is stubborn, consider heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\\n9. If the plastic cannot be removed, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such a case, it's recommended to call a service technician.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution, then rub the area again.\\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n\\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun, which may make it easier to peel off. However, you may not be able to remove all the plastic. In such cases, you might need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If replacing the drum is necessary, it is recommended to call a service technician.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n1. Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n2. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n3. Rinse the area with a damp cloth.\\n4. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water and dip a clean cloth in this solution. Rub the area again.\\n5. Rinse the area with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove and heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun does not help, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you decide to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete the repair.\"]", "time_sec": 39.708, "generation_time_seconds": 38.6644, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0293, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 23579, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 432, 374, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 498, 525, 11889, 311, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 311, 4583, 419, 943, 315, 12733, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.479496664170526, "g_worst_claim": 0.32981576522191364, "g_content": 1.91561099939179, "g_traj_mean": 1.4323656558990479}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 311, 57128, 279, 12188, 1007, 11, 1660, 16585, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 3082, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 51396, 11, 2908, 23579, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 4157, 387, 6963, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 758, 1741, 264, 1142, 11, 432, 594, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse the area well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is stubborn, consider heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If the plastic cannot be removed, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such a case, it's recommended to call a service technician.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3290974577203274, "g_worst_claim": 0.22888545195261636, "g_content": 1.7029188623968161, "g_traj_mean": 1.2618680000305176}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 11, 1221, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 624, 21, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 382, 2679, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 23579, 432, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 11, 892, 1231, 1281, 432, 8661, 311, 57112, 1007, 13, 4354, 11, 498, 1231, 537, 387, 2952, 311, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 13, 758, 1741, 5048, 11, 498, 2578, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 1416, 24891, 279, 23196, 374, 5871, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 13, 151645], "pred": "If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun, which may make it easier to peel off. However, you may not be able to remove all the plastic. In such cases, you might need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If replacing the drum is necessary, it is recommended to call a service technician.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.425473766044143, "g_worst_claim": -0.07851053476333618, "g_content": 1.8534083816240419, "g_traj_mean": 1.36920964717865}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 311, 57128, 279, 12188, 1007, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 13, 2823, 16585, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 17, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 92100, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 18, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 624, 19, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 41284, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 2679, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 323, 23579, 432, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 1558, 537, 1492, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 1416, 498, 10279, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 311, 4583, 279, 12733, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n1. Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\n2. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n3. Rinse the area with a damp cloth.\n4. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water and dip a clean cloth in this solution. Rub the area again.\n5. Rinse the area with a cloth dipped in clean water.\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove and heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun does not help, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you decide to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete the repair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1974395065441559, "g_worst_claim": 0.30850611130396527, "g_content": 1.7680962456597222, "g_traj_mean": 1.2795730829238892}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "44", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic does not come off with this method, another option is to use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic until it becomes soft and pliable. Then, attempt to peel it off carefully. However, be aware that this method may not work, and in that case, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. It is recommended to call a service technician for this type of repair.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to get plastic out of clothes dryer is:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper.\n3. Apply nail polish remover to dissolve the plastic.\n4. Rinse with a damp cloth and soap solution.\n5. Use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic if necessary.\n\nIf the plastic still does not come off, consider replacing the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, one should first run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Carefully scrape off the plastic with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Apply 1 to 2 tsp of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth, then mix 1 tsp of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. If the plastic does not come off easily or if it melts during drying, replace the drum or the entire dryer and call a service technician for assistance.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, one should first run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Carefully scrape off the plastic with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Apply 1 to 2 tsp of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth, then mix 1 tsp of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. If the plastic does not come off easily or if it melts during drying, replace the drum or the entire dryer and call a service technician for assistance.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n1. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic area gently to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth.\\n2. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n3. If the plastic remains, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if not all of the plastic is removed, it may be necessary to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In this case, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete the repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you may try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun, and once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if not all of the plastic can be removed, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In this case, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete the repair.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove plastic from a clothes dryer, one should first run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Carefully scrape off the plastic with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Apply 1 to 2 tsp of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth, then mix 1 tsp of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. If the plastic does not come off easily or if it melts during drying, replace the drum or the entire dryer and call a service technician for assistance.\"]", "time_sec": 35.47, "generation_time_seconds": 34.1401, "selection_time_seconds": 1.3189, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 23579, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 432, 374, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 498, 525, 11889, 311, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 311, 4583, 419, 943, 315, 12733, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\n6. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\n7. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n8. If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once it is heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic.\n9. If you are unable to remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, it is recommended to call a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4799100275288573, "g_worst_claim": 0.2552730441093445, "g_content": 1.9358495076497395, "g_traj_mean": 1.4388455152511597}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 3082, 29273, 311, 72639, 432, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 624, 17, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 279, 12188, 8458, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 23579, 279, 12188, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646,