, 6157, 1787, 279, 11296, 906, 624, 17, 13, 758, 279, 11296, 906, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 1156, 2999, 24849, 739, 320, 5493, 11, 21969, 11, 10500, 11, 2355, 4292, 18, 13, 758, 279, 2115, 38452, 11, 4205, 7899, 10500, 624, 19, 13, 1913, 279, 1290, 24067, 11, 9059, 1495, 311, 279, 4895, 6929, 3772, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10349, 6929, 4343, 320, 269, 894, 6929, 1008, 1091, 17225, 8, 311, 16400, 279, 22201, 458, 906, 2999, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 389, 279, 1008, 6929, 315, 697, 5754, 11, 1741, 438, 5085, 17225, 11, 311, 738, 432, 438, 279, 1638, 6929, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to set the default browser to Windows 7, follow these steps:\n1. Open the Settings app. To do so, open the Start menu and then click the Settings icon. Alternatively, use the Windows + I keyboard shortcut to quickly open the Settings app.\n2. In the Settings app, click on the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down to the Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal the Choose an app option, and then click on the other browser of your choice, such as Google Chrome, to set it as the default browser.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2101693543605907, "g_worst_claim": 0.03756896158059438, "g_content": 1.7737490157006492, "g_traj_mean": 1.3907971382141113}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 738, 279, 1638, 6929, 304, 5515, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 11296, 906, 13, 2014, 653, 773, 11, 1787, 5145, 5022, 323, 1221, 4205, 11296, 4603, 13, 38478, 11, 990, 5515, 488, 358, 13625, 37115, 311, 6157, 1787, 11296, 906, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 279, 1156, 2999, 24849, 739, 320, 5493, 11, 21969, 11, 10500, 11, 2355, 4292, 18, 13, 758, 279, 2115, 38452, 11, 4205, 7899, 10500, 624, 19, 13, 1913, 279, 1290, 24067, 11, 9059, 1495, 311, 1490, 4895, 6929, 3772, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10349, 6929, 4343, 320, 269, 894, 6929, 1008, 1091, 17225, 8, 311, 16400, 22201, 458, 906, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 5085, 17225, 311, 738, 432, 438, 1638, 6929, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Open Settings app. To do so, open Start menu and then click Settings icon. Alternatively, use Windows + I keyboard shortcut to quickly open Settings app.\n2. Click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down to see Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8546140380167166, "g_worst_claim": 0.515007217725118, "g_content": 2.1044211387634277, "g_traj_mean": 1.818947196006775}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "63", "question": "set default browser to windows", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to set the default browser to Windows:\n\nMethod 1:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and then clicking the Settings icon, or by using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. In the Settings app, click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\n\nAlternatively, you can also set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser by following these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\n3. When the pop-out menu appears, select Options.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "These steps are specific to setting Google Chrome as the default browser. For other browsers like Mozilla Firefox, the process is slightly different.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These steps are specific to setting Google Chrome as the default browser. For other browsers like Mozilla Firefox, the process is slightly different.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to set the default browser in Windows, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Settings icon in the Start menu or using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\\n2. Click on the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\\n4. Scroll down to the Web browser section.\\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as the default browser.\\n\\nThese steps are specific to setting Google Chrome as the default browser. For other browsers like Mozilla Firefox, the process is slightly different.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to set the default browser in Windows:\\n\\n1. Open Settings app. To do so, open Start menu and then click Settings icon. Alternatively, you can use Windows + I keyboard shortcut to quickly open Settings app.\\n2. Click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\\n4. Now, on the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\\n\\nThese steps are for Windows 10.\", \"Based on the given passages, to set the default browser in Windows to Google Chrome:\\n\\n1. Open the Start menu and click on the Settings icon.\\n2. Alternatively, use the keyboard shortcut Windows + I to quickly open Settings.\\n3. In the Settings app, click on the first option titled \\\"System\\\".\\n4. In the left-pane, click on \\\"Default apps\\\".\\n5. On the right-side, scroll down to the \\\"Web browser\\\" section.\\n6. Click on the \\\"Edge\\\" browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal \\\"Choose an app\\\".\\n7. From the list of browsers, click on Google Chrome to set it as the default browser.\", \"Based on the given passages, to set the default browser in Windows, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Settings app by opening the Start menu and clicking the Settings icon, or use the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\\n2. Click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\\n4. On the right-side, scroll down to the Web browser section.\\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry or any other browser you want to set as default, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\\n\\nFor Mozilla Firefox, the steps are:\\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\\n3. When the pop-out menu appears, select Options.\"]", "time_sec": 29.565, "generation_time_seconds": 28.7589, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7949, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 738, 279, 1638, 6929, 304, 5515, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 11296, 906, 553, 18458, 279, 11296, 4603, 304, 279, 5145, 5022, 476, 1667, 279, 5515, 488, 358, 13625, 37115, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 1156, 2999, 24849, 739, 320, 5493, 11, 21969, 11, 10500, 11, 2355, 4292, 18, 13, 758, 279, 2115, 38452, 11, 4205, 7899, 10500, 624, 19, 13, 22392, 1495, 311, 279, 4895, 6929, 3772, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10349, 6929, 4343, 320, 269, 894, 6929, 1008, 1091, 17225, 8, 311, 16400, 22201, 458, 906, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 5085, 17225, 311, 738, 432, 438, 279, 1638, 6929, 382, 9485, 7354, 525, 3151, 311, 6243, 5085, 17225, 438, 279, 1638, 6929, 13, 1752, 1008, 32857, 1075, 34733, 25929, 11, 279, 1882, 374, 10078, 2155, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps are specific to setting Google Chrome as the default browser. For other browsers like Mozilla Firefox, the process is slightly different.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3300265236442708, "g_worst_claim": 0.0658054103453954, "g_content": 1.9656187693277996, "g_traj_mean": 1.4707934856414795}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 7354, 311, 738, 279, 1638, 6929, 304, 5515, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 11296, 906, 13, 2014, 653, 773, 11, 1787, 5145, 5022, 323, 1221, 4205, 11296, 4603, 13, 38478, 11, 498, 646, 990, 5515, 488, 358, 13625, 37115, 311, 6157, 1787