{"id": "68", "question": "what is the proper way to dispose of a worn usa flag", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn US flag is to either:\n\n1. Remove the blue field and burn it in a peaceful manner, then bury the ashes.\n2. Fold the flag in the customary triangle fold and burn it in a proper ceremony.\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\n1. Remove the blue field and burn it, or\n2. Fold the flag in the customary triangle fold and burn it in a proper ceremony.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it in a proper ceremony if you are able to personally discharge your worn flag from service. This ceremony should follow the customary triangle fold.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it in a proper ceremony if you are able to personally discharge your worn flag from service. This ceremony should follow the customary triangle fold.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.\", \"Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it in a proper ceremony if you are able to personally discharge your worn flag from service. This ceremony should follow the customary triangle fold.\", \"Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to either put the flag out for collection only after removing the blue field and burning it in a peaceful manner with the ashes buried, or to burn the flag yourself in a proper ceremony if you are able to personally discharge your worn flag from service. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.\", \"The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag, according to the passage, is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. This ceremony involves folding the flag in the customary triangle fold.\"]", "time_sec": 14.745, "generation_time_seconds": 13.8954, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8346, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181, 374, 311, 8231, 432, 6133, 304, 264, 6169, 21536, 13, 576, 5181, 1969, 387, 47035, 304, 279, 72248, 21495, 11555, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.355583109157254, "g_worst_claim": 0.30649564663569134, "g_content": 1.7507940928141277, "g_traj_mean": 1.4673939943313599}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181, 374, 311, 8231, 432, 304, 264, 6169, 21536, 421, 498, 525, 2952, 311, 15726, 31543, 697, 23704, 5181, 504, 2473, 13, 1096, 21536, 1265, 1795, 279, 72248, 21495, 11555, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to burn it in a proper ceremony if you are able to personally discharge your worn flag from service. This ceremony should follow the customary triangle fold.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8081127838849167, "g_worst_claim": 0.30649564663569134, "g_content": 3.100161345108696, "g_traj_mean": 1.9350258111953735}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181, 374, 311, 2987, 2182, 279, 5181, 700, 369, 4426, 1172, 1283, 17592, 279, 6303, 2070, 323, 19675, 432, 304, 264, 25650, 11566, 448, 279, 66001, 26918, 11, 476, 311, 8231, 279, 5181, 6133, 304, 264, 6169, 21536, 421, 498, 525, 2952, 311, 15726, 31543, 697, 23704, 5181, 504, 2473, 13, 576, 5181, 1969, 387, 47035, 304, 279, 72248, 21495, 11555, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag is to either put the flag out for collection only after removing the blue field and burning it in a peaceful manner with the ashes buried, or to burn the flag yourself in a proper ceremony if you are able to personally discharge your worn flag from service. The flag must be folded in the customary triangle fold.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.916591045014544, "g_worst_claim": 0.3109596570332845, "g_content": 2.972066930822424, "g_traj_mean": 2.190626382827759}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 27390, 315, 264, 23704, 7279, 5181, 11, 4092, 311, 279, 21085, 11, 374, 311, 8231, 432, 6133, 304, 264, 6169, 21536, 13, 1096, 21536, 17601, 44742, 279, 5181, 304, 279, 72248, 21495, 11555, 13, 151645], "pred": "The proper way to dispose of a worn USA flag, according to the passage, is to burn it yourself in a proper ceremony. This ceremony involves folding the flag in the customary triangle fold.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2648790828432097, "g_worst_claim": -0.04462195336818695, "g_content": 1.9246885511610243, "g_traj_mean": 1.4693878889083862}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.07, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "73", "question": "how to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you:\n\n1. Physical contact: Avoid physical contact that could be misinterpreted as fondling or sexual activity (Passage 1).\n2. Eye contact: If your coworker is consistently staring at you, it may be a sign that they are interested in you (Passage 2).\n3. Smiling: If your coworker smiles at you excessively, even when there is no apparent reason to do so, it may be a sign of flirtation (Passage 2).\n4. Seeking contact: If your coworker consistently finds reasons to be near you or seek you out discreetly, it may indicate that they have feelings for you (Passage 3).\n\nHowever, it is essential to remember that these signs alone do not necessarily mean that your coworker is interested in you romantically. It's important to pay attention to the context of their behavior and communicate openly to avoid misunderstandings.\n\nIf you are unsure about your coworker's intentions, it may be best to avoid physical contact and observe their behavior over time before making any conclusions. Additionally, it's crucial to respect your coworker's boundaries and maintain a professional work environment.", "pred": "1. Look for physical contact that might be misconstrued as sexual activity or fondling. If your male coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, stop the interaction.\n2. Observe if your male coworker is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly. This is a strong sign that he likes you.\n3. Be aware of any reasons he has to have contact with you. If he frequently seeks you out or finds any reason to interact with you, it's an obvious sign of affection or admiration.\n4. If your male coworker is smiling at you for no apparent reason, it could be a sign of interest. You can ask him out if you like him.\n5. Pay attention to any signs of discomfort or suggestions from your male coworker that you should stop flirting. Losing your job should not be a risk when the person is not interested.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Look for physical contact that might be misconstrued as sexual activity or fondling. If your male coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, stop the interaction.\n2. Observe if your male coworker is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly. This is a strong sign that he likes you.\n3. Be aware of any reasons he has to have contact with you. If he frequently seeks you out or finds any reason to interact with you, it's an obvious sign of affection or admiration.\n4. If your male coworker is smiling at you for no apparent reason, it could be a sign of interest. You can ask him out if you like him.\n5. Pay attention to any signs of discomfort or suggestions from your male coworker that you should stop flirting. Losing your job should not be a risk when the person is not interested.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you, look for signs such as:\\n1. Physical contact that eludes to sexual activity or can be misconstrued as fondling.\\n2. If the coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, do so.\\n3. If the coworker finds any reason to touch you, it is a sign of flirting.\\n4. If the coworker always smiles at you at work when there is no good reason for it, she may like you.\\n5. If the coworker is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly, it's a guarantee that the person likes you.\\n6. Finding any reason to have contact with you is an obvious sign of affection or admiration.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you:\\n\\n1. Look for physical contact that might be misconstrued as sexual activity or fondling. If your male coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, stop the interaction.\\n2. Observe if your male coworker is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly. This is a strong sign that he likes you.\\n3. Be aware of any reasons he has to have contact with you. If he frequently seeks you out or finds any reason to interact with you, it's an obvious sign of affection or admiration.\\n4. If your male coworker is smiling at you for no apparent reason, it could be a sign of interest. You can ask him out if you like him.\\n5. Pay attention to any signs of discomfort or suggestions from your male coworker that you should stop flirting. Losing your job should not be a risk when the person is not interested.\", \"Based on the given passages, to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you, look for signs of physical contact that may be misconstrued as sexual activity or fondling, and observe if he seems uncomfortable or suggests that you should stop flirting. Additionally, consider whether he is constantly seeking you out discreetly, as this is a sign of affection or admiration.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell if your male coworker is flirting with you by observing the following signs:\\n\\n1. Avoid physical contact that eludes to sexual activity or can be misconstrued as fondling.\\n2. If the guy you're flirting with seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, do so. You don't want to risk losing your job flirting with him, especially when he's not interested.\\n3. Use it as an opportunity if you want to go out with her. Your co-worker is flirting with you if her finds any reason to touch you. If she didn’t like you, she probably wouldn’t do this since it is a little obnoxious.\\n4. Smiling is one of the signs a co-worker is flirting with you. If you notice a co-worker always smiles at you at work when there is no good reason for it, she may like you.\\n5. Finding reasons to be near you. If she, or he, is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly, it's a guarantee that the person likes you. Finding any reason to have contact with you is an obvious sign of affection or admiration.\"]", "time_sec": 31.778, "generation_time_seconds": 30.6482, "selection_time_seconds": 1.115, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 3291, 421, 697, 8593, 59968, 261, 374, 87242, 448, 498, 11, 1401, 369, 11929, 1741, 438, 510, 16, 13, 27379, 3645, 429, 655, 28146, 311, 7244, 5702, 476, 646, 387, 29671, 495, 3260, 438, 21208, 2718, 624, 17, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 4977, 28113, 476, 13230, 429, 498, 537, 3060, 87242, 448, 1435, 11, 653, 773, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 13719, 894, 2874, 311, 5796, 498, 11, 432, 374, 264, 1841, 315, 87242, 624, 19, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 2677, 42532, 518, 498, 518, 975, 979, 1052, 374, 902, 1661, 2874, 369, 432, 11, 1340, 1231, 1075, 498, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 279, 59968, 261, 374, 14971, 518, 697, 18010, 323, 10887, 498, 700, 61404, 398, 11, 432, 594, 264, 15440, 429, 279, 1697, 13151, 498, 624, 21, 13, 42797, 894, 2874, 311, 614, 3645, 448, 498, 374, 458, 8036, 1841, 315, 36705, 476, 65839, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to tell if your male coworker is flirting with you, look for signs such as:\n1. Physical contact that eludes to sexual activity or can be misconstrued as fondling.\n2. If the coworker seems uncomfortable or suggests that you not continue flirting with him, do so.\n3. If the coworker finds any reason to touch you, it is a sign of flirting.\n4. If the coworker always smiles at you at work when there is no good reason for it, she may like you.\n5. If the coworker is constantly at your desk and seeking you out discreetly, it's a guarantee that the person likes you.\n6. Finding any reason to have contact with you is an obvious sign of affection or admirati