 for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n4. Place the bratwursts in a large stock pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n5. Add the red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\n6. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n7. Cook the bratwursts on the preheated grill, turning them occasionally to brown evenly, for 10 to 14 minutes.\n8. Serve the cooked bratwursts with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.145384901764394, "g_worst_claim": 0.15190593401590982, "g_content": 1.4667917170994718, "g_traj_mean": 1.0173684358596802}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 78.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "77", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n4. Place the bratwurst in a large pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n5. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and continue cooking on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally.\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "pred": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n1. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\n5. Place the bratwurst on the preheated grill and cook for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n1. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\n5. Place the bratwurst on the preheated grill and cook for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to cook brats:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\\n\\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. Preheat the grill for medium-high heat.\\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\\n6. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the onion and beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n1. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\\n5. Place the bratwurst on the preheated grill and cook for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\"]", "time_sec": 28.394, "generation_time_seconds": 27.0276, "selection_time_seconds": 1.3555, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 20980, 624, 20, 13, 2691, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 311, 279, 3338, 624, 21, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 23, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 16, 15, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1728908839596353, "g_worst_claim": 0.11862123757600784, "g_content": 1.6908161113788556, "g_traj_mean": 1.077266812324524}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 7354, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 20, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 13876, 41047, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to cook brats:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate.\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0669017253051023, "g_worst_claim": 0.24898658196131387, "g_content": 1.3389880840594952, "g_traj_mean": 0.9822563529014587}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 20, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 5978, 1496, 293, 50420, 624, 21, 13, 52932, 279, 29105, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 279, 37327, 323, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding.\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. Preheat the grill for medium-high heat.\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\n6. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the onion and beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0758446318033559, "g_worst_claim": 0.24898658196131387, "g_content": 1.400862421308245, "g_traj_mean": 0.9513447880744934}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1411, 1862, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 2340, 865, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 2337, 17233, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 39058, 311, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 5978, 1496, 293, 50420, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook brats, follow these steps:\n1. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\n5. Place the bratwurst on the preheated grill and cook for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0850374494467963, "g_worst_claim": 0.137055903673172, "g_content": 1.4640564918518066, "g_traj_mean": 0.968920886516571}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 80.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "78", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\n\nStep 1: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n\nStep 2: Lightly oil the grate.\n\nStep 3: Combine beer and onions in a large pot, bring to a boil, and submerge the bratwurst. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n\nStep 4: Simmer the bratwurst in the beer mixture for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n\nStep 5: Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and grill it on the preheated grill for an additional 5 to 10 minutes, turning occasionally, until browned and cooked through.\n\nStep 6: Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side dish.\n\nNote: It's important to prick the bratwurst with a fork before cooking to prevent them from exploding while cooking. Also, cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for up to 5 days or frozen for up to 3 months.", "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine the beer, onions, butter, and bratwurst in a large pot.\n4. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n5. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding while cooking.\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\n7. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine the beer, onions, butter, and bratwurst in a large pot.\n4. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n5. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding while cooking.\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\n7. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\\n3. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n4. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding.\\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\\n7. The bratwurst should cook for 10 to 14 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n3. Add the onions to a large stock pot.\\n4. Brown the onions in the butter for 1-2 minutes, stirring frequently to ensure even browning.\\n5. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture along with onions, butter, and beer.\\n6. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n7. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally to ensure even browning, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n8. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to cook brats:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\\n3. Combine the beer, onions, butter, and bratwurst in a large pot.\\n4. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n5. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding while cooking.\\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\\n7. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\"]", "time_sec": 30.527, "generation_time_seconds": 29.4501, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0639, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 20980, 624, 20, 13, 2691, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 311, 279, 3338, 624, 21, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 23, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 16, 15, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1728908839596353, "g_worst_claim": 0.11862123757600784, "g_content": 1.6908161113788556, "g_traj_mean": 1.077266812324524}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 624, 21, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 13876, 41047, 624, 22, 13, 576, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 1265, 4296, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n4. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding.\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n7. The bratwurst should cook for 10 to 14 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1707731473676781, "g_worst_claim": 0.32708761692047117, "g_content": 1.5655683370736928, "g_traj_mean": 1.0474159717559814}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561,