, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 2340, 865, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 1393, 17233, 624, 21, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 5978, 1496, 293, 50420, 624, 22, 13, 52932, 279, 29105, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine the beer, onions, butter, and bratwurst in a large pot.\n4. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n5. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding while cooking.\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\n7. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9830818875426299, "g_worst_claim": 0.24898658196131387, "g_content": 1.2541346315477715, "g_traj_mean": 0.8615223169326782}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "79", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief guide on how to cook brats:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine beer, onions, red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper in a large pot. Bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Reduce heat to medium and cook for 10 to 12 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and place them on the preheated grill.\n7. Cook the bratwurst for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once.\n8. Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\n\nSo, to cook brats, you first prepare the grill, then cook the bratwurst in a beer mixture before grilling them until they're done.", "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. In a large pot, combine the beer, onions, and butter.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add any desired spices such as red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n6. Bring the mixture to a boil.\n7. Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally to ensure even browning, for 10 to 14 minutes.\n9. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. In a large pot, combine the beer, onions, and butter.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add any desired spices such as red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n6. Bring the mixture to a boil.\n7. Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally to ensure even browning, for 10 to 14 minutes.\n9. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\\n3. In a large pot, combine the beer, onions, and butter.\\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\\n5. Add any desired spices such as red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\\n6. Bring the mixture to a boil.\\n7. Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally to ensure even browning, for 10 to 14 minutes.\\n9. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. Lightly oil the grate.\\n2. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\\n3. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n4. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\\n5. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n6. Once cooked, remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and cook it on the preheated grill, turning once every 5 to 10 minutes.\\n7. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\\n\\n1. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot along with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. Preheat the grill for medium-high heat.\\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\\n6. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\"]", "time_sec": 33.274, "generation_time_seconds": 32.294, "selection_time_seconds": 0.968, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 20980, 624, 20, 13, 2691, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 311, 279, 3338, 624, 21, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 23, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 16, 15, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\n6. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n7. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n8. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n9. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n10. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1623874529760085, "g_worst_claim": 0.11616793274879456, "g_content": 1.7088579450334822, "g_traj_mean": 1.0675320625305176}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 758, 264, 3460, 3338, 11, 15963, 279, 12883, 11, 44597, 11, 323, 14100, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 20980, 624, 20, 13, 2691, 894, 12685, 48559, 1741, 438, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 624, 21, 13, 39124, 279, 20980, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 22, 13, 52153, 279, 8628, 311, 3347, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 5978, 1496, 293, 50420, 11, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 52932, 279, 29105, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. In a large pot, combine the beer, onions, and butter.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Add any desired spices such as red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n6. Bring the mixture to a boil.\n7. Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning occasionally to ensure even browning, for 10 to 14 minutes.\n9. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7919654528930861, "g_worst_claim": 0.07988688349723816, "g_content": 0.9220389782542914, "g_traj_mean": 0.7242188453674316}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 17, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 2337, 17233, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 19, 13, 2691, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 311, 279, 3338, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 9646, 29105, 11, 4057, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 504, 279, 12883, 20980, 323, 4296, 432, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 1449, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 22, 13, 52932, 279, 29105, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. Lightly oil the grate.\n2. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\n3. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\n4. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper to the pot.\n5. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n6. Once cooked, remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and cook it on the preheated grill, turning once every 5 to 10 minutes.\n7. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.159575555423776, "g_worst_claim": 0.18965351581573486, "g_content": 1.5658352995572025, "g_traj_mean": 1.0354094505310059}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4296, 1411, 1862, 1447, 16, 13, 2340, 865, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 2337, 17233, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 3156, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 20, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 5978, 1496, 293, 50420, 624, 21, 13, 52932, 279, 29105, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding during cooking.\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot along with onions, butter, and beer.\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n4. Preheat the grill for medium-high heat.\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\n6. Serve the cooked bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.100066990947877, "g_worst_claim": 0.24915266036987305, "g_content": 1.6401755349677907, "g_traj_mean": 0.9998852014541626}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 65.81, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "80", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "gt": "The cause of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is unknown. However, it is believed to be a result of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in communication between the brain and the GI tract, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors may include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (either too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food. Symptoms of IBS can include diarrhea, constipation, or alternating between the two, belly pains or cramps that worsen after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, as well as a lot of gas or bloating.", "pred": "Causes of IBS are thought to include abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. The following are risk factors thought to cause IBS: 1 Abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong) 2 Hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas. 3 Food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Causes of IBS are thought to include abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. The following are risk factors thought to cause IBS: 1 Abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong) 2 Hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas. 3 Food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) include diarrhea, constipation, and alternating between the two. Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement. A lot of gas or bloating.\\n\\nThe causes of IBS are thought to be a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is also believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors thought to cause IBS include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.\", \"Based on the given passages, symptoms of IBS include diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea), constipation, and constipation alternating with diarrhea. Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement. A lot of gas or bloating.\\n\\nCauses of IBS are thought to include abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. The following are risk factors thought to cause IBS: 1 Abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong) 2 Hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas. 3 Food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\nSymptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, and constipation alternating with diarrhea. Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement. A lot of gas or bloating.\\n\\nCauses of IBS include abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. Alteration in the gastrointestinal tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.\", \"Based on the given passages, the symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) can include diarrhea, constipation, and diarrhea alternating with constipation. Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement. A lot of gas or bloating.\\n\\nThe causes of irritable bowel syndrome are currently unknown. It is believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.\"]", "time_sec": 30.236, "generation_time_seconds": 29.4054, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8126, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 13495, 315, 6216, 22533, 65258, 27339, 320, 3256, 50, 8, 2924, 68293, 11, 733, 48586, 11, 323, 72362, 1948, 279, 1378, 13, 96585, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 5990, 304, 279, 4722, 4279, 315, 279, 35417, 11, 429, 633, 10960, 1283, 20969, 323, 2666, 2664, 1283, 264, 65258, 7203, 13, 362, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 382, 785, 11137, 315, 358, 7347, 525, 3381, 311, 387, 264, 10601, 315, 34563, 79211, 320, 28034, 8, 41829, 19029, 11, 7172, 17526, 315, 47031, 5746, 11, 323, 264, 43119, 304, 279, 10535, 1948, 279, 8109, 323, 279, 48509, 41829, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 11585, 311, 387, 4152, 311, 264, 1372, 315, 9363, 11, 2670, 72581, 304, 279, 79211, 320, 28034, 8, 41829, 3852, 1403, 11, 34563, 22596, 1849, 17289, 11, 7172, 26443, 311, 6646, 11, 323, 3607, 71629, 3020, 13, 31288, 9363, 3381, 311, 5240, 358, 7347, 2924, 34563, 19029, 315, 279, 14889, 323, 2613, 38308, 1543, 320, 36127, 4937, 476, 6301, 11, 476, 2238, 3746, 701, 86652, 47837, 311, 6646, 504, 264, 2480, 65258, 476, 6819, 11, 323, 3607, 73533, 42379, 11, 10767, 8881, 553, 7852, 43125, 315, 69813, 476, 32869, 304, 3607, 13, 151645], "pred": "The causes of IBS are thought to be a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is also believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors thought to cause IBS include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7864888555575813, "g_worst_claim": 0.32051801681518555, "g_content": 2.813501731636598, "g_traj_mean": 1.7620694637298584}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 13495, 315, 358, 7347, 2924, 68293, 320, 60817, 7481, 438, 16401, 17770, 315, 68293, 701, 733, 48586, 11, 323, 733, 48586, 72362, 448, 68293, 1