664, 1283, 264, 65258, 7203, 382, 785, 11137, 315, 358, 7347, 525, 1083, 7481, 438, 1660, 9788, 11, 714, 3381, 311, 387, 279, 1102, 315, 264, 10601, 315, 9363, 13, 4220, 2924, 34563, 79211, 41829, 19029, 11, 7172, 17526, 315, 47031, 5746, 11, 323, 264, 43119, 304, 279, 10535, 1948, 279, 8109, 323, 279, 48509, 41829, 13, 576, 46769, 653, 537, 3410, 3151, 10295, 476, 5109, 5435, 311, 1493, 11137, 13, 151645], "pred": "The causes of IBS are also described as being unknown, but thought to be the result of a combination of factors. These include abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. The passages do not provide specific examples or numbers related to these causes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1761098944399722, "g_worst_claim": -0.039972198860985894, "g_content": 1.8000320434570312, "g_traj_mean": 1.0212666988372803}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.4, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "85", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, first sterilize a needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end. Then, take another clean slide and holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry and label clearly. Once dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers. Always avoid coming into contact with another person's blood and if it is unavoidable, wear rubber gloves.", "pred": "To prepare a blood slide as described in the passages, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end.\n2. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the edge of the slide to the drop of blood, allowing the blood to run along the edge by capillary action.\n3. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood.\n4. Make 2 smears to ensure enough material is present for analysis.\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely.\n6. Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\n7. Place the dried slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage or further analysis.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To prepare a blood slide as described in the passages, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end.\n2. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the edge of the slide to the drop of blood, allowing the blood to run along the edge by capillary action.\n3. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood.\n4. Make 2 smears to ensure enough material is present for analysis.\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely.\n6. Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\n7. Place the dried slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage or further analysis.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears.\\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\\n8. Label the smears clearly.\\n9. Once dried, place the smears in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to prepare a blood slide:\\n\\n1. Prepare your workspace: Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add blood: Put a small drop of blood toward one end of the slide.\\n3. Make the smear: Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood on one end of the second slide, and use capillary action to let the blood run along the edge of the slide. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood.\\n4. Create multiple smears: Make 2 smears in total, allowing them to air dry completely.\\n5. Label: Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\\n6. Store: Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage or further analysis.\", \"To prepare a blood slide as described in the passages, follow these steps:\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end.\\n2. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the edge of the slide to the drop of blood, allowing the blood to run along the edge by capillary action.\\n3. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood.\\n4. Make 2 smears to ensure enough material is present for analysis.\\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely.\\n6. Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\\n7. Place the dried slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage or further analysis.\"]", "time_sec": 32.147, "generation_time_seconds": 31.4082, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7209, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7733437825468237, "g_worst_claim": 0.24458893140157065, "g_content": 2.070835629025021, "g_traj_mean": 1.4737027883529663}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 429, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 624, 22, 13, 26530, 279, 1525, 7444, 311, 3720, 9058, 624, 23, 13, 9402, 279, 1525, 7444, 9355, 624, 24, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 1525, 7444, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\