completely.\n5. Label: Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\n6. Store: Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage or further analysis.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5438747607483732, "g_worst_claim": 0.24535465240478516, "g_content": 2.0671390035878057, "g_traj_mean": 1.4024837017059326}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 438, 7481, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 323, 912, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 624, 17, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 13, 19338, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 311, 279, 5943, 315, 6543, 11, 10693, 279, 6543, 311, 1598, 3156, 279, 6821, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 18, 13, 22950, 279, 2086, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 1855, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 19, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 311, 5978, 3322, 3684, 374, 3042, 369, 6358, 624, 20, 13, 26530, 279, 1525, 7444, 311, 3720, 9058, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 9402, 279, 21521, 9355, 3055, 807, 525, 9058, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 31620, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 369, 5819, 476, 4623, 6358, 13, 151645], "pred": "To prepare a blood slide as described in the passages, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end.\n2. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the edge of the slide to the drop of blood, allowing the blood to run along the edge by capillary action.\n3. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood.\n4. Make 2 smears to ensure enough material is present for analysis.\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely.\n6. Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\n7. Place the dried slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage or further analysis.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2889537897795733, "g_worst_claim": 0.05740043024222056, "g_content": 1.5747231983003163, "g_traj_mean": 1.2227718830108643}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.27, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "86", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, you will need a clean glass slide and a drop of blood. Place the slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Take another clean slide and touch the blood with one end at a 45-degree angle so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly before placing them in slide transport containers.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears.\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\n9. Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears.\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\n9. Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, and touch the blood with one end of the slide. Allow the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n4. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n5. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly once they are dried.\\n6. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to prepare a blood slide:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears.\\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\\n9. Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage.\"]", "time_sec": 28.304, "generation_time_seconds": 27.4443, "selection_time_seconds": 0.851, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8061748679805303, "g_worst_claim": 0.24326966206232706, "g_content": 2.0567420753272803, "g_traj_mean": 1.5161868333816528}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 11, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 11, 323, 5796, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 13, 26530, 279, 6543, 311, 1598, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 19, 13, 22950, 279, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 20, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 3055, 807, 525, 31620, 624, 21, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, and touch the blood with one end of the slide. Allow the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n4. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n5. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly once they are dried.\n6. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7148404363687937, "g_worst_claim": 0.24326966206232706, "g_content": 2.119610595703125, "g_traj_mean": 1.4882526397705078}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 7354, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.925152976333859, "g_worst_claim": 0.24326966206232706, "g_content": 2.1396081712510853, "g_traj_mean": 1.5616689920425415}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 624, 22, 13, 26530, 279, 1525, 7444, 311, 3720, 9058, 624, 23, 13, 9402, 279, 21521, 9355, 3055, 807, 525, 31620, 624, 24, 13, 10771, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 369, 5819, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears.\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\n9. Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.738314066286029, "g_worst_claim": 0.24326966206232706, "g_content": 1.9999162722856572, "g_traj_mean": 1.4902541637420654}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.44, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "88", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that! Here are the steps to prepare a blood slide based on the provided passages:\n\n1. First, sterilize a needle with a flame as described in Passage 1.\n2. Next, obtain a blood sample by pricking your finger or using a blood donation kit. This will require adult supervision, especially if you are doing it yourself.\n3. Place a drop of blood towards one end of a clean glass slide as instructed in Passage 2.\n4. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide through capillary action. Gently push the blood along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Repeat this step to make two smears.\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely before labeling them clearly and placing them in the provided slide transport containers as suggested in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n4. Push the second slide along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n5. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n6. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n4. Push the second slide along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n5. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n6. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n4. Push the second slide along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n5. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n6. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to prepare a blood slide:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood on the first slide with one end of the second slide.\\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make a second smear if needed.\\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\\n9. Place the dried slides in the provided slide transport containers if necessary.\", \"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood with one end of the slide, allowing it to run along the edge by capillary action.\\n4. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n5. Make 2 smears, allowing them to air dry.\\n6. Label the slides clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers.\"]", "time_sec": 28.882, "generation_time_seconds": 28.0012, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8723, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7403479914494377, "g_worst_claim": 0.2100814382235209, "g_content": 2.0794885996225716, "g_traj_mean": 1.4772028923034668}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 11, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 11, 323, 5796, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 19, 13, 22950, 279, 2086, 14983, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 20, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 21, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n4. Push the second slide along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n5. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n6. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6830997237792384, "g_worst_claim": 0.2100814382235209, "g_content": 1.9407010013110018, "g_traj_mean": 1.3986811637878418}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 389, 279, 1156, 14983, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 2086, 14983, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 2086, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 264, 2086, 80503, 421, 4362, 624, 22, 13, 26530, 279, 1525, 7444, 311, 3720, 9058, 624, 23, 13, 9402, 279, 21521, 9355, 3055, 807, 525, 9058, 624, 24, 13, 10771, 279, 31620, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 421, 5871, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood on the first slide with one end of the second slide.\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make a second smear if needed.\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\n9. Place the dried slides in the provided slide transport containers if necessary.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3378966050715297, "g_worst_claim": 0.21637725830078125, "g_content": 1.7432889436420642, "g_traj_mean": 1.1673104763031006}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 1598, 3156, 279, 6821, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 19, 13, 22950, 279, 2086, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 20, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 10693, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 624, 21, 13, 9402, 279, 21521, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 1105, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood with one end of the slide, allowing it to run along the edge by capillary action.\n4. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n5. Make 2 smears, allowing them to air dry.\n6. Label the slides clearly.\n7. Once dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6666354382964743, "g_worst_claim": 0.2100814382235209, "g_content": 2.063444189123205, "g_traj_mean": 1.4124820232391357}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.3, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "89", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to prepare a blood slide:\n\n1. Sterilize the needle with a flame before using it to prick your finger or obtain blood from another source.\n2. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n3. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n4. Hold another clean slide at an angle of about 45 degrees and gently touch the blood with one end of the slide, allowing the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Carefully push the slide along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Repeat step 4 and 5 to make two smears.\n7. Allow the slides to air dry.\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\n9. Place the slides in provided slide transport containers.\n\nNote: It is important to avoid coming into contact with another person's blood, and to wear rubber gloves if it is unavoidable.", "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the second slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears and allow them to air dry.\n7. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\n8. Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the second slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears and allow them to air dry.\n7. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\n8. Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the second slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears and allow them to air dry.\\n7. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\\n8. Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears if necessary.\\n7. Allow the smears to air dry.\\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\\n9. Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers if necessary.\", \"Based on the given passages, to prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the second slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\"]", "time_sec": 28.319, "generation_time_seconds": 27.3982, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9087, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4