ourse of the year, the temperature typically varies from 22°F to 85°F and is rarely below 3°F or above 92°F.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8800580879998587, "g_worst_claim": 0.5285436312357584, "g_content": 2.642078399658203, "g_traj_mean": 1.7775609493255615}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 14260, 9104, 304, 21591, 5646, 510, 16, 13, 79648, 525, 1293, 11, 8205, 11, 65938, 11, 323, 14401, 624, 17, 13, 467, 49940, 525, 80875, 323, 92921, 624, 18, 13, 1084, 374, 27037, 73549, 1042, 21015, 624, 19, 13, 74683, 2789, 11136, 13289, 504, 220, 17, 17, 58472, 311, 220, 23, 20, 58472, 624, 20, 13, 576, 49411, 477, 1042, 12433, 518, 41351, 572, 220, 16, 24, 18, 19, 448, 220, 17, 19, 13, 24, 22, 14924, 315, 16878, 11174, 624, 21, 13, 576, 14401, 1944, 1042, 12433, 518, 41351, 572, 220, 16, 23, 22, 21, 448, 220, 20, 22, 13, 21, 20, 14924, 315, 16878, 11174, 624, 22, 13, 576, 1429, 11794, 13464, 12433, 304, 825, 3200, 572, 220, 22, 19, 13, 20, 14924, 304, 9127, 8187, 624, 23, 13, 576, 7192, 15088, 59950, 572, 916, 220, 16, 21, 14924, 304, 5768, 220, 17, 15, 15, 18, 323, 220, 17, 15, 15, 19, 518, 64715, 15900, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the typical weather in Indiana includes:\n1. Summers are long, warm, humid, and wet.\n2. Winters are chilly and windy.\n3. It is partly cloudy year-round.\n4. Temperatures typically vary from 22°F to 85°F.\n5. The driest year recorded at Indianapolis was 1934 with 24.97 inches of measured rain.\n6. The wettest year recorded at Indianapolis was 1876 with 57.65 inches of measured rain.\n7. The most snowfall recorded in one season was 74.5 inches in Rockford.\n8. The maximum monthly precipitation was over 16 inches in July 2003 and 2004 at Kokomo.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8261686945785611, "g_worst_claim": 0.5162285566329956, "g_content": 2.242163489846622, "g_traj_mean": 1.4621301889419556}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "100", "question": "how to sync audiobook from iphone to itunes", "gt": "To sync an audiobook from iPhone to iTunes, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open iTunes on your computer.\n2. Turn on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes.\n3. Download the audiobook from iTunes onto your iPhone.\n4. Connect your iPhone to the USB cable and plug the other end of the USB cable into a USB port on the computer.\n5. Wait for iTunes to sync the audiobook to your iPhone.\n6. After the sync is complete, the audiobook will be on your iPhone.", "pred": "The audiobook will be available in the \"Audiobooks\" section in your iTunes library after the sync is complete.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The audiobook will be available in the \"Audiobooks\" section in your iTunes library after the sync is complete.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to sync an audiobook from an iPhone to iTunes, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Connect your iPhone to the computer using a USB cable.\\n2. Open iTunes on your computer.\\n3. In the left pane of iTunes, click on \\\"Audiobooks.\\\"\\n4. Select the audiobook you want to sync by checking the box next to its title.\\n5. Click \\\"Sync Audiobooks\\\" and choose the audiobook you want to transfer or select \\\"All Audiobooks\\\" to transfer all of them.\\n6. Click \\\"Apply\\\" at the bottom of the screen to complete the syncing process.\", \"Based on the given passages, the process to sync audiobooks from an iPhone to iTunes is as follows:\\n\\n1. Download the audiobook you want from iTunes.\\n2. In iTunes, go to the \\\"Audiobooks\\\" section on the left task pane.\\n3. Click the checkbox next to the title of the audiobook to select it.\\n4. Connect your iPhone to the USB cable and plug the other end of the USB cable into a USB port on the computer.\\n5. Wait for iTunes to sync the audiobook to your iPhone.\\n\\nThe audiobook will be available in the \\\"Audiobooks\\\" section in your iTunes library after the sync is complete.\", \"Based on the given passages, syncing an audiobook from an iPhone to iTunes involves the following steps:\\n1. Launch iTunes on your computer and connect your iPhone to the PC.\\n2. Click on \\\"Audiobooks\\\" in the left task pane of the iTunes window.\\n3. Select the audiobook you want to sync by clicking the box next to the title.\\n4. Connect your iPhone to the USB cable and plug the other end into a USB port on the computer.\\n5. Wait for iTunes to sync the audiobook to your iPhone.\\n6. After the sync is complete, the audiobook will be on your iPhone.\\n7. You can then import the audiobook into your iTunes library by clicking \\\"Import\\\" and selecting the audiobook from the PC to add it to your iOS device.\", \"To sync audiobooks from an iPhone to iTunes, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Launch iTunes on your computer.\\n2. Connect your iPhone to the computer using a USB cable.\\n3. Click on the name of your iPhone under \\\"Devices\\\" in the left column of iTunes.\\n4. Choose \\\"Books\\\" above the main iTunes window.\\n5. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer by clicking the checkbox next to their titles.\\n6. Click \\\"Sync Audiobooks\\\" and choose the audiobooks you want to transfer or select \\\"All Audiobooks\\\" to transfer all of them to the iPhone.\\n7. Click \\\"Apply\\\" at the bottom of the screen to initiate the syncing process.\\n8. Optionally, you can click \\\"Import\\\" to add new audiobooks from your PC to your iOS devices.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully sync audiobooks from your iPhone to your iTunes library.\"]", "time_sec": 30.248, "generation_time_seconds": 29.2054, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0298, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 12811, 458, 46368, 73328, 504, 458, 12167, 311, 13025, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 13015, 697, 1