is complete, the audiobooks will be available in your iTunes library on your computer.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.4923391161133377, "g_worst_claim": -0.0015850931406021119, "g_content": 0.6760972173590409, "g_traj_mean": 0.5864768028259277}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.93, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "103", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The various systems in the human body work together to ensure its normal functioning. For instance, the urinary system works with all other systems to clean the blood by removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. This includes organs like the kidneys and lower intestines. Similarly, the respiratory system also collaborates with all other systems to provide oxygen to all body parts and remove carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. The respiratory system comprises the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, several body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems are interconnected. The urinary system works closely with all other systems to clean waste products, while the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, several body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems are interconnected. The urinary system works closely with all other systems to clean waste products, while the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.\", \"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. The urinary system cleans waste products from multiple systems, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from several systems, including the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. This collaboration ensures that all parts of the body can operate efficiently and maintain homeostasis.\", \"Based on the given passages, several body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems are interconnected. The urinary system works closely with all other systems to clean waste products, while the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide.\", \"Based on the given passages, the human body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. The skeletal system provides structure and support, while the muscular system aids in movement. The digestive system processes food and absorbs nutrients, and the respiratory system provides oxygen and removes carbon dioxide. The circulatory system transports substances throughout the body, and the urinary system cleans waste products. Additionally, the endocrine system regulates growth and development, the lymphatic system helps fight infections, and the immune system defends against pathogens. The nervous system coordinates and controls all body functions. Each system works in harmony with the others, working together to maintain the body's normal functioning.\"]", "time_sec": 21.9, "generation_time_seconds": 20.8999, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9893, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 4220, 5942, 525, 82316, 323, 17188, 389, 1817, 1008, 311, 10306, 279, 2487, 594, 4622, 30201, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0238290003910453, "g_worst_claim": 0.0496651753783226, "g_content": 1.8095264840633312, "g_traj_mean": 1.099526047706604}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 5248, 5942, 11, 2670, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 311, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 3807, 5942, 11, 2670, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 1096, 20031, 25351, 429, 678, 5479, 315, 279, 2487, 646, 14476, 29720, 323, 10306, 2114, 535, 10718, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. The urinary system cleans waste products from multiple systems, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from several systems, including the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. This collaboration ensures that all parts of the body can operate efficiently and maintain homeostasis.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0280540261209312, "g_worst_claim": 0.06960185617208481, "g_content": 1.7614721622107163, "g_traj_mean": 1.033772349357605}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3807, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 4622, 30201, 13, 576, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 835, 77638, 11, 42645, 774, 11, 22077, 11, 41789, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 525, 82316, 13, 576, 71635, 1849, 4278, 15148, 448, 678, 1008, 5942, 311, 4240, 12291, 3871, 11, 1393, 279, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 311, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, several body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems are interconnected. The urinary system works closely with all other systems to clean waste products, while the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.050728286788577, "g_worst_claim": 0.24873507022857666, "g_content": 1.8636026149842797, "g_traj_mean": 1.3024457693099976}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 3738, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 68297, 1849, 5707, 5944, 323, 1824, 11, 1393, 279, 51092, 1849, 51697, 304, 7203, 13, 576, 58971, 1849, 11364, 3607, 323, 90011, 36393, 11, 323, 279, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 13, 576, 4225, 37120, 1849, 68069, 32055, 6814, 279, 2487, 11, 323, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 79312, 6513, 323, 4401, 11, 279, 42645, 774, 1849, 8609, 4367, 28920, 11, 323, 279, 22077, 1849, 80960, 2348, 77184, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 13934, 323, 11574, 678, 2487, 5746, 13, 8886, 1849, 4278, 304, 25281, 448, 279, 3800, 11, 3238, 3786, 311, 10306, 279, 2487, 594, 4622, 30201, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the human body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. The skeletal system provides structure and support, while the muscular system aids in movement. The digestive system processes food and absorbs nutrients, and the respiratory system provides oxygen and removes carbon dioxide. The circulatory system transports substances throughout the body, and the urinary system cleans waste products. Additionally, the endocrine system regulates growth and development, the lymphatic system helps fight infections, and the immune system defends against pathogens. The nervous system coordinates and controls all body functions. Each system works in harmony with the others, working together to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.519912784343416, "g_worst_claim": 0.03653908371925354, "g_content": 0.7275891621907552, "g_traj_mean": 0.500986635684967}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.86, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "104", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The body systems work together in order to maintain the normal functioning of the human body. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. Each system has its own specific functions, but they also work in conjunction with one another to ensure the overall well-being of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from various systems such as the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "pred": "These interactions highlight the complexity and interdependence of the body systems in maintaining overall health and function.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These interactions highlight the complexity and interdependence of the body systems in maintaining overall health and function.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.\", \"Based on the given passages, several systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body, cleaning waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system, in turn, works closely with all other systems, providing oxygen for all body parts and removing carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\", \"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together in several ways:\\n\\n1. **Integration of Functions**: The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems all function together to maintain the body's normal operations. Each system has specific roles but is dependent on others for various processes.\\n\\n2. **Elimination and Maintenance**: The urinary system and the respiratory system are particularly intertwined. The urinary system cleans blood from the body by removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system, on the other hand, provides the oxygen needed by all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from these same systems.\\n\\n3. **Cooperation in Specific Roles**: For example, the digestive system not only processes food but also releases nutrients that are absorbed and used by the rest of the body. The circulatory system distributes these nutrients throughout the body.\\n\\n4. **Supportive Roles**: The circulatory system supports the transportation of oxygen and nutrients from the respiratory system to all parts of the body and helps remove waste products to the urinary system.\\n\\n5. **Coordination Through Communication**: The nervous system coordinates these efforts, sending signals to ensure that each system works efficiently and in harmony with the others.\\n\\nThese interactions highlight the complexity and interdependence of the body systems in maintaining overall health and function.\", \"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The Systems: Several systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. These systems are the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive and the nervous.\\nThe urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory and nervous systems. It is used to clean blood from the body, and the system includes the kidneys and lower intestines.\\nThe respiratory system also works closely with all other systems of the body, including the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary and nervous systems. It provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary and nervous systems. This system includes the nose, larynx, trachea and the lungs.\\nThese examples show how the body systems work together to help keep the body functioning normally.\"]", "time_sec": 34.346, "generation_time_seconds": 32.9944, "selection_time_seconds": 1.3402, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 4220, 5942, 525, 82316, 323, 17188, 389, 1817, 1008, 311, 10306, 279, 2487, 594, 4622, 30201, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0238290003910453, "g_worst_claim": 0.0496651753783226, "g_content": 1.8095264840633312, "g_traj_mean": 1.099526047706604}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3807, 5942, 304, 279, 3738, 2487, 975, 3786, 311, 1492, 2506, 432, 30201, 14279, 13, 4220, 5942, 2924, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 835, 77638, 11, 42645, 774, 11, 22077, 11, 323, 41789, 5942, 13, 576, 71635, 1849, 4278, 15148, 448, 678, 1008, 5942, 315, 279, 2487, 11, 15826, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 11, 304, 2484, 11, 4278, 15148, 448, 678, 1008, 5942, 11, 8241, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 17592, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, several systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body, cleaning waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system, in turn, works closely with all other systems, providing oxygen for all body parts and removing carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3843063479755229, "g_worst_claim": 0.3504815498987834, "g_content": 2.0335414025091354, "g_traj_mean": 1.3069757223129272}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 52464, 315, 23550, 95518, 576, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 835, 77638, 11, 42645, 774, 11, 22077, 11, 41789, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 678, 729, 3786, 311, 10306, 279, 2487, 594, 4622, 7525, 13, 8886, 1849, 702, 3151, 12783, 714, 374, 17749, 389, 3800, 369, 5257, 11364, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 41013, 2554, 323, 38206, 95518, 576, 71635, 1849, 323, 279, 41531, 1849, 525, 7945, 98792, 13, 576, 71635, 1849, 34194, 6543, 504, 279, 2487, 553, 17592, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 5707, 279, 23552, 4362, 553, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 1493, 1852, 5942, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 7339, 9262, 304, 28262, 50907, 95518, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 58971, 1849, 537, 1172, 11364, 3607, 714, 1083, 19232, 36393, 429, 525, 41001, 323, 1483, 553, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 4225, 37120, 1849, 95735, 1493, 36393, 6814, 279, 2487, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 7916, 533, 50907, 95518, 576, 4225, 37120, 1849, 11554, 279, 17903, 315, 23552, 323, 36393, 504, 279, 41531, 1849, 311, 678, 5479, 315, 279, 2487, 323, 8609, 4057, 12291, 3871, 311, 279, 71635, 1849, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 19437, 2554, 16904, 30866, 95518, 576, 22596, 1849, 13934, 1493, 8869, 11, 11628, 17289, 311, 5978, 429, 1817, 1849, 4278, 29720, 323, 304, 25281, 448, 279, 3800, 382, 9485, 21880, 11167, 279, 23094, 323, 946, 90646, 315, 279, 2487, 5942, 304, 20337, 8084, 2820, 323, 729, 13, 151645], "pred": "These interactions highlight the complexity and interdependence of the body systems in maintaining overall health and function.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6364046389202462, "g_worst_claim": 0.120433509349823, "g_content": 0.918308230212135, "g_traj_mean": 0.5801325440406799}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 1492, 2506, 279, 2487, 30201, 14279, 13, 576, 14917, 25, 25694, 5942, 304, 279, 3738, 2487, 975, 3786, 311, 1492, 2506, 432, 30201, 14279, 13, 4220, 5942, 525, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 835, 77638, 11, 42645, 774, 11, 22077, 11, 41789, 323, 279, 22596, 624, 785, 71635, 1849, 4278, 15148, 448, 678, 1008, 5942, 315, 279, 2487, 11, 2670, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 1084, 374, 1483, 311, 4240, 6543, 504, 279, 2487, 11, 323, 279, 1849, 5646, 279, 80860, 323, 4722, 38308, 1543, 624, 785, 41531, 1849, 1083, 4278, 15148, 448, 678, 1008, 5942, 315, 279, 2487, 11, 2670, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 1084, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 1096, 1849, 5646, 279, 19142, 11, 326, 658, 23357, 11, 489, 1777, 64, 323, 279, 44174, 624, 9485, 10295, 1473, 1246, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 1492, 2506, 279, 2487, 30201, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The Systems: Several systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. These systems are the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive and the nervous.\nThe urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory and nervous systems. It is used to clean blood from the body, and the system includes the kidneys and lower intestines.\nThe respiratory system also works closely with all other systems of the body, including the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary and nervous systems. It provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary and nervous systems. This system includes the nose, larynx, trachea and the lungs.\nThese examples show how the body systems work together to help keep the body functioning normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2337532910281814, "g_worst_claim": 0.2749422858743107, "g_content": 1.5507273257357403, "g_traj_mean": 1.12331223487854}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.98, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "105", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how the body systems work together:\n\n1. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and nervous systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. (Passage 1)\n2. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body to clean blood from the body and remove waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. (Passage 2)\n3. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the body systems work together in the following ways:\n\n* The skeletal system provides support and structure for the body, while the muscular system helps move the body and its parts.\n* The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that can be absorbed and used by the body, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for energy production.\n* The circulatory system delivers oxygenated blood to the body's cells and removes carbon dioxide, while the urinary system removes waste products from the blood.\n* The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, metabolism, and reproductive processes.\n* The lymphatic system helps defend the body against infection and disease, while the immune system fights off foreign invaders.\n* The nervous system controls and coordinates the body's functions, including movement, sensation, and thought processes.\n\nOverall, the body's systems work together in a complex interplay to maintain homeostasis and ensure the proper functioning of the body.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.\", \"Based on the given passages, several body systems work together to keep the human body functioning normally. The passages do not provide specific examples, numbers, or comparisons.\", \"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together in a coordinated manner to maintain overall body function. While individual systems each have specific functions, they also collaborate to support one another. For example, the urinary system cleans blood from other systems, whereas the respiratory system provides oxygen and removes carbon dioxide. These interactions demonstrate the interconnected nature of the body's systems, ensuring that even when one system is performing its primary function, it continues to support the rest of the body's operations.\", \"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together through their interdependence and collaboration in maintaining homeostasis and overall body function. The skeletal system provides support and structure, while the muscular system enables movement and maintains posture. The digestive system processes food, the respiratory system supplies oxygen and removes carbon dioxide, the circulatory system transports nutrients and oxygen throughout the body, and the urinary system removes waste products. The endocrine system regulates hormones, the lymphatic system helps in immune defense, and the reproductive system ensures genetic continuity. Each system works in harmony with the others to ensure the body's optimal functioning.\"]", "time_sec": 19.929, "generation_time_seconds": 19.2013, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7167, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 4220, 5942, 525, 82316, 323, 17188, 389, 1817, 1008, 311, 10306, 279, 2487, 594, 4622, 30201, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0087911323985967, "g_worst_claim": 0.048078056424856186, "g_content": 1.805272528465758, "g_traj_mean": 1.0965031385421753}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3807, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 2506, 279, 3738, 2487, 30201, 14279, 13, 576, 46769, 653, 537, 3410, 3151, 10295, 11, 5109, 11, 476, 35495, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, several body systems work together to keep the human body functioning normally. The passages do not provide specific examples, numbers, or comparisons.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6522244212464389, "g_worst_claim": 0.19604232907295227, "g_content": 1.2171192169189453, "g_traj_mean": 0.6922515630722046}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 304, 264, 46572, 11566, 311, 10306, 8084, 2487, 729, 13, 5976, 3842, 5942, 1817, 614, 3151, 5746, 11, 807, 1083, 50596, 311, 1824, 825, 2441, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 6543, 504, 1008, 5942, 11, 19853, 279, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 13, 4220, 21880, 19869, 279, 82316, 6993, 315, 279, 2487, 594, 5942, 11, 22573, 429, 1496, 979, 825, 1849, 374, 16380, 1181, 6028, 729, 11, 432, 9539, 311, 1824, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 2487, 594, 7525, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together in a coordinated manner to maintain overall body function. While individual systems each have specific functions, they also collaborate to support one another. For example, the urinary system cleans blood from other systems, whereas the respiratory system provides oxygen and removes carbon dioxide. These interactions demonstrate the interconnected nature of the body's systems, ensuring that even when one system is performing its primary function, it continues to support the rest of the body's operations.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7289380960191542, "g_worst_claim": 0.0749966303507487, "g_content": 0.909169589771944, "g_traj_mean": 0.6477811336517334}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 1526, 862, 946, 90646, 323, 20031, 304, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 323, 8084, 2487, 729, 13, 576, 68297, 1849, 5707, 1824, 323, 5944, 11, 1393, 279, 51092, 1849, 20081, 7203, 323, 31995, 47278, 13, 576, 58971, 1849, 11364, 3607, 11, 279, 41531, 1849, 16720, 23552, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 11, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 68069, 36393, 323, 23552, 6814, 279, 2487, 11, 323, 279, 71635, 1849, 28160, 12291, 3871, 13, 576, 835, 77638, 1849, 79312, 43215, 11, 279, 42645, 774, 1849, 8609, 304, 22077, 9055, 11, 323, 279, 41789, 1849, 25351, 18929, 49006, 13, 8886, 1849, 4278, 304, 25281, 448, 279, 3800, 311, 5978, 279, 2487, 594, 22823, 30201, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together through their interdependence and collaboration in maintaining homeostasis and overall body function. The skeletal system provides support and structure, while the muscular system enables movement and maintains posture. The digestive system processes food, the respiratory system supplies oxygen and removes carbon dioxide, the circulatory system transports nutrients and oxygen throughout the body, and the urinary system removes waste products. The endocrine system regulates hormones, the lymphatic system helps in immune defense, and the reproductive system ensures genetic continuity. Each system works in harmony with the others to ensure the body's optimal functioning.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.3327990405468477, "g_worst_claim": -0.0374748669564724, "g_content": 0.4259854468746462, "g_traj_mean": 0.298526793718338}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.66, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "106", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together as follows:\n\nThe skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The urinary system helps to clean waste products from the other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the other systems. The nervous system plays a crucial role in coordinating the functions of all the other systems.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.\", \"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together through various interactions and dependencies. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems all collaborate to maintain the body's normal functioning. The urinary system cleans waste products from several other systems, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, and circulatory systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. The information focuses on the urinary and respiratory systems but implies that all systems interact to ensure overall bodily health.\", \"Based on the given passages, several systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. \\n\\n- The urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems.\\n- The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\\n- These systems are interconnected, with the urinary system including the kidneys and lower intestines, and the respiratory system including the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.\\n- This cooperation ensures the body maintains a healthy balance and functions efficiently.\", \"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by performing specific functions that support each other's operations. For instance, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\"]", "time_sec": 21.836, "generation_time_seconds": 20.8694, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9532, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 4220, 5942, 525, 82316, 323, 17188, 389, 1817, 1008, 311, 10306, 279, 2487, 594, 4622, 30201, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems are interconnected and rely on each other to maintain the body's normal functioning.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0087911323985967, "g_worst_claim": 0.048078056424856186, "g_content": 1.805272528465758, "g_traj_mean": 1.0965031385421753}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 1526, 5257, 21880, 323, 19543, 13, 576, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 835, 77638, 11, 42645, 774, 11, 22077, 11, 323,