{"id": "107", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "The Windward and Leeward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea. The Windward Islands are in the southeast and are exposed to the northeast trade winds, hence they receive more rain and are wetter. On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are located in the northwest and are away from the wind, making them drier.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind and receive more rain, making them wetter. The leeward islands, on the other hand, are away from the wind and receive less rain, making them drier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind and receive more rain, making them wetter. The leeward islands, on the other hand, are away from the wind and receive less rain, making them drier.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind and receive more rain, making them wetter. The leeward islands, on the other hand, are away from the wind and receive less rain, making them drier.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands are closer to the northeast trade winds and are exposed to the wind, resulting in more rain and being wetter. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are farther from the trade winds and are less exposed to the wind, leading to less rain and being drier.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the Windward Islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean. On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain. Additionally, the Windward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea and are southeastern islands of the Caribbean.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind and receive more rain, making them wetter and having the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. The leeward islands, on the other hand, are farthest from the shore and are drier but still receive some rain.\"]", "time_sec": 18.06, "generation_time_seconds": 17.4919, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5595, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 374, 429, 279, 9956, 1606, 29000, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 323, 5258, 803, 11174, 11, 3259, 1105, 14401, 465, 13, 576, 512, 24035, 29000, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 525, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 323, 5258, 2686, 11174, 11, 3259, 1105, 294, 7253, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind and receive more rain, making them wetter. The leeward islands, on the other hand, are away from the wind and receive less rain, making them drier.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6276659637231093, "g_worst_claim": -0.039615952968597413, "g_content": 1.025068759918213, "g_traj_mean": 0.4565964937210083}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 12128, 311, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 323, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 11, 12942, 304, 803, 11174, 323, 1660, 14401, 465, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 42626, 504, 279, 6559, 28492, 323, 