ast trade winds (northeasterlies) and thus receive more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles and are away from the wind (\"lee\"), resulting in them being drier but still receiving some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4455238747326826, "g_worst_claim": 0.4032247066497803, "g_content": 2.2340706273129114, "g_traj_mean": 1.5457128286361694}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.4, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "112", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between the Windward Islands and the Leeward Islands is their exposure to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and are therefore wetter and receive more rainfall, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, but still receive some rainfall. Additionally, the Windward Islands are located southeast of the Caribbean Sea, while the Leeward Islands are located northwest of the Caribbean Sea.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain due to their exposure to the northeast trade winds, making them wetter. The Leeward Islands are farther from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain due to their exposure to the northeast trade winds, making them wetter. The Leeward Islands are farther from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind and receive more rain, making them wetter. The leeward islands, on the other hand, are away from the wind and receive less rain, making them drier.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind, receive more rain, and are wetter. They are also the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the leeward islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain due to their exposure to the northeast trade winds, making them wetter. The Leeward Islands are farther from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.\", \"Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are those exposed to the wind, specifically the northeast trade winds, and are located in the southeastern part of the Caribbean Sea. The Leeward Islands, on the other hand, are the northwestern islands and are positioned away from the wind. One of the main differences mentioned is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are generally wetter than the Leeward Islands.\"]", "time_sec": 17.701, "generation_time_seconds": 17.065, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6256, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 374, 429, 279, 9956, 1606, 29000, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 323, 5258, 803, 11174, 11, 3259, 1105, 14401, 465, 13, 576, 512, 24035, 29000, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 525, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 323, 5258, 2686, 11174, 11, 3259, 1105, 294, 7253, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind and receive more rain, making them wetter. The leeward islands, on the other hand, are away from the wind and receive less rain, making them drier.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6431554993605002, "g_worst_claim": -0.007711160182952881, "g_content": 0.968017578125, "g_traj_mean": 0.45291173458099365}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 374, 429, 279, 9956, 1606, 29000, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 11, 5258, 803, 11174, 11, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 13, 2379, 525, 1083, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 512, 24035, 29000, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 714, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind, receive more rain, and are wetter. They are also the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the leeward islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1789680043307165, "g_worst_claim": 0.3255249460538228, "g_content": 2.0069236755371094, "g_traj_mean": 1.0283266305923462}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 4152, 311, 862, 14338, 311, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 11, 3259, 1105, 14401, 465, 13, 576, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 42626, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 714, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain due to their exposure to the northeast trade winds, making them wetter. The Leeward Islands are farther from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9236330868614523, "g_worst_claim": 0.3255249460538228, "g_content": 1.7044700622558593, "g_traj_mean": 0.9751980304718018}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 1846, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 11, 11689, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 11, 323, 525, 7407, 304, 279, 82109, 949, 315, 279, 34274, 15029, 13, 576, 1967, 24035, 22235, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 525, 279, 10200, 30282, 29000, 323, 525, 34228, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 13, 3776, 315, 279, 1887, 11799, 9733, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 8789, 14401, 465, 1091, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are those exposed to the wind, specifically the northeast trade winds, and are located in the southeastern part of the Caribbean Sea. The Leeward Islands, on the other hand, are the northwestern islands and are positioned away from the wind. One of the main differences mentioned is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are generally wetter than the Leeward Islands.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8732660401474821, "g_worst_claim": 0.14649826288223267, "g_content": 1.5248041152954102, "g_traj_mean": 0.7877610325813293}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.73, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "113", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "To transfer water shares, the seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of it. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. After these steps, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner. If the original certificate is lost, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the Company and must be signed and notarized.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process for transferring water shares involves the following steps:\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the process for transferring water shares involves the following steps:\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through the following steps:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\", \"Based on the given passages, water shares can be transferred through the following steps:\\n\\n1. Return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to the seller and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. Provide proof of ownership to the new owner of the property.\\n3. Pay a fee of $75.00 to process the Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n5. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the Company and must be signed and notarized.\", \"Based on the given passages, the process for transferring water shares involves the following steps:\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\", \"Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through the following steps:\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\"]", "time_sec": 21.496, "generation_time_seconds": 20.8619, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6251, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3015, 13248, 525, 22409, 1526, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22856, 1969, 470, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 429, 572, 12607, 311, 1105, 323, 1841, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 15748, 624, 17, 13, 576, 501, 6372, 315, 279, 3343, 1969, 3410, 11064, 315, 15278, 624, 18, 13, 362, 11060, 315, 400, 22, 20, 13, 15, 15, 19