{"id": "116", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how water shares are transferred:\n\n1. Passage 1 states that a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. The passage also mentions that a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n2. Passage 2 outlines the steps required to transfer a Water Stock Certificate: (a) The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate, (b) the new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership, (c) a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and (d) a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner.\n3. Passage 3 provides general information about buying a home with water shares or rights, including the need to understand the steps involved in transferring water rights into the buyer's name. However, this passage does not provide specific instructions for transferring water shares.\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, the answer to the question is:\n\nTransferring water shares involves paying a fee of $75.00 to process the transfer, returning the Water Stock Certificate to the company, providing proof of ownership, and obtaining a new Water Stock Certificate in the new owner's name.", "pred": "1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n3. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form.\n4. To transfer a Water Stock Certificate, a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer.\n5. The seller must also provide proof of ownership.\n6. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued once the transfer is completed.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n3. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form.\n4. To transfer a Water Stock Certificate, a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer.\n5. The seller must also provide proof of ownership.\n6. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued once the transfer is completed.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through the following steps:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\", \"Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through the following steps:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n3. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form.\\n4. To transfer a Water Stock Certificate, a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer.\\n5. The seller must also provide proof of ownership.\\n6. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued once the transfer is completed.\", \"Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through a series of steps:\\n\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\\n5. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the Company and must be signed and notarized.\"]", "time_sec": 23.119, "generation_time_seconds": 22.3971, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7055, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3015, 13248, 525, 22409, 1526, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22856, 1969, 470, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 429, 572, 12607, 311, 1105, 323, 1841, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 15748, 624, 17, 13, 576, 501, 6372, 315, 279, 3343, 1969, 3410, 11064, 315, 15278, 624, 18, 13, 362, 11060, 315, 400, 22, 20, 13, 15, 15, 1969, 387, 7171, 311, 1882, 264, 9959, 12648, 31402, 8317, 624, 19, 13, 362, 501, 9959, 12648, 31402, 686, 387, 10897, 311, 279, 501, 6372, 315, 3255, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, water shares are transferred through the following steps:\n\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4600506397036763, "g_worst_claim": 0.21950276692708334, "g_content": 2.004104282545007, "g_traj_mean": 1.5169837474822998}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3015, 13248, 525, 22409, 1526, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22856, 1969, 470, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 429, 572, 12607, 311, 1105, 323, 18