{"id": "119", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek, American, Italian, and Spanish origin. In Greek and American, it means 'Reap; from Therasia.' In Italian, it is interpreted as 'Harvester.' In Spanish, the name is associated with two popular saints, 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.' The name is also thought to originate from the Greek “therizein” meaning “to harvest, harvester” or from the Greek “theros” meaning “summer”.", "pred": "The passages also mention that Teresa is the Spanish, Portuguese, and Italian form of Theresa, and it is thought to come from the Greek \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or from the Greek \"theros\" meaning \"summer.\" Additionally, there is a reference to Therasia as the name of a Greek island, and the usage of Teresa as a female given name can be traced back to Spain and Portugal pre-Middle Ages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The passages also mention that Teresa is the Spanish, Portuguese, and Italian form of Theresa, and it is thought to come from the Greek \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or from the Greek \"theros\" meaning \"summer.\" Additionally, there is a reference to Therasia as the name of a Greek island, and the usage of Teresa as a female given name can be traced back to Spain and Portugal pre-Middle Ages.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the name Teresa has different meanings depending on its origin:\\n\\n1. Greek Meaning: The name Teresa is a Greek baby name. In Greek, the meaning of the name Teresa is \\\"Reap; from Therasia.\\\"\\n2. American Meaning: The name Teresa is an American baby name. In American, the meaning of the name Teresa is \\\"Reap; from Therasia.\\\"\\n3. Italian Meaning: The name Teresa is an Italian baby name. In Italian, the meaning of the name Teresa is \\\"Harvester.\\\"\\n4. Spanish Meaning: The name Teresa is a Spanish baby name. In Spanish, the meaning of the name Teresa is \\\"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'.\\\"\\n\\nThe name Theresa is also mentioned, which is a Greek baby name with a similar meaning to Teresa. In Greek, the meaning of the name Theresa is \\\"Reaper; from Therasia.\\\"\", \"Based on the given passages, the name Teresa has different meanings in various languages and cultural contexts:\\n\\n1. Greek Meaning: Teresa means \\\"Reap; from Therasia\\\" in Greek.\\n2. American Meaning: Teresa means \\\"Reap; from Therasia\\\" in American.\\n3. Italian Meaning: Teresa means \\\"Harvester\\\" in Italian.\\n4. Spanish Meaning: Teresa is a name of two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux, in Spanish.\\n\\nThe passages also mention that Teresa is the Spanish, Portuguese, and Italian form of Theresa, and it is thought to come from the Greek \\\"therizein\\\" meaning \\\"to harvest, harvester\\\" or from the Greek \\\"theros\\\" meaning \\\"summer.\\\" Additionally, there is a reference to Therasia as the name of a Greek island, and the usage of Teresa as a female given name can be traced back to Spain and Portugal pre-Middle Ages.\", \"Based on the given passages, the name Teresa has different meanings in various languages:\\n\\n1. In Greek, the name Teresa means \\\"Reap; from Therasia.\\\"\\n2. In American, the name Teresa means \\\"Reap; from Therasia.\\\"\\n3. In Italian, the name Teresa means \\\"Harvester.\\\"\\n4. In Spanish, the name Teresa refers to two popular saints, \\\"Teresa of Avila\\\" and \\\"Therese of Lisieux.\\\"\\n\\nThe passages also mention that the name Theresa, which is related to Teresa, has a Greek meaning of \\\"Reaper; from Therasia.\\\" The name Teresa, as a female given name, can be traced back to its usage in Spain and Portugal pre-Middle Ages, and it is thought to come from the Greek words \\\"therizein,\\\" meaning \\\"to harvest, harvester,\\\" or \\\"theros,\\\" meaning \\\"summer.\\\"\", \"Based on the given passages, the name Teresa has different meanings in various languages and cultures:\\n\\n1. In Greek (Theresa), the meaning is \\\"Reaper; from Therasia.\\\"\\n2. In American, the meaning is \\\"Reaper; from Therasia.\\\"\\n3. In Italian, the meaning is \\\"Harvester.\\\"\\n4. In Spanish and Portuguese, the meaning is \\\"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.'\\\"\\n\\nThe name Teresa is derived from the Greek word \\\"therizein,\\\" which means \\\"to harvest\\\" or \\\"harvester.\\\" It is also associated with the Greek island of Therasia. The name's usage as a female given name has historical roots in Spain and Portugal before the Middle Ages.\"]", "time_sec": 33.196, "generation_time_seconds": 31.6504, "selection_time_seconds": 1.5333, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 702, 2155, 49700, 11649, 389, 1181, 6238, 1447, 16, 13, 17860, 48103, 25, 576, 829, 63440, 374, 264, 17860, 8770, 829, 13, 758, 17860, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 63440, 374, 330, 693, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 10040, 17, 13, 3693, 48103, 25, 576, 829, 63440, 374, 458, 3693, 8770, 829, 13, 758, 3693, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 63440, 374, 330, 693, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 10040, 18, 13, 14811, 48103, 25, 576, 829, 63440, 374, 458, 14811, 8770, 829, 13, 758, 14811, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 63440, 374, 330, 26490, 82738, 10040, 19, 13, 15154, 48103, 25, 576, 829, 63440, 374, 264, 15154, 8770, 829, 13, 758, 15154, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 63440, 374, 330, 675, 315, 1378, 5411, 67120, 364, 51, 37586, 315, 7519, 10524, 6, 323, 364, 1001, 261, 2367, 315, 43072, 52719, 6, 2217, 785, 829, 42712, 374, 1083, 9733, 11, 892, 374, 264, 17860, 8770, 829, 448, 264, 4428, 7290, 311, 63440, 13, 758, 17860, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 42712, 374, 330, 693, 3191, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 1189, 151645], "pred": "The name Th