365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 624, 21, 13, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 323, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 22, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 23, 13, 18678, 279, 14285, 369, 279, 24354, 25156, 323, 1221, 4828, 1105, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 24, 13, 576, 24354, 15336, 525, 220, 21, 7541, 1293, 553, 220, 19, 7541, 6884, 11, 714, 498, 646, 6707, 9225, 1181, 15336, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17, 476, 220, 19, 7541, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Prepare the site by laying down a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4x4 skids to the required length and set them on the prepared site, ensuring they are level.\n3. Cut two 2x6 rim joists to the required length and six joists to the required length.\n4. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids following the shed building plans.\n5. Check for square and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n6. Position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n7. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n8. Construct the walls for the shed separately and then raise them onto the frame.\n9. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, but you can easily expand its dimensions in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.695096574441678, "g_worst_claim": 0.22346870104471842, "g_content": 2.7864059294113006, "g_traj_mean": 1.6943615674972534}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "126", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "pred": "1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches.\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches.\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n10. Construct the shed's walls separately and then raise them onto the frame.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches.\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches.\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n10. Construct the shed's walls separately and then raise them onto the frame.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches.\\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n10. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\\n11. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"Based on the given passages, to build a lean-to shed, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches.\\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches.\\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n10. Construct the shed's walls separately and then raise them onto the frame.\", \"Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several detailed steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Site**: Begin by compacting the ground to a layer of 4 inches of gravel to ensure a stable foundation. This ensures the shed has a solid base.\\n\\n2. **Cutting and Setting Skids**: Cut two 4 by 4 skids to a length of 6 feet. Set these skids and ensure they are level. Following the shed building plans, cut two 2 by 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\\n\\n3. **Assembling the Floor**: Assemble the floor using the rim joists and joists, ensuring everything is square. Anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles for stability.\\n\\n4. **Securing the Floor Joists**: Position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to secure them. This step is crucial for maintaining the structure's integrity.\\n\\n5. **Flooring Installation**: Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. This waterproofs the shed and adds durability.\\n\\n6. **Building the Walls**: Construct the walls separately and then raise them onto the frame. This allows for flexibility in expanding the shed's dimensions.\\n\\n7. **Frame Dimensions**: The shed described is 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, but the instructions indicate that the dimensions can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet, providing flexibility in design.\\n\\nBy following these steps, one can construct a lean-to shed that is both functional and adaptable.\", \"Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several key steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site with a 4\\\" layer of compacted gravel.\\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 6 feet.\\n3. Set the skids on the compacted gravel, following the shed building plans.\\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4\\\" and six joists to a length of 44 3/4\\\".\\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids.\\n6. Check the structure for square.\\n7. Anchor the frame to the skids using four joist clip angles.\\n\\nThese steps form the base foundation for constructing the lean-to shed, ensuring a sturdy and square base for further construction.\"]", "time_sec": 45.9, "generation_time_seconds": 44.9382, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9415, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 518, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 18, 13, 2573, 323, 2188, 279, 1901, 3365, 2701, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 624, 19, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 20, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 738, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 438, 6839, 304, 279, 6422, 57949, 3772, 315, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 6649, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 17105, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 624, 22, 13, 19649, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 23, 13, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 323, 11, 979, 9334, 11, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 24, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 14285, 369, 279, 24354, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 1221, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 16, 1