53, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 13, 2573, 1493, 1901, 3365, 323, 5978, 807, 525, 2188, 13, 22713, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 553, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 2121, 41964, 279, 16581, 95518, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 1667, 279, 30130, 7647, 1671, 323, 7647, 1671, 11, 22573, 4297, 374, 9334, 13, 48772, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 369, 19753, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 8430, 1677, 279, 16581, 10946, 1671, 95518, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 323, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 9767, 1105, 13, 1096, 3019, 374, 16587, 369, 20337, 279, 5944, 594, 16614, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 51444, 287, 39145, 95518, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 1096, 46419, 82, 279, 24354, 323, 11367, 38565, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 30133, 279, 71178, 95518, 18678, 279, 14285, 25156, 323, 1221, 4828, 1105, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 1096, 6147, 369, 24177, 304, 23175, 279, 24354, 594, 15336, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 4369, 32023, 95518, 576, 24354, 7481, 374, 220, 21, 7541, 1293, 553, 220, 19, 7541, 6884, 11, 714, 279, 11221, 13216, 429, 279, 15336, 646, 387, 6707, 17183, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17, 476, 220, 19, 7541, 11, 8241, 24177, 304, 2884, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 825, 646, 9245, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 429, 374, 2176, 15629, 323, 93748, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, one can construct a lean-to shed that is both functional and adaptable.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.051277907423749, "g_worst_claim": 0.01789966970682144, "g_content": 1.7669977115679392, "g_traj_mean": 1.0814119577407837}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 1376, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 1, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 624, 18, 13, 2573, 279, 1901, 3365, 389, 279, 16830, 291, 41523, 11, 2701, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 624, 19, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 1, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 22956, 20, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 738, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 279, 5944, 369, 9334, 624, 22, 13, 48772, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 1667, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 382, 9485, 7354, 1352, 279, 2331, 16266, 369, 49353, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 22573, 264, 44552, 323, 9334, 2331, 369, 4623, 8086, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps form the base foundation for constructing the lean-to shed, ensuring a sturdy and square base for further construction.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4361975532095534, "g_worst_claim": 0.011897614369025597, "g_content": 1.9584258665521461, "g_traj_mean": 1.2551954984664917}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.34, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "127", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Sure! Here's my attempt to answer your question based on the provided passages:\n\nHow do you prepare the site for building a lean-to shed?\n\nAccording to passage 1, step 1, you should prepare the site by laying down a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. This will provide a stable base for the shed's foundation. Additionally, passage 2 mentions cutting two pressure-treated 4x4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids, which will serve as the foundation for the shed. Finally, passage 3 provides instructions for building the shed's floor, including cutting rim joists to a length of 6 feet. Based on these passages, it appears that preparing the site involves laying down a layer of gravel and setting the skids in place before constructing the floor.", "pred": "The shed dimensions can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The shed dimensions can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches.\\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n10. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\\n11. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"Based on the given passages, to build a lean-to shed, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\\n2. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\\n3. Position the skids and level them according to the shed building plans.\\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\\n6. Check for square and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n7. Position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to the skids.\\n8. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n9. Construct the walls for the shed separately and then raise them onto the frame.\\n\\nThe shed dimensions can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps:\\n\\n1. **Site Preparation**: Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. This ensures a stable foundation for the shed.\\n\\n2. **Cutting Skids**: Cut two 4x4 skids to the required length (not specified in the passages but typically around 6 feet for a standard shed).\\n\\n3. **Setting Skids**: Set the skids on the prepared site. Level them as needed following the shed building plans.\\n\\n4. **Cutting Rim Joists**: Cut two 4x4 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches. Cut six joists to 44 3/4 inches.\\n\\n5. **Assembling the Floor**: Assemble the floor using the cut joists and set it on the skids. Ensure the frame is square before anchoring it to the skids with joist clip angles.\\n\\n6. **Positioning the Frame**: Position the framed floor on the skids, ensuring it is square.\\n\\n7. **Flooring Installation**: Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n\\n8. **Wall Construction**: The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\\n\\n9. **Floor Framing Adjustment**: Adjust the flooring to fit snugly over the frame.\\n\\n10. **Dimensions**: The shed dimensions can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4 inches and set them at the base, ensuring they are level. Following the shed building plans, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. For flooring, cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to 6 feet for the skids, position the frame, toenail the floor joists to the skids, and attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring. Finally, construct the shed's walls separately and raise them onto the frame.\"]", "time_sec": 43.372, "generation_time_seconds": 42.6784, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6845, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 518, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 18, 13, 2573, 323, 2188, 279, 1901, 3365, 2701, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 624, 19, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 20, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 738, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 438, 6839, 304, 279, 6422, 57949, 3772, 315, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 6649, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 17105, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 624, 22, 13, 19649, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 23, 13, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 323, 11, 979, 9334, 11, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 24, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 14285, 369, 279, 24354, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 1221, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 24354, 15336, 525, 220, 21, 7541, 1293, 553, 220, 19, 7541, 6884, 11, 448, 279, 2999, 311, 9225, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17, 476, 220, 19, 7541, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches.\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n10. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\n11. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.970537156409385, "g_worst_claim": 0.5251326560974121, "g_content": 2.567323486328125, "g_traj_mean": 1.763537883758545}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1936, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21,