11, 3931, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 311, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 2309, 279, 4034, 11, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 323, 15498, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 13, 17375, 11, 9245, 279, 24354, 594, 14285, 25156, 323, 4828, 1105, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to 70 2/4 inches and set them at the base, ensuring they are level. Following the shed building plans, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. For flooring, cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to 6 feet for the skids, position the frame, toenail the floor joists to the skids, and attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring. Finally, construct the shed's walls separately and raise them onto the frame.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.043654700290429, "g_worst_claim": 0.7422070503234863, "g_content": 2.9197884025154535, "g_traj_mean": 1.846696376800537}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "129", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "What are the dimensions of the shed in passage 3?\n\nThe dimensions of the shed in passage 3 are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the first step in building a lean-to shed is to prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 6 feet. Position the frame on the skids, ensuring it is square, and toenail the floor joists to the skids. Next, attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. Finally, construct the shed walls separately and raise them onto the frame.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the first step in building a lean-to shed is to prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 6 feet. Position the frame on the skids, ensuring it is square, and toenail the floor joists to the skids. Next, attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. Finally, construct the shed walls separately and raise them onto the frame.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches.\\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n10. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\\n11. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"Based on the given passages, the first step in building a lean-to shed is to prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 6 feet. Position the frame on the skids, ensuring it is square, and toenail the floor joists to the skids. Next, attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. Finally, construct the shed walls separately and raise them onto the frame.\", \"Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several detailed steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Site**: Start by preparing the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel to ensure a stable foundation.\\n\\n2. **Cutting Materials**: Cut two 4x4 skids at 70 2/4 inches. These skids will serve as the base for the shed. Additionally, cut two 2x6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches.\\n\\n3. **Set and Level the Skids**: Set the cut skids at a 70 2/4-inch length. Ensure they are level and secure them to the ground.\\n\\n4. **Assemble the Floor Frame**: Use the cut 2x6 rim joists and six joists to assemble the floor. Place the assembled floor on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\\n\\n5. **Check for Square**: Before anchoring the frame to the skids, check that the floor is square to ensure structural integrity.\\n\\n6. **Anchor the Frame**: Secure the floor frame to the skids using four joist clip angles.\\n\\n7. **Flooring Installation**: Position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to the skids. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n\\n8. **Construct Wall Framework**: Build the shed walls separately and then raise them onto the frame.\\n\\n9. **Adjust Dimensions**: The shed dimensions can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet to accommodate larger sizes as needed.\\n\\nThese steps provide a comprehensive guide on how to construct a lean-to shed, including the necessary materials, measurements, and assembly techniques.\", \"Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\\n2. Cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and level them.\\n3. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches.\\n4. Assemble the floor frame on the skids and check for square.\\n5. Anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n6. Position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to them.\\n7. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n8. Construct the shed walls separately and raise them onto the frame.\\n9. Adjust the dimensions of the shed as needed in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\"]", "time_sec": 42.624, "generation_time_seconds": 41.4615, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1522, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 518, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 18, 13, 2573, 323, 2188, 279, 1901, 3365, 2701, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 624, 19, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 20, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 738, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 438, 6839, 304, 279, 6422, 57949, 3772, 315, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 6649, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 17105, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 624, 22, 13, 19649, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 23, 13, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 323, 11, 979, 9334, 11, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 24, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 14285, 369, 279, 24354, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 1221, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 24354, 15336, 525, 220, 21, 7541, 1293, 553, 220, 19, 7541, 6884, 11, 448, 279, 2999, 311, 9225, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17, 476, 220, 19, 7541, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches.\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 inches and six joists at 44 3/4 inches.\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n10. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\n11. The shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, with the option to expand in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9859363204285025, "g_worst_claim": 0.5289517243703207, "g_content": 2.58345947265625, "g_traj_mean": 1.774147629737854}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1156, 3019, 304, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 374, 311, 10549, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 5005, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 13, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 22573, 432, 374, 9334, 11, 323, 99034, 604, 279, 6422,