0, 3973, 369, 15619, 95518, 13235, 33230, 5503, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 1779, 429, 279, 6422, 374, 9334, 311, 5978, 23759, 16614, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 14677, 279, 16321, 95518, 34502, 279, 6422, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 1667, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 51444, 287, 39145, 95518, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 323, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 382, 23, 13, 3070, 28468, 9736, 23752, 95518, 7854, 279, 24354, 14285, 25156, 323, 1221, 4828, 1105, 8630, 279, 4034, 382, 24, 13, 3070, 38616, 32023, 95518, 576, 24354, 15336, 646, 387, 6707, 17183, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17, 476, 220, 19, 7541, 311, 28276, 8131, 12282, 438, 4362, 382, 9485, 7354, 3410, 264, 15817, 8474, 389, 1246, 311, 9245, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 2670, 279, 5871, 7236, 11, 21595, 11, 323, 14614, 12538, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps provide a comprehensive guide on how to construct a lean-to shed, including the necessary materials, measurements, and assembly techniques.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0662834470340723, "g_worst_claim": 0.10901138931512833, "g_content": 1.8311601760070448, "g_traj_mean": 1.164921760559082}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 2188, 1105, 624, 18, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 19, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 323, 1779, 369, 9334, 624, 20, 13, 48772, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 624, 21, 13, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 323, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 1105, 624, 22, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 23, 13, 18678, 279, 24354, 14285, 25156, 323, 4828, 1105, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 24, 13, 27196, 279, 15336, 315, 279, 24354, 438, 4362, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17, 476, 220, 19, 7541, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and level them.\n3. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to 7 3/4 inches and six joists to 44 3/4 inches.\n4. Assemble the floor frame on the skids and check for square.\n5. Anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n6. Position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to them.\n7. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n8. Construct the shed walls separately and raise them onto the frame.\n9. Adjust the dimensions of the shed as needed in increments of 2 or 4 feet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7355821736059538, "g_worst_claim": 0.5034766991933187, "g_content": 2.554430397607947, "g_traj_mean": 1.6047471761703491}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 13.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "130", "question": "difference between vietnam and india", "gt": "The passages suggest that trends in India are more typical than those in Vietnam, particularly in the area of education. Vietnam's education system is described as relatively equitable, where poorer children receive the same treatment as their better-off counterparts. In contrast, India's early focus was on getting children into school, which involved setting up schools, and training teachers. Politically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War. Both countries have a history of colonialism, with India being a former colony of the United Kingdom and Vietnam of France. Post-colonization, India experienced division and conflict among Hindus, Muslims and Sikhs. Cultural and economic links between India and Vietnam date back to the 2nd century.", "pred": "Additionally, India and Vietnam have a strong bilateral relationship, which dates back to the 2nd century. This cultural and economic connection is evident in the influence of the Indic Chăm Pa kingdom on Vietnamese music. On the other hand, both countries faced significant historical challenges during the colonial era, with India losing its colonies to partition and Vietnam losing its colonies to France. Despite these shared experiences, the contrasting education systems and cultural exchanges highlight the distinct differences between Vietnam and India.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Additionally, India and Vietnam have a strong bilateral relationship, which dates back to the 2nd century. This cultural and economic connection is evident in the influence of the Indic Chăm Pa kingdom on Vietnamese music. On the other hand, both countries faced significant historical challenges during the colonial era, with India losing its colonies to partition and Vietnam losing its colonies to France. Despite these shared experiences, the contrasting education systems and cultural exchanges highlight the distinct differences between Vietnam and India.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between Vietnam and India lies in their education systems and historical relationships. Vietnam's education system is relatively equitable, ensuring that poorer children receive the same opportunities as those who are better-off. In contrast, India's early focus was on getting children into school, which involved looking at resources and facilities, setting up schools, and training teachers. Additionally, Vietnam and India have strong bilateral relations, with cultural and economic links dating back to the 2nd century. India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, while France lost the colony of Indochina, modern-day Vietnam, shortly after World War II.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between Vietnam and India lies in their education systems and historical relations with France. Vietnam's education system is described as relatively equitable, meaning poorer children receive the same education as those who are better-off, ensuring they are not disadvantaged. In contrast, India's early focus was on getting children into school, which involved setting up schools, training teachers, and ensuring basic resources and facilities. These differences in education systems reflect the unique historical and social contexts of each country.\\n\\nAdditionally, India and Vietnam have a strong bilateral relationship, which dates back to the 2nd century. This cultural and economic connection is evident in the influence of the Indic Chăm Pa kingdom on Vietnamese music. On the other hand, both countries faced significant historical challenges during the colonial era, with India losing its colonies to partition and Vietnam losing its colonies to France. Despite these shared experiences, the contrasting education systems and cultural exchanges highlight the distinct differences between Vietnam and India.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between Vietnam and India is that Vietnam had a strong focus on providing equitable education to all children, regardless of their socio-economic status, by setting up schools, training teachers, and looking at resources and facilities. India, on the other hand, faced significant challenges in providing basic education for its children, which led to the early focus on getting children into school. Additionally, Vietnam had strong bilateral relations with India, while India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War.\", \"Based on the given passages, the main differences between Vietnam and India are as follows:\\n\\n1. Education System: Vietnam's education system is described as relatively equitable, ensuring that poorer children receive the same opportunities as those who are better-off. In contrast, the focus in India was on getting children into school and setting up resources and facilities, which is considered more typical in India's context.\\n\\n2. Cultural and Economic Links: India and Vietnam have strong bilateral relations, with cultural and economic links dating back to the 2nd century. In contrast, the United Kingdom and France, which also had large colonies, suffered colonial losses during the same period.\\n\\n3. Decolonization and Independence: India gained independence from British rule in 1947, leading to the partition of the country and numerous conflicts. Vietnam gained independence from French rule shortly after World War II, in 1945.\"]", "time_sec": 31.088, "generation_time_seconds": 30.3569, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7191, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 22500, 323, 6747, 15448, 304, 862, 6731, 5942, 323, 13656, 11871, 13, 22500, 594, 6731, 1849, 374, 12040, 76009, 11, 22573, 429, 65181, 2841, 5258, 279, 1852, 10488, 438, 1846, 879, 525, 2664, 12462, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 6747, 594, 4124, 5244, 572, 389, 3709, 2841, 1119, 2906, 11, 892, 6398, 3330, 518, 4963, 323, 12786, 11, 6243, 705, 8682, 11, 323, 4862, 13336, 13, 22406, 11, 22500, 323, 6747, 614, 3746, 51203, 4300, 11, 448, 12752, 323, 6955, 7746, 4924, 1182, 311, 279, 220, 17, 303, 9294, 13, 6747, 7248, 22500, 594, 23665, 504, 9625, 323, 16087, 3693, 21587, 304, 279, 22500, 5004, 11, 1393, 9625, 5558, 279, 40936, 315, 2263, 4953, 2210, 11, 6481, 11228, 22500, 11, 19620, 1283, 4337, 5004, 7946, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between Vietnam and India lies in their education systems and historical relationships. Vietnam's education system is relatively equitable, ensuring that poorer children receive the same opportunities as those who are better-off. In contrast, India's early focus was on getting children into school, which involved looking at resources and facilities, setting up schools, and training teachers. Additionally, Vietnam and India have strong bilateral relations, with cultural and economic links dating back to the 2nd century. India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, while France lost the colony of Indochina, modern-day Vietnam, shortly after World War II.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.838000528401037, "g_worst_claim": 0.4639122486114502, "g_content": 2.9040074002915532, "g_traj_mean": 1.8122153282165527}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 22500, 323, 6747, 15448, 304, 862, 6731, 5942, 323, 13656, 4300, 448, 9625, 13, 22500, 594, 6731, 1849, 374, 7481, 438, 12040, 76009, 11, 7290, 65181, 2841, 5258, 279, 1852, 6731, 438, 1846, 879, 525, 2664, 12462, 11, 22573, 807, 525, 537, 79847, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 6747, 594, 4124, 5244, 572, 389, 3709, 2841, 1119, 2906, 11, 892