1203, 4300, 448, 6747, 11, 1393, 6747, 7248, 22500, 594, 23665, 504, 9625, 323, 16087, 3693, 21587, 304, 279, 22500, 5004, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between Vietnam and India is that Vietnam had a strong focus on providing equitable education to all children, regardless of their socio-economic status, by setting up schools, training teachers, and looking at resources and facilities. India, on the other hand, faced significant challenges in providing basic education for its children, which led to the early focus on getting children into school. Additionally, Vietnam had strong bilateral relations with India, while India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.428653140406831, "g_worst_claim": 0.32669364322315564, "g_content": 2.1803538484393425, "g_traj_mean": 1.3276504278182983}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1887, 11799, 1948, 22500, 323, 6747, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 11668, 739, 25, 22500, 594, 6731, 1849, 374, 7481, 438, 12040, 76009, 11, 22573, 429, 65181, 2841, 5258, 279, 1852, 10488, 438, 1846, 879, 525, 2664, 12462, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 5244, 304, 6747, 572, 389, 3709, 2841, 1119, 2906, 323, 6243, 705, 4963, 323, 12786, 11, 892, 374, 6509, 803, 14260, 304, 6747, 594, 2266, 382, 17, 13, 40233, 323, 22546, 25422, 25, 6747, 323, 22500, 614, 3746, 51203, 4300, 11, 448, 12752, 323, 6955, 7746, 4924, 1182, 311, 279, 220, 17, 303, 9294, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 3639, 15072, 323, 9625, 11, 892, 1083, 1030, 3460, 47928, 11, 16256, 36583, 17683, 2337, 279, 1852, 4168, 382, 18, 13, 3714, 72269, 2022, 323, 43077, 25, 6747, 18163, 23665, 504, 7855, 5912, 304, 220, 16, 24, 19, 22, 11, 6388, 311, 279, 16658, 315, 279, 3146, 323, 12114, 25800, 13, 22500, 18163, 23665, 504, 8585, 5912, 19620, 1283, 4337, 5004, 7946, 11, 304, 220, 16, 24, 19, 20, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. Decolonization and Independence: India gained independence from British rule in 1947, leading to the partition of the country and numerous conflicts. Vietnam gained independence from French rule shortly after World War II, in 1945.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6025104100458942, "g_worst_claim": 0.4311061658357319, "g_content": 2.1220779418945312, "g_traj_mean": 1.3445903062820435}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.82, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "132", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, but keep the skins of the individual cloves intact. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices if you like. Roasting time is dependent on the size of the cloves and may take up to 45 minutes or an hour for larger cloves. Once roasted, the garlic cloves can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n4. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n4. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\\n4. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n6. Roast the garlic cloves in the oven until they are tender and the cloves are soft, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour, depending on the size of the cloves.\"]", "time_sec": 33.078, "generation_time_seconds": 32.1644, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8962, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 320, 32, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 11, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 28175, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4441777676866203, "g_worst_claim": 0.15618095795313516, "g_content": 1.7355931921850276, "g_traj_mean": 1.5131055116653442}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 11616, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 624, 19, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n4. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3600465329725622, "g_worst_claim": 0.15618095795313516, "g_content": 1.6138804844447545, "g_traj_mean": 1.4995510578155518}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5768