1410, 1896, 705, 311, 220, 19, 20, 4420, 476, 1496, 458, 6460, 624, 22, 13, 9129, 279, 53562, 30635, 84288, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 304, 279, 44944, 369, 705, 311, 220, 16, 15, 2849, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves, exposing the individual cloves.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic head and rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Roast the garlic in the preheated oven for the appropriate time, depending on the size of the cloves, which could take up to 45 minutes or even an hour.\n7. Store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2677684223566907, "g_worst_claim": 0.3649773597717285, "g_content": 1.582837291599549, "g_traj_mean": 1.1709755659103394}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 1393, 9380, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 34439, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 279, 84288, 311, 28141, 1105, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 448, 279, 3931, 3108, 705, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 315, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 279, 14900, 30635, 84288, 1667, 697, 19225, 624, 22, 13, 11830, 559, 279, 30635, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 264, 882, 17749, 389, 279, 1379, 315, 279, 84288, 11, 892, 1231, 1896, 705, 311, 220, 19, 20, 4420, 476, 1496, 458, 6460, 369, 8131, 84288, 624, 23, 13, 9129, 279, 53562, 30635, 84288, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 304, 279, 44944, 369, 705, 311, 220, 16, 15, 2849, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb while leaving the skins of the individual cloves intact.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves to expose them.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan with the cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head.\n6. Rub the olive oil over the exposed garlic cloves using your fingers.\n7. Roast the garlic in the oven for a time dependent on the size of the cloves, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour for larger cloves.\n8. Store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1916740980728993, "g_worst_claim": 0.4726112842559814, "g_content": 1.502370834350586, "g_traj_mean": 1.0846527814865112}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "136", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Sure! Here's how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nTo roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices, if desired.\n7. Roast the garlic in the preheated oven for up to 45 minutes or until the cloves are softened to your liking.\n8. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nNote that the roasting time may vary depending on the size of your garlic cloves, so check on them periodically to avoid overcooking.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves:\n1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves:\n1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\nThese steps are necessary to ensure the garlic cloves are evenly coated with olive oil and will roast properly in the oven.\", \"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the individual cloves intact.\\n3. Cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove to expose them.\\n4. Place the garlic heads, cut side up, in a baking pan or a muffin pan.\\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic clove and rub the oil over all the cut cloves with your fingers.\\n6. Roast in the preheated oven until the cloves are soft, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour, depending on their size.\"]", "time_sec": 31.636, "generation_time_seconds": 30.5519, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0719, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842