ive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5487593572677265, "g_worst_claim": 0.3649773597717285, "g_content": 1.9199276218166599, "g_traj_mean": 1.5586481094360352}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 34439, 624, 18, 13, 19649, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 1817, 5292, 586, 311, 28141, 1105, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 11, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 476, 264, 54304, 258, 7215, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 315, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 30635, 5292, 586, 323, 10273, 279, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 84288, 448, 697, 19225, 624, 21, 13, 11830, 559, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 84288, 525, 8413, 11, 892, 1231, 1896, 705, 311, 220, 19, 20, 4420, 476, 1496, 458, 6460, 11, 11649, 389, 862, 1379, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the individual cloves intact.\n3. Cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove to expose them.\n4. Place the garlic heads, cut side up, in a baking pan or a muffin pan.\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic clove and rub the oil over all the cut cloves with your fingers.\n6. Roast in the preheated oven until the cloves are soft, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour, depending on their size.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1254318728042318, "g_worst_claim": 0.3649773597717285, "g_content": 1.406701492936644, "g_traj_mean": 1.1177536249160767}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "137", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Roast in the preheated oven for 45 minutes to an hour, or until the cloves are softened.\n7. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nYou can also season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices before roasting.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the individual cloves intact.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves, exposing the individual cloves.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut-side up. A muffin pan is recommended as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic head.\\n6. Rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves using your fingers.\\n7. Roast in the preheated oven for the appropriate time depending on the size of your garlic cloves, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour for larger cloves.\"]", "time_sec": 32.338, "generation_time_seconds": 31.6699, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6521, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 320, 32, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 11, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 28175, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4740991149212466, "g_worst_claim": 0.33988118171691895, "g_content": 1.7824529333959651, "g_traj_mean": 1.510764718055725}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 311, 28141, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 362, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 11, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4051609366574334, "g_worst_claim": 0.33988118171691895, "g_content": 1.7299727427808544, "g_traj_mean": 1.410718560218811}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.361809381822584, "g_worst_claim": 0.33988118171691895, "g_content": 1.6764950343540737, "g_traj_mean": 1.3964749574661255}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 34439, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 264, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 279, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 24067, 705, 13, 362, 54304, 258, 7215, 374, 11102, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 315, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 30635, 1968, 624, 21, 13, 12839, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 1667, 697, 19225, 624, 22, 13, 11830, 559, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 369, 279, 8311, 882, 11649, 389, 279, 1379, 315, 697, 30635, 84288, 11, 892, 1231, 1896, 705, 311, 220, 19, 20, 4420, 476, 1496, 458, 6460, 369, 8131, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the individual cloves intact.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves, exposing the individual cloves.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut-side up. A muffin pan is recommended as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed garlic head.\n6. Rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves using your fingers.\n7. Roast in the preheated oven for the appropriate time depending on the size of your garlic cloves, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour for larger cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3309592347508088, "g_worst_claim": 0.33988118171691895, "g_content": 1.4762931986058012, "g_traj_mean": 1.2091071605682373}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 81.59, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.9, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "138", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded as per section 43(6). This is done under the block concept, where all assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any changes to the block's value must abide by the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961. Additionally, the assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, even if it's not used for the purposes of business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "3. If the asset is not used for business purposes after its disposal, the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV (Written Down Value) of the asset less its scrap value.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "3. If the asset is not used for business purposes after its disposal, the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV (Written Down Value) of the asset less its scrap value.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded, the treatment under the Income Tax Act is as follows:\\n\\n1. If the asset is discarded and not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This adjustment is permitted by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act.\\n\\n2. The block concept is applied where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Alterations to the value of the block must strictly follow the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\\n\\n3. If the asset is not used for business purposes after its disposal, the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV (Written Down Value) of the asset less its scrap value.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded as per Income Tax Act, the treatment is as follows:\\n\\n1. If an asset is discarded but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\\n\\n2. The asset is considered as a single asset under the block concept. This means all assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are combined and treated as one.\\n\\n3. Any alterations to the value of the block must strictly comply with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961. \\n\\n4. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening WDV of the asset less the scrap value, even if the discarded asset is not used for business purposes in subsequent years.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act, it is treated according to the block concept. This means that all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered a single asset. If the asset is not sold but discarded by the business, its scrap value can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset was discarded. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening Weighted Depreciable Value (WDV) of the asset minus its scrap value.\"]", "time_sec": 29.311, "generation_time_seconds": 28.2184, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0691, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 5420, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7708427548984398, "g_worst_claim": 0.3310006459554036, "g_content": 2.244593253502479, "g_traj_mean": 1.8093825578689575}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 279, 6380, 1212, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 374, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 1416, 279, 9329, 374, 43210, 323, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 27075, 374, 15129, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 382, 17, 13, 576, 2504, 7286, 374, 9251, 1380, 678, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 42851, 804, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 25470, 1795, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 382, 18, 13, 1416, 279, 9329, 374, 537, 1483, 369, 2562, 9895, 1283, 1181, 33445, 11, 279, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 467, 61971, 320, 35624, 6285, 5162, 8, 315, 279, 9329, 2686, 1181, 20843, 897, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. If the asset is not used for business purposes after its disposal, the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV (Written Down Value) of the asset less its scrap value.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4476687907731263, "g_worst_claim": 0.33079057931900024, "g_content": 2.1512630462646483, "g_traj_mean": 1.5505001544952393}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 438, 817, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 279, 6380, 374, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 1416, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 382, 17, 13, 576, 9329, 374, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 1212, 279, 2504, 7286, 13, 1096, 3363, 678, 11770, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 10856, 323, 11758, 438, 825, 382, 18, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 25470, 25017, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 4710, 19, 13, 576, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 1741, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 467, 61971, 315, 279, 9329, 2686, 279, 20843, 897, 11, 1496, 421, 279, 43210, 9329, 374, 537, 1483, 369, 2562, 9895, 304, 17420, 1635, 13, 151645], "pred": "4. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening WDV of the asset less the scrap value, even if the discarded asset is not used for business purposes in subsequent years.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6086866798171675, "g_worst_claim": 0.33079057931900024, "g_content": 2.189678057502298, "g_traj_mean": 1.6373053789138794}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 438, 817, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 432, 374, 11758, 4092, 311, 279, 2504, 7286, 13, 1096, 3363, 429, 678, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6509, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 1416, 279, 9329, 374, 537, 6088, 714, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 11, 1181, 20843, 897, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 279, 9329, 572, 43210, 13, 576, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 16516, 291, 4148, 2758, 2156, 5162, 320, 17563, 53, 8, 315, 279, 9329, 27283, 1181, 20843, 897, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act, it is treated according to the block concept. This means that all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered a single asset. If the asset is not sold but discarded by the business, its scrap value can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset was discarded. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening Weighted Depreciable Value (WDV) of the asset minus its scrap value.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6875264612704393, "g_worst_claim": 0.33079057931900024, "g_content": 2.7964875962999134, "g_traj_mean": 1.7140486240386963}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "139", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded. The block concept is followed, where assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if it is not used for business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "1. The scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\n2. Under the block concept, all the assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset.\n3. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening WDV of such asset less the scrap value.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. The scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\n2. Under the block concept, all the assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset.\n3. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening WDV of such asset less the scrap value.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, under the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset is permitted to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961, which allows for alterations to the value of the block according to the provisions of Chapter IV D. This means that the depreciation of the asset is adjusted based on the scrap value, ensuring that the asset's value does not continue to depreciate after its removal from service.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961 permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded, the treatment in income tax acts as follows:\\n\\n1. The scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\\n2. Under the block concept, all the assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset.\\n3. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening WDV of such asset less the scrap value.\"]", "time_sec": 24.542, "generation_time_seconds": 23.5811, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9509, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 5420, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8038889371254592, "g_worst_claim": 0.46173826853434247, "g_content": 2.291203425480769, "g_traj_mean": 1.8327419757843018}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 1212, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 374, 15129, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 26702, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 11, 892, 6147, 369, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 4092, 311, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 13, 1096, 3363, 429, 279, 93089, 315, 279, 9329, 374, 23368, 3118, 389, 279, 20843, 897, 11, 22573, 429, 279, 9329, 594, 897, 1558, 537, 3060, 311, 71958, 349, 1283, 1181, 16652, 504, 2473, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, under the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset is permitted to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961, which allows for alterations to the value of the block according to the provisions of Chapter IV D. This means that the depreciation of the asset is adjusted based on the scrap value, ensuring that the asset's value does not continue to depreciate after its removal from service.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3597724974434278, "g_worst_claim": 0.16539560423956978, "g_content": 2.104987071110652, "g_traj_mean": 1.465061902999878}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 949, 315, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 1380, 678, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6335, 2721, 3786, 323, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 614, 311, 387, 25470, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961 permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8311653453880494, "g_worst_claim": 0.46180184682210285, "g_content": 2.6499012134693287, "g_traj_mean": 1.8518083095550537}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 279, 6380, 304, 7911, 3742, 14056, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 624, 17, 13, 9449, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 678, 279, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6335, 2721, 3786, 323, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 624, 18, 13, 576, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 1741, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 467, 61971, 315, 1741, 9329, 2686, 279, 20843, 897, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. The scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\n2. Under the block concept, all the assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset.\n3. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening WDV of such asset less the scrap value.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7393477990705817, "g_worst_claim": 0.26396024227142334, "g_content": 2.56951036640242, "g_traj_mean": 1.7517147064208984}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "140", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that when an asset is discarded by a business but not sold, the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be deducted from the opening work-in-progress (WDV) of such asset in the previous year in which it was discarded. This reduction is taken into account while computing the depreciation expense for the subsequent years. However, any changes made to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act 1961.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act, the treatment involves the following steps:\n1. All assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together under the block concept.\n2. The scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.\n3. Any alterations to the value of the block must be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\n4. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening written-down value of the asset less the scrap value.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act, the treatment involves the following steps:\n1. All assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together under the block concept.\n2. The scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.\n3. Any alterations to the value of the block must be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\n4. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening written-down value of the asset less the scrap value.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, as per the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment allows the assessee to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is calculated as the opening WDV of such asset less its scrap value.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961 permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. The block concept allows all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation to be clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act, the treatment involves the following steps:\\n1. All assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together under the block concept.\\n2. The scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.\\n3. Any alterations to the value of the block must be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\\n4. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening written-down value of the asset less the scrap value.\"]", "time_sec": 22.984, "generation_time_seconds": 21.9864, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9796, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 5420, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.820964908110347, "g_worst_claim": 0.3278131087621053, "g_content": 2.310885942899264, "g_traj_mean": 1.8699631690979004}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 438, 817, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 6147, 279, 79040, 4060, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 1741, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 16588, 438, 279, 8568, 467, 61971, 315, 1741, 9329, 2686, 1181, 20843, 897, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, as per the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment allows the assessee to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is calculated as the opening WDV of such asset less its scrap value.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6819983526622122, "g_worst_claim": 0.3278131087621053, "g_content": 2.410950738030511, "g_traj_mean": 1.9673479795455933}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 576, 2504, 7286, 6147, 678, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 311, 387, 6335, 2721, 3786, 323, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 614, 311, 387, 25470, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961 permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. The block concept allows all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation to be clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.954400863586532, "g_worst_claim": 0.3278767267862956, "g_content": 2.747594197591146, "g_traj_mean": 1.99678635597229}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 438, 817, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 279, 6380, 17601, 279, 2701, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 2009, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 40041, 3786, 1212, 279, 2504, 7286, 624, 17, 13, 576, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 374, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 279, 9329, 374, 43210, 624, 18, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 387, 25470, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 624, 19, 13, 576, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 5326, 14875, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 2686, 279, 20843, 897, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act, the treatment involves the following steps:\n1. All assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together under the block concept.\n2. The scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded.\n3. Any alterations to the value of the block must be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\n4. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening written-down value of the asset less the scrap value.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4358955427719966, "g_worst_claim": 0.11858127514521281, "g_content": 2.2171349158653846, "g_traj_mean": 1.5668742656707764}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "141", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nAccording to passage 1, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This reduction is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act.\n\nPassage 3 further states that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even though such discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in such year and subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the block value of the asset by the scrap value in the previous year in which it is discarded, and to claim depreciation on the residual value of the asset in the year of discard and subsequent years.", "pred": "These provisions ensure that the treatment of an asset being discarded is in accordance with the Income Tax Act's provisions, allowing for appropriate accounting and tax treatment.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These provisions ensure that the treatment of an asset being discarded is in accordance with the Income Tax Act's provisions, allowing for appropriate accounting and tax treatment.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded under the Income Tax Act, 1961, the treatment involves the following:\\n\\n1. The scrap value of the asset is allowed to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as permitted by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act.\\n\\n2. Under the block concept, all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset.\\n\\n3. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is calculated as the opening written-down value (WDV) of the asset less its scrap value, even if the asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in subsequent years.\\n\\nThese provisions ensure that the treatment of an asset being discarded is in accordance with the Income Tax Act's provisions, allowing for appropriate accounting and tax treatment.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all the assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\\n\\n1. The asset is considered as a single asset within its class, following the block concept.\\n2. All alterations to the value of the block must strictly comply with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\\n3. If the asset is discarded, its scrap value is permitted to be reduced from the block in the previous year.\"]", "time_sec": 25.547, "generation_time_seconds": 24.6049, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9313, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 5420, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7383255579909265, "g_worst_claim": 0.3884841998418172, "g_content": 2.3637454693134012, "g_traj_mean": 1.777246356010437}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 1212, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 11, 279, 6380, 17601, 279, 2701, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 374, 5420, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 279, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 438, 15129, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 382, 17, 13, 9449, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 678, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 40041, 3786, 323, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 382, 18, 13, 576, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 16588, 438, 279, 8568, 5326, 14875, 897, 320, 17563, 53, 8, 315, 279, 9329, 2686, 1181, 20843, 897, 11, 1496, 421, 279, 9329, 374, 537, 1483, 369, 279, 9895, 315, 2562, 476, 4808, 304, 17420, 1635, 382, 9485, 19156, 5978, 429, 279, 6380, 315, 458, 9329, 1660, 43210, 374, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 594, 19156, 11, 10693, 369, 8311, 23168, 323, 3742, 6380, 13, 151645], "pred": "These provisions ensure that the treatment of an asset being discarded is in accordance with the Income Tax Act's provisions, allowing for appropriate accounting and tax treatment.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1976398985957675, "g_worst_claim": 0.01093154028058052, "g_content": 1.7371019385326867, "g_traj_mean": 1.2647708654403687}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 6147, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 949, 315, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 1380, 678, 279, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 614, 311, 387, 25470, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all the assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8044420362990579, "g_worst_claim": 0.3885478178660075, "g_content": 2.5242453182444855, "g_traj_mean": 1.8291823863983154}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6380, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 438, 817, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 374, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 9329, 374, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 2878, 1181, 536, 11, 2701, 279, 2504, 7286, 624, 17, 13, 2009, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 25470, 25017, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 279, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 1181, 20843, 897, 374, 15129, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\n1. The asset is considered as a single asset within its class, following the block concept.\n2. All alterations to the value of the block must strictly comply with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\n3. If the asset is discarded, its scrap value is permitted to be reduced from the block in the previous year.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7997271858510515, "g_worst_claim": 0.18266090750694275, "g_content": 2.2302808973524306, "g_traj_mean": 1.3839339017868042}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "142", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nThe scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as per Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept applies to all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, and any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act. The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even if the asset is not used for business or professional purposes in that year or subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the scrap value from the block in the previous year and claim depreciation on the residual value.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block must strictly follow the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block must strictly follow the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block must strictly follow the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the Income Tax Act, 1961, permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded, under section 43(6). This treatment allows for the depreciation of the asset based on its residual value, even if it is not used for the purposes of business or profession in subsequent years.\"]", "time_sec": 22.47, "generation_time_seconds": 21.4162, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0418, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 5420, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7863386271944368, "g_worst_claim": 0.2830416758855184, "g_content": 2.3986539107102613, "g_traj_mean": 1.8421363830566406}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 4092, 311, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 949, 315, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 1380, 678, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 25470, 1795, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block must strictly follow the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8513087627557, "g_worst_claim": 0.2830416758855184, "g_content": 2.5856903076171873, "g_traj_mean": 1.9067727327346802}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 4092, 311, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 949, 315, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 1380, 678, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 387, 1865, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7663797756786044, "g_worst_claim": 0.2831053137779236, "g_content": 2.3115608508770285, "g_traj_mean": 1.701464056968689}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 11, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 568, 1096, 6380, 6147, 369, 279, 93089, 315, 279, 9329, 3118, 389, 1181, 32147, 897, 11, 1496, 421, 432, 374, 537, 1483, 369, 279, 9895, 315, 2562, 476, 4808, 304, 17420, 1635, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the Income Tax Act, 1961, permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded, under section 43(6). This treatment allows for the depreciation of the asset based on its residual value, even if it is not used for the purposes of business or profession in subsequent years.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.835841289822127, "g_worst_claim": 0.2830416758855184, "g_content": 2.4357430873773036, "g_traj_mean": 1.8339952230453491}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "144", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "1. Trace all the pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4\" away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with right side facing down.\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n8. Repeat sewing the other side of the zipper gusset.\n9. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Trace all the pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4\" away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with right side facing down.\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n8. Repeat sewing the other side of the zipper gusset.\n9. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\\n7. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\\n9. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\", \"Based on the given passages, to sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Calculate the total inches to be added to the sides of your dress. In this case, add 2 inches to each side.\\n\\n2. Make a zipper sandwich by placing one piece of lining fabric face up, the zipper, and the outer fabric right side facing down. Align the three edges.\\n\\n3. Use a zipper foot to sew a line across the top between the edge of your zipper sandwich and the zipper teeth (closer to the zipper feet).\\n\\n4. Repeat this process for the other side of the zipper, ensuring the fabric goes all the way to the end of the zipper.\\n\\n5. Trace all pattern pieces to the rest of the fabric and cut.\\n\\n6. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4 inch away from the center) with right sides facing each other.\\n\\n7. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\\n\\n8. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with right sides facing down, and stitch on the seam line.\\n\\n9. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset, and top stitch near the seam line.\\n\\n10. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\\n\\n11. Ensure the width of the zipper in between the gusset measures 1/2 inch.\\n\\n12. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to ensure the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\", \"Based on the given passages, to sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Trace all the pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4\\\" away from the center) with right side facing each other.\\n4. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with right side facing down.\\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\\n8. Repeat sewing the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n9. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. Trace the pattern onto the fabric and cut it out.\\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right sides facing each other.\\n4. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the main zipper gusset with right sides facing down.\\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\\n8. Repeat sewing on the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n9. Ensure the width of the zipper in between the gusset is 1/2″.\\n10. Change the presser foot back to the normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\"]", "time_sec": 43.986, "generation_time_seconds": 42.6476, "selection_time_seconds": 1.3266, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 27163, 678, 5383, 311, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 624, 18, 13, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 320, 16, 14, 19, 21580, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 8, 448, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1817, 1008, 624, 19, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 68761, 4478, 11, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 311, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 2309, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 1105, 448, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 13, 67923, 389, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 21, 13, 40284, 279, 35371, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1909, 32861, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 22, 13, 44801, 51219, 2441, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 624, 23, 13, 576, 2374, 315, 279, 68761, 304, 1948, 279, 342, 355, 746, 1265, 6629, 220, 16, 14, 17, 21580, 624, 24, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 1182, 311, 4622, 4478, 11, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 40358, 2163, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 773, 429, 279, 1887, 323, 35371, 13055, 15498, 3786, 28821, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n7. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\n9. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.086516929137404, "g_worst_claim": 0.3358105818430583, "g_content": 2.6523931166704964, "g_traj_mean": 2.006693124771118}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 20517, 279, 2790, 14924, 311, 387, 3694, 311, 279, 11067, 315, 697, 8511, 13, 758, 419, 1142, 11, 912, 220, 17, 14924, 311, 1817, 3108, 382, 17, 13, 7405, 264, 68761, 27874, 553, 24047, 825, 6573, 315, 35371, 13055, 3579, 705, 11, 279, 68761, 11, 323, 279, 15955, 13055, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 13, 49472, 279, 2326, 12822, 382, 18, 13, 5443, 264, 68761, 4478, 311, 22352, 264, 1555, 3941, 279, 1909, 1948, 279, 6821, 315, 697, 68761, 27874, 323, 279, 68761, 17832, 320, 32578, 799, 311, 279, 68761, 7541, 3593, 19, 13, 44801, 419, 1882, 369, 279, 1008, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 11, 22573, 279, 13055, 5780, 678, 279, 1616, 311, 279, 835, 315, 279, 68761, 382, 20, 13, 27163, 678, 5383, 9666, 311, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 382, 21, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 13, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 320, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 8, 448, 1290, 11067, 12880, 1817, 1008, 382, 22, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 264, 68761, 4478, 323, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 2309, 382, 23, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 342, 355, 746, 448, 1290, 11067, 12880, 1495, 11, 323, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 1555, 382, 24, 13, 40284, 279, 35371, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 323, 1909, 32861, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 382, 16, 15, 13, 44801, 51219, 2441, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 382, 16, 16, 13, 29279, 279, 2374, 315, 279, 68761, 304, 1948, 279, 342, 355, 746, 10953, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 382, 16, 17, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 1182, 311, 264, 4622, 4478,