pper gusset lining on top of the gusset with right side facing down.\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n8. Repeat sewing the other side of the zipper gusset.\n9. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8220992992352882, "g_worst_claim": 0.3358105818430583, "g_content": 2.478003904991543, "g_traj_mean": 1.7220977544784546}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 27163, 279, 5383, 8630, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 432, 700, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 624, 18, 13, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 320, 16, 14, 19, 21580, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 8, 448, 1290, 11067, 12880, 1817, 1008, 624, 19, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 264, 68761, 4478, 323, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 2309, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 448, 1290, 11067, 12880, 1495, 624, 21, 13, 67923, 389, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 22, 13, 40284, 279, 35371, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 323, 1909, 32861, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 23, 13, 44801, 51219, 389, 279, 1008, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 624, 24, 13, 29279, 279, 2374, 315, 279, 68761, 304, 1948, 279, 342, 355, 746, 374, 220, 16, 14, 17, 21580, 624, 16, 15, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 1182, 311, 279, 4622, 4478, 323, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 40358, 2163, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 773, 429, 279, 1887, 323, 35371, 13055, 15498, 3786, 28821, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Trace the pattern onto the fabric and cut it out.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right sides facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the main zipper gusset with right sides facing down.\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\n8. Repeat sewing on the other side of the zipper gusset.\n9. Ensure the width of the zipper in between the gusset is 1/2″.\n10. Change the presser foot back to the normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7728937906795452, "g_worst_claim": 0.49347939491271975, "g_content": 2.4301436018235614, "g_traj_mean": 1.6090761423110962}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "146", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sew a zipper gusset:\n\n1. Make a casing in the side seams by stitching the outer edge of the gusset and the back side seam.\n2. Slide the boning right down into the casing.\n3. Push the seam allowance to the back and tack the casing to the lining, if necessary, so it doesn't move.\n4. Make a zipper sandwich by placing one piece of lining fabric face up, followed by the zipper, and then the outer fabric right side facing down.\n5. Sew across the top of the zipper sandwich with a zipper foot, making sure to line up the three edges.\n6. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper.\n7. Trace all pattern pieces to the remaining fabric and cut them out.\n8. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, with the right sides facing each other, and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\n9. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the zipper gusset, with the right sides facing down, and stitch along the seam line.\n10. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\n11. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\n12. The width of the zipper between the gusset should measure 1/2\".\n13. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch along the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabrics together nicely.\n\nTherefore, to sew a zipper gusset, you need to make a casing in the side seams, insert the boning, make a zipper sandwich, sew the zipper gusset to the zipper, and attach the lining to the zipper gusset.", "pred": "1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down.\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n8. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\n9. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\n10. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down.\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n8. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\n9. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\n10. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\\n7. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\\n9. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\", \"Based on the provided passages, to sew a zipper gusset:\\n\\n1. Trace the pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut it.\\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4 inch away from the center) with the right sides facing each other.\\n4. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with the right side facing down and stitch on the seam line.\\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\\n7. Repeat sewing on the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2 inch.\\n9. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabric nicely.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to sew a zipper gusset:\\n\\n1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down.\\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\\n8. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\\n9. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\\n10. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\", \"Based on the given passages, to sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the fabric pieces: Cut out all necessary fabric pieces as per the pattern. This includes the lining fabric, outer fabric, and the zipper gusset.\\n\\n2. Align the lining and outer fabric: Place one piece of lining fabric face up, then place the zipper between them, followed by the outer fabric right side facing down. Ensure that all three edges are lined up.\\n\\n3. Sew the zipper sandwich: Using a zipper foot, sew across the top between the edge of your zipper sandwich and the zipper teeth. This step is crucial for securing the position of the zipper.\\n\\n4. Secure the zipper gusset: Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4 inch away from the center) with the right sides facing each other.\\n\\n5. Change the presser foot: Switch to a zipper foot and sew a line near to the seam line to secure the gusset's position.\\n\\n6. Place the zipper gusset lining: Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with the right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\\n\\n7. Flip the lining: Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line. Repeat this step for the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n\\n8. Attach the main fabric: Change the presser foot back to the normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabric together nicely.\\n\\n9. Finish the edges: Flip lightly on the piping seam allowance at the curve. Place the zipper gusset on the pencil case body, align the ends to the center markings, and sew from marking to marking at both ends. Finally, place the lining on top of them with the right side facing down.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset onto your fabric.\"]", "time_sec": 48.025, "generation_time_seconds": 46.3249, "selection_time_seconds": 1.6893, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 27163, 678, 5383, 311, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 624, 18, 13, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 320, 16, 14, 19, 21580, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 8, 448, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1817, 1008, 624, 19, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 68761, 4478, 11, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 311, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 2309, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 1105, 448, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 13, 67923, 389, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 21, 13, 40284, 279, 35371, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1909, 32861, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 22, 13, 44801, 51219, 2441, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 624, 23, 13, 576, 2374, 315, 279, 68761, 304, 1948, 279, 342, 355, 746, 1265, 6629, 220, 16, 14, 17, 21580, 624, 24, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 1182, 311, 4622, 4478, 11, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 40358, 2163, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 773, 429, 279, 1887, 323, 35371, 13055, 15498, 3786, 28821, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n7. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\n9. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.086516929137404, "g_worst_claim": 0.3358105818430583, "g_content": 2.6523931166704964, "g_traj_mean": 2.006693124771118}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 311, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 1447, 16, 13, 27163, 279, 5383, 311, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 432, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 624, 18, 13, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 320, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 8, 448, 279, 1290, 11067, 12880, 1817, 1008, 624, 19, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 264, 68761, 4478, 323, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 2309, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 342, 355, 746, 448, 279, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 323, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 21, 13, 40284, 279, 35371, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 323, 1909, 32861, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 22, 13, 44801, 51219, 389, 279, 1008, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 624, 23, 13, 576, 2374, 315, 279, 68761, 304, 1948, 279, 342, 355, 746, 1265, 6629, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 624, 24, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 1182, 311, 264, 4622, 4478, 323, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 40358, 2163, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 15498, 279, 1887, 323, 35371, 13055, 28821, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Trace the pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut it.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4 inch away from the center) with the right sides facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with the right side facing down and stitch on the seam line.\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\n7. Repeat sewing on the other side of the zipper gusset.\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2 inch.\n9. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabric nicely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.79570023897521, "g_worst_claim": 0.2843130826950073, "g_content": 2.532713946174173, "g_traj_mean": 1.6627936363220215}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 1447, 16, 13, 27163, 678, 5383, 311, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 624, 18, 13, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 320, 16, 14, 19, 21580, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 8, 448, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1817, 1008, 624, 19, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 68761, 4478, 11, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 311, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 2309, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 1105, 448, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 624, 21, 13, 67923, 389, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 22, 13, 40284, 279, 35371, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1909, 32861, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 624, 23, 13, 44801, 51219, 2441, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 624, 24, 13, 576, 2374, 315, 279, 68761, 304, 1948, 279, 342, 355, 746, 1265, 6629, 220, 16, 14, 17, 21580, 624, 16, 15, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 1182, 311, 4622, 4478, 11, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 40358, 2163, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 773, 429, 279, 1887, 323, 35371, 13055, 15498, 3786, 28821, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Trace all pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut.\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4″ away from the center) with right side facing each other.\n4. Change the presser foot to zipper foot, sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of them with right side facing down.\n6. Stitch on the seam line.\n7. Flip the lining to the bottom of main zipper gusset, top stitch near the seam line.\n8. Repeat sewing another side of the zipper gusset.\n9. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2″.\n10. Change the presser foot back to normal foot, stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.197594959768351, "g_worst_claim": 0.3806626796722412, "g_content": 2.6928046198174505, "g_traj_mean": 1.9879599809646606}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 13055, 9666, 25, 19649, 700, 678, 5871, 13055, 9666, 438, 817, 279, 5383, 13, 1096, 5646, 279, 35371, 13055, 11, 15955, 13055, 11, 323, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 382, 17, 13, 49472, 279, 35371, 323, 15955, 13055, 25, 10771, 825, 6573, 315, 35371, 13055, 3579, 705, 11, 1221, 1992, 279, 68761, 1948, 1105, 11, 8110, 553, 279, 15955, 13055, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 13, 29279, 429, 678, 2326, 12822, 525, 31293, 705, 382, 18, 13, 49213, 279, 68761, 27874, 25, 12091, 264, 68761, 4478, 11, 22352, 3941, 279, 1909, 1948, 279, 6821, 315, 697, 68761, 27874, 323, 279, 68761, 17832, 13, 1096, 3019, 374, 16587, 369, 40477, 279, 2309, 315, 279, 68761, 382, 19, 13, 34502, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 25, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 320, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 8, 448, 279, 1290, 11067, 12880, 1817, 1008, 382, 20, 13, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 25, 15586, 311, 264, 68761, 4478, 323, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 311, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 342, 355, 746, 594, 2309, 382, 21, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 25, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 342, 355, 746, 448, 279, 1290, 31