{"id": "150", "question": "how to bake hard boiled egg", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to bake hard-boiled eggs:\n\n1. Place cold eggs in a single layer in a pan with enough cold water to cover them by about 1 inch.\n2. Place the pan on the stove over high heat.\n3. As soon as the water comes to a boil, turn the heat off, cover the pan, and remove it from the heat.\n4. Allow the eggs to sit in the water for the appropriate amount of time, depending on the size of the eggs (9 minutes for medium, 12 minutes for large, and 15 minutes for extra-large).\n\nNote: Do not peek during the cooking process, and do not worry if the eggs are not perfectly symmetrical or have a slightly greenish-gray yolk.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the instructions for baking hard-boiled eggs are as follows:\\n\\n1. Place the cold eggs in a single layer in a pan with enough cold water to cover them by about 1 inch.\\n2. Place the pan on the stove over high heat.\\n3. As soon as the water comes to a boil, turn the heat off, cover the pan, and remove it from the heat.\\n4. Allow the eggs to sit in the water until they are cooked; about 9 minutes for a medium egg, 12 minutes for a large egg, and 15 minutes for an extra-large egg.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Based on the given passages, there is no information about how to bake hard-boiled eggs. The passages discuss methods for boiling eggs, not baking them. Therefore, the answer is: Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Based on the given passages, the instructions to bake hard-boiled eggs are as follows:\\n1. Place cold eggs in a single layer in a pan with enough cold water to cover them by about 1 inch.\\n2. Place the pan on the stove over high heat.\\n3. Once the water comes to a boil, turn the heat off, cover the pan, and remove it from the heat.\\n4. Allow the eggs to sit in the water until they are cooked:\\n   - About 9 minutes for a medium egg\\n   - 12 minutes for a large egg\\n   - 15 minutes for an extra-large egg\"]", "time_sec": 19.525, "generation_time_seconds": 18.1534, "selection_time_seconds": 1.3532, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11221, 369, 27815, 2588, 69466, 2181, 18805, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 279, 9255, 18805, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 304, 264, 7215, 448, 3322, 9255, 3015, 311, 3421, 1105, 553, 911, 220, 16, 17122, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 7215, 389, 279, 44015, 916, 1550, 8628, 624, 18, 13, 1634, 5135, 438, 279, 3015, 4041, 311, 264, 43690, 11, 2484, 279, 8628, 1007, 11, 3421, 279, 7215, 11, 323, 4057, 432, 504, 279, 8628, 624, 19, 13, 26530, 279, 18805, 311, 2444, 304, 279, 3015, 3080, 807, 525, 29105, 26, 911, 220, 24, 4420, 369, 264, 11051, 18636, 11, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 369, 264, 3460, 18636, 11, 323, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 369, 458, 4960, 39148, 18636, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place the cold eggs in a single layer in a pan with enough cold water to cover them by about 1 inch.\n2. Place the pan on the stove over high heat.\n3. As soon as the water comes to a boil, turn the heat off, cover the pan, and remove it from the heat.\n4. Allow the eggs to sit in the water until they are cooked; about 9 minutes for a medium egg, 12 minutes for a large egg, and 15 minutes for an extra-large egg.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8689549417498541, "g_worst_claim": 0.19978391040455212, "g_content": 0.9835653305053711, "g_traj_mean": 0.8306986689567566}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.11327371001243591, "g_worst_claim": -0.1132737100124359