{"id": "158", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, you can follow the steps mentioned in passage 3. Slide the Notifications panel open, tap on Storage, then Factory data reset, and finally tap on Reset phone and Erase everything.", "pred": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap on the Storage Factory data reset option.\n2. Tap on Reset phone and then tap Erase everything.\n\nBe sure to back up any data and files you want to keep before doing a factory reset.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap on the Storage Factory data reset option.\n2. Tap on Reset phone and then tap Erase everything.\n\nBe sure to back up any data and files you want to keep before doing a factory reset.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.\", \"To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap on the Storage Factory data reset option.\\n2. Tap on Reset phone and then tap Erase everything.\\n\\nBe sure to back up any data and files you want to keep before doing a factory reset.\", \"Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. First, switch off the phone by using the Power rocker.\\n2. After that, press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds.\\n3. You can release all keys when the Bootloader Mode appears on the screen.\\n4. Choose the Factory Reset by pressing the Volume Down button to scroll and the Power key to select.\\n5. Then press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds.\\n6. When you see the Bootloader Mode menu, release the held buttons.\\n7. From the menu, choose the option \\\"RECOVERY MODE\\\" by using the Volume buttons to scroll and the Power key to select options.\\n8. Congratulations! You should now be in the expected mode.\", \"Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.\\n4. If required, back up any data and files you want to keep before proceeding with the factory reset.\"]", "time_sec": 21.213, "generation_time_seconds": 20.2953, "selection_time_seconds": 0.865, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 8633, 7585, 264, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 43364, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 14693, 16937, 821, 7585, 624, 18, 13, 36134, 16932, 4540, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 9740, 519, 4297, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.881403689481774, "g_worst_claim": 0.1986008882522583, "g_content": 2.049322457149111, "g_traj_mean": 1.6528557538986206}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 8633, 7585, 458, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 43364, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 389, 279, 14693, 16937, 821, 7585, 2999, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 389, 16932, 4540, 323, 1221, 15239, 9740, 519, 4297, 382, 3430, 2704, 311, 1182, 705, 894, 821, 323, 3542, 498, 1366, 311, 2506, 1573, 3730, 264, 8633, 7585, 13, 151645], "pred": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap on the Storage Factory data reset option.\n2. Tap on Reset phone and then tap Erase everything.\n\nBe sure to back up any data and files you want to keep before doing a factory reset.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.933786619110414, "g_worst_claim": 0.13953345020612082, "g_content": 2.166821872486788, "g_traj_mean": 1.659130573272705}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 8633, 7585, 264, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5512, 11, 3398, 1007, 279, 4540, 553, 1667, 279, 7420, 95126, 624, 17, 13, 4636, 429, 11, 3493, 323, 3331, 279, 20265, 6285, 323, 7420, 12424, 3786, 369, 264, 5625, 315, 6486, 624, 18, 13, 1446, 646, 4879, 678, 6894, 979, 279, 15004, 8355, 14562, 7952, 389, 279, 4171, 624, 19, 13, 22201, 279, 16937, 16932, 553, 25352, 279, 20265, 6285, 3137, 311, 9059, 323, 279, 7420, 1376, 311, 3293, 624, 20, 13, 5005, 3493, 323, 3331, 279, 20265, 6285, 488, 7420, 1376, 369, 264, 5625, 315, 6486, 624, 21, 13, 3197, 498, 1490, 279, 15004, 8355, 14562, 5022, 11, 4879, 279, 5644, 12424, 624, 22, 13, 5542, 279, 5022, 11, 5157, 279, 2999, 330, 787, 70976, 22690, 1, 553, 1667, 279, 20265, 12424, 311, 9059, 323, 279, 7420, 1376, 311, 3293, 2606, 624, 23, 13, 70541, 0, 1446, 1265, 1431, 387, 304, 279, 3601, 3856, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. First, switch off the phone by using the Power rocker.\n2. After that, press and hold the Volume Down and Power buttons together for a couple of seconds.\n3. You can release all keys when the Bootloader Mode appears on the screen.\n4. Choose the Factory Reset by pressing the Volume Down button to scroll and the Power key to select.\n5. Then press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds.\n6. When you see the Bootloader Mode menu, release the held buttons.\n7. From the menu, choose the option \"RECOVERY MODE\" by using the Volume buttons to scroll and the Power key to select options.\n8. Congratulations! You should now be in the expected mode.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.765082169644187, "g_worst_claim": 0.1900497873624166, "g_content": 1.9527265108548677, "g_traj_mean": 1.525134801864624}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 8633, 7585, 264, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 43364, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 14693, 16937, 821, 7585, 624, 18, 13, 36134, 16932, 4540, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 9740, 519, 4297, 624, 19, 13, 1416, 2567, 11, 1182, 705, 894, 821, 323, 3542, 498, 1366, 311, 2506, 1573, 38447, 448, 279, 8633, 7585, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.\n4. If required, back up any data and files you want to keep before proceeding with the factory reset.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8243427878501368, "g_worst_claim": 0.1986008882522583, "g_content": 1.8261931981795874, "g_traj_mean": 1.4636802673339844}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "159", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Switch off the device by holding down the Power button for a while.\n2. Press and hold the Volume Down + Power key for a couple of seconds until Bootloader Mode menu appears on the screen.\n3. From the menu, choose \"Factory Data Reset\" by using Volume buttons to scroll and Power key to select.\n4. Confirm the reset by pressing \"Erase Everything\".\n5. Release all keys when the process is complete.", "pred": "To factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Backup any important data and files.\n2. Open the Notifications panel.\n3. Tap on 'Storage Factory data reset'.\n4. Tap 'Reset phone' and then tap 'Erase everything'.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Backup any important data and files.\n2. Open the Notifications panel.\n3. Tap on 'Storage Factory data reset'.\n4. Tap 'Reset phone' and then tap 'Erase everything'.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.\", \"Based on the given passages, to factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap on the \\\"Storage\\\" option.\\n2. Tap on \\\"Factory data reset.\\\"\\n3. Tap on \\\"Reset phone\\\" and then tap on \\\"Erase everything.\\\"\", \"Based on the given passages, to factory reset an HTC One VX follow these steps:\\n\\n1. First, ensure you have backed up any data and files you want to keep before starting the process.\\n2. Access the notifications panel on your device.\\n3. Tap on the \\\"Storage\\\" option within the notifications panel.\\n4. Next, select \\\"Factory data reset.\\\"\\n5. Confirm your choice by tapping on \\\"Reset phone\\\" and then \\\"Erase everything.\\\"\\n\\nBy following these steps, you will initiate a factory reset on your HTC One VX.\", \"To factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Backup any important data and files.\\n2. Open the Notifications panel.\\n3. Tap on 'Storage Factory data reset'.\\n4. Tap 'Reset phone' and then tap 'Erase everything'.\"]", "time_sec": 18.513, "generation_time_seconds": 17.363, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1211, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 8633, 7585, 264, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 43364, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 14693, 16937, 821, 7585, 624, 18, 13, 36134, 16932, 4540, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 9740, 519, 4297, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.800840561730521, "g_worst_claim": 0.35040422280629474, "g_content": 2.015356655778556, "g_traj_mean": 1.572878122329712}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 8633, 7585, 458, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 43364, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 389, 279, 330, 5793, 1, 2999, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 389, 330, 4153, 821, 7585, 10040, 18, 13, 36134, 389, 330, 14828, 4540, 1, 323, 1221, 15239, 389, 330, 36, 10632, 4297, 1189, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap on the \"Storage\" option.\n2. Tap on \"Factory data reset.\"\n3. Tap on \"Reset phone\" and then tap on \"Erase everything.\"", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_cla