ap 'Reset phone' and then tap 'Erase everything'.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9380563042684933, "g_worst_claim": 0.23847822348276773, "g_content": 1.8041606771534886, "g_traj_mean": 1.535965085029602}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.08, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "162", "question": "what is psa levels mean", "gt": "PSA, or Prostate-specific antigen, is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. The level of PSA in a man's blood is measured by the PSA test, which involves sending a blood sample to a laboratory for analysis. The results are usually reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. Elevated PSA levels may indicate conditions such as prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition like prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. Total PSA levels between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml may indicate prostate cancer, benign prostate hyperplasia, or inflammation of the prostate.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels are used to measure the protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels are often indicative of prostate cancer, although they can also be associated with noncancerous conditions such as prostatitis or an enlarged prostate. Total PSA levels between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml may suggest prostate cancer, benign prostate hyperplasia (BPH), or inflammation of the prostate.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels are used to measure the protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels are often indicative of prostate cancer, although they can also be associated with noncancerous conditions such as prostatitis or an enlarged prostate. Total PSA levels between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml may suggest prostate cancer, benign prostate hyperplasia (BPH), or inflammation of the prostate.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, PSA levels are a measure of the protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man’s blood, and the results are usually reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood.\", \"Based on the given passages, PSA levels refer to the amount of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) present in the blood. PSA is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels can indicate several conditions, including prostate cancer, benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH), or inflammation of the prostate. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man’s blood, typically reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. These conditions are more common in the elderly, and a general increase in PSA levels may be associated with these conditions.\", \"Based on the given passages, PSA (Prostate-specific antigen) is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man's blood, which is reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. Levels between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml may suggest prostate cancer (about a 25% chance), benign prostate hyperplasia (BPH), or inflammation of the prostate, which are more common in the elderly. A free PSA test may be used to look at the ratio of free to total PSA when the DRE is normal but the PSA is moderately elevated, to distinguish between prostate cancer and other non-cancer causes of elevated PSA.\", \"Based on the given passages, PSA levels are used to measure the protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels are often indicative of prostate cancer, although they can also be associated with noncancerous conditions such as prostatitis or an enlarged prostate. Total PSA levels between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml may suggest prostate cancer, benign prostate hyperplasia (BPH), or inflammation of the prostate.\"]", "time_sec": 25.264, "generation_time_seconds": 24.2405, "selection_time_seconds": 1.006, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 69486, 5866, 525, 264, 6629, 315, 279, 12833, 8947, 553, 7761, 315, 279, 46347, 66069, 13, 96593, 69486, 5866, 1231, 13216, 46347, 9387, 11, 264, 2477, 66, 11705, 782, 2971, 1741, 438, 462, 9878, 19435, 11, 476, 458, 73017, 46347, 13, 576, 69486, 1273, 10953, 279, 2188, 315, 69486, 304, 264, 883, 748, 6543, 11, 323, 279, 3059, 525, 5990, 4961, 438, 20021, 55385, 315, 69486, 817, 2544, 321, 2015, 320, 968, 92322, 8, 315, 6543, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels are a measure of the protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man’s blood, and the results are usually reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8016675326141519, "g_worst_claim": 0.38361016909281415, "g_content": 0.9769589273553145, "g_traj_mean": 0.8553364872932434}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 69486, 5866, 8300, 311, 279, 3311, 315, 46347, 18906, 81989, 320, 5012, 32, 8, 3042, 304, 279, 6543, 13, 69486, 374, 264, 12833, 8947, 553, 7761, 315, 279, 46347, 66069, 13, 96593, 69486, 5866, 646, 13216, 3807, 4682, 11, 2670, 46347, 9387, 11, 64209, 462, 1978, 17071, 500, 35159, 320, 33, 10842, 701, 476, 36040, 315, 279, 46347, 13, 576, 69486, 1273, 10953, 279, 2188, 315, 69486, 304, 264, 883, 748, 6543, 11, 11136, 4961, 438, 20021, 55385, 315, 69486, 817, 2544, 321, 2015, 320, 968, 92322, 8, 315, 6543, 13, 4220, 4682, 525, 803, 4185, 304, 279, 28820, 11, 323, 264, 4586, 5263, 304, 69486, 5866, 1231, 387, 5815, 448, 1493, 4682, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels refer to the amount of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) present in the blood. PSA is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels can indicate several conditions, including prostate cancer, benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH), or inflammation of the prostate. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man’s blood, typically reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. These conditions are more common in the elderly, and a general increase in PSA levels may be associated with these conditions.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.747177527865616, "g_worst_claim": -0.11526143550872803, "g_content": 0.9040686508704876, "g_traj_mean": 0.775299072265625}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 69486, 320, 1336, 2454, 18906, 81989, 8, 374, 264, 12833, 8947, 553, 7761, 315, 279, 46347, 66069, 13, 576, 69486, 1273, 10953, 279, 2188, 315, 69486, 304, 264, 883, 594, 6543, 11, 892, 374, 4961, 438, 20021, 55385, 315, 69486, 817, 2544, 321, 2015, 320, 968, 92322, 8, 315, 6543, 13, 96593, 69486, 5866, 1231, 13216, 46347, 9387, 11, 264, 2477, 66, 11705, 782, 2971, 1741, 438, 462, 9878, 19435, 11, 476, 458, 73017, 46347, 13, 52693, 1948, 220, 19, 13, 15, 7777, 59548, 323, 220, 16, 15, 13, 15, 7777, 59548, 1231, 4190, 46347, 9387, 320, 9096, 264, 220, 17, 20, 4, 6012, 701, 64209, 46347, 17071, 500, 35159, 320, 33, 10842, 701, 476, 36040, 315, 279, 46347, 11, 892, 525, 803, 4185, 304, 279, 28820, 13, 362, 1910, 69486, 1273, 1231, 387, 1483, 311, 1401, 518, 279, 11341, 315, 1910, 311, 2790, 69486, 979, 279, 422, 787, 374, 4622, 714, 279, 69486, 374, 69251, 31289, 11, 311, 32037, 1948, 46347, 9387, 323, 1008, 2477, 1786, 11705, 11137, 315, 31289, 69486, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, PSA (Prostate-specific antigen) is a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man's blood, which is reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. Levels between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml may suggest prostate cancer (about a 25% chance), benign prostate hyperplasia (BPH), or inflammation of the prostate, which are more common in the elderly. A free PSA test may be used to look at the ratio of free to total PSA when the DRE is normal but the PSA is moderately elevated, to distinguish between prostate cancer and other non-cancer causes of elevated PSA.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0841329633070877, "g_worst_claim": 0.3883324861526489, "g_content": 1.1581168236670556, "g_traj_mean": 1.1541297435760498}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 69486, 5866, 525, 1483, 311, 6629, 279, 12833, 8947, 553, 7761, 315, 279, 46347, 66069, 13, 96593, 69486, 5866, 525, 3545, 62905, 315, 46347, 9387, 11, 7892, 807, 646, 1083, 387, 5815, 448, 2477, 66, 11705, 782, 4682, 1741, 438, 462, 9878, 19435, 476, 458, 73017, 46347, 13, 10657, 69486, 5866, 1948, 220, 19, 13, 15, 7777, 59548, 323, 220, 16, 15, 13, 15, 7777, 59548, 1231, 4190, 46347, 9387, 11, 64209, 46347, 17071, 500, 35159, 320, 33, 10842, 701, 476, 36040, 315, 279, 46347, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels are used to measure the protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels are often indicative of prostate cancer, although they can also be associated with noncancerous conditions such as prostatitis or an enlarged prostate. Total PSA levels between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml may suggest prostate cancer, benign prostate hyperplasia (BPH), or inflammation of the prostate.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.979284779368369, "g_worst_claim": 0.1996001720428467, "g_content": 1.3362427605523004, "g_traj_mean": 0.9050462245941162}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.72, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "166", "question": "what is psa levels mean", "gt": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels refer to the amount of prostate-specific antigen present in a man's blood. The level of PSA is measured in nanograms per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. Normal PSA levels range between 4.0 ng/ml and 10.0 ng/ml, and a moderate elevation in PSA levels may require further testing, such as a free PSA test, to determine the ratio of free to total PSA and help distinguish between prostate cancer and other non-cancer causes of elevated PSA. Therefore, the PSA test is used to monitor the progression of prostate cancer and to detect elevated PSA levels that may indicate prostate cancer or other prostate issues.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels are a measure of the amount of prostate-specific antigen in a man's blood. The PSA test is used to detect prostate cancer, as well as noncancerous conditions such as prostatitis or an enlarged prostate. Elevated PSA levels may indicate these conditions, while moderately elevated levels could suggest prostate cancer.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, PSA levels are a measure of the amount of prostate-specific antigen in a man's blood. The PSA test is used to detect prostate cancer, as well as noncancerous conditions such as prostatitis or an enlarged prostate. Elevated PSA levels may indicate these conditions, while moderately elevated levels could suggest prostate cancer.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, PSA levels are a measure of the protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man’s blood, and the results are usually reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood.\", \"Based on the given passages, PSA levels are measurements of a protein produced by cells of the prostate gland. The PSA test, originally approved by the FDA in 1986, measures the level of PSA in a man's blood. Results are reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate.\", \"Based on the given passages, a PSA level indicates the amount of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) present in a man's blood. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man’s blood and is often used to monitor the progression of prostate cancer in men who have already been diagnosed with the disease. Elevated PSA levels may indicate prostate cancer, a noncancerous condition such as prostatitis, or an enlarged prostate. The PSA test measures the level of PSA in a man’s blood. For this test, a blood sample is sent to a laboratory for analysis. The results are usually reported as nanograms of PSA per milliliter (ng/mL) of blood.\", \"Based on the given passages, PSA levels are a measure of the amount of prostate-specific antigen in a man's blood. The PSA test is used to detect prostate cancer, as well as noncancerous conditions such as prostatitis or an enlarged prostate. Elevated PSA levels may indicate these conditions, while moderately elevated levels could suggest prostate cancer.\"]", "time_sec": 20.76, "generation_time_seconds": 20.0174, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7294, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 69486, 5866, 525, 264, 6629, 315, 279, 12833, 8947, 553, 7761, 315, 279, 46347, 66069, 13, 96593, 69486, 5866, 1231, 13216, 46347, 9387, 11, 264, 2477, 66, 11705, 782, 2971, 1741, 438, 462, 9878, 19435, 11, 476, 458, 73017, 46347, 13, 576, 69486, 1273, 10953, 279, 2188, 315, 69486, 304, 264, 883, 