is. This will help you accurately represent the data.\n5. Create the bars for the graph, ensuring they are proportionate to the data they represent. This will make the graph easier to understand and visually appealing.\n6. Use colors to enhance the visual representation and make the graph more engaging.\n7. Review the graph to ensure the story of your data is clear and well represented. If necessary, consider using a pie chart as a backup option when dealing with a small number of data points or disproportionate responses.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8950113125850289, "g_worst_claim": 0.003592525919278463, "g_content": 1.3696774934467517, "g_traj_mean": 0.949968695640564}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 7354, 311, 1281, 264, 3619, 4771, 1447, 16, 13, 20513, 697, 821, 25, 48995, 678, 279, 1995, 498, 1184, 311, 9429, 4221, 11059, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 421, 498, 1366, 311, 30235, 821, 389, 1246, 1657, 14924, 315, 52858, 264, 3283, 3949, 1948, 279, 3951, 315, 7400, 220, 17, 15, 15, 20, 323, 7400, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 6530, 52858, 821, 369, 1846, 1378, 3951, 382, 17, 13, 29901, 279, 2608, 315, 279, 4771, 25, 98881, 1246, 1550, 697, 4771, 3880, 311, 728, 13, 1096, 686, 6761, 389, 279, 2088, 315, 279, 821, 498, 2299, 26297, 13, 1752, 2867, 11, 421, 498, 2299, 26297, 52858, 11, 279, 2608, 315, 279, 15904, 686, 4009, 279, 3311, 315, 52858, 304, 14924, 382, 18, 13, 10869, 279, 4771, 25, 20678, 697, 4771, 264, 52844, 2265, 773, 432, 594, 2797, 1128, 279, 821, 10868, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 498, 1410, 2265, 432, 330, 59039, 13464, 304, 508, 12730, 3988, 60, 504, 7400, 220, 17, 15, 15, 20, 311, 7400, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 2217, 19, 13, 4230, 279, 15904, 25, 11992, 15904, 369, 1817, 5582, 13, 576, 2608, 315, 1817, 3619, 1265, 387, 21117, 349, 311, 279, 897, 432, 10868, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 421, 825, 3619, 10868, 220, 20, 14924, 315, 52858, 323, 2441, 10868, 220, 16, 15, 14924, 315, 52858, 11, 279, 2086, 3619, 1265, 387, 10917, 438, 16217, 438, 279, 1156, 382, 20, 13, 5443, 4771, 5567, 25, 1416, 498, 1366, 11, 498, 646, 990, 4771, 5567, 311, 1492, 498, 1281, 264, 28485, 323, 16645, 4771, 13, 1096, 686, 1281, 697, 3037, 1401, 6584, 323, 387, 8661, 311, 1349, 382, 21, 13, 2691, 1894, 25, 30370, 1894, 311, 697, 4771, 646, 1492, 1281, 432, 803, 42295, 32252, 323, 8661, 311, 3535, 13, 5443, 2155, 7987, 369, 2155, 11059, 311, 1281, 432, 2797, 892, 15904, 9173, 311, 892, 5582, 382, 22, 13, 4248, 279, 5452, 25, 29279, 429, 279, 379, 35321, 702, 264, 5452, 429, 29257, 10868, 279, 2750, 315, 279, 821, 13, 1096, 686, 5358, 279, 4771, 504, 3330, 61136, 4152, 311, 79053, 14507, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1855, 264, 3619, 4771, 429, 13444, 42465, 279, 52858, 821, 369, 279, 1378, 3951, 498, 3003, 14548, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a bar graph that effectively compares the rainfall data for the two months you've collected.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7032398955098619, "g_worst_claim": 0.027550915877024334, "g_content": 1.023808566006747, "g_traj_mean": 0.6745744943618774}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "170", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "To soften brown sugar, you can place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Then put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. To make hardened granulated sugar soft again, preheat an oven to its lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from its package and put it in an ovenproof container. Place it in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.", "pred": "2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to soften sugar, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep it in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n\\n2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to soften sugar:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar:\\n   - Place brown sugar in a plastic container.\\n   - Cover it tightly with plastic wrap or foil and a damp paper towel.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar:\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees).\\n   - Place the sugar in an ovenproof container and put it in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon to help it soften.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.\", \"Based on the given passages, there are two main methods to soften sugar:\\n\\n1. Using the oven:\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees).\\n   - Place the sugar in an ovenproof container.\\n   - Put the container in the oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon to help it soften.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the warm oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location to prevent moisture absorption.\\n\\n2. Using the fridge:\\n   - The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container.\\n   - Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible to minimize air exposure.\\n   - Limit the amount of air space between the sugar and the lid to prevent moisture from affecting the sugar.\", \"Based on the given passages, there are two methods to soften sugar:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar: Preheat oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator). When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\"]", "time_sec": 38.097, "generation_time_seconds": 36.9509, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1358, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 13, 10783, 279, 13163,