 10747, 11, 279, 23387, 1265, 387, 6519, 1007, 323, 279, 13163, 1265, 387, 2115, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to soften sugar, granulated sugar can be softened by preheating the oven to a low temperature between 150-200 degrees and placing the sugar in an ovenproof container. The sugar should be placed in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes, then tapped with a spoon to stir it. If the sugar starts to fall apart, the oven should be turned off and the sugar should be left in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3536027367578614, "g_worst_claim": 0.31094696124394733, "g_content": 1.8689153334673714, "g_traj_mean": 1.3018392324447632}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 1616, 311, 79945, 70736, 13163, 374, 311, 1992, 432, 304, 264, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, a way to soften hardened sugar is to place it in a warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1082464229492914, "g_worst_claim": 0.31020502249399823, "g_content": 2.419122060139974, "g_traj_mean": 1.1884222030639648}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "173", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to soften sugar:\n\n1. To soften brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel after a couple of days. (Passage 1)\n2. To soften hardened granulated sugar, preheat the oven to a low temperature (150-200°F), remove the sugar from its package, and place it in an ovenproof container. Warm the sugar in the oven for about 15 minutes, then tap it with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, leave it in the oven for a longer period of time to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. (Passage 2)\n3. To keep brown sugar soft, pack it into the smallest container possible to minimize air exposure. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to soften other types of sugar, such as confectioner's sugar.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to soften sugar:\n1. For brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.\n2. For granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator). When it gets moist, it develops lumps.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to soften sugar:\n1. For brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.\n2. For granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator). When it gets moist, it develops lumps.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to soften sugar, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep it in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n\\n2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.\", \"Based on the given passages, there are two main methods to soften sugar:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\", \"Based on the given passages, to soften hardened granulated sugar, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, between 150-200 degrees.\\n2. Remove the sugar from its package and place it in an ovenproof container that can hold the sugar.\\n3. Place the container with the sugar in the warm oven for about 15 minutes.\\n4. Tap the sugar with a spoon.\\n5. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the container in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n6. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n7. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\", \"Based on the given passages, to soften sugar:\\n1. For brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n2. For granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator). When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\"]", "time_sec": 37.669, "generation_time_seconds": 36.5289, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1308, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 13, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 13, 10771, 279, 5476, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 2506, 432, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 3593, 17, 13, 1752, 13876, 13163, 25, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 13, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 13, 17757, 38969, 13, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 13, 576, 1429, 11050, 1616, 311, 2506, 13876, 13163, 8413, 374, 311, 2506, 432, 19046, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 11, 32894, 279, 3311, 315, 3720, 14338, 438, 1753, 438, 3204, 13, 13795, 279, 13163, 1119, 279, 24632, 5476, 3204, 773, 429, 1052, 374, 20171, 894, 3720, 3550, 1948, 279, 13163, 323, 279, 26334, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6358854604837458, "g_worst_claim": 0.3283536632855733, "g_content": 2.1421271732875278, "g_traj_mean": 1.5777592658996582}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1052, 525, 1378, 1887, 5413, 311, 79945, 13163, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 13876, 13163, 25, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 13, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 13, 17757, 38969, 13, 10783, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 13, 10783, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 13, 10771, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 36134, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 279, 23387, 1007, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 568, 151645], "pred": "2. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8047409439830522, "g_worst_claim": 0.3113459348678589, "g_content": 2.337143984707919, "g_traj_mean": 1.6948944330215454}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 79945, 70736, 15732, 7757, 13163, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 1948, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 1181, 6328, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 646, 3331, 279, 13163, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 5476, 448, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 279, 13163, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 5476, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 624, 21, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 624, 22, 13, 9129, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 568, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, between 150-200 degrees.\n2. Remove the sugar from its package and place it in an ovenproof container that can hold the sugar.\n3. Place the container with the sugar in the warm oven for about 15 minutes.\n4. Tap the sugar with a spoon.\n5. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the container in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\n6. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\n7. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5154384968297103, "g_worst_claim": 0.3113459348678589, "g_content": 1.9334586172392874, "g_traj_mean": 1.337738037109375}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 