ontent": 2.430471420288086, "g_traj_mean": 1.7641942501068115}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "175", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to soften sugar:\n\n1. Place brown sugar in an airtight container with a damp paper towel or napkin on top. Cover tightly and let it sit for a couple of days. Remove the damp paper towel, and the sugar should be soft. (Passage 1)\n2. Preheat the oven to a low temperature (150-200 degrees), place hardened granulated sugar in an ovenproof container, and tap it with a spoon after 15 minutes. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave it in for an hour or two to dry out completely. Store granulated sugar in an airtight container. (Passage 2)\n3. Keep brown sugar soft by storing it in an airtight container with minimal air space between the sugar and the lid. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible. (Passage 3)", "pred": "2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to soften sugar, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep it in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n\\n2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.\", \"Based on the given passages, to soften sugar, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator). When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\", \"Based on the given passages, there are two methods to soften hardened sugar:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar:\\n- Place the brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar.\\n- Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil.\\n- Cover tightly.\\n- Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar:\\n- Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees.\\n- Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\\n- Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n- Tap the sugar with a spoon.\\n- If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n- Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n- Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n- When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar, it should be sealed in a plastic container with a damp paper towel on top and covered tightly. Remove the damp paper towel after a couple of days.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar that has hardened, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and leave it in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon, and if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location to prevent it from getting moist and developing lumps.\"]", "time_sec": 38.456, "generation_time_seconds": 37.7082, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7365, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 13, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 13, 10771, 279, 5476, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 2506, 432, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 3593, 17, 13, 1752, 13876, 13163, 25, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 13, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 13, 17757, 38969, 13, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 13, 576, 1429, 11050, 1616, 311, 2506, 13876, 13163, 8413, 374, 311, 2506, 432, 19046, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 11, 32894, 279, 3311, 315, 3720, 14338, 438, 1753, 438, 3204, 13, 13795, 279, 13163, 1119, 279, 24632, 5476, 3204, 773, 429, 1052, 374, 20171, 894, 3720, 3550, 1948, 279, 13163, 323, 279, 26334, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. The most efficient way to keep brown sugar soft is to keep it sealed in an airtight container, limiting the amount of air exposure as much as possible. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible so that there is hardly any air space between the sugar and the lid.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5930339801740203, "g_worst_claim": 0.16902080774307252, "g_content": 2.075444766453334, "g_traj_mean": 1.5361500978469849}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_id