51, 11221, 537, 9761, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 8300, 311, 697, 10350, 1849, 594, 1196, 11376, 476, 1824, 4963, 13, 151645], "pred": "For other Windows versions or specific instructions not covered in the passages, refer to your operating system's user manual or support resources.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7328757787424502, "g_worst_claim": 0.04711944858233134, "g_content": 0.7548715367036707, "g_traj_mean": 0.6838473677635193}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 2297, 279, 6084, 882, 389, 697, 6366, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 7420, 14566, 389, 697, 5515, 220, 16, 15, 6673, 553, 19496, 330, 13175, 2606, 1, 304, 279, 2711, 3745, 389, 279, 3383, 2257, 624, 17, 13, 758, 279, 7420, 14566, 3241, 11, 4205, 389, 330, 4072, 979, 279, 6366, 71390, 10040, 18, 13, 8427, 330, 4072, 1246, 1293, 3080, 279, 3037, 10577, 1007, 1, 476, 330, 4072, 979, 279, 6366, 71390, 10040, 19, 13, 2573, 279, 12685, 6084, 882, 369, 697, 6366, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to change the sleep time on your computer:\n\n1. Open Power Options on your Windows 10 PC by typing \"power options\" in the search box on the taskbar.\n2. In the Power Options window, click on \"Change when the computer sleeps.\"\n3. Select \"Change how long until the display turns off\" or \"Change when the computer sleeps.\"\n4. Set the desired sleep time for your computer.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5236036786957393, "g_worst_claim": 0.14153742790222168, "g_content": 0.3897929080696993, "g_traj_mean": 0.4998835623264313}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "180", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Hugging has significant psychological effects. It creates a warm feeling that affects the entire body, akin to the effect of many drugs operating simultaneously. This could be due to the feeling of a loving embrace, leading to good relationships and emotional intimacy. It also enhances empathy and listening skills, which can lead to a psychological hug. Furthermore, research has found that hugging can significantly reduce worries about mortality and boost self-esteem. This soothing effect can be achieved even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, hugging has psychological effects that include reducing worry about mortality and fostering emotional intimacy and happy marriages. Hugs are claimed to affect the entire body to such an extent that many scientists consider it equivalent to the effect of many different drugs. Empathic listening can sometimes lead to a conversation partner feeling like they are receiving a psychological hug, further emphasizing the positive psychological effects of hugging.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, hugging has psychological effects that include reducing worry about mortality and fostering emotional intimacy and happy marriages. Hugs are claimed to affect the entire body to such an extent that many scientists consider it equivalent to the effect of many different drugs. Empathic listening can sometimes lead to a conversation partner feeling like they are receiving a psychological hug, further emphasizing the positive psychological effects of hugging.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, hugging has several psychological effects. It can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Additionally, hugging can reduce worry of mortality and soothe existential fears. The use of empathy and listening skills during hugging can also create a psychological hug, making the person feel like they are receiving a real hug.\", \"Based on the given passages, the psychological effects of hugging include:\\n\\n1. Reduction of existential fears: In a study published in the journal Psychological Science, hugging, whether it was a real hug or an inanimate object like a teddy bear, significantly reduced individuals' worry about mortality.\\n2. Feelings of empathy and emotional intimacy: Empathic listening, sometimes leading to a conversation partner feeling like they are receiving a psychological hug, can lead to good relationships and emotional intimacy.\", \"Based on the given passages, hugging has psychological effects that include reducing worry about mortality and fostering emotional intimacy and happy marriages. Hugs are claimed to affect the entire body to such an extent that many scientists consider it equivalent to the effect of many different drugs. Empathic listening can sometimes lead to a conversation partner feeling like they are receiving a psychological hug, further emphasizing the positive psychological effects of hugging.\", \"Based on the given passages, the psychological effects of hugging include:\\n\\n1. Feeling good and reducing worry: The first passage suggests that hugging not only provides a warm feeling but also affects the entire body, which can reduce worry and make people feel good.\\n\\n2. Promoting empathy and emotional intimacy: The second passage indicates that using empathy and listening skills, known as empathic listening, can lead to good relationships and emotional intimacy, often associated with psychological hugs.\\n\\n3. Reducing existential fears: The third passage reveals that hugs, even when inanimate, such as a teddy bear, can help soothe individuals' existential fears, as shown in a study published in the journal Psychological Science.\"]", "time_sec": 22.162, "generation_time_seconds": 21.3966, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7512, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 305, 35268, 702, 3807, 23187, 6239, 13, 1084, 646, 2990, 311, 1661, 11871, 11, 14269, 65164, 11, 323, 6247, 46351, 13, 22406, 11, 305, 35268, 646, 7949, 10955, 315, 28428, 323, 43176, 1782, 66639, 23209, 13, 576, 990, 315, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 2337, 305, 35268, 646, 1083, 1855, 264, 23187, 29784, 11, 3259, 279, 1697, 2666, 1075, 807, 525, 12308, 264, 1931, 29784, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, hugging has several psychological effects. It can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Additionally, hugging can reduce worry of mortality and soothe existential fears. The use of empathy and listening skills during hugging can also create a psychological hug, making the person feel like they are receiving a real hug.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0649622383989206, "g_worst_claim": 0.3335377772649129, "g_content": 3.644140455457899, "g_traj_mean": 2.1158087253570557}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 23187, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 58100, 315, 66639, 23209, 25, 758, 264, 3920, 4652, 304, 279, 8322, 68969, 9965, 11, 305, 35268, 11, 3425, 432, 572, 264, 1931, 29784, 476, 458, 304, 22030, 1633, 1075, 264, 41223, 10258, 11722, 11, 11941, 11046, 7775, 6, 10955, 911, 28428, 624, 17, 13, 31733, 819, 315, 47351, 323, 14269, 65164, 25, 13409, 587, 292, 14289, 11, 7025, 6388, 311, 264, 10435, 8263, 8266, 1075, 807, 525, 12308, 264, 23187, 29784, 11, 646, 2990, 311, 1661, 11871, 323, 14269, 65164, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Reduction of existential fears: In a study published in the journal Psychological Science, hugging, whether it was a real hug or an inanimate object like a teddy bear, significantly reduced individuals' worry about mortality.\n2. Feelings of empathy and emotional intimacy: Empathic listening, sometimes leading to a conversation partner feeling like they are receiving a psychological hug, can lead to good relationships and emotional intimacy.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7072547406026672, "g_worst_claim": 0.3335377772649129, "g_content": 2.8331729125976564, "g_traj_mean": 1.7695739269256592}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 305, 35268, 702, 23187, 6239, 429, 2924, 17719, 10955, 911, 28428, 323, 85544, 14269, 65164, 323, 6247, 46351, 13, 472, 13299, 525, 11660, 311, 7802, 279, 4453, 2487, 311, 1741, 458, 12818, 429, 1657, 13923, 2908, 432, 13578, 311, 279, 2456, 315, 1657, 2155, 10975, 13, 13409, 587, 292, 14289, 646, 7025, 2990, 311, 264, 10435, 8263, 8266, 1075, 807, 525, 12308, 264, 23187, 29784, 11, 4623, 80903, 279, 6785, 23187, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, hugging has psychological effects that include reducing worry about mortality and fostering emotional intimacy and happy marriages. Hugs are claimed to affect the entire body to such an extent that many scientists consider it equivalent to the effect of many different drugs. Empathic listening can sometimes lead to a conversation partner feeling like they are receiving a psychological hug, further emphasizing the positive psychological effects of hugging.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8573772093473586, "g_worst_claim": 0.3335377772649129, "g_content": 3.298534478081597, "g_traj_mean": 2.2307913303375244}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 23187, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 73558, 1661, 323, 17719, 10955, 25, 576, 1156, 21085, 13230, 429, 305, 35268, 537, 1172, 5707, 264, 8205, 8266, 714, 1083, 21501, 279, 4453, 2487, 11, 892, 646, 7949, 10955, 323, 1281, 1251, 2666, 1661, 382, 17, 13, 17582, 11519, 47351, 323, 14269, 65164, 25, 576, 2086, 21085, 14807, 429, 1667, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 11, 3881, 438, 35581, 