{"id": "183", "question": "how to cook a small prime rib roast in oven", "gt": "Before cooking the prime rib roast, let it stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Place the roast on a rack in a pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Roast it in the oven for 1 hour. After cooking, you can prepare au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat. Add wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits. Add beef stock and cook to reduce the juice by half, which might take about 20 minutes. Add salt and pepper to taste.", "pred": "1. Set the oven to 450°F and allow it to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes.\n2. Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper. Using any other spices will take away the flavor from the prime rib.\n3. Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up.\n4. Roast the roast for 1 hour.\n5. Turn off the oven and let the roast rest for at least 1 hour at room temperature.\n6. While the roast is resting, prepare the au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat, adding in the wine, cooking for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits, adding in the beef stock, cooking and reducing the juice by half (this might take about 20 minutes), and adding salt and pepper to taste.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Set the oven to 450°F and allow it to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes.\n2. Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper. Using any other spices will take away the flavor from the prime rib.\n3. Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up.\n4. Roast the roast for 1 hour.\n5. Turn off the oven and let the roast rest for at least 1 hour at room temperature.\n6. While the roast is resting, prepare the au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat, adding in the wine, cooking for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits, adding in the beef stock, cooking and reducing the juice by half (this might take about 20 minutes), and adding salt and pepper to taste.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to cook a small prime rib roast in the oven, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Set the oven to 450°F and allow it to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes.\\n2. Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper. Using any other spices will take away the flavor from the prime rib.\\n3. Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up.\\n4. Roast the roast for 1 hour.\\n5. Turn off the oven and let the roast rest for at least 1 hour at room temperature.\\n6. While the roast is resting, prepare the au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat, adding in the wine, cooking for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits, adding in the beef stock, cooking and reducing the juice by half (this might take about 20 minutes), and adding salt and pepper to taste.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook a small prime rib roast in the oven:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 375 degree F.\\n2. Allow the oven to preheat for at least 1 hour.\\n3. Rub the roast with House Seasoning.\\n4. Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up.\\n5. Roast the prime rib roast for 1 hour.\\n6. Turn off the oven to let the roast rest.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook a small prime rib roast in the oven follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Set the oven to 450°F and allow it to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes.\\n2. Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper (using any other spices will take away the flavor from the prime rib!).\\n3. While the roast is resting, prepare the au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat.\\n4. Add in the wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits.\\n5. Add in the beef stock and cook and reduce the juice by half (this might take about 20 minutes).\\n6. Add salt and pepper to taste.\\n7. Once the roast is seasoned and the au jus is prepared, place the roast in the preheated oven.\", \"Based on the given passages, here's how to cook a small prime rib roast in the oven:\\n\\n1. Set the oven to 450°F and allow it to preheat for at least 15 minutes.\\n2. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Avoid using any other spices as they may take away the flavor from the prime rib.\\n3. Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up.\\n4. Let the roast stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour before cooking.\\n5. Roast the prime rib in the preheated oven for the desired time.\\n6. Once done, turn off the oven and allow the roast to rest for a while before serving.\\n7. While the roast is resting, prepare the au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat, adding in the wine, cooking for 8-10 minutes stirring and scraping any brown bits, adding in the beef stock, cooking and reducing the juice by half (this might take about 20 minutes), and adding salt and pepper to taste.\"]", "time_sec": 34.742, "generation_time_seconds": 33.8122, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9137, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 264, 2613, 10250, 20131, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 2573, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 323, 2138, 432, 311, 855, 19963, 369, 264, 8028, 315, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 57685, 448, 1172, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 12021, 714, 10077, 315, 7722, 4910, 3691, 24353, 13, 12091, 894, 1008, 48559, 686, 1896, 3123, 279, 17172, 504, 279, 10250, 20131, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 57685, 389, 264, 29659, 304, 279, 7215, 448, 279, 20131, 3108, 1495, 323, 279, 38985, 3108, 705, 624, 19, 13, 11830, 559, 279, 57685, 369, 220, 16, 6460, 624, 20, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1077, 279, 57685, 2732, 369, 518, 3245, 220, 16, 6460, 518, 3054, 9315, 624, 21, 13, 5976, 279, 57685, 374, 40119, 11, 10549, 279, 7906, 44807, 553, 24047, 279, 926, 14725, 7215, 389, 279, 44015, 916, 1550, 8628, 11, 7842, 304, 279, 13078, 11, 17233, 369, 220, 23, 12, 16, 15, 4420, 11, 53954, 323, 81438, 894, 13876, 9472, 11, 7842, 304, 279, 24317, 5591, 11, 17233, 323, 17719, 279, 22815, 553, 4279, 320, 574, 2578, 1896, 911, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 701, 323, 7842, 12021, 323, 24353, 311, 12656, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Set the oven to 450°F and allow it to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes.\n2. Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper. Using any other spices will take away the flavor from the prime rib.\n3. Place the roast on a rack in the pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up.\n4. Roast the roast for 1 hour.\n5. Turn off the oven and let the roast rest for at least 1 hour at room temperature.\n6. While the roast is resting, prepare the au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat, adding in the wine, cooking for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits, adding in the beef stock, cooking and reducing the juice by half (this might take about 20 minutes), and adding salt and pepper to taste.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.362816406093345, "g_worst_claim": 0.19299123684565225, "g_content": 1.490007034455887, "g_traj_mean": 1.3518593311309814}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 264, 2613, 10250, 20131, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 22, 20, 8381, 434, 624, 17, 13, 26530, 279, 23387, 311, 855