], "pred": "1. Set the oven to 450°F and allow it to preheat for a minimum of 15 minutes.\n2. Season the roast with only a small amount of salt but lots of fresh ground black pepper (using any other spices will take away the flavor from the prime rib!).\n3. While the roast is resting, prepare the au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat.\n4. Add in the wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits.\n5. Add in the beef stock and cook and reduce the juice by half (this might take about 20 minutes).\n6. Add salt and pepper to taste.\n7. Once the roast is seasoned and the au jus is prepared, place the roast in the preheated oven.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.33601491886692, "g_worst_claim": 0.21392955780029296, "g_content": 1.4786101593368355, "g_traj_mean": 1.366174578666687}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 594, 1246, 311, 4296, 264, 2613, 10250, 20131, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 1447, 16, 13, 2573, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 323, 2138, 432, 311, 855, 19963, 369, 518, 3245, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 57685, 448, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 12021, 323, 10077, 315, 7722, 4910, 3691, 24353, 13, 34006, 1667, 894, 1008, 48559, 438, 807, 1231, 1896, 3123, 279, 17172, 504, 279, 10250, 20131, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 57685, 389, 264, 29659, 304, 279, 7215, 448, 279, 20131, 3108, 1495, 323, 279, 38985, 3108, 705, 624, 19, 13, 6771, 279, 57685, 2498, 518, 3054, 9315, 369, 518, 3245, 220, 16, 6460, 1573, 17233, 624, 20, 13, 11830, 559, 279, 10250, 20131, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 369, 279, 12685, 882, 624, 21, 13, 9646, 2814, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 57685, 311, 2732, 369, 264, 1393, 1573, 13480, 624, 22, 13, 5976, 279, 57685, 374, 40119, 11, 10549, 279, 7906, 44807, 553, 24047, 279, 926, 14725, 7215, 389, 279, 44015, 916, 1550, 8628, 11, 7842, 304, 279, 13078, 11, 17233, 369, 220, 23, 12, 16, 15, 4420, 53954, 323, 81438, 