{"id": "185", "question": "how long does it take to make chicken tender in crock pot", "gt": "To make chicken tender in a crock pot, you can cook it on low for 6 - 8 hours or until done. Alternatively, you can cook it on high for 1 hour, then on low for about 5 hours or until done. Another option is cooking it for 4 hours on high.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, it takes 4 hours on high or 8 hours on low to make chicken tender in the crock pot.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, it takes 4 hours on high or 8 hours on low to make chicken tender in the crock pot.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot when cooking on low.\", \"Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours of cooking on low for chicken to become tender in a crock pot.\", \"Based on the given passages, it takes 4 hours on high or 8 hours on low to make chicken tender in the crock pot.\", \"Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot when cooked on low.\"]", "time_sec": 11.739, "generation_time_seconds": 11.0664, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6609, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 432, 4990, 220, 21, 481, 220, 23, 4115, 311, 1281, 16158, 27582, 304, 264, 14093, 377, 3338, 979, 17233, 389, 3347, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot when cooking on low.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7007562283313635, "g_worst_claim": 0.4290403525034587, "g_content": 0.6694788251604352, "g_traj_mean": 0.8039886355400085}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 432, 4990, 220, 21, 481, 220, 23, 4115, 315, 17233, 389, 3347, 369, 16158, 311, 3635, 27582, 304, 264, 14093, 377, 3338, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours of cooking on low for chicken to become tender in a crock pot.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.76976109760395, "g_worst_claim": 0.4290403525034587, "g_content": 0.7150802612304688, "g_traj_mean": 0.9184187650680542}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 432, 4990, 220, 19, 4115, 389, 1550, 476, 220, 23, 4115, 389, 3347, 311, 1281, 16158, 27582, 304, 279, 14093, 377, 3338, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, it takes 4 hours on high or 8 hours on low to make chicken tender in the crock pot.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.48772373579550476, "g_worst_claim": 0.4290403525034587, "g_content": 0.49172172546386717, "g_traj_mean": 0.5020160675048828}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 432, 4990, 220, 21, 481, 220, 23, 4115, 311, 1281, 16158, 27582, 304, 264, 14093, 377, 3338, 979, 29105, 389, 3347, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot when cooked on low.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7304604523109668, "g_worst_claim": 0.4290403525034587, "g_content": 0.7503018379211426, "g_traj_mean": 0.8509578108787537}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.81, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "189", "question": "how long does it take to make chicken tender in crock pot", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"How long does it take to make chicken tender in a crock pot?\" is:\n\n6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.\n\nThe first passage suggests cooking the chicken on low for 6-8 hours, or 1 hour on high and then 5 hours on low. The second passage repeats the same information. The third passage provides additional information that chicken breast will always come out tender as long as there is enough moisture, and suggests cooking it for 4 hours on high if you're short on time.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is 6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot. To achieve this, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place 8 chicken breasts in the crock pot.\n2. Cook on low for 8 hours.\n3. Alternatively, you can cook on high for 4 hours if time is an issue.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot. To achieve this, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place 8 chicken breasts in the crock pot.\n2. Cook on low for 8 hours.\n3. Alternatively, you can cook on high for 4 hours if time is an issue.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot when cooking on low.\", \"Based on the given passages, the chicken will take 8 hours to cook on low in a crock pot.\", \"Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot. To achieve this, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place 8 chicken breasts in the crock pot.\\n2. Cook on low for 8 hours.\\n3. Alternatively, you can cook on high for 4 hours if time is an issue.\", \"Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a slow cooker when cooked on low.\"]", "time_sec": 13.053, "generation_time_seconds": 12.3414, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7021, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 432, 4990, 220, 21, 481, 220, 23, 4115, 311, 1281, 16158, 27582, 304, 264, 14093, 377, 3338, 979, 17233, 389, 3347, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot when cooking on low.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7007562283313635, "g_worst_claim": 0.4290403525034587, "g_content": 0.6694788251604352, "g_traj_mean": 0.8039886355400085}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 16158, 686, 1896, 220, 23, 4115, 311, 4296, 389, 3347, 304, 264, 14093, 377, 3338, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the chicken will take 8 hours to cook on low in a crock pot.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8206474664164525, "g_worst_claim": 0.4290403525034587, "g_content": 1.117248448458585, "g_traj_mean": 0.947038471698761}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 432, 4990, 220, 21, 481, 220, 23, 4115, 311, 1281, 16158, 27582, 304, 264, 14093, 377, 3338, 13, 2014, 11075, 419, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 220, 23, 16158, 36349, 304, 279, 14093, 377, 3338, 624, 17, 13, 12514, 389, 3347, 369, 220, 23, 4115, 624, 18, 13, 38478, 11, 498, 646, 4296, 389, 1550, 369, 220, 19, 4115, 421, 882, 374, 458, 4265, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a crock pot. To achieve this, follow these steps:\n\n1. Place 8 chicken breasts in the crock pot.\n2. Cook on low for 8 hours.\n3. Alternatively, you can cook on high for 4 hours if time is an issue.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.733567514085265, "g_worst_claim": -0.22742090622584024, "g_content": 1.081914520263672, "g_traj_mean": 0.7231082916259766}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 432, 4990, 220, 21, 481, 220, 23, 4115, 311, 1281, 16158, 27582, 304, 264, 6301, 62083, 979, 29105, 389, 3347, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, it takes 6 - 8 hours to make chicken tender in a slow cooker when cooked on low.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7711908646992275, "g_worst_claim": 0.4290403525034587, "g_content": 0.8210571834019252, "g_traj_mean": 0.9035307765007019}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.81, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "191", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "To attach multiple picture frames together, you can use small hinges to connect the frames. Lay the frames beside each other to determine the desired arrangement. For two frames, use identical ones, and for three frames, either choose three identical frames or use a larger one as the middle frame. Mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides of the frames, ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges. Attach the hinges to securely join the frames.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together:\n\n1. Select frames of the same wood molding.\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n3. Mark the hinge placement on the frames.\n4. Ensure the placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame.\n5. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together:\n\n1. Select frames of the same wood molding.\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n3. Mark the hinge placement on the frames.\n4. Ensure the placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame.\n5. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\\n2. For joining two frames, use identical frames.\\n3. For joining three frames, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\\n4. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\\n5. Put two frames together back to back and mark the hinge placement.\\n6. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\\n7. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\", \"Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding for grouping.\\n2. For joining two frames, use identical frames. For joining three frames, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\\n3. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\\n4. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement.\\n5. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\\n6. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\\n7. Screw the frame to the backer board and repeat with each frame.\\n8. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the grouped frames and hang it up.\", \"Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together:\\n\\n1. Select frames of the same wood molding.\\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\\n3. Mark the hinge placement on the frames.\\n4. Ensure the placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame.\\n5. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\", \"Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\\n2. Decide whether to join two or three frames together, using identical frames for two, or one larger frame for three.\\n3. Lay the frames beside each other to see the effect.\\n4. Mark the hinge placement on the frames, ensuring the distance from the bottom edges is the same for each frame to ensure secure standing on the table top.\\n5. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\\n\\nThese steps ensure a secure and aesthetically pleasing arrangement of multiple picture frames.\"]", "time_sec": 24.561, "generation_time_seconds": 23.7641, "selection_time_seconds": 0.786, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 15498, 5248, 6802, 14087, 3786, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 1378, 476, 2326, 14087, 315, 279, 1852, 7579, 65057, 624, 17, 13, 1752, 18169, 1378, 14087, 11, 990, 19516, 14087, 624, 18, 13, 1752, 18169, 2326, 14087, 11, 5157, 2987, 2326, 315, 279, 1852, 476, 825, 892, 374, 8131, 311, 387, 279, 6149, 4034, 624, 19, 13, 43924, 279, 14087, 29388, 1817, 1008, 311, 1490, 421, 498, 1075, 279, 2456, 624, 20, 13, 10224, 1378, 14087, 3786, 1182, 311, 1182, 323, 1868, 279, 75593, 21448, 624, 21, 13, 29279, 279, 75593, 21448, 374, 279, 1852, 6010, 504, 279, 5622, 12822, 315, 1817, 4034, 311, 5978, 279, 40041, 9185, 2498, 51023, 389, 279, 1965, 1909, 624, 22, 13, 48384, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\n2. For joining two frames, use identical frames.\n3. For joining three frames, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\n4. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n5. Put two frames together back to back and mark the hinge placement.\n6. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n7. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2292772081527077, "g_worst_claim": 0.25068291028340656, "g_content": 2.9815832439221834, "g_traj_mean": 2.1316444873809814}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 15498, 5248, 6802, 14087, 3786, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 8427, 1378, 476, 2326, 14087, 315, 279, 1852, 7579, 65057, 369, 49184, 624, 17, 13, 1752, 18169, 1378, 14087, 11, 990, 19516, 14087, 13, 1752, 18169, 2326, 14087, 11, 5157, 2987, 2326, 315, 279, 1852, 476, 825, 892, 374, 8131, 311, 387, 279, 6149, 4034, 624, 18, 13, 43924, 279, 14087, 29388, 1817, 1008, 311, 1490, 421, 498, 1075, 279, 2456, 624, 19, 13, 10224, 1378, 14087, 3786, 1182, 311, 1182, 11, 323, 1868, 279, 75593, 21448, 624, 20, 13, 48384, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 624, 21, 13, 29279, 279, 75593, 21448, 374, 279, 1852, 6010, 504, 279, 5622, 12822, 315, 1817, 4034, 311, 5978, 279, 40041, 9185, 2498, 51023, 389, 279, 1965, 1909, 624, 22, 13, 72175, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1182, 261, 4479, 323, 13153, 448, 1817, 4034, 624, 23, 13, 48384, 264, 20704, 9067, 311, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 40041, 14087, 323, 14678, 432, 705, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding for grouping.\n2. For joining two frames, use identical frames. For joining three frames, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\n3. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n4. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement.\n5. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\n6. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n7. Screw the frame to the backer board and repeat with each frame.\n8. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the grouped frames and hang it up.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.155818538445057, "g_worst_claim": 0.24094935258229574, "g_content": 2.7582115760216346, "g_traj_mean": 1.9780255556106567}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 15498, 5248, 6802, 14087, 3786, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 14087, 315, 279, 1852, 7579, 65057, 624, 17, 13, 43924, 279, 14087, 29388, 1817, 1008, 311, 1490, 421, 498, 1075, 279, 2456, 624, 18, 13, 4389, 279, 75593, 21448, 389, 279, 14087, 624, 19, 13, 29279, 279, 21448, 374, 279, 1852, 6010, 504, 279, 5622, 12822, 315, 1817, 4034, 624, 20, 13, 48384, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together:\n\n1. Select frames of the same wood molding.\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n3. Mark the hinge placement on the frames.\n4. Ensure the placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame.\n5. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.119968216123536, "g_worst_claim": 0.3075987895329793, "g_content": 2.808399963378906, "g_traj_mean": 1.7543078660964966}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 15498, 5248, 6802, 14087, 3786, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 1378, 476, 2326, 14087, 315, 279, 1852, 7579, 65057, 624, 17, 13, 98881, 3425, 311, 5138, 1378, 476, 2326, 14087, 3786, 11, 1667, 19516, 14087, 369, 1378, 11, 476, 825, 8131, 4034, 369, 2326, 624, 18, 13, 43924, 279, 14087, 29388, 1817, 1008, 311, 1490, 279, 2456, 624, 19, 13, 4389, 279, 75593, 21448, 389, 279, 14087, 11, 22573, 279, 6010, 504, 279, 5622, 12822, 374, 279, 1852, 369, 1817, 4034, 311, 5978, 9767, 11259, 389, 279, 1965, 1909, 624, 20, 13, 48384, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 382, 9485, 7354, 5978, 264, 9767, 323, 26816, 13803, 2673, 53699, 26112, 315, 5248, 6802, 14087, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps ensure a secure and aesthetically pleasing arrangement of multiple picture frames.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.652872612997137, "g_worst_claim": 0.14938953518867493, "g_content": 2.323065744319432, "g_traj_mean": 1.577642798423767}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "193", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some steps for attaching multiple picture frames together:\n\nPassage 1: Table-Stand Grouping\nTo join two or three frames together, you can use identical frames or one larger frame as the middle piece. Place the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect, and then mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nPassage 2: Hanging Multiple Pictures Together\nBefore attaching the frames together, test different arrangements of the group of multiple pictures on the floor. Once you have decided on the layout, screw the frames to the backer board, repeating the process for each frame. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the frames and hang them on the wall to enjoy the finished result.\n\nPassage 3: Attaching Frames Together\nTo attach two frames together, place them back to back and mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. The placement should be the same distance from the bottom edge of each frame to ensure stability when the grouped pictures are placed on a table. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nIn conclusion, the recommended method for attaching multiple picture frames together involves using identical or matching frames, marking the hinge placement on the connecting sides, and attaching small hinges to join the frames together. It's also important to test different arrangements of the group of pictures on the floor before attaching the frames together, and to ensure that the frames are securely attached to the backer board before hanging them on the wall.", "pred": "1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\n2. For joining two frames, use identical frames.\n3. For joining three frames, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\n4. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n5. Put two frames together back to back and mark the hinge placement.\n6. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n7. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\n2. For joining two frames, use identical frames.\n3. For joining three frames, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\n4. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n5. Put two frames together back to back and mark the hinge placement.\n6. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n7. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\\n2. For joining two frames, use identical frames.\\n3. For joining three frames, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\\n4. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\\n5. Put two frames together back to back and mark the hinge placement.\\n6. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\\n7. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\", \"Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together:\\n\\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\\n2. Depending on the number of frames, choose frames to be identical or match in size if joining three.\\n3. Lay the frames beside each other to test the effect.\\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\\n5. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame for stability.\\n6. Save time by having the pictures ready in the frames beforehand.\\n7. Screw the frame to the backer board for each frame.\\n8. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the frames and hang them up for display.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\\n2. For joining two frames, use identical frames.\\n3. For joining three frames, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\\n4. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\\n5. Put two frames together back to back and mark the hinge placement.\\n6. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\\n7. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\", \"Based on the given passages, to attach multiple picture frames together, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select either two or three frames of the same wood molding.\\n2. For joining two together, use identical frames.\\n3. For joining three together, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\\n4. Lay them beside each other to see if you like the effect.\\n5. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement.\\n6. The placement must be the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\\n7. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\\n8. Screw the frame to the backer board, repeating with each frame.\\n9. Save time by having the pictures all ready in the frames.\\n10. You can always unscrew them at a later date to change the picture if you want.\\n11. Attach a hanging wire to the back.\\n12. Hang it up and step back to enjoy the results.\"]", "time_sec": 30.975, "generation_time_seconds": 30.0364, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9276, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 15498, 5248, 6802, 14087, 3786, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 1378, 476, 2326, 14087, 315, 279, 1852, 7579, 65057, 624, 17, 13, 1752, 18169, 1378, 14087, 11, 990, 19516, 14087, 624, 18, 13, 1752, 18169, 2326, 14087, 11, 5157, 2987, 2326, 315, 279, 1852, 476, 825, 892, 374, 8131, 311, 387, 279, 6149, 4034, 624, 19, 13, 43924, 279, 14087, 29388, 1817, 1008, 311, 1490, 421, 498, 1075, 279, 2456, 624, 20, 13, 10224, 1378, 14087, 3786, 1182, 311, 1182, 323, 1868, 279, 75593, 21448, 624, 21, 13, 29279, 279, 75593, 21448, 374, 279, 1852, 6010, 504, 279, 5622, 12822, 315, 1817, 4034, 311, 5978, 279, 40041, 9185, 2498, 51023, 389, 279, 1965, 1909, 624, 22, 13, 48384, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\n2. For joining two frames, use identical frames.\n3. For joining three frames, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\n4. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n5. Put two frames together back to back and mark the hinge placement.\n6. Ensure the hinge placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n7. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2292772081527077, "g_worst_claim": 0.25068291028340656, "g_content": 2.9815832439221834, "g_traj_mean": 2.1316444873809814}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 15498, 5248, 6802, 14087, 3786, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 1378, 476, 2326, 14087, 315, 279, 1852, 7579, 65057, 624, 17, 13, 39630, 389, 279, 1372, 315, 14087, 11, 5157, 1408