35537719727}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 15498, 5248, 6802, 14087, 3786, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 1378, 476, 2326, 14087, 315, 279, 1852, 7579, 65057, 13, 1752, 18169, 1378, 3786, 11, 990, 19516, 14087, 13, 1752, 18169, 2326, 3786, 11, 5157, 2987, 2326, 315, 279, 1852, 476, 825, 892, 374, 8131, 311, 387, 279, 6149, 4034, 624, 17, 13, 43924, 1105, 29388, 1817, 1008, 311, 1490, 421, 498, 1075, 279, 2456, 624, 18, 13, 10224, 1378, 14087, 3786, 1182, 311, 1182, 323, 1868, 279, 75593, 21448, 13, 576, 21448, 1969, 387, 279, 1852, 6010, 504, 279, 5622, 12822, 315, 1817, 4034, 311, 5978, 429, 279, 40041, 9185, 2498, 51023, 389, 279, 1965, 1909, 624, 19, 13, 48384, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding. For joining two together, use identical frames. For joining three together, choose either three of the same or one which is larger to be the middle frame.\n2. Lay them beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n3. Put two frames together back to back and mark the hinge placement. The placement must be the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2714000210607606, "g_worst_claim": 0.1696132222811381, "g_content": 3.233159454775528, "g_traj_mean": 2.36102032661438}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 13.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "197", "question": "leasing meaning", "gt": "Leasing refers to a process in which a firm obtains the use of fixed assets by making contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments to the owner of those assets. The lessee is the party receiving the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of certain fixed assets for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of certain fixed assets for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.\", \"Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.\", \"Based on the given passages, leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of certain fixed assets for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.\", \"Based on the given passages, leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments.\"]", "time_sec": 19.274, "generation_time_seconds": 18.3851, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8669, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 70319, 374, 264, 1882, 553, 892, 264, 7474, 646, 6851, 279, 990, 315, 264, 3654, 8356, 9329, 369, 892, 432, 1969, 2291, 264, 4013, 315, 75443, 11, 38345, 11, 3742, 77812, 14173, 13, 576, 3541, 4060, 374, 279, 13964, 315, 279, 3516, 476, 279, 11770, 1212, 279, 25064, 5116, 323, 279, 2686, 269, 374, 279, 6372, 315, 279, 11770, 13, 576, 5025, 1948, 279, 25239, 323, 279, 40147, 374, 2598, 264, 5779, 6572, 11, 323, 646, 387, 369, 264, 8356, 476, 458, 80856, 4168, 315, 882, 13, 576, 17879, 369, 279, 25064, 374, 2598, 8016, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7837141269954515, "g_worst_claim": 0.11195485790570577, "g_content": 2.732598281488186, "g_traj_mean": 1.8161749839782715}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2304, 4422, 374, 264, 1882, 553, 892, 264, 7474, 646, 6851, 279, 990, 315, 264, 3654, 8356, 9329, 369, 892, 432, 1969, 2291, 264, 4013, 315, 75443, 11, 38345, 11, 3742, 77812, 14173, 13, 576, 5025, 1948, 279, 25239, 323, 279, 40147, 374, 2598, 264, 5779, 6572, 11, 323, 646, 387, 369, 264, 8356, 476, 458, 80856, 4168, 315, 882, 13, 576, 3541, 4060, 374, 279, 13964, 315, 279, 3516, 476, 279, 11770, 1212, 279, 25064, 5116, 323, 279, 2686, 269, 374, 279, 6372, 315, 279, 11770, 13, 151645], "pred": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1294972517551516, "g_worst_claim": 1.1544698568490834, "g_content": 3.032074872185202, "g_traj_mean": 1.9449102878570557}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 70319, 374, 264, 1882, 553, 892, 264, 7474, 646, 6851, 279, 990, 315, 3654, 8356, 11770, 369, 892, 432, 1969, 2291, 264, 4013, 315, 75443, 11, 38345, 11, 3742, 77812, 14173, 13, 576, 3541, 4060, 374, 279, 13964, 315, 279, 3516, 476, 11770, 1212, 279, 25064, 5116, 323, 279, 26