ctive tissue below the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6740787006748385, "g_worst_claim": 0.20567989349365234, "g_content": 1.2065277099609375, "g_traj_mean": 0.7364230155944824}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 19053, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 11, 2670, 1874, 362, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 320, 38, 1911, 8, 23157, 11, 357, 1342, 88, 1074, 91311, 11, 323, 3800, 13, 4220, 23157, 646, 33427, 279, 58815, 15195, 685, 11, 264, 6193, 315, 4564, 533, 19847, 3685, 279, 6787, 13, 25311, 315, 1493, 23157, 2924, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 4510, 11706, 288, 11, 892, 646, 1083, 5240, 5412, 79, 27591, 323, 3163, 295, 7836, 13, 63124, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 646, 387, 8881, 553, 1493, 23157, 304, 8848, 5048, 323, 646, 387, 264, 803, 11406, 18873, 7707, 311, 279, 28920, 807, 5990, 5240, 11, 892, 525, 3545, 23034, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria, staphylococcus, and others. These bacteria can infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. Examples of these bacteria include Streptococcus pyogenes, which can also cause strep throat and impetigo. Necrotizing fasciitis can be caused by these bacteria in rare cases and can be a more dangerous infection compared to the infections they usually cause, which are often mild.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0050015850785856, "g_worst_claim": 0.21440265576044717, "g_content": 1.7193840182557398, "g_traj_mean": 1.0508782863616943}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 19053, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 13, 4220, 23157, 2924, 1874, 362, 13440, 2832, 336, 5730, 28050, 5412, 417, 509, 509, 5855, 320, 623, 265, 417, 509, 91311, 4510, 11706, 288, 701, 357, 1342, 88, 1074, 91311, 11, 323, 3800, 13, 576, 28920, 8881, 553, 1493, 23157, 525, 5990, 23034, 11, 714, 304, 8848, 5048, 11, 807, 646, 2990, 311, 264, 803, 11406, 18873, 429, 646, 6921, 6787, 11, 8664, 11, 323, 279, 19847, 18202, 279, 23648, 13, 576, 8457, 374, 7025, 13862, 311, 438, 24955, 5655, 1095, 23157, 323, 646, 387, 1602, 8848, 714, 6001, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria. These bacteria include group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes), staphylococcus, and others. The infections caused by these bacteria are usually mild, but in rare cases, they can lead to a more dangerous infection that can destroy skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles. The disease is sometimes referred to as flesh-eating bacteria and can be very rare but serious.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0672334137336008, "g_worst_claim": 0.21440265576044717, "g_content": 2.033461282419604, "g_traj_mean": 1.0721620321273804}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "203", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main cause of necrotizing fasciitis is bacterial infection, specifically group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) and Staphylococcus. Additionally, other types of bacteria have also been associated with the disease. Trauma, such as cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or needle puncture wounds, can also play a role in the development of necrotizing fasciitis. Surgical incision sites and various surgical procedures can also serve as a source of infection. Therefore, the answer is: Bacterial infection, including group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) and Staphylococcus, and trauma.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria. Group A Streptococcus is also responsible for strep throat and impetigo. Other bacteria such as staphylococcus and others have also been associated with the disease.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria. Group A Streptococcus is also responsible for strep throat and impetigo. Other bacteria such as staphylococcus and others have also been associated with the disease.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria. These bacteria can include group A Streptococcus (GAS), staphylococcus, and others. The infections caused by these bacteria are usually mild, but in rare cases, they can lead to a more dangerous infection that can destroy skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles within a very short time. This condition is sometimes referred to as flesh-eating bacteria.\", \"Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria. Group A Streptococcus is also responsible for strep throat and impetigo. Other bacteria such as staphylococcus and others have also been associated with the disease.\", \"Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is primarily caused by bacteria, with group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) being the most common cause. Other bacteria, including staphylococcus, can also cause the disease. The infections typically affect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. Necrotizing fasciitis is an infection that can destroy skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles within a very short time. While the infections caused by these bacteria are usually mild, they can rarely lead to a more dangerous and serious condition known as flesh-eating bacteria.\", \"Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS), which is also responsible for strep throat and impetigo. In rare cases, fungi can also lead to this condition. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin, which can result in the destruction of skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles within a very short time. This infection is sometimes referred to as flesh-eating bacteria and is very rare but serious.\"]", "time_sec": 23.58, "generation_time_seconds": 22.5195, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0483, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 19053, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 13, 4220, 23157, 646, 2924, 1874, 362, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 320, 38, 1911, 701, 357, 1342, 88, 1074, 91311, 11, 323, 3800, 13, 576, 28920, 8881, 553, 1493, 23157, 525, 5990, 23034, 11, 714, 304, 8848, 5048, 11, 807, 646, 2990, 311, 264, 803, 11406, 18873, 429, 646, 6921, 6787, 11, 8664, 11, 323, 279, 19847, 18202, 279, 23648, 2878, 264, 1602, 2805, 882, 13, 1096, 2971, 374, 7025, 13862, 311, 438, 24955, 5655, 1095, 23157, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria. These bacteria can include group A Streptococcus (GAS), staphylococcus, and others. The infections caused by these bacteria are usually mild, but in rare cases, they can lead to a more dangerous infection that can destroy skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles within a very short time. This condition is sometimes referred to as flesh-eating bacteria.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.034265229897403, "g_worst_claim": 0.3328805168469747, "g_content": 1.9975913443216464, "g_traj_mean": 1.1097984313964844}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 19053, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 11, 2670, 1874, 362, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 320, 38, 1911, 8, 23157, 13, 5737, 362, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 374, 1083, 8480, 369, 5412, 79, 27591, 323, 3163, 295, 7836, 13, 6944, 23157, 1741, 438, 357, 1342, 88, 1074, 91311, 323, 3800, 614, 1083, 1012, 5815, 448, 279, 8457, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria. Group A Streptococcus is also responsible for strep throat and impetigo. Other bacteria such as staphylococcus and others have also been associated with the disease.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7587274805016815, "g_worst_claim": 0.3328805168469747, "g_content": 1.6484642028808594, "g_traj_mean": 0.8109639286994934}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 19053, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 15503, 8881, 553, 23157, 11, 448, 1874, 362, 13440, 2832, 336, 5730, 28050, 5412, 417, 509, 509, 5855, 320, 623, 265, 417, 509, 91311, 4510, 11706,