 311, 438, 24955, 5655, 1095, 23157, 323, 374, 1602, 8848, 714, 6001, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS), which is also responsible for strep throat and impetigo. In rare cases, fungi can also lead to this condition. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin, which can result in the destruction of skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles within a very short time. This infection is sometimes referred to as flesh-eating bacteria and is very rare but serious.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1061818092579976, "g_worst_claim": 0.31032666293057526, "g_content": 1.8457677413006217, "g_traj_mean": 1.1080607175827026}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "204", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Chard, also known as Swiss chard, is a vegetable with large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a flavor that is stronger and more assertive than spinach, and some people find it bitter. Chard can be eaten raw in salads when it's young, but mature leaves and stalks are usually cooked or sautéed. Chard is actually a type of beet that is grown for its leaves rather than its root. It can produce white, yellow, or red leaf stalks. Chard is highly perishable and should be kept in the refrigerator for only 2 to 3 days.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of beet that has been cultivated for leaf production, resulting in large, fleshy, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Unlike spinach, chard has a stronger, more assertive flavor, sometimes described as bitter. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is not related to spinach but is similar to it in some aspects. It is also noted that chard can be harvested at different stages, from young and tender to mature with slightly tougher stems.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of beet that has been cultivated for leaf production, resulting in large, fleshy, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Unlike spinach, chard has a stronger, more assertive flavor, sometimes described as bitter. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is not related to spinach but is similar to it in some aspects. It is also noted that chard can be harvested at different stages, from young and tender to mature with slightly tougher stems.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 days.\", \"Based on the given passages, chard is a type of beet that has been cultivated for leaf production, resulting in large, fleshy, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Unlike spinach, chard has a stronger, more assertive flavor, sometimes described as bitter. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is not related to spinach but is similar to it in some aspects. It is also noted that chard can be harvested at different stages, from young and tender to mature with slightly tougher stems.\", \"Based on the given passages, chard is a leaf vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, which some people perceive as bitter. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is commonly used in dishes like pizzoccheri. It is a descendant of the sea beet and is cultivated for its leaf production.\", \"Based on the given passages, chard is a type of vegetable that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked.\"]", "time_sec": 24.59, "generation_time_seconds": 23.4987, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0771, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 521, 567, 374, 264, 15933, 88, 6176, 35481, 429, 374, 264, 4462, 315, 279, 48012, 2997, 13, 1084, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 14689, 1744, 11, 25180, 8, 17172, 13, 29160, 3908, 521, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7112, 304, 76752, 11, 1393, 14851, 521, 567, 10901, 323, 54872, 82, 525, 11136, 29105, 13, 910, 567, 374, 9016, 82117, 480, 11, 773, 432, 1265, 387, 9768, 304, 279, 44944, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 2849, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 days.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.537680443805172, "g_worst_claim": 0.24905182917912802, "g_content": 1.9432360590720663, "g_traj_mean": 1.4024550914764404}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 521, 567, 374, 264, 943, 315, 48012, 429, 702, 1012, 66066, 369, 15933, 5670, 11, 12942, 304, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 11, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 26048, 67698, 11, 521, 567, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 17172, 11, 7025, 7481, 438, 25180, 13, 29160, 3908, 521, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7112, 304, 76752, 11, 1393, 14851, 521, 567, 10901, 323, 54872, 82, 525, 11136, 29105, 13, 910, 567, 374, 537, 5435, 311, 67698, 714, 374, 4428, 311, 432, 304, 1045, 13566, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 10342, 429, 521, 567, 646, 387, 66472, 518, 2155, 17628, 11, 504, 3908, 323, 27582, 311, 14851, 448, 10078, 48231, 43714, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of beet that has been cultivated for leaf production, resulting in large, fleshy, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Unlike spinach, chard has a stronger, more assertive flavor, sometimes described as bitter. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is not related to spinach but is similar to it in some aspects. It is also noted that chard can be harvested at different stages, from young and tender to mature with slightly tougher stems.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.359357583482249, "g_worst_claim": 0.24905182917912802, "g_content": 2.156387730648643, "g_traj_mean": 1.3433399200439453}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 521, 567, 374, 264, 15933, 35481, 429, 374, 264, 4462, 315, 279, 48012, 2997, 13, 1084, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 17172, 11, 892, 1045, 1251, 44393, 438, 25180, 13, 29160, 3908, 521, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7112, 304, 76752, 11, 1393, 14851, 10901, 323, 54872, 82, 525, 11136, 29105, 13, 910, 567, 374, 16626, 1483, 304, 25779, 1075, 281, 8759, 509, 9034, 72, 13, 1084, 374, 264, 75851, 315, 279, 9396, 48012, 323, 374, 66066, 369, 1181, 15933, 5670, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a leaf vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, which some people perceive as bitter. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is commonly used in dishes like pizzoccheri. It is a descendant of the sea beet and is cultivated for its leaf production.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3959809521200712, "g_worst_claim": 0.24905182917912802, "g_content": 2.271136713962929, "g_traj_mean": 1.418736457824707}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 521, 567, 374, 264, 943, 315, 35481, 429, 702, 1012, 11882, 369, 15933, 5670, 518, 279, 20284, 315, 5819, 3704, 18003, 13, 1084, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 14689, 1744, 11, 25180, 8, 17172, 13, 13263, 521, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7112, 304, 76752, 11, 1393, 14851, 521, 567, 10901, 323, 54872, 82, 525, 11136, 29105, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of vegetable that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7240647033466177, "g_worst_claim": 0.24905182917912802, "g_content": 2.6097573779878163, "g_traj_mean": 1.8209106922149658}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.81, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "205", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Chard is a vegetable that has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked or sautéed. Chard is in the same subspecies as beetroot and is cultivated for leaf production. It can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when the stems are slightly tougher. Chard is perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a minimum amount of time.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 days.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 days.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 days.\", \"Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is closely related to beets. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked, such as in pizzoccheri or sauteed dishes. The bitterness of chard fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor more delicate than that of cooked spinach.\", \"Based on the given passages, chard is a type of vegetable that is closely related to beets. It is characterized by large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard shares some similarities with spinach, but it has a stronger, more assertive (and some might say bitter) flavor. While chard can be used raw in salads, it is often cooked in dishes like pizzoccheri or sautéed, where its bitterness diminishes, leaving a refined flavor that is more delicate than cooked spinach. Chard can be harvested in its fresh white, yellow, or red leaf stalks and is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.\", \"Based on the given passages, chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It produces fresh white, yellow, or red leaf stalks. Chard is an attractive ornamental that can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when larger. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive, and some think bitter flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored unwashed in plastic bags in the crisper for 2 to 3 days.\"]", "time_sec": 25.908, "generation_time_seconds": 24.9017, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9958, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 521, 567, 374, 264, 15933, 88, 6176, 35481, 429, 374, 264, 4462, 315, 279, 48012, 2997, 13, 1084, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 14689, 1744, 11, 25180, 8, 17172, 13, 29160, 3908, 521, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7112, 304, 76752, 11, 1393, 14851, 521, 567, 10901, 323, 54872, 82, 525, 11136, 29105, 13, 910, 567, 374, 9016, 82117, 480, 11, 773, 432, 1265, 387, 9768, 304, 279, 44944, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 2849, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is a member of the beet family. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 days.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.537680443805172, "g_worst_claim": 0.24905182917912802, "g_content": 1.9432360590720663, "g_traj_mean": 1.4024550914764404}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 521, 567, 374, 264, 15933, 88, 6176, 35481, 429, 374, 15148, 5435, 311, 387, 1415, 13, 1084, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 14689, 1744, 11, 25180, 8, 17172, 13, 29160, 3908, 521, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7112, 304, 76752, 11, 1393, 14851, 521, 567, 10901, 323, 54872, 82, 525, 11136, 29105, 11, 1741, 438, 304, 281, 8759, 509, 9034, 72, 476, 822, 1070, 291, 25779, 13, 576, 78996, 315, 521, 567, 86409, 448, 17233, 11, 9380, 264, 37191, 17172, 803, 35201, 1091, 429, 315, 29105, 67698, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a leafy green vegetable that is closely related to beets. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked, such as in pizzoccheri or sauteed dishes. The bitterness of chard fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor more delicate than that of cooked spinach.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7350236764961622, "g_worst_claim": 0.24905182917912802, "g_content": 2.5136816636571346, "g_traj_mean": 1.6878732442855835}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 521, 567, 374, 264, 943, 315, 35481, 429, 374, 15148, 5435, 311, 387, 1415, 13, 1084, 374, 31871, 553, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 13248, 1045, 42774, 448, 67698, 11, 714, 432, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 437, 1045, 2578, 1977, 25180, 8, 17172, 13, 5976, 521, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7112, 304, 76752, 11, 432, 374, 3545, 29105, 304, 25779, 1075, 281, 8759, 509, 9034, 72, 476, 822, 332, 963, 291, 11, 1380, 1181, 78996, 56060, 288, 11, 9380, 264, 37191, 17172, 429, 374, 803, 35201, 1091, 29105, 67698, 13, 910, 567, 646, 387, 66472, 304, 1181, 7722, 4158, 11, 13753, 11, 476, 2518, 15933, 54872, 82, 323, 374, 458, 18879, 39445, 43086, 429, 11367, 1894, 311, 279, 35481, 13551, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of vegetable that is closely related to beets. It is characterized by large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard shares some similarities with spinach, but it has a stronger, more assertive (and some might say bitter) flavor. While chard can be used raw in salads, it is often cooked in dishes like pizzoccheri or sautéed, where its bitterness diminishes, leaving a refined flavor that is more delicate than cooked spinach. Chard can be harvested in its fresh white, yellow, or red leaf stalks and is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4750530808068385, "g_worst_claim": 0.24905182917912802, "g_content": 2.2820697907478578, "g_traj_mean": 1.49541175365448}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 521, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429, 702, 1012, 11882, 369, 15933, 5670, 518, 279, 20284, 315, 5819, 3704, 18003, 13, 1084, 18644, 7722, 4158, 11, 13753, 11, 476, 2518, 15933, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 374, 458, 18879, 39445, 43086, 429, 646, 387, 66472, 1393, 279, 10901, 525, 3908, 323, 27582, 476, 1283, 47161, 979, 8131, 13, 1084, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 11, 323, 1045, 1744, 25180, 17172, 13, 29160, 3908, 521, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7112, 304, 76752, 11, 1393, 14851, 521, 567, 10901, 323, 54872, 82, 525, 11136, 29105, 13, 910, 567, 374, 9016, 82117, 480, 11, 773, 432, 1265, 387, 9768, 15025, 13571, 304, 12188, 17899, 304, 279, 1560, 27370, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 2849, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It produces fresh white, yellow, or red leaf stalks. Chard is an attractive ornamental that can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when larger. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive, and some think bitter flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is extremely perishable, so it should be stored unwashed in plastic bags in the crisper for 2 to 3 days.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.774107601515002, "g_worst_claim": 0.24905182