{"id": "211", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, with all atoms having the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded, allowing for easy separation of the components using physical methods.", "pred": "Mixtures:\n- A physical combination of elements or compounds.\n- The parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded.\n- Retain their own identity.\n- Mixtures show the properties of constituent substances.\n- The constituents can be easily separated by physical methods.\n- Have a variable composition.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Mixtures:\n- A physical combination of elements or compounds.\n- The parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded.\n- Retain their own identity.\n- Mixtures show the properties of constituent substances.\n- The constituents can be easily separated by physical methods.\n- Have a variable composition.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are as follows:\\n\\n1. Elements are composed of only one type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance.\\n2. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. The elements in a compound are chemically bonded and cannot be separated by physical means.\\n3. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means. Mixtures can have a variable composition and show the properties of their constituent substances.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. All atoms in an element have the same number of protons.\\n\\n2. Compounds are substances made up of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances and can be separated by physical means.\\n\\n3. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. The individual components of a mixture can be physically separated from each other.\\n\\nThe main differences are:\\n- Elements consist of a single type of atom.\\n- Compounds are pure substances made of multiple elements.\\n- Mixtures are combinations of elements or compounds that are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical methods.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are as follows:\\n\\n1. Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. All of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons.\\n\\n2. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. They are also pure substances. The elements that make up a compound are chemically bonded together, so they cannot be separated by physical means.\\n\\n3. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Mixtures can be separated by physical means.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are as follows:\\n\\nElements:\\n- Composed of only one type of atom.\\n- Purest form of a chemical substance.\\n- All atoms in an element have the same number of protons.\\n\\nCompounds:\\n- Substances composed of two or more different elements.\\n- Pure substances.\\n- Elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.\\n\\nMixtures:\\n- A physical combination of elements or compounds.\\n- The parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded.\\n- Retain their own identity.\\n- Mixtures show the properties of constituent substances.\\n- The constituents can be easily separated by physical methods.\\n- Have a variable composition.\"]", "time_sec": 27.986, "generation_time_seconds": 27.2158, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7566, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 5424, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 34157, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 323, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 624, 17, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 323, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 13, 576, 5424, 304, 264, 23628, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 4157, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 624, 18, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 614, 264, 3890, 18037, 323, 1473, 279, 5888, 315, 862, 74064, 32055, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Elements are composed of only one type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance.\n2. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. The elements in a compound are chemically bonded and cannot be separated by physical means.\n3. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means. Mixtures can have a variable composition and show the properties of their constituent substances.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7889554397400256, "g_worst_claim": 0.18101884424686432, "g_content": 1.109125750405448, "g_traj_mean": 0.855959951877594}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 34157, 525, 10526, 32055, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 1