363, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Mixtures can be separated by physical means.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7093336294240276, "g_worst_claim": -0.0806849135292901, "g_content": 0.8777207999393858, "g_traj_mean": 0.8408998847007751}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 5424, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 11868, 510, 12, 1198, 3865, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 624, 12, 29588, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 624, 12, 2009, 32199, 304, 458, 2392, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 382, 13552, 3095, 510, 12, 3719, 9436, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 624, 12, 29588, 32055, 624, 12, 34157, 323, 31146, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 382, 58083, 18513, 510, 12, 362, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 624, 12, 576, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 624, 12, 10392, 466, 862, 1828, 9569, 624, 12, 19219, 18513, 1473, 279, 5888, 315, 74064, 32055, 624, 12, 576, 50620, 646, 387, 6707, 18663, 553, 6961, 5413, 624, 12, 12243, 264, 3890, 18037, 13, 151645], "pred": "Mixtures:\n- A physical combination of elements or compounds.\n- The parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded.\n- Retain their own identity.\n- Mixtures show the properties of constituent substances.\n- The constituents can be easily separated by physical methods.\n- Have a variable composition.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3177528050927048, "g_worst_claim": 0.20222498973210654, "g_content": 1.628790128028999, "g_traj_mean": 1.1237436532974243}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "212", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Here are my answers to the question based on the provided passages:\n\nQ: What are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures?\nA: Based on the passages provided, here are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures:\n\nElements:\n\n* Are the purest form of a chemical substance (Passage 3)\n* Consist of only one type of atom with the same number of protons (Passage 3)\n\nCompounds:\n\n* Are substances composed of two or more different elements (Passage 3)\n* Are also pure substances (Passage 3)\n\nMixtures:\n\n* Contain two or more substances that are relatively easy to separate (Passage 1)\n* Have a variable composition (Passage 2)\n* Show the properties of their constituent substances (Passage 2)\n* Can be separated by physical means (Passage 2)", "pred": "Mixtures do not form new compounds, whereas compounds are formed through chemical bonding between elements. Elements are the purest form and cannot be chemically separated into simpler substances. Mixtures can be easily separated by physical means, while compounds cannot.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Mixtures do not form new compounds, whereas compounds are formed through chemical bonding between elements. Elements are the purest form and cannot be chemically separated into simpler substances. Mixtures can be easily separated by physical means, while compounds cannot.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are as follows:\\n\\n1. Elements are composed of only one type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance.\\n2. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. The elements in a compound are chemically bonded and cannot be separated by physical means.\\n3. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means. Mixtures can have a variable composition and show the properties of their constituent substances.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are as follows:\\nElements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances composed of two or more different elements, where the elements are chemically bonded. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. Elements cannot be separated by physical means, while compounds and mixtures can be separated by physical methods. Mixtures have a variable composition and show the properties of the constituent substances.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are as follows:\\n\\n1. Elements are composed of only one type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance.\\n2. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. They are also pure substances where the elements are chemically bonded.\\n3. Mixtures are formed by physically combining elements or compounds where the parts do not form a new compound and retain their own identity.\\n4. Elements cannot be separated into simpler elements.\\n5. Compounds can be separated into their constituent elements.\\n6. Mixtures can be physically separated into their constituent elements or compounds.\\n7. Elements have a fixed composition.\\n8. Compounds have a variable composition.\\n9. Elements show the properties of only one type of atom.\\n10. Compounds show the properties of all the atoms present.\\n11. Mixtures show the properties of the constituent substances.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are as follows:\\n\\n1. **Elements**:\\n   - Composed of only one type of atom.\\n   - Pure substances where all atoms have the same number of protons.\\n   - Cannot be separated into simpler substances by physical means.\\n\\n2. **Compounds**:\\n   - Substances composed of two or more different elements.\\n   - Pure substances where the elements are chemically bonded together.\\n   - Cannot be separated into simpler substances by physical means.\\n\\n3. **Mixtures**:\\n   - Physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded.\\n   - Variable composition.\\n   - Properties of constituent substances are observable.\\n   - Components can be easily separated by physical methods.\\n\\nMixtures do not form new compounds, whereas compounds are formed through chemical bonding between elements. Elements are the purest form and cannot be chemically separated into simpler substances. Mixtures can be easily separated by physical means, while compounds cannot.\"]", "time_sec": 31.435, "generation_time_seconds": 30.3818, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0348, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 5424, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 34157, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 323, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 624, 17, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 323, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 13, 576, 5424, 304, 264, 23628, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 4157, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 624, 18, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 614, 264, 3890, 18037, 323, 1473, 279, 5888, 315, 862, 74064, 32055, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Elements are composed of only one type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance.\n2. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. The elements in a compound are chemically bonded and cannot be separated by physical means.\n3. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means. Mixtures can have a variable composition and show the properties of their constituent substances.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7889554397400256, "g_worst_claim": 0.18101884424686432, "g_content": 1.109125750405448, "g_traj_mean": 0.855959951877594}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 5424, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 525, 438, 11017, 510, 11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 10526, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 11, 1380, 279, 5424, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 34157, 4157, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 11, 1393, 31146, 323, 6514, 18513, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 5413, 13, 19219, 18513, 614, 264, 3890, 18037, 323, 1473, 279, 5888, 315, 279, 74064, 32055, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are as follows:\nElements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances composed of two or more different elements, where the elements are chemically bonded. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. Elements cannot be separated by physical means, while compounds and mixtures can be separated by physical methods. Mixtures have a variable composition and show the properties of the constituent substances.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7252998429842484, "g_worst_claim": 0.20222498973210654, "g_content": 1.304223077947443, "g_traj_mean": 0.8871556520462036}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 5424, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 34157, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 323, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 624, 17, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 2379, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 1380, 279, 5424, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 624, 18, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 14122, 553, 21893, 34171, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 653, 537, 1352, 264, 501, 23628, 323, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 624, 19, 13, 34157, 4157, 387, 18663, 1119, 34288, 5424, 624, 20, 13, 13317, 3095, 646, 387, 18663, 1119, 862, 74064, 5424, 624, 21, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 387, 21893, 18663, 1119, 862, 74064, 5424, 476, 31146, 624, 22, 13, 34157, 614, 264, 8356, 18037, 624, 23, 13, 13317, 3095, 614, 264, 3890, 18037, 624, 24, 13, 34157, 1473, 279, 5888, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 624, 16, 15, 13, 13317, 3095, 1473, 279, 5888, 315, 678, 279, 32199, 3042, 624, 16, 16, 13, 19219, 18513, 1473, 279, 5888, 315, 279, 74064, 32055, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Elements are composed of only one type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance.\n2. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. They are also pure substances where the elements are chemically bonded.\n3. Mixtures are formed by physically combining elements or compounds where the parts do not form a new compound and retain their own identity.\n4. Elements cannot be separated into simpler elements.\n5. Compounds can be separated into their constituent elements.\n6. Mixtures can be physically separated into their constituent elements or compounds.\n7. Elements have a fixed composition.\n8. Compounds have a variable composition.\n9. Elements show the properties of only one type of atom.\n10. Compounds show the properties of all the atoms present.\n11. Mixtures show the properties of the constituent substances.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5851915834501772, "g_worst_claim": -0.0019324123859405518, "g_content": 0.8345505608452691, "g_traj_mean": 0.6399669051170349}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 5424, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 11868, 334, 510, 256, 481, 1198, 3865, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 624, 256, 481, 29588, 32055, 1380, 678, 32199, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 624, 256, 481, 34655, 387, 18663, 1119, 34288, 32055, 553, 6961, 3363, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 13552, 3095, 334, 510, 256, 481, 3719, 9436, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 624, 256, 481, 29588, 32055, 1380, 279, 5424, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 3786, 624, 256, 481, 34655, 387, 18663, 1119, 34288, 32055, 553, 6961, 3363, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 58083, 18513, 334, 510, 256, 481, 27379, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 624, 256, 481, 12407, 18037, 624, 256, 481, 11831, 315, 74064, 32055, 525, 39535, 624, 256, 481, 34085, 646, 387, 6707, 18663, 553, 6961, 5413, 382, 58083, 18513, 653, 537, 1352, 501, 31146, 11, 19853, 31146, 525, 14122, 1526, 11483, 63086, 1948, 5424, 13, 34157, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 323, 4157, 387, 8424, 2673, 18663, 1119, 34288, 32055, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 387, 6707, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 11, 1393, 31146, 4157, 13, 151645], "pred": "Mixtures do not form new compounds, whereas compounds are formed through chemical bonding between elements. Elements are the purest form and cannot be chemically separated into simpler substances. Mixtures can be easily separated by physical means, while compounds cannot.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7683752770304891, "g_worst_claim": -0.08117043972015381, "g_content": 1.2008084615071615, "g_traj_mean": 0.6