5648, 5557, 624, 18, 13, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1177, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 624, 19, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 21, 13, 57368, 325, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 624, 22, 13, 30841, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 624, 23, 13, 1752, 51396, 13078, 48132, 11, 72639, 27815, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 311, 4057, 279, 48132, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water.\n2. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n3. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\n4. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n5. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n6. Rinse thoroughly with hot water.\n7. Dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n8. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve baking soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes to remove the residue.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6975694844185325, "g_worst_claim": 0.4182094732920329, "g_content": 1.818347651784013, "g_traj_mean": 1.5353578329086304}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 323, 11369, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 17, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 624, 18, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 19, 13, 431, 1330, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 624, 20, 13, 1752, 51396, 13078, 48132, 11, 72639, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 27815, 38862, 304, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 311, 4057, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\n1. Use a small amount of detergent and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n2. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n3. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n4. Rinsing thoroughly with hot water and dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n5. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes to remove any residual wine adhering to the glass.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4065288052382157, "g_worst_claim": 0.13130101561546326, "g_content": 1.9038142903645834, "g_traj_mean": 1.4228694438934326}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 72.13, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "215", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To wash wine glasses properly, start by using hot water and mild detergent to clean the outside of the glass. If there are stubborn wine residues, use baking soda to dissolve them by mixing a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it sit in the glass for a few minutes. For cleaning the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. Rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth. To avoid damage, wash one wine glass at a time, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "pred": "1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n4. Scrub the wine glasses by hand to avoid chips and spots. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. Red wine can leave stains if left overnight, so be cautious to avoid this.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n4. Scrub the wine glasses by hand to avoid chips and spots. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. Red wine can leave stains if left overnight, so be cautious to avoid this.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n4. Clean your wine glasses by hand for the safest method. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n6. Avoid chips and spots by following these tips.\", \"Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use hot water and mild detergent to remove any wine residue.\\n2. Dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes to dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n3. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n4. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n5. To avoid chips and spots, wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage and use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n6. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\", \"Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\n2. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles.\\n\\n3. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\n4. To avoid chips and spots, clean your wine glasses by hand. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n\\n5. To keep soap from flavoring your next glass of wine, use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\", \"Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n4. Scrub the wine glasses by hand to avoid chips and spots. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n6. Red wine can leave stains if left overnight, so be cautious to avoid this.\"]", "time_sec": 38.699, "generation_time_seconds": 37.5769, "selection_time_seconds": 1.113, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 17, 13, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 646, 944, 633, 697, 28147, 4240, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 311, 4057, 894, 51396, 13078, 48132, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 624, 19, 13, 9590, 697, 13078, 28147, 553, 1424, 369, 279, 61744, 1714, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 323, 990, 432, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1177, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 624, 21, 13, 34006, 23595, 323, 18773, 553, 2701, 1493, 10414, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n4. Clean your wine glasses by hand for the safest method. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. Avoid chips and spots by following these tips.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9557432625949056, "g_worst_claim": 0.3309231797854106, "g_content": 2.4134271795099433, "g_traj_mean": 1.9360393285751343}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 311, 4057, 894, 13078, 48132, 624, 17, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 27815, 38862, 304, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 311, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 624, 18, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 19, 13, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 624, 20, 13, 2014, 5648, 23595, 323, 18773, 11, 11369, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 323, 990, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1177, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 624, 21, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Use hot water and mild detergent to remove any wine residue.\n2. Dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes to dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n3. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n4. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n5. To avoid chips and spots, wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage and use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\n6. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5984941775202932, "g_worst_claim": 0.3309231797854106, "g_content": 2.128314929062061, "g_traj_mean": 1.610692024230957}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 646, 1405, 633, 697, 28147, 4240, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 311, 4057, 894, 51396, 13078, 48132, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 382, 17, 13, 2014, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 264, 8991, 11, 990, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 382, 18, 13, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 382, 19, 13, 2014, 5648, 23595, 323, 18773, 11, 4240, 697, 13078, 28147, 553, 1424, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 382, 20, 13, 2014, 2506, 26785, 504, 17172, 287, 697, 1790, 8991, 315, 13078, 11, 990, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 323, 990, 432, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1177, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 13, 151645], "pred": "5. To keep soap from flavoring your next glass of wine, use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.939551524195151, "g_worst_claim": 0.3309231797854106, "g_content": 2.4520480869052648, "g_traj_mean": 1.9596678018569946}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 17, 13, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 646, 1405, 633, 697, 28147, 4240, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 624, 19, 13, 32134, 392, 279, 13078, 28147, 553, 1424, 311, 5648, 23595, 323, 18773, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 323, 990, 432, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1177, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 624, 21, 13, 3731, 13078, 646, 5274, 62463, 421, 2115, 24398, 11, 773, 387, 45778, 311, 5648, 419, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n4. Scrub the wine glasses by hand to avoid chips and spots. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. Red wine can leave stains if left overnight, so be cautious to avoid this.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8989114331251864, "g_worst_claim": 0.3309231797854106, "g_content": 2.3903992798951297, "g_traj_mean": 1.8890358209609985}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.13, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "216", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent cannot remove wine residue, use baking soda to dissolve and loosen the adhesive residue (Passage 1).\n2. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles and rinse thoroughly with hot water (Passage 2).\n3. For hand cleaning, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage (Passage 3). Use a small amount of detergent and only in the bottom of the glass and around the rim to avoid flavoring future wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n4. Clean your wine glasses by hand for the safest method. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. Avoid chips and spots by following these tips.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n4. Clean your wine glasses by hand for the safest method. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. Avoid chips and spots by following these tips.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n4. Clean your wine glasses by hand for the safest method. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n6. Avoid chips and spots by following these tips.\", \"Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n2. Rinse the glass thoroughly with hot water.\\n3. Dry the glass with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n4. Alternatively, if hot water and mild detergent can't get the glasses clean, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n5. If washing by hand is preferred, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n6. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed – in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n7. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\", \"Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly:\\n\\n1. For stubborn wine residues, dissolve baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes to remove any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n2. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n3. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n4. For hand washing, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n5. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n6. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n7. Avoid leaving wine stains overnight, as red wine can leave stains if left overnight.\", \"Based on the given passages, to wash wine glasses properly:\\n\\n1. Use baking soda and hot water to remove stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\n2. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n\\n3. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\n4. If cleaning by hand, follow these tips to avoid chips and spots:\\n   - Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water.\\n   - Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n   - Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n   - Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\"]", "time_sec": 37.725, "generation_time_seconds": 36.8669, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8451, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 17, 13, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 646, 944, 633, 697, 28147, 4240, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 311, 4057, 894, 51396, 13078, 48132, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 624, 19, 13, 9590, 697, 13078, 28147, 553, 1424, 369, 279, 61744, 1714, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 323, 990, 432, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1177, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 624, 21, 13, 34006, 23595, 323, 18773, 553, 2701, 1493, 10414, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n2. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n3. If hot water and mild detergent can't get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n4. Clean your wine glasses by hand for the safest method. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. Avoid chips and spots by following these tips.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9557432625949056, "g_worst_claim": 0.3309231797854106, "g_content": 2.4134271795099433, "g_traj_mean": 1.9360393285751343}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 17, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 8991, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 624, 18, 13, 30841, 279, 8991, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 624, 19, 13, 38478, 11, 421, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 646, 944, 633, 279, 28147, 4240, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 27686, 553, 1424, 374, 14890, 11, 10962, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 13