4, 4362, 1177, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 624, 21, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 624, 22, 13, 34006, 9380, 13078, 62463, 24398, 11, 438, 2518, 13078, 646, 5274, 62463, 421, 2115, 24398, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. For stubborn wine residues, dissolve baking soda in hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes to remove any residual wine adhering to the glass.\n2. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n3. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\n4. For hand washing, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n5. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\n6. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n7. Avoid leaving wine stains overnight, as red wine can leave stains if left overnight.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9096256687780708, "g_worst_claim": 0.4528687397638957, "g_content": 2.17973673712347, "g_traj_mean": 1.715956687927246}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 27815, 38862, 323, 4017, 3015, 311, 4057, 51396, 13078, 48132, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 27815, 38862, 304, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 382, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 382, 18, 13, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 382, 19, 13, 1416, 15826, 553, 1424, 11, 1795, 1493, 10414, 311, 5648, 23595, 323, 18773, 510, 256, 481, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 448, 4017, 3015, 624, 256, 481, 5985, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 256, 481, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 323, 990, 432, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1177, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 624, 256, 481, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 13, 151645], "pred": "4. If cleaning by hand, follow these tips to avoid chips and spots:\n   - Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water.\n   - Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n   - Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\n   - Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.799719590796054, "g_worst_claim": 0.4528687397638957, "g_content": 2.2680986365493463, "g_traj_mean": 1.6994444131851196}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.31, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "221", "question": "how to peel potatoes fast", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Boil the potatoes for about 15 minutes.\n3. Place the potatoes in a bowl of ice water and swish them around for a few seconds.\n4. Remove the potatoes from the water and remove the skin.\n\nAlternatively, you can also try the following method:\n\n1. Cut the potato skin, making a cut all around the potato lengthwise.\n2. Boil the potato in a pot of boiling water.\n3. Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds.\n4. Rub the potato with both hands, and the skin should fall right off.\n\nThese methods should help you peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Place the scored potatoes in a pot of boiling water and boil for about 15 minutes.\n3. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the boiled potatoes in it.\n4. Swish the potatoes in the ice water for a few seconds to cool them down.\n5. Remove the potatoes from the ice water and peel the skin easily.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Place the scored potatoes in a pot of boiling water and boil for about 15 minutes.\n3. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the boiled potatoes in it.\n4. Swish the potatoes in the ice water for a few seconds to cool them down.\n5. Remove the potatoes from the ice water and peel the skin easily.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to peel potatoes fast:\\n\\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\\n2. Place the scored potatoes in a pot of boiling water and boil for about 15 minutes.\\n3. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the boiled potatoes in it.\\n4. Swish the potatoes in the ice water for a few seconds to cool them down.\\n5. Remove the potatoes from the ice water and peel the skin easily.\", \"The easiest way to peel potatoes fast is to follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Cut the potato skin: Make a cut all around the potato, lengthwise. Try to slice only the skin, not the actual potato.\\n2. Boil it: Put the potato in a pot of boiling water.\\n3. Cool it off: Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds. The surface of the potato will shrink, while the center remains hot.\\n4. Remove the skin: Rub the potato with both hands and watch the skin fall right off.\", \"Based on the given passages, to peel potatoes fast, follow these steps:\\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it's cool enough to handle.\\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.\\nThis method allows you to peel the potatoes easily and quickly, making it an efficient way to prepare them for cooking.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to peel potatoes fast:\\n1. Cut the potato skin: Make a cut all around the potato, lengthwise. Try to slice only the skin, not the actual potato.\\n2. Boil it: Put the potato in a pot of boiling water.\\n3. Cool it off: Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds. The surface of the potato will shrink, while the center remains hot.\\n4. Remove the skin: Rub the potato with both hands and watch the skin fall right off.\"]", "time_sec": 24.935, "generation_time_seconds": 24.1176, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8062, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 57112, 34167, 4937, 1447, 16, 13, 18115, 279, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 448, 264, 21430, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 16548, 34167, 304, 264, 3338, 315, 49837, 3015, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 18, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 279, 65085, 34167, 304, 432, 624, 19, 13, 4492, 812, 279, 34167, 304, 279, 9853, 3015, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 311, 7010, 1105, 1495, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 279, 34167, 504, 279, 9853, 3015, 323, 57112, 279, 6787, 6707, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Place the scored potatoes in a pot of boiling water and boil for about 15 minutes.\n3. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the boiled potatoes in it.\n4. Swish the potatoes in the ice water for a few seconds to cool them down.\n5. Remove the potatoes from the ice water and peel the skin easily.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0012846991963023, "g_worst_claim": 0.3727436860402425, "g_content": 1.0862170509670093, "g_traj_mean": 0.8760868310928345}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 29589, 1616, 311, 57112, 34167, 4937, 374, 311, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 19649, 279, 38734, 6787, 25, 7405, 264, 3931, 678, 2163, 279, 38734, 11, 3084, 4482, 13, 9735, 311, 15983, 1172, 279, 6787, 11, 537, 279, 5042, 38734, 624, 17, 13, 2516, 321, 432, 25, 10224, 279, 38734, 304, 264, 3338, 315, 49837, 3015, 624, 18, 13, 23931, 432, 1007, 25, 1818, 13884, 279, 38734, 304, 9853, 3015, 369, 220, 16, 15, 6486, 13, 576, 7329, 315, 279, 38734, 686, 28900, 11, 1393, 279, 4126, 8458, 4017, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 6787, 25, 12839, 279, 38734, 448, 2176, 6078, 323, 3736, 279, 6787, 4399, 1290, 1007, 13, 151645], "pred": "The easiest way to peel potatoes fast is to follow these steps:\n\n1. Cut the potato skin: Make a cut all around the potato, lengthwise. Try to slice only the skin, not the actual potato.\n2. Boil it: Put the potato in a pot of boiling water.\n3. Cool it off: Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds. The surface of the potato will shrink, while the center remains hot.\n4. Remove the skin: Rub the potato with both hands and watch the skin fall right off.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9105856418213862, "g_worst_claim": 1.0136465659508338, "g_content": 2.3936066260704627, "g_traj_mean": 1.676247000694275}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 57112, 34167, 4937, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 3085, 264, 21430, 11, 5456, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 624, 19, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 624, 20, 13, 4492, 812, 432, 2163, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 1101, 3322, 773, 429, 432, 594, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 697, 38734, 504, 279, 3015, 323, 4057, 279, 6787, 624, 1986, 1714, 6147, 498, 311, 57112, 279, 34167, 6707, 323, 6157, 11, 3259, 432, 458, 11050, 1616, 311, 10549, 1105, 369, 17233, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to peel potatoes fast, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it's cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.\nThis method allows you to peel the potatoes easily and quickly, making it an efficient way to prepare them for cooking.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2536700007706163, "g_worst_claim": 0.13309013843536377, "g_content": 1.3245507558186849, "g_traj_mean": 1.2711504697799683}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 57112, 34167, 4937, 510, 16, 13, 19649, 279, 38734, 6787, 25, 7405, 264, 3931, 678, 2163, 279, 38734, 11, 3084, 4482, 13, 9735, 311, 15983, 1172, 279, 6787, 11, 537, 279, 5042, 38734, 624, 17, 13, 2516, 321, 432, 25, 10224, 279, 38734, 304, 264, 3338, 315, 49837, 3015, 624, 18, 13, 23931, 432, 1007, 25, 1818, 13884, 279, 38734, 304, 9853, 3015, 369, 220, 16, 15, 6486, 13, 576, 7329, 315, 279, 38734, 686, 28900, 11, 1393, 279, 4126, 8458, 4017, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 6787, 25, 12839, 279, 38734, 448, 2176, 6078, 323, 3736, 279, 6787, 4399, 1290, 1007, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to peel potatoes fast:\n1. Cut the potato skin: Make a cut all around the potato, lengthwise. Try to slice only the skin, not the actual potato.\n2. Boil it: Put the potato in a pot of boiling water.\n3. Cool it off: Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds. The surface of the potato will shrink, while the center remains hot.\n4. Remove the skin: Rub the potato with both hands and watch the skin fall right off.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7979521123807953, "g_worst_claim": 0.3722909291585286, "g_content": 2.228096756280637, "g_traj_mean": 1.6622697114944458}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "223", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, to fix a lift valve in a toilet, you should follow these steps:\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain.\n4. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n5. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n6. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm closest to the edge.\n8. Use pliers to securely fasten the chain.\n9. Turn the water valve back on.\n10. Test the flush of the toilet and adjust the chain if needed.\n\nNote: The given passages provide step-by-step instructions for fixing a lift valve in a toilet.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n6. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n7. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n8. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n9. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n6. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n7. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n8. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n9. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and removing the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n4. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if needed, and cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n5. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and screw it in tightly if a screw is included.\\n6. Push the lift arm until there is no more give and it is secure, with the other end hanging freely.\\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n9. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n\\nThese steps provide a comprehensive guide on how to fix the lift valve in a toilet, including the necessary steps and precautions to be taken.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n6. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n8. Use pliers to make sure the chain is securely fastened.\\n9. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n10. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n6. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n7. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n8. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n9. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\"]", "time_sec": 43.834, "generation_time_seconds": 42.9492, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8665, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 1128, 748, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 22, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 23, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 16, 15, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 16, 17, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 18, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 20, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 16, 21, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0823258496562436, "g_worst_claim": 0.21261213223139444, "g_content": 2.5520501515221974, "g_traj_mean": 1.8024693727493286}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 323, 17592, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 18, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 323, 18198, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 19, 13, 27196, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 421, 4362, 11, 323, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 323, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 421, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 624, 21, 13, 22950, 279, 11893, 6773, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 11, 448, 279, 1008, 835, 20704, 25580, 624, 22, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 11, 892, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 11, 323, 990, 625, 4813, 311, 5978, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 23, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 382, 9485, 7354, 3410, 264, 15817, 8474, 389, 1246, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 2670, 279, 5871, 7354, 323, 59903, 311, 387, 4429, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps provide a comprehensive guide on how to fix the lift valve in a toilet, including the necessary steps and precautions to be taken.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7732472251919627, "g_worst_claim": 0.07910037040710449, "g_content": 2.4372221423733618, "g_traj_mean": 1.7020008563995361}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 323, 4057, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 18, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 19, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 21, 13, 3197, 498, 2299, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 22, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 11, 892, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 23, 13, 5443, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 279, 8781, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 24, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 16, 15, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n6. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n8. Use pliers to make sure the chain is securely fastened.\n9. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n10. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6000748639556879, "g_worst_claim": 0.21128771702448526, "g_content": 2.2440068408696336, "g_traj_mean": 1.5443463325500488}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 13, 10783, 1128, 748, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 18, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 19, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 20, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 22, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 24, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n6. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n7. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n8. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n9. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9327530957371835, "g_worst_claim": 0.21261213223139444, "g_content": 2.6103071966091123, "g_traj_mean": 1.8617314100265503}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "224", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Fill the tank by turning on the water valve and then flushing the toilet. Adjust the lift chain as needed by moving the metal clip up or down a few links. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n5. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. Make sure it is securely fastened.\n6. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove the remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove the remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n6. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n7. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n8. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n9. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n10. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\", \"Based on the given passages: \\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve and lift chain.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n4. Check the correct operation by flushing the toilet.\\n5. Adjust the lift chain if needed by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n6. Cut off the excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n8. Screw in the included screw tightly.\\n9. Push the lift arm until it is secure.\\n10. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\n11. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush.\\n12. Adjust the chain if the toilet flushes slowly.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to fix the lift valve in a toilet:\\n\\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove the remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n7. When satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n14. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 43.984, "generation_time_seconds": 43.0981, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8764, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 1128, 748, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 22, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 23, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 16, 15, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 16, 17, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 18, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 20, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 16, 21, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0584075526060626, "g_worst_claim": 0.2665452758471171, "g_content": 2.538329109312996, "g_traj_mean": 1.7897526025772095}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 5046, 264, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 13, 10783, 1128, 748, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 18, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 19, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 20, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 22, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 23, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 16, 15, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n6. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n7. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n8. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n9. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n10. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9579163469347087, "g_worst_claim": 0.30482590198516846, "g_content": 2.5896839206501587, "g_traj_mean": 1.8208613395690918}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 25, 715, 16, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 323, 11893, 8781, 624, 18, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 19, 13, 4248, 279, 4396, 5666, 553, 90532, 279, 26214, 624, 20, 13, 27196, 279, 11893, 8781, 421, 4362, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 21, 13, 19649, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 21878, 2718, 624, 22, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 23, 13, 72175, 304, 279, 5230, 21966, 38969, 624, 24, 13, 22950, 279, 11893, 6773, 3080, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 15, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 16, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 279, 18198, 624, 16, 17, 13, 27196, 279, 8781, 421, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages: \n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve and lift chain.\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n4. Check the correct operation by flushing the toilet.\n5. Adjust the lift chain if needed by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n6. Cut off the excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n8. Screw in the included screw tightly.\n9. Push the lift arm until it is secure.\n10. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n11. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush.\n12. Adjust the chain if the toilet flushes slowly.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.047065445333835, "g_worst_claim": 0.2016429901123047, "g_content": 2.690036190257353, "g_traj_mean": 1.6395046710968018}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 1447, 16, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 279, 9664, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 22, 13, 3197, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 23, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 16, 15, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 16, 17, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 18, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 19, 13, 5443, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 20, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 16, 21, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove the remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0840806285273827, "g_worst_claim": 0.30482590198516846, "g_content": 2.547119140625, "g_traj_mean": 1.725998878479004}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 74.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "225", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet before starting the repair (Passage 1).\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms, and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm (Passage 1).\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If necessary, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links (Passage 2).\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm (Passage 3). Secure it using pliers to ensure it is tightly fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test the toilet's flush function. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide instructions on how to fix a specific issue with the lift valve, such as a stuck or leaking valve.", "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove what's left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove what's left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n6. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n8. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n9. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n10. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n11. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n12. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n13. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n14. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Based on the given passages, the steps to fix a lift valve in a toilet are as follows:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove what's left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n7. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and take out any broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if needed. Cut off the excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\\n5. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, securing it tightly.\\n6. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge.\\n7. Use pliers to ensure the chain is securely fastened.\\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush to make sure it operates correctly.\\n9. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 46.15, "generation_time_seconds": 45.2414, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8953, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 1128, 748, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 22, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 23, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 16, 15, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 16, 17, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 18, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 20, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 16, 21, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0584075526060626, "g_worst_claim": 0.2665452758471171, "g_content": 2.538329109312996, "g_traj_mean": 1.7897526025772095}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 5046, 264, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 13, 10783, 1128, 748, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 18, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 19, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 21, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 22, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 24, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 15, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 16, 16, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 17, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 18, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 16, 19, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n6. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n8. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n9. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n10. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n11. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n12. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n13. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n14. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1384312462618107, "g_worst_claim": 0.30482590198516846, "g_content": 2.6504674192334785, "g_traj_mean": 1.846212387084961}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 7354, 311, 5046, 264, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 1128, 594, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 22, 13, 3197, 498, 2299, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 23, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 16, 15, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 16, 17, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 18, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 20, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove what's left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1224000434283177, "g_worst_claim": 0.14561002071087176, "g_content": 2.6447873322860054, "g_traj_mean": 1.7524186372756958}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 323, 1896, 700, 894, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 18, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 19, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 13, 27196, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 421, 4362, 13, 19649, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 21878, 2718, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 11, 40477, 432, 38969, 624, 21, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 11, 892, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 624, 22, 13, 5443, 625, 4813, 311, 5978, 279, 8781, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 23, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 279, 18198, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 26057, 12440, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and take out any broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if needed. Cut off the excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n5. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, securing it tightly.\n6. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge.\n7. Use pliers to ensure the chain is securely fastened.\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush to make sure it operates correctly.\n9. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.701356872041094, "g_worst_claim": 0.2665452758471171, "g_content": 2.5184805326372666, "g_traj_mean": 1.6444042921066284}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "226", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve and any remaining pieces of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install the new flapper valve and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, making sure it is securely fastened.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to test for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the chain as needed to ensure a proper flush. Cut off any excess chain to prevent tangling.\n\nNote: If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n6. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n6. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Based on the given passages, fixing a lift valve in a toilet involves the following steps:\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Connect the new lift chain to the lift arm.\\n5. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n6. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n7. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n8. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\n9. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n10. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n11. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n12. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n13. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n14. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n6. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\", \"Based on the given passages, to fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n7. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm.\\n13. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n14. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n15. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n16. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 46.765, "generation_time_seconds": 45.5131, "selection_time_seconds": 1.2427, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 1128, 748, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 2621