 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n4. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n6. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.808308103110941, "g_worst_claim": 0.4632393519083659, "g_content": 2.420252153950353, "g_traj_mean": 1.7271941900253296}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 1128, 748, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 22, 13, 3197, 498, 3129, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 23, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 16, 15, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 16, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 17, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 18, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 624, 16, 19, 13, 3393, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 382, 2679, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9916411090086534, "g_worst_claim": 0.17333332697550455, "g_content": 2.5773580799932065, "g_traj_mean": 1.7679764032363892}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.2, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "231", "question": "oil stain on concrete driveway", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question \"How do you remove oil stains from a concrete driveway?\"\n\nTo remove oil stains from a concrete driveway, you can use one of the following methods:\n\n1. Oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner (as mentioned in Passage 1).\n2. A commercial-grade cleaner applied with a brush or broom, followed by scrubbing with a pressure washer (as described in Passage 3).\n\nBefore starting the cleaning process, it is recommended to wash away any dirt or debris from the affected area (Passage 2). Additionally, it is important to avoid using high-pressure hoses to clean the stain, as this can push the oil deeper into the pavement (Passage 2).\n\nIt is also noted that the size of the oil spill and the length of time the stain has been present will affect the method of removal (Passage 3). For small and stubborn stains, the poultice method may be effective (Passage 2).", "pred": "3. Apply a commercial-grade cleaner to the oil stain and scrub with a brush or broom. Then add detergent to your pressure washer and begin spraying. Move at an even pace and keep the nozzle at the same distance from the surface of the concrete at all times to ensure that no streaking occurs.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "3. Apply a commercial-grade cleaner to the oil stain and scrub with a brush or broom. Then add detergent to your pressure washer and begin spraying. Move at an even pace and keep the nozzle at the same distance from the surface of the concrete at all times to ensure that no streaking occurs.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, there are several methods to remove oil stains from a concrete driveway. One method involves using a commercial-grade cleaner, scrubbing with a brush or broom, and then adding detergent to a pressure washer to spray the area evenly. Another method involves using a poultice method for fresh or stubborn stains. It is important to clean the area with water before applying any cleaner to remove dirt and debris. High pressure hoses should be avoided as they can push the oil deeper into the pavement.\", \"Based on the given passages, there are several methods to remove oil stains from a concrete driveway. One method involves using a commercial-grade cleaner and scrubbing with a brush or broom. After scrubbing, detergent can be added to a pressure washer and sprayed at an even pace with the nozzle kept at a consistent distance from the surface of the concrete to avoid streaking. Another method mentioned is the poultice method, which can be used for fresh or stubborn oil stains. Additionally, it is advised to clean the affected area with water before applying any cleaning solutions to avoid pushing the oil deeper into the pavement.\", \"Based on the given passages, there are several methods for removing oil stains from a concrete driveway:\\n\\n1. Clean the area with oil stains with water from a hose or bucket. Prior to cleaning the pavement, wash off any dirt and debris that is in the way of the oil stain on your driveway. However, do not use a high pressure hose to clean off the affected area, because you could end up pushing the oil deeper into the pavement.\\n\\n2. If you have an oil stain that is still fresh or if you have a small and stubborn stain, you may want to use the poultice method to get out your stain.\\n\\n3. Apply a commercial-grade cleaner to the oil stain and scrub with a brush or broom. Then add detergent to your pressure washer and begin spraying. Move at an even pace and keep the nozzle at the same distance from the surface of the concrete at all times to ensure that no streaking occurs.\", \"Based on the given passages, there are several methods to remove oil stains from a concrete driveway:\\n\\n1. **Using a poultice method**: For fresh or stubborn oil stains, apply a poultice method to remove the stain. This involves using a commercial-grade cleaner and scrubbing with a brush or broom before adding detergent to a pressure washer and spraying the affected area.\\n\\n2. **Pressure washing**: If the stain is older and more set, apply a commercial-grade cleaner and scrub with a brush or broom. Then, add detergent to your pressure washer and spray the area evenly at a consistent distance from the surface to avoid streaking.\\n\\n3. **Cleaning with water**: Prior to cleaning any oil stains, wash off any dirt and debris. Use a water hose or bucket to clean the affected area, but avoid using a high-pressure hose as it could push the oil deeper into the pavement.\"]", "time_sec": 30.275, "generation_time_seconds": 29.4003, "selection_time_seconds": 0.864, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1052, 525, 3807, 5413, 311, 4057, 5590, 62463, 504, 264, 14175, 52142, 13, 3776, 1714, 17601, 1667, 264, 8353, 40227, 31881, 11, 44901, 7132, 448, 264, 15625, 476, 2896, 316, 11, 323, 1221, 7842, 90134, 311, 264, 7262, 52892, 311, 22899, 279, 3082, 41047, 13, 13293, 1714, 17601, 1667, 264, 16836, 4832, 558, 1714, 369, 7722, 476, 51396, 62463, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 311, 4240, 279, 3082, 448, 3015, 1573, 18950, 894, 31881, 311, 4057, 25284, 323, 33998, 13, 5124, 7262, 95836, 1265, 387, 30790, 438, 807, 646, 4484, 279, 5590, 19117, 1119, 279, 64342, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, there are several methods to remove oil stains from a concrete driveway. One method involves using a commercial-grade cleaner, scrubbing with a brush or broom, and then adding detergent to a pressure washer to spray the area evenly. Another method involves using a poultice method for fresh or stubborn stains. It is important to clean the area with water before applying any cleaner to remove dirt and debris. High pressure hoses should be avoided as they can push the oil 