ational average.\\n\\nOverall, Sausalito has a relatively mild climate with average temperatures and moderate amounts of precipitation, making it a comfortable place to live year-round.\", \"Based on the given passages, the average weather in Sausalito can be summarized as follows:\\n\\n1. Monthly temperature:\\n   - Highest average temperature: September, around 69 degrees.\\n   - Lowest average temperature: December, around 43 degrees.\\n\\n2. Precipitation:\\n   - Annual precipitation: 34 inches.\\n   - Snowfall: 0 inches.\\n   - Days with measurable precipitation: 56 days.\\n\\n3. Sunlight:\\n   - Number of sunny days per year: 256.\\n\\n4. Comfort index:\\n   - Average comfort index: 84 out of 100.\\n   - US average: 54.\\n   - The comfort index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees, with a penalty for days of excessive humidity.\\n\\n5. Pollution and air quality:\\n   - Air quality index: 13% better than the national average.\\n   - Pollution index: 61% worse than the national average.\\n\\nThese details provide a comprehensive view of the average weather conditions in Sausalito, highlighting its warm climate with moderate rainfall and relatively high comfort levels throughout the year.\", \"Based on the given passages, the average weather in Sausalito is characterized by a temperature range. The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito for September is 58 degrees, while the lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito for December is 50 degrees. The monthly precipitation is highest in January with 0 inches. The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average, and the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average. Additionally, Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain per year, with the US average being 39 inches. Snowfall in Sausalito is 0 inches, which is lower than the average US city that gets 26 inches of snow per year. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito, California. The July high is around 69 degrees, and the January low is 43 degrees. The Sperling's comfort index for Sausalito is a 84 out of 100, indicating a more comfortable year-around climate.\"]", "time_sec": 42.01, "generation_time_seconds": 41.2221, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7774, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 5461, 9104, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 11017, 1447, 12, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 304, 6122, 624, 12, 576, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 304, 6652, 624, 12, 576, 1429, 15088, 59950, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 13666, 304, 6058, 448, 220, 15, 14924, 624, 12, 576, 5461, 2274, 3283, 5221, 220, 17, 21, 14924, 315, 11794, 817, 1042, 11, 1393, 328, 79074, 6357, 5221, 220, 15, 14924, 315, 11794, 624, 12, 576, 5461, 2274, 3283, 702, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 11, 1393, 328, 79074, 6357, 702, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 624, 12, 576, 5768, 1550, 374, 2163, 220, 21, 24, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 6058, 3347, 374, 220, 19, 18, 12348, 624, 12, 328, 79074, 6357, 594, 6838, 1922, 374, 220, 23, 19, 700, 315, 220, 16, 15, 15, 11, 892, 374, 220, 18, 15, 3501, 5080, 1091, 279, 2274, 5461, 315, 220, 20, 19, 624, 12, 576, 2274, 5461, 369, 279, 6838, 1922, 374, 220, 20, 19, 624, 12, 576, 1922, 374, 3118, 389, 279, 2790, 1372, 315, 2849, 29071, 2878, 279, 6838, 2088, 315, 220, 22, 15, 12, 23, 15, 12348, 11, 323, 264, 16346, 374, 9251, 369, 2849, 315, 26541, 37093, 13, 151645], "pred": "- The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September.\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 50 degrees in December.\n- The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches.\n- The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year, while Sausalito gets 0 inches of snow.\n- The average US city h