{"id": "240", "question": "how do crab traps work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a crab trap is a large square metal cage with a system of nets inside that allows crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the top. To set the trap, the ends with lead-ins are placed in the water and the crabs are attracted to the free meal offered by the trap. The Alaska Department of Fish and Game recommends using king crab pots that range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights between 2 and 3 feet. Over time, these mechanisms may disable the trap, preventing it from ghost fishing.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, crab traps work similarly to other crustacean pots such as lobster traps, prawn traps, and some minnow traps. They are large metal cages made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The entrances into the traps are narrow slits, and the crabs must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crabs are attracted to the bait inside the traps, and once they enter, they are unable to escape due to the narrow entrances.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, crab traps work similarly to other crustacean pots such as lobster traps, prawn traps, and some minnow traps. They are large metal cages made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The entrances into the traps are narrow slits, and the crabs must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crabs are attracted to the bait inside the traps, and once they enter, they are unable to escape due to the narrow entrances.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\", \"Based on the given passages, crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\", \"Based on the given passages, crab traps work similarly to other crustacean pots such as lobster traps, prawn traps, and some minnow traps. They are large metal cages made of wire or flat metal mesh reinforced with steel bars. The entrances into the traps are narrow slits, and the crabs must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crabs are attracted to the bait inside the traps, and once they enter, they are unable to escape due to the narrow entrances.\", \"Based on the given passages, crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs to enter but not leave. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide with two ends that have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\"]", "time_sec": 25.11, "generation_time_seconds": 24.4271, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6631, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled":