{"id": "243", "question": "how do crab traps work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how crab traps work:\n\nCrab traps are large square structures made of wire or flat metal mesh, with two ends that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. Crabs are attracted to bait inside the pot and must crawl up the leads to reach it, but once they enter, they cannot escape due to the narrow opening. The pot is designed to allow crabs in but not let them out, making it an effective tool for catching crabs.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How do crab traps work?\" is: Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage with a narrow entrance that allows crabs to enter but not exit, making it an effective tool for catching crabs.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter but not exit. Crab pots are large metal cages with nets inside, reinforced with steel bars. The edges of the pot have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, forming a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot, which is the only entrance. Crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food, which is the bait inside the trap. The topless crab trap is recommended for effectiveness.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter but not exit. Crab pots are large metal cages with nets inside, reinforced with steel bars. The edges of the pot have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, forming a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot, which is the only entrance. Crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food, which is the bait inside the trap. The topless crab trap is recommended for effectiveness.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\", \"Based on the given passages, crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter but not exit. Crab pots are large metal cages with nets inside, reinforced with steel bars. The edges of the pot have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, forming a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot, which is the only entrance. Crabs must crawl up the leads to reach their food, which is the bait inside the trap. The topless crab trap is recommended for effectiveness.\", \"Based on the given passages, crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter but not exit. Crab pots are large square traps about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide with lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal, effectively trapping them inside the pot.\", \"Based on the given passages, crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. Some crab pots are large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\"]", "time_sec": 24.06, "generation_time_seconds": 22.8143, "selection_time_seconds": 1.2341, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 59412, 44560, 975, 553, 1667, 264, 1849, 315, 52457, 4766, 264, 3460, 9317, 35360, 1865, 315, 9067, 476, 10063, 9317, 11294, 429, 374, 48580, 448, 9509, 15904, 13, 576, 44560, 525, 6188, 311, 2138, 1560, 3435, 304, 714, 537, 1077, 1105, 700, 13, 576, 59412, 3338, 374, 264, 3460, 9334, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1550, 323, 220, 23, 7541, 6884, 13, 9043, 10335, 614, 2990, 21853, 429, 9210, 1119, 279, 22862, 504, 279, 11067, 323, 5622, 311, 264, 15026, 78030, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1119, 279, 3338, 13, 1096, 78030, 374, 279, 1172, 19809, 1119, 279, 22862, 13, 576, 1560, 3435, 13083, 807, 1969, 45664, 705, 279, 11508, 311, 633, 311, 862, 1910, 15145, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.169273732076474, "g_worst_claim": 0.31723010540008545, "g_content": 3.3986587524414062, "g_traj_mean": 2.567513942718506}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 59412, 44560, 975, 553, 10693, 1560, 3435, 311, 3725, 714, 537, 4869, 13, 74104, 50031, 525, 3460, 9317, 80847, 448, 52457, 4766, 11, 48580, 448, 9509, 15904, 13, 576, 12822, 315, 279, 3338, 614, 2990, 21853, 429, 9210, 1119, 279, 22862, 504, 279, 11067, 323, 5622, 11, 29064, 264, 15026, 78030, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1119, 279, 3338, 11, 892, 374, 279, 1172, 19809, 13, 4553, 3435, 1969, 45664, 705, 279, 