": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 59412, 44560, 975, 553, 1667, 264, 1849, 315, 52457, 4766, 264, 3460, 9317, 35360, 1865, 315, 9067, 476, 10063, 9317, 11294, 429, 374, 48580, 448, 9509, 15904, 13, 576, 44560, 525, 6188, 311, 2138, 1560, 3435, 304, 714, 537, 1077, 1105, 700, 13, 4329, 59412, 50031, 525, 3460, 9334, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1550, 323, 220, 23, 7541, 6884, 13, 9043, 10335, 614, 2990, 21853, 429, 9210, 1119, 279, 22862, 504, 279, 11067, 323, 5622, 311, 264, 15026, 78030, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1119, 279, 3338, 13, 1096, 78030, 374, 279, 1172, 19809, 1119, 279, 22862, 13, 576, 1560, 3435, 13083, 807, 1969, 45664, 705, 279, 11508, 311, 633, 311, 862, 1910, 15145, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. Some crab pots are large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.103439527453463, "g_worst_claim": 0.31723010540008545, "g_content": 3.3414956454573006, "g_traj_mean": 2.506093740463257}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "244", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "The FEHA (Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) have several differences. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Another important difference is the requirement of disability. The ADA requires a physical or mental impairment to substantially limit a major life activity, while the FEHA only requires that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without the need for it to be a substantial limit.", "pred": "1. The FEHA applies to a broader range of employees compared to the ADA, which only applies to employers with four to fifteen employees.\n2. The FEHA does not distinguish between private and public employers, unlike the ADA.\n3. The ADA requires a substantial limitation on a major life activity to qualify as a disability, while the FEHA only requires a limitation on a major life activity, without the substantial limitation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. The FEHA applies to a broader range of employees compared to the ADA, which only applies to employers with four to fifteen employees.\n2. The FEHA does not distinguish between private and public employers, unlike the ADA.\n3. The ADA requires a substantial limitation on a major life activity to qualify as a disability, while the FEHA only requires a limitation on a major life activity, without the substantial limitation.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between FEHA and ADA are:\\n\\n1. Scope of Application:\\n   - FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers.\\n   - The ADA applies to all employers with four to fifteen employees in the private sector.\\n\\n2. Requirements for Disability:\\n   - FEHA requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without a substantial limit requirement.\\n   - Under the ADA, to qualify as a disability, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between FEHA and ADA are:\\n\\n1. ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA affects more employees and applies to both private and public employers without distinction.\\n2. ADA requires a disability to substantially limit a major life activity, whereas FEHA requires a mental and physical disability to limit a major life activity, but not necessarily to substantially limit it.\", \"Based on the given passages, the key differences between the FEHA and ADA are:\\n\\n1. The FEHA applies to a broader range of employees compared to the ADA, which only applies to employers with four to fifteen employees.\\n2. The FEHA does not distinguish between private and public employers, unlike the ADA.\\n3. The ADA requires a substantial limitation on a major life activity to qualify as a disability, while the FEHA only requires a limitation on a major life activity, without the substantial limitation.\"]", "time_sec": 21.247, "generation_time_seconds": 20.3658, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8722, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 19853, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 13, 22406, 11, 27931, 17020, 7460, 264, 27254, 11, 1393, 78325, 7460, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1297132004008574, "g_worst_claim": 0.30797624588012695, "g_content": 1.2145174298967634, "g_traj_mean": 1.2342796325683594}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 525, 1447, 16, 13, 34920, 315, 7323, 510, 256, 481, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 1558, 537, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 624, 256, 481, 576, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 382, 17, 13, 33784, 369, 74268, 510, 256, 481, 27931, 17020, 7460, 1172, 429, 264, 10502, 323, 6961, 27254, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 2041, 264, 11924, 3930, 16287, 624, 256, 481, 9449, 279, 78325, 11, 311, 25384, 438, 264, 27254, 11, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 1969, 31202, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. Requirements for Disability:\n   - FEHA requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without a substantial limit requirement.\n   - Under the ADA, to qualify as a disability, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.251572816363527, "g_worst_claim": 0.36118316650390625, "g_content": 1.351