rs with four to fifteen employees.\n2. The FEHA does not distinguish between private and public employers, unlike the ADA.\n3. The ADA requires a substantial limitation on a major life activity to qualify as a disability, while the FEHA only requires a limitation on a major life activity, without the substantial limitation.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0532812622377816, "g_worst_claim": 0.36118316650390625, "g_content": 1.3012308161309425, "g_traj_mean": 0.9608919620513916}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.41, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "245", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "One difference between FEHA and ADA is that the ADA applies to all private sector employers with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA affects more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like ADA does.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the differences between the FEHA and ADA are as follows:\n\n1. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers.\n2. The ADA requires a substantial limitation on a major life activity to qualify as a disability, whereas the FEHA only requires a limitation on a major life activity, not necessarily a substantial one.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the differences between the FEHA and ADA are as follows:\n\n1. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers.\n2. The ADA requires a substantial limitation on a major life activity to qualify as a disability, whereas the FEHA only requires a limitation on a major life activity, not necessarily a substantial one.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.\", \"Based on the given passages, the primary differences between FEHA and ADA include the following:\\n\\n1. Scope of application: FEHA applies to more employees and includes both private and public employers, while ADA applies only to private employers with four to fifteen employees.\\n\\n2. Requirements for disability: FEHA requires a disability, defined as a physical and mental condition that limits a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.\\n\\nThese differences highlight the distinct provisions each act has for employees with disabilities, emphasizing the broader applicability and different standards of disability under FEHA compared to ADA.\", \"Based on the given passages, the main differences between the FEHA (Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) are:\\n\\n1. FEHA covers a wider range of employees, including those in public and private sectors, while the ADA applies specifically to private employers with four to fifteen employees.\\n2. FEHA requires that a disability must be present, whereas the ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity.\\n3. FEHA does not distinguish between private and public employers, unlike the ADA.\\n4. The FEHA requires only that a disability limits a major life activity, without the need for a substantial limit, as required by the ADA.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between the FEHA and ADA are as follows:\\n\\n1. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers.\\n2. The ADA requires a substantial limitation on a major life activity to qualify as a disability, whereas the FEHA only requires a limitation on a major life activity, not necessarily a substantial one.\"]", "time_sec": 23.423, "generation_time_seconds": 22.6814, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7324, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 19853, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 13, 22406, 11, 27931, 17020, 7460, 264, 27254, 11, 1393, 78325, 7460, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1131589440270966, "g_worst_claim": 0.26484107971191406, "g_content": 1.1863851274762836, "g_traj_mean": 1.2071266174316406}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6028, 11799, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 2924, 279, 2701, 1447, 16, 13, 34920, 315, 3766, 25, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 5646, 2176, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 1393, 78325, 16790, 1172, 311, 869, 22426, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 382, 17, 13, 33784, 369, 27254, 25, 27931, 17020, 7460, 264, 27254, 11, 4512, 438, 264, 6961, 323, 10502, 2971, 429, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 19853, 78325, 7460, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 382, 9485, 11799, 11167, 279, 12460, 19156, 1817, 1160, 702, 369, 8256, 448, 35701, 11, 80903, 279, 26829, 4563, 2897, 323, 2155, 10659, 315, 27254, 1212, 27931, 17020, 7707, 311, 78325, 13, 151645], "pred": "These differences highlight the distinct provisions each act has for employees with disabilities, emphasizing the broader applicability and different standards of disability under FEHA compared to ADA.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8465966862167857, "g_worst_claim": 0.14944742707645192, "g_content": 0.9102425077068272, "g_traj_mean": 0.7854520678520203}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1887, 11799, 1948, 279, 27931, 17020, 320, 60795, 40852, 323, 30333, 3218, 8, 323, 279, 78325, 320, 91686, 448, 97449, 3218, 8, 525, 1447, 16, 13, 27931, 17020, 14521, 264, 21864, 2088, 315, 8256, 11, 2670, 1846, 304, 584, 323, 869, 25512, 11, 1393, 279, 78325, 16790, 11689, 311, 869, 22426, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 624, 17, 13, 27931, 17020, 7460, 429, 264, 27254, 1969, 387, 3042, 11, 19853, 279, 78325, 7460, 429, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 624, 18, 13, 27931, 17020, 1558, 537, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 19836, 279, 78325, 624, 19, 13, 576, 27931, 17020, 7460, 1172, 429, 264, 27254, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 2041, 279, 1184, 369, 264, 11924, 3930, 11, 438, 2567, 553, 279, 78325, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. FEHA covers a wider range of employees, including those in public and private sectors, while the ADA applies specifically to private employers with four to fifteen employees.\n2. FEHA requires that a disability must be present, whereas the ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity.\n3. FEHA does not distinguish between private and public employers, unlike the ADA.\n4. The FEHA requires only that a disability limits a major life activity, without the need for a substantial limit, as required by the ADA.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9023652868333595, "g_worst_claim": 0.14087929328282675, "g_content": 1.1371067745584837, "g_traj_mean": 0.8548765778541565}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 279, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 1393, 279, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 1558, 537, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 624, 17, 13, 576, 78325, 7460, 264, 11924, 20278, 389, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 311, 25384, 438, 264, 27254, 11, 19853, 279, 27931, 17020, 1172, 7460, 264, 20278, 389, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 537, 14312, 264, 11924, 825, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the differences between the FEHA and ADA are as follows:\n\n1. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA applies to more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers.\n2. The ADA requires a substantial limitation on a major life activity to qualify as a disability, whereas the FEHA only requires a limitation on a major life activity, not necessarily a substantial one.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1117625273827827, "g_worst_claim": 0.32492480675379437, "g_content": 1.199342505876408, "g_traj_mean": 1.1232167482376099}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "246", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between the Fair Employment and Housing Act (FEHA) and the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) are:\n\n1. Scope of application: The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.\n2. Definition of disability: The FEHA requires that a disability must limit a major life activity, while the ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity.\n3. Number of employees: The ADA applies to employers with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA has no such requirement.\n\nTherefore, the main difference between FEHA and ADA is the scope of application and the definition of disability.", "pred": "3. Definition of Disability: The ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity, whereas FEHA only requires that a mental or physical disability limits a major life activity, without specifying the degree of limitation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "3. Definition of Disability: The ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity, whereas FEHA only requires that a mental or physical disability limits a major life activity, without specifying the degree of limitation.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between FEHA and ADA include the following:\\n\\n1. **Application Scope**: The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, whereas FEHA affects more employees and doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers as the ADA does.\\n\\n2. **Responsibility for Supervisors and Managers**: FEHA is specifically designed for supervisors and managers to learn the basic provisions of the California's Fair Employment and Housing Act and understand their responsibilities during the reasonable accommodation process.\\n\\n3. **Disability Definition**: Under the ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity to qualify as a disability, whereas FEHA requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without needing a substantial limit.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between the FEHA (Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) include:\\n\\n1. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers.\\n2. The ADA defines a disability as a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only that a disability limit a major life activity without the need for substantial limitation.\\n3. FEHA specifically addresses housing discrimination, while the ADA focuses on employment discrimination and reasonable accommodation processes.\", \"Based on the given passages, the key differences between the FEHA and ADA are as follows:\\n\\n1. Scope of Coverage: The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector, including small businesses with four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA applies to a broader range of employers, including private and public entities, with no specific size requirement.\\n\\n2. Provisions Specificity: The FEHA does not specify which provisions are covered, while the ADA does, making it easier for employers to understand the requirements.\\n\\n3. Definition of Disability: The ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity, whereas FEHA only requires that a mental or physical disability limits a major life activity, without specifying the degree of limitation.\"]", "time_sec": 27.223, "generation_time_seconds": 26.3002, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9128, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 19853, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 13, 22406, 11, 27931, 17020, 7460, 264, 27254, 11, 1393, 78325, 7460, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1131589440270966, "g_worst_claim": 0.26484107971191406, "g_content": 1.1863851274762836, "g_traj_mean": 1.2071266174316406}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 2924, 279, 2701, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 4988, 34920, 95518, 576, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 19853, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 323, 3171, 1405, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 438, 279, 78325, 1558, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 82162, 3147, 369, 61824, 41214, 323, 61434, 95518, 27931, 17020, 374, 11689, 6188, 369, 72951, 323, 19680, 311, 3960, 279, 6770, 19156, 315, 279, 7043, 594, 14588, 40852, 323, 30333, 3218, 323, 3535, 862, 27323, 2337, 279, 13276, 27278, 1882, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 4839, 2897, 19709, 95518, 9449, 279, 78325, 11, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 1969, 31202, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 311, 25384, 438, 264, 27254, 11, 19853, 27931, 17020, 7460, 1172, 429, 264, 10502, 323, 6961, 27254, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 2041, 32821, 264, 11924, 3930, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. **Disability Definition**: Under the ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity to qualify as a disability, whereas FEHA requires only that a mental and physical disability limit a major life activity, without needing a substantial limit.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.35505149283044, "g_worst_claim": 0.3238556186358134, "g_content": 1.752777295234876, "g_traj_mean": 1.4819719791412354}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 279, 27931, 17020, 320, 60795, 40852, 323, 30333, 3218, 8, 323, 279, 78325, 320, 91686, 448, 97449, 3218, 8, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 1393, 279, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 323, 1558, 537, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 624, 17, 13, 576, 78325, 18653, 264, 27254, 438, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 19853, 279, 27931, 17020, 7460, 1172, 429, 264, 27254, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 2041, 279, 1184, 369, 11924, 20278, 624, 18, 13, 27931, 17020, 11689, 14230, 11721, 21240, 11, 1393, 279, 78325, 23497, 389, 14402, 21240, 323, 13276, 27278, 11364, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers.\n2. The ADA defines a disability as a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity, whereas the FEHA requires only that a disability limit a major life activity without the need for substantial limitation.\n3. FEHA specifically addresses housing discrimination, while the ADA focuses on employment discrimination and reasonable accommodation processes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.075636679870839, "g_worst_claim": 0.3238556186358134, "g_content": 1.261875437266791, "g_traj_mean": 1.0262348651885986}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1376, 11799, 1948, 279, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 34920, 315, 55669, 25, 576, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 11, 2670, 2613, 9675, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 19853, 279, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 264, 26829, 2088, 315, 22426, 11, 2670, 869, 323, 584, 14744, 11, 448, 902, 3151, 1379, 16287, 382, 17, 13, 1298, 40015, 28262, 487, 25, 576, 27931, 17020, 1558, 537, 13837, 892, 19156, 525, 9761, 11, 1393, 279, 78325, 1558, 11, 3259, 432, 8661, 369, 22426, 311, 3535, 279, 8502, 382, 18, 13, 19709, 315, 74268, 25, 576, 78325, 7460, 429, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 19853, 27931, 17020, 1172, 7460, 429, 264, 10502, 476, 6961, 27254, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 2041, 37838, 279, 8381, 315, 20278, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. Definition of Disability: The ADA requires that a physical or mental impairment substantially limits a major life activity, whereas FEHA only requires that a mental or physical disability limits a major life activity, without specifying the degree of limitation.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7617512407617855, "g_worst_claim": 0.09883405764897664, "g_content": 0.9020083618164062, "g_traj_mean": 0.7341668605804443}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "248", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nThe main difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to all employers in California, regardless of size or sector, while ADA applies to private employers with 4 to 15 employees and does not cover public employers. Additionally, FEHA has a broader definition of disability, requiring only that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a substantial limitation.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the main differences between the FEHA and ADA are their scope of application and the criteria for defining a disability.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the main differences between the FEHA and ADA are their scope of application and the criteria for defining a disability.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.\", \"Based on the given passages, one difference between FEHA (the Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) is that FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.\", \"Based on the given passages, the key differences between FEHA and ADA are as follows:\\n\\n1. ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA affects more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers.\\n2. FEHA is specifically designed for supervisors and managers to understand their responsibilities during the reasonable accommodation process, indicating a focus on workplace policy compliance.\\n3. Under ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity to be considered a disability, whereas FEHA requires only that a disability limit a major life activity.\", \"The FEHA (Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) differ in several ways:\\n\\n1. **Applicability**: The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, including public employers, and does not distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.\\n\\n2. **Disability Definition**: Under the ADA, a disability is defined as a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity. The FEHA, however, requires only that a disability limit a major life activity, without specifying the level of limitation.\\n\\nBased on the given passages, the main differences between the FEHA and ADA are their scope of application and the criteria for defining a disability.\"]", "time_sec": 21.309, "generation_time_seconds": 20.6653, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6365, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 374, 429, 27931, 17020, 16790, 311, 803, 8256, 323, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 11, 19853, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 13, 22406, 11, 27931, 17020, 7460, 264, 27254, 11, 1393, 78325, 7460, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers, whereas ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability, while ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1345165575158362, "g_worst_claim": 0.3339952826499939, "g_content": 1.2240633283342635, "g_traj_mean": 1.2093100547790527}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 825, 6672, 1948, 27931, 17020, 320, 1782, 14588, 40852, 323, 30333, 3218, 8, 323, 279, 78325, 320, 91686, 448, 97449, 3218, 8, 374, 429, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 11, 323, 432, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 1075, 279, 78325, 1558, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, one difference between FEHA (the Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) is that FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn't distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0893990410698784, "g_worst_claim": 0.4801165262858073, "g_content": 1.5525214153787363, "g_traj_mean": 1.2022713422775269}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1376, 11799, 1948, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 1393, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 323, 3171, 944, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 624, 17, 13, 27931, 17020, 374, 11689, 6188, 369, 72951, 323, 19680, 311, 3535, 862, 27323, 2337, 279, 13276, 27278, 1882, 11, 18860, 264, 5244, 389, 26368, 4842, 8733, 624, 18, 13, 9449, 78325, 11, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 1969, 31202, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 311, 387, 6509, 264, 27254, 11, 19853, 27931, 17020, 7460, 1172, 429, 264, 27254, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while FEHA affects more employees and doesn't distinguish between private and public employers.\n2. FEHA is specifically designed for supervisors and managers to understand their responsibilities during the reasonable accommodation process, indicating a focus on workplace policy compliance.\n3. Under ADA, a physical or mental impairment must substantially limit a major life activity to be considered a disability, whereas FEHA requires only that a disability limit a major life activity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2369619375973397, "g_worst_claim": 0.4794081449508667, "g_content": 1.4839557585169056, "g_traj_mean": 1.2652643918991089}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 27931, 17020, 320, 60795, 40852, 323, 30333, 3218, 8, 323, 279, 78325, 320, 91686, 448, 97449, 3218, 8, 1745, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2164, 415, 2897, 95518, 576, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 19853, 279, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 11, 2670, 584, 22426, 11, 323, 1558, 537, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 1075, 279, 78325, 1558, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 4839, 2897, 19709, 95518, 9449, 279, 78325, 11, 264, 27254, 374, 4512, 438, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 429, 31202, 13388, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 13, 576, 27931, 17020, 11, 4764, 11, 7460, 1172, 429, 264, 27254, 3930, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 2041, 37838, 279, 2188, 315, 20278, 382, 28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1887, 11799, 1948, 279, 27931, 17020, 323, 78325, 525, 862, 6891, 315, 3766, 323, 279, 12890, 369, 26312, 264, 27254, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the main differences between the FEHA and ADA are their scope of application and the criteria for defining a disability.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9755498671222921, "g_worst_claim": 0.11614578420465643, "g_content": 1.2872215906778972, "g_traj_mean": 0.8791884183883667}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 21.21, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "249", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, start by preheating an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse the pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow to stand for 10 minutes. Finally, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Based on the given passages, here's how to grill pork chops:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to grill pork chops:\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n4. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\"]", "time_sec": 26.616, "generation_time_seconds": 25.8755, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7308, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 39058, 35067, 90078, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19212, 11, 6514, 3786, 279, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 37327, 16723, 11, 25298, 40454, 11, 73188, 12570, 34448, 19187, 11, 323, 16205, 17172, 287, 3080, 26364, 10856, 624, 18, 13, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 11, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 624, 19, 13, 3085, 697, 6078, 11, 6245, 279, 41686, 10273, 1119, 279, 13041, 26, 2138, 311, 2498, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3698749072522787, "g_worst_claim": 0.09561812877655029, "g_content": 1.7883120144114775, "g_traj_mean": 1.4409515857696533}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 3