per, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3634561183739777, "g_worst_claim": 0.09561812877655029, "g_content": 1.7812264386345358, "g_traj_mean": 1.4327194690704346}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 88.73, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "250", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat for about 12 minutes per side or until they are no longer pink inside.", "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to grill pork chops:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n3. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n4. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\\n3. Mix seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring in a bowl.\\n4. Rinse the pork chops.\\n5. Sprinkle the spice mixture on both sides of the pork chops.\\n6. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat.\\n7. Allow the pork chops to stand for 10 minutes.\\n8. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\"]", "time_sec": 24.242, "generation_time_seconds": 23.5439, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6879, "record_pr