, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n4. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n5. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat.\n6. Allow the pork chops to stand for 10 minutes.\n7. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2894631108473906, "g_worst_claim": 0.3450189431508382, "g_content": 1.7279851640973771, "g_traj_mean": 1.319379210472107}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 39058, 35067, 90078, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19212, 11, 6514, 3786, 279, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 37327, 16723, 11, 25298, 40454, 11, 73188, 12570, 34448, 19187, 11, 323, 16205, 17172, 287, 3080, 26364, 10856, 624, 18, 13, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 624, 19, 13, 3085, 697, 6078, 11, 6245, 279, 41686, 10273, 1119, 279, 13041, 323, 2138, 432, 311, 2498, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow it to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2592922125801647, "g_worst_claim": 0.10027648011843364, "g_content": 1.82116138233858, "g_traj_mean": 1.3802552223205566}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.61, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "252", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. (Passage 1)\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. (Passage 1)\n3. For Oven-Fried Pork Chops, use stuffing mix for the breading. The pork chops come out tender and juicy. This recipe takes 30 minutes to prepare and 10 minutes to prep. (Passage 2)\n4. To grill pork chops over indirect heat, rinse the chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat for 10 minutes before grilling. Grill the chops until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com, you should preheat the grill, season the pork chops with a spice mixture, and grill them over indirect heat until they are cooked through.", "pred": "1. Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the spice mixture on both sides of the chops.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat.\n5. Allow the pork chops to stand for 10 minutes.\n6. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the spice mixture on both sides of the chops.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat.\n5. Allow the pork chops to stand for 10 minutes.\n6. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the spice mixture on both sides of the chops.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat.\\n5. Allow the pork chops to stand for 10 minutes.\\n6. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow it to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\"]", "time_sec": 27.168, "generation_time_seconds": 26.5307, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6291, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 39058, 35067, 90078, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19212, 11, 6514, 3786, 279, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 37327, 16723, 11, 25298, 40454, 11, 73188, 12570, 34448, 19187, 11, 323, 16205, 17172, 287, 3080, 26364, 10856, 624, 18, 13, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 11, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 624, 19, 13, 3085, 697, 6078, 11, 6245, 279, 41686, 10273, 1119, 279, 13041, 26, 2138, 311, 2498, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3850598360644002, "g_worst_claim": 0.10659712553024292, "g_content": 1.7683744991526884, "g_traj_mean": 1.4546757936477661}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 39058, 35067, 90078, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19212, 11, 6514, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 37327, 16723, 11, 25298, 40454, 11, 73188, 12570, 34448, 19187, 11, 323, 16205, 17172, 287, 3080, 26364, 10856, 624, 18, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 35067, 90078, 323, 84847, 279, 41686, 20980, 389, 2176, 11067, 315, 279, 90078, 624, 19, 13, 3085, 697, 6078, 11, 6245, 279, 41686, 10273, 1119, 279, 13041, 624, 20, 13, 26530, 279, 35067, 90078, 311, 2498, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the spice mixture on both sides of the chops.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat.\n5. Allow the pork chops to stand for 10 minutes.\n6. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.179983628717551, "g_worst_claim": 0.10659712553024292, "g_content": 1.4838110882302988, "g_traj_mean": 1.1467927694320679}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 39058, 35067, 90078, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19212, 11, 6514, 3786, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 37327, 16723, 11, 25298, 40454, 11, 73188, 12570, 34448, 19187, 11, 323, 16205, 17172, 287, 3080, 26364, 10856, 624, 18, 13, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 624, 19, 13, 3085, 697, 6078, 11, 6245, 279, 41686, 10273, 1119, 279, 13041, 323, 2138, 432, 311, 2498, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow it to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2550562376775953, "g_worst_claim": 0.10659712553024292, "g_content": 1.6858637192670036, "g_traj_mean": 1.3660155534744263}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 39058, 35067, 90078, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19212, 11, 6514, 3786, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 37327, 16723, 11, 25298, 40454, 11, 73188, 12570, 34448, 19187, 11, 323, 16205, 17172, 287, 3080, 26364, 10856, 624, 18, 13, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 624, 19, 13, 3085, 697, 6078, 11, 6245, 279, 41686, 10273, 1119, 279, 13041, 26, 2138, 311, 2498, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to grill pork chops, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2907237940009624, "g_worst_claim": 0.10659712553024292, "g_content": 1.6909970676197725, "g_traj_mean": 1.3992141485214233}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "255", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove the cover.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole of the vent.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n6. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning that area as well.\n7. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and remove the lint filter frame for easier access to clean.\n8. This thorough cleaning will help your dryer run efficiently and reduce the risk of house fires.\n\nNote: The information provided in the given passages is sufficient to answer the question.", "pred": "Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, and by removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, allowing a vac nozzle to be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, and by removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, allowing a vac nozzle to be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"Based on the given passages, to clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vacuum nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. It will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\nAdditionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, and by removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, allowing a vac nozzle to be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"To clean the dryer vent, first, locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole of the vent duct. Next, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer. Finally, reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\"]", "time_sec": 37.304, "generation_time_seconds": 36.2401, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0531, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4240, 264, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 624, 49574, 11, 498, 1231, 1366, 311, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 1083, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 11, 2238, 13, 3216, 17592, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 11, 8661, 2615, 311, 57920, 33651, 646, 387, 18163, 11, 323, 264, 9283, 81881, 646, 387, 42478, 304, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 13, 1096, 686, 1083, 1492, 697, 46622, 1598, 438, 29720, 438, 432, 646, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9365059589037235, "g_worst_claim": 0.29501567284266156, "g_content": 2.391640403053977, "g_traj_mean": 1.8766058683395386}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "tok