und the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vacuum nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. It will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9340732433284815, "g_worst_claim": 0.07395359873771667, "g_content": 2.321080525716146, "g_traj_mean": 1.8715579509735107}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4240, 264, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 382, 49574, 11, 2908, 17592, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 15826, 1052, 1083, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 11, 323, 553, 17592, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 11, 8661, 2615, 311, 57920, 33651, 646, 387, 18163, 11, 10693, 264, 9283, 81881, 311, 387, 42478, 304, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 13, 1096, 686, 1083, 1492, 697, 46622, 1598, 438, 29720, 438, 432, 646, 13, 151645], "pred": "Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, and by removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, allowing a vac nozzle to be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.947201250665227, "g_worst_claim": 0.29501567284266156, "g_content": 2.4007919773910986, "g_traj_mean": 1.9043216705322266}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 279, 46622, 10378, 11, 1156, 11, 24523, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 315, 279, 10378, 44239, 13, 9295, 11, 4057, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 13, 17375, 11, 50036, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 13, 151645], "pred": "To clean the dryer vent, first, locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole of the vent duct. Next, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer. Finally, reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8097965317428426, "g_worst_claim": 0.643509308497111, "g_content": 2.3276514689127605, "g_traj_mean": 1.7609015703201294}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "256", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the outside cover on the vent.\n2. Use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.\n3. If possible, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there as well.\n4. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and clean it thoroughly.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to clean a dryer vent:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove it.\\n2. Remove the vent duct if it is not fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Unscrew the vent clamp and slide the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n7. Optionally, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there.\\n8. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and remove the lint filter frame for easier access.\\n9. Use a vacuum nozzle to slip into the area for a more thorough cleaning.\\n10. Ensure that the dryer runs efficiently after cleaning.\", \"Based on the given passages, to clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house. Remove the cover, and the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior. Next, using a dryer vent brush, remove lint from inside the hole. Then, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Using the dryer vent brush, remove lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer. Finally, reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, while cleaning the vents, you may also want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vacuum nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. It will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\"]", "time_sec": 37.115, "generation_time_seconds": 36.2504, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8423, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4240, 264, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 624, 49574, 11, 498, 1231, 1366, 311, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 1083, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 11, 2238, 13, 3216, 17592, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 11, 8661, 2615, 311, 57920, 33651, 646, 387, 18163, 11, 323, 264, 9283, 81881, 646, 387, 42478, 304, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 13, 1096, 686, 1083, 1492, 697, 46622, 1598, 438, 29720, 438, 432, 646, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8765140935757363, "g_worst_claim": 0.21141443649927774, "g_content": 2.3868791984789297, "g_traj_mean": 1.843329668045044}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4240, 264, 46622, 10378, 1447, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 44239, 421, 432, 374, 537, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 5443, 264, 46622, 10378, 15625, 311, 4057, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 61043, 38617, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 14983, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 264, 46622, 10378, 15625, 311, 4057, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 624, 22, 13, 96195, 11, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 624, 23, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 323, 4057, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 369, 8661, 2615, 624, 24, 13, 5443, 264, 28202, 81881, 311, 21134, 1119, 279,