7, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 13, 12091, 279, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 13, 17375, 11, 50036, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 13, 22406, 11, 1393, 15826, 279, 80207, 11, 498, 1231, 1083, 1366, 311, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 1083, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 11, 2238, 13, 3216, 17592, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 11, 8661, 2615, 311, 57920, 33651, 646, 387, 18163, 11, 323, 264, 28202, 81881, 646, 387, 42478, 304, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 13, 1084, 686, 1083, 1492, 697, 46622, 1598, 438, 29720, 438, 432, 646, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, first locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house. Remove the cover, and the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior. Next, using a dryer vent brush, remove lint from inside the hole. Then, remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint. Using the dryer vent brush, remove lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer. Finally, reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, while cleaning the vents, you may also want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vacuum nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. It will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7980322826175208, "g_worst_claim": 0.32216741641362506, "g_content": 2.3996644954091493, "g_traj_mean": 1.8612196445465088}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "257", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the steps to clean a dryer vent based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house (passage 1) and remove it by sliding it out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the exterior (step 2).\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from the hole where the vent connects to the dryer (step 3).\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint (step 4).\n4. Clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the dryer vent brush (step 4).\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall (step 5).\n6. If desired, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean the area around the lint filter (passage 2).\n7. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits in the area around the lint filter frame (passage 2).\n\nNote: Passage 3 provides additional information but does not provide specific instructions for cleaning the dryer vent. Therefore, these steps are based on the information provided in passages 1-2.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to clean dryer vent:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\nAdditionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and the lint filter frame for a more thorough cleaning. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter too.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to clean a dryer vent:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\", \"To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover, ensuring the vent duct slides out if not fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Clean the inside of the hole using a dryer vent brush.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Clean the vent at the back of the dryer using the dryer vent brush.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\nAdditionally, you can clean the bottom front panel of the dryer and the area around the lint filter for thorough cleaning.\"]", "time_sec": 32.213, "generation_time_seconds": 31.6175, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5853, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4240, 264, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 624, 49574, 11, 498, 1231, 1366, 311, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 1083, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 11, 2238, 13, 3216, 17592, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 11, 8661, 2615, 311, 57920, 33651, 646, 387, 18163, 11, 323, 264, 9283, 81881, 646, 387, 42478, 304, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 13, 1096, 686, 1083, 1492, 697, 46622, 1598, 438, 29720, 438, 432, 646, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9229471160960354, "g_worst_claim": 0.23498680194218954, "g_content": 2.410444625700363, "g_traj_mean": 1.8700737953186035}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 4240, 46622, 10378, 1447, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 382, 49574, 11, 2908, 17592, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 2238, 13, 151645], "pred": "Addit