{"id": "280", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "gt": "Based on the given passages, severe osteoporosis refers to a advanced stage of the disease where the bones have weakened significantly, leading to severe bone loss and increased risk of fractures. At this stage, symptoms such as back pain, loss of height, and fractures are more pronounced and frequent. The risk of fractures is particularly high in the spine, hips, and wrists, and can occur even without a fall or injury.\n\nIn summary, severe osteoporosis is characterized by significant bone weakening, heightened risk of fractures, and more pronounced symptoms.", "pred": "Severe osteoporosis can be characterized by symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with a stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, a person with severe osteoporosis is likely to have fractures, most often in the spine or hips (which support the body's weight) or in the wrists from bracing against a fall. Fractures of the spine can happen even without a fall or an injury, as the bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Severe osteoporosis can be characterized by symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with a stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, a person with severe osteoporosis is likely to have fractures, most often in the spine or hips (which support the body's weight) or in the wrists from bracing against a fall. Fractures of the spine can happen even without a fall or an injury, as the bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.", "cot": "[\"Severe osteoporosis can be characterized by symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with a stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, a person with severe osteoporosis is likely to have fractures, most often in the spine or hips (which support the body's weight) or in the wrists from bracing against a fall. Fractures of the spine can happen even without a fall or an injury, as the bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.\", \"Based on the given passages, severe osteoporosis is characterized by symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with a stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, a person with osteoporosis is likely to have fractures, most often in the spine or hips (which support the body's weight) or in the wrists from bracing against a fall. The bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.\", \"Severe osteoporosis is characterized by symptoms that include sudden, severe back pain that worsens when standing or walking, which may provide some relief when lying down. This condition is often accompanied by loss of height over time, stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, a person with severe osteoporosis is at high risk for fractures, particularly in the spine or hips, or in the wrists from bracing against a fall. The progression of bone density loss leads to weakened bones, making them susceptible to compression fractures, even without a fall or injury.\", \"Severe osteoporosis is characterized by severe bone damage that is virtually undetectable until symptoms become apparent. The symptoms of severe osteoporosis include back pain, loss of height over time with a stooped posture, fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones, and a high likelihood of fractures, especially in the spine or hips. Without treatment, these fractures can occur even without a fall or injury, as the bones become so weak that they start to compress.\"]", "time_sec": 23.16, "generation_time_seconds": 22.2874, "selection_time_seconds": 0.856, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1514, 19289, 51268, 88666, 10704, 646, 387, 31871, 553, 13495, 1741, 438, 1182, 6646, 11, 4709, 315, 2608, 916, 882, 448, 264, 42032, 16367, 47278, 11, 323, 77232, 315, 279, 5198, 50213, 68, 11, 85778, 11, 42423, 11, 476, 1008, 24854, 13, 17147, 6380, 11, 264, 1697, 448, 15386, 51268, 88666, 10704, 374, 4363, 311, 614, 77232, 11, 1429, 3545, 304, 279, 34676, 476, 42423, 320, 8206, 1824, 279, 2487, 594, 4680, 8, 476, 304, 279, 85778, 504, 1411, 4527, 2348, 264, 4399, 13, 2869, 531, 1413, 315, 279, 34676, 646, 3537, 1496, 2041, 264, 4399, 476, 458, 10895, 11, 438, 279, 24854, 315, 279, 34676, 3635, 773, 7469, 429, 807, 1191, 311, 24611, 13, 151645], "pred": "Severe osteoporosis can be characterized by symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with a stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, a person with severe osteoporosis is likely to have fractures, most often in the spine or hips (which support the body's weight) or in the wrists from bracing against a fall. Fractures of the spine can happen even without a fall or an injury, as the bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5642794408998288, "g_worst_claim": 0.8699373006820679, "g_content": 2.0170273158861245, "g_traj_mean": 1.5214420557022095}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 15386, 51268, 88666, 10704, 374, 31871, 553, 13495, 1741, 438, 1182, 6646, 11, 4709, 315, 2608, 916, 882, 448, 264, 42032, 16367, 47278, 11, 323, 77232, 315, 279, 5198, 50213, 68, 11, 85778, 11, 42423, 11, 476, 1008, 24854, 13, 17147, 6380, 11, 264, 1697, 448, 51268, 88666, 10704, 374, 4363, 311, 614, 77232, 11, 1429, 3545, 304, 279, 34676, 476, 42423, 320, 8206, 1824, 279, 2487, 594, 4680, 8, 476, 304, 279, 85778, 504, 1411, 4527, 2348, 264, 4399, 13, 576, 24854, 315, 