, 448, 24649, 46399, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin roast in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. \n4. Insert a meat thermometer into the center of the roast and test the meat after cooking.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.803449109963295, "g_worst_claim": 0.08114676674207051, "g_content": 1.0152066040039063, "g_traj_mean": 0.9296513795852661}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 624, 17, 13, 10224, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 624, 18, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 624, 19, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 311, 1779, 279, 5306, 9315, 624, 20, 13, 3197, 279, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 24491, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 624, 21, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n4. Insert a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready.\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9428324679919581, "g_worst_claim": 0.15223564704259238, "g_content": 1.0279254059293377, "g_traj_mean": 1.009437084197998}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "289", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\nPassage 1 states to defrost the roast first and then place it in the oven at 250°F for about an hour. After taking it out, season the roast and turn the oven temperature to 350°F. Cook for 1.5 to 3 hours, depending on the size of the roast, making sure it's cooked all the way through.\n\nPassage 2 provides specific instructions for preparing the roast before cooking. Rub the surface of the frozen pork loin with olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and any desired herbs. Place the roast in a preheated oven at 325°F and determine the cooking time based on the weight of the roast.\n\nPassage 3 suggests starting by preheating the oven to 350°F and then placing the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on a roasting rack. Cook for 20-30 minutes per pound, inserting a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature once cooked. Once the temperature reaches 150°F, remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 30 minutes before slicing and serving.\n\nBased on these passages, the general steps to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven are:\n\n1. Defrost the roast if not already thawed.\n2. Season the roast with salt, pepper, and herbs.\n3. Place the roast in a preheated oven at the appropriate temperature (250°F or 325°F) for the specified time.\n4. Check the internal temperature of the roast using a meat thermometer to ensure it reaches the desired doneness.\n5. Remove the roast from the oven and let it rest for 30 minutes before slicing and serving.", "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan.\n3. Put the pork loin on a roasting rack to ensure even cooking.\n4. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n5. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n6. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready.\n7. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat your oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan.\n3. Put the pork loin on a roasting rack to ensure even cooking.\n4. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n5. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n6. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready.\n7. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin roast in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound, checking the internal temperature with a meat thermometer. Once the internal temperature reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, remove it from the oven, cover with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"Based on the given passages, to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan.\\n3. Put the pork loin on a roasting rack to ensure even cooking.\\n4. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\\n5. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\\n6. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready.\\n7. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\"]", "time_sec": 26.841, "generation_time_seconds": 26.0771, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7533, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 624, 18, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 624, 19, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 624, 20, 13, 3197, 279, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 24491, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 624, 21, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven.\n6. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.91263129694849, "g_worst_claim": 0.08883598446846008, "g_content": 1.0219082302517362, "g_traj_mean": 1.025903344154358}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 855, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 13, 10771, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 11, 13295, 279, 5306, 9315, 448, 264, 13041, 92197, 13, 9646, 279, 5306, 9315, 24491, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 4057, 432, 504, 279, 23387, 11, 3421, 448, 24649, 46399, 11, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin roast in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound, checking the internal temperature with a meat thermometer. Once the internal temperature reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, remove it from the oven, cover with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6627358644899696, "g_worst_claim": 0.05549412965774536, "g_content": 0.8360087530953544, "g_traj_mean": 0.8454494476318