 369, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 979, 807, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 13, 10440, 11, 1414, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 11, 438, 432, 686, 8253, 279, 943, 323, 11639, 315, 64291, 4362, 13, 20861, 11, 2736, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 6629, 279, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 315, 279, 17171, 11, 323, 990, 264, 64291, 448, 279, 8311, 36043, 13, 17375, 11, 3796, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 323, 1779, 429, 279, 15933, 41642, 33682, 1182, 705, 979, 24326, 389, 26, 421, 807, 10962, 10063, 11, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps: first, fertilize at the right time of year, such as at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when they turn green at the beginning of spring. Second, know the type of grass you have, as it will determine the type and frequency of fertilizer needed. Third, perform a pH soil test to measure the alkalinity or acidity of the soil, and use a fertilizer with the appropriate pH. Finally, apply the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern and check that the leaf blades bounce back up when stepped on; if they lay flat, you have over-fertilized.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.210040950647628, "g_worst_claim": 0.4086216290791829, "g_content": 2.105373194960297, "g_traj_mean": 1.3821760416030884}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 22201, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 1042, 25, 434, 85695, 551, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 369, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 979, 279, 16359, 12033, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 624, 17, 13, 14187, 697, 16359, 943, 25, 576, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 686, 8253, 279, 943, 315, 64291, 4362, 323, 1246, 3545, 432, 1265, 387, 9251, 624, 18, 13, 3155, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 25, 1096, 10953, 279, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 315, 279, 17171, 323, 8609, 311, 8253, 279, 36043, 2188, 697, 64291, 1265, 614, 624, 19, 13, 34104, 697, 36025, 25, 1096, 25351, 498, 614, 279, 4396, 3311, 315, 64291, 369, 697, 36025, 1379, 624, 20, 13, 20552, 279, 64291, 25, 25968, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 279, 17171, 2033, 25, 14822, 389, 279, 58990, 13, 1416, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 11, 697, 36025, 374, 304, 1661, 6083, 13, 1416, 432, 56522, 10063, 11, 498, 3003, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Choose the right time of year: Fertilize at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\n2. Know your grass type: The type of grass you have will determine the type of fertilizer needed and how often it should be applied.\n3. Do a pH soil test: This measures the alkalinity or acidity of the soil and helps to determine the pH level your fertilizer should have.\n4. Measure your lawn: This ensures you have the correct amount of fertilizer for your lawn size.\n5. Apply the fertilizer: Pour the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern.\n6. Check the soil response: Step on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, your lawn is in good shape. If it lays flat, you've over-fertilized.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4435985203905046, "g_worst_claim": 0.4086216290791829, "g_content": 1.8893173572628996, "g_traj_mean": 1.306065320968628}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "295", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass is to:\n\n1. Fertilize at the right time of year, which is at the beginning of the growing season, and varies for different types of grasses.\n2. Choose a fertilizer that is suitable for your type of grass and soil pH, as determined by a soil test.\n3. Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, avoiding over-fertilization, which can be determined by checking if the leaf blades bounce back up after being stepped on.", "pred": "5. **Application**: Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern. Step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up, indicating the lawn is fertilized correctly. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "5. **Application**: Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern. Step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up, indicating the lawn is fertilized correctly. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps:\\n\\n1. Timing: Fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\\n2. Type of grass: Know your grass type to determine the appropriate fertilizer and frequency of application.\\n3. Soil pH: Conduct a pH soil test to measure the alkalinity or acidity of the soil, which helps in determining the appropriate pH for your fertilizer.\\n4. Lawn size: Measure your lawn to ensure you have the right amount of fertilizer.\\n5. Application: Pour in the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern.\\n6. Check: Step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up, indicating that the lawn is in good shape. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.\", \"Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass includes:\\n1. Timing: Fertilize at the right time of year, which varies for different types of grasses. For warm season grasses, fertilize when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\\n2. Grass Type: Knowing the type of grass you have will determine the type of fertilizer and the frequency of application.\\n3. Soil pH: Conduct a pH soil test to determine the appropriate pH level for your fertilizer.\\n4. Application Method: Pour in the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern. Step on the turf; if the leaf blade bounces back up, the lawn is in good shape. If it lays flat, you've over-fertilized.\", \"Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass involves several key steps:\\n\\n1. **Timing**: Fertilize at the beginning of the growing season, which is different for various types of grasses. For example, warm season grasses should be fertilized when the grass begins to turn green at the start of spring.\\n\\n2. **Type of Grass**: Knowing the type of grass you have is crucial as it determines the type of fertilizer needed and the frequency of application.\\n\\n3. **Soil pH Test**: Conduct a pH soil test to determine the soil's alkalinity or acidity. This step helps in choosing the correct pH for the fertilizer.\\n\\n4. **Lawn Measurement**: Measure the size of your lawn to ensure you have the right amount of fertilizer for its area.\\n\\n5. **Application**: Apply the fertilizer by pouring it on the lawn and following a perpendicular pattern. \\n\\n6. **Checking Fertilizer Application**: After application, check the grass by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back, it indicates that the lawn is in good shape. If it stays flat, it suggests over-fertilization.\", \"Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass involves several key steps:\\n\\n1. **Timing**: Fertilize at the beginning of the growing season, which varies depending on the type of grass. Warm season grasses should be fertilized when they begin to turn green in the spring.\\n\\n2. **Type of Grass**: The type of grass you have determines the type of fertilizer needed and how often you need to fertilize.\\n\\n3. **Soil pH**: Conduct a pH soil test to determine the acidity or alkalinity of the soil. This will help you choose a fertilizer with the correct pH level.\\n\\n4. **Lawn Measurement**: Measure the size of your lawn to determine the amount of fertilizer needed.\\n\\n5. **Application**: Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern. Step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up, indicating the lawn is fertilized correctly. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.\"]", "time_sec": 36.36, "generation_time_seconds": 35.4733, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8767, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 70813, 25, 434, 85695, 551, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 1042, 11, 11689, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 369, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 979, 279, 16359, 12033, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 624, 17, 13, 3990, 315, 16359, 25, 14187, 697, 16359, 943, 311, 8253, 279, 8311, 64291, 323, 11639, 315, 3766, 624, 18, 13, 75519, 36043, 25, 49835, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 6629, 279, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 315, 279, 17171, 11, 892, 8609, 304, 25597, 279, 8311, 36043, 369, 697, 64291, 624, 19, 13, 68392, 1379, 25, 34104, 697, 36025, 311, 5978, 498, 614, 279, 1290, 3311, 315, 64291, 624, 20, 13, 7323, 25, 25968, 304, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 25, 14822, 389, 279, 58990, 311, 1779, 421, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 11, 18860, 429, 279, 36025, 374, 304, 1661, 6083, 13, 1416, 432, 56522, 10063, 11, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Timing: Fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\n2. Type of grass: Know your grass type to determine the appropriate fertilizer and frequency of application.\n3. Soil pH: Conduct a pH soil test to measure the alkalinity or acidity of the soil, which helps in determining the appropriate pH for your fertilizer.\n4. Lawn size: Measure your lawn to ensure you have the right amount of fertilizer.\n5. Application: Pour in the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern.\n6. Check: Step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up, indicating that the lawn is in good shape. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.480807776159189, "g_worst_claim": 0.4426770607630412, "g_content": 2.0581505435636673, "g_traj_mean": 1.4625823497772217}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 5646, 510, 16, 13, 70813, 25, 434, 85695, 551, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 1042, 11, 892, 34227, 369, 2155, 4494, 315, 16359, 288, 13, 1752, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 11, 35114, 551, 979, 279, 16359, 12033, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 624, 17, 13, 39946, 3990, 25, 57633, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 686, 8253, 279, 943, 315, 64291, 323, 279, 11639, 315, 3766, 624, 18, 13, 75519, 36043, 25, 49835, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 8253, 279, 8311, 36043, 2188, 369, 697, 64291, 624, 19, 13, 7323, 6730, 25, 25968, 304, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 13, 14822, 389, 279, 58990, 26, 421, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 11, 279, 36025, 374, 304, 1661, 6083, 13, 1416, 432, 56522, 10063, 11, 498, 3003, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass includes:\n1. Timing: Fertilize at the right time of year, which varies for different types of grasses. For warm season grasses, fertilize when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\n2. Grass Type: Knowing the type of grass you have will determine the type of fertilizer and the frequency of application.\n3. Soil pH: Conduct a pH soil test to determine the appropriate pH level for your fertilizer.\n4. Application Method: Pour in the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern. Step on the turf; if the leaf blade bounces back up, the lawn is in good shape. If it lays flat, you've over-fertilized.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5396702621223375, "g_worst_claim": 0.4426770607630412, "g_content": 1.8979686792346016, "g_traj_mean": 1.3797762393951416}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 3807, 1376, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 62805, 95518, 434, 85695, 551, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 11, 892, 374, 2155, 369, 5257, 4494, 315, 16359, 288, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 1265, 387, 35114, 1506, 979, 279, 16359, 12033, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 1191, 315, 10464, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 929, 315, 39946, 95518, 57633, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 374, 16587, 438, 432, 26569, 279, 943, 315, 64291, 4362, 323, 279, 11639, 315, 3766, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 4416, 321, 36043, 3393, 95518, 49835, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 8253, 279, 17171, 594, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 13, 1096, 3019, 8609, 304, 18774, 279, 4396, 36043, 369, 279, 64291, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 43, 6379, 54240, 95518, 34104, 279, 1379, 315, 697, 36025, 311, 5978, 498, 614, 279, 1290, 3311, 315, 64291, 369, 1181, 3082, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 4988, 95518, 20552, 279, 64291, 553, 50413, 432, 389, 279, 36025, 323, 2701, 264, 76833, 5383, 13, 4710, 21, 13, 3070, 40129, 434, 85695, 3135, 7323, 95518, 4636, 3766, 11, 1779, 279, 16359, 553, 35467, 389, 279, 58990, 13, 1416, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 11, 432, 14807, 429, 279, 36025, 374, 304, 1661, 6083, 13, 1416, 432, 26558, 10063, 11, 432, 13230, 916, 2220, 85695, 2022, 13, 151645], "pred": "6. **Checking Fertilizer Application**: After application, check the grass by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back, it indicates that the lawn is in good shape. If it stays flat, it suggests over-fertilization.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1127558871472518, "g_worst_claim": 0.22985153198242186, "g_content": 1.540138614987864, "g_traj_mean": 1.0273929834365845}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 3807, 1376, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 62805, 95518, 434, 85695, 551, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 11, 892, 34227, 11649, 389, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 13, 45763, 3200, 16359, 288, 1265, 387, 35114, 1506, 979, 807, 3161, 311, 2484, 6176, 304, 279, 10464, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 929, 315, 39946, 95518, 576, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 26569, 279, 943, 315, 64291, 4362, 323, 1246, 3545, 498, 1184, 311, 35114, 551, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 4416, 321, 36043, 95518, 49835, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 8253, 279, 96926, 476, 65687, 13489, 315, 279, 17171, 13, 1096, 686, 1492, 498, 5157, 264, 64291, 448, 279, 4396, 36043, 2188, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 43, 6379, 54240, 95518, 34104, 279, 1379, 315, 697, 36025, 311, 8253, 279, 3311, 315, 64291, 4362, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 4988, 95518, 20552, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 13, 14822, 389, 279, 58990, 311, 1779, 421, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 11, 18860, 279, 36025, 374, 35114, 1506, 12440, 13, 1416, 432, 56522, 10063, 11, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 13, 151645], "pred": "5. **Application**: Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern. Step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up, indicating the lawn is fertilized correctly. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0663838740450078, "g_worst_claim": 0.2839069565137227, "g_content": 1.5373943811175468, "g_traj_mean": 1