{"id": "296", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "gt": "Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight, due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher, which can have a large amount of kinetic energy due to its fast velocity. Examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy, which is the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy. Other activities like a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit also involve potential and kinetic energy.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's position or height, such as a satellite in orbit, and examples of kinetic energy include an object's motion, such as a car moving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's position or height, such as a satellite in orbit, and examples of kinetic energy include an object's motion, such as a car moving.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a satellite in orbit. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and rides in an amusement park.\", \"Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy (stored in an object due to its vertical position or height) and elastic potential energy (not mentioned but implied as a form of potential energy). Examples of kinetic energy include the kinetic energy of an object in motion (such as an airplane in flight, a baseball in motion, a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit).\", \"Based on the given passages, examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its small mass but fast velocity. Examples of potential energy are not explicitly provided in the passages.\", \"Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's position or height, such as a satellite in orbit, and examples of kinetic energy include an object's motion, such as a car moving.\"]", "time_sec": 15.985, "generation_time_seconds": 15.0517, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9229, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10295, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 25311, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 264, 2487, 49226, 553, 1181, 11379, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 323, 31227, 304, 458, 61368, 6118, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a satellite in orbit. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and rides in an amusement park.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.433571594102042, "g_worst_claim": 0.10212781031926473, "g_content": 1.6577479771205357, "g_traj_mean": 1.3287544250488281}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10295, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 69919, 4650, 4802, 320, 71249, 304, 458, 1633, 4152, 311, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 8, 323, 35473, 4650, 4802, 320, 1921, 9733, 714, 6131, 438, 264, 1352, 315, 4650, 4802, 568, 25311, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 279, 70323, 4802, 315, 458, 1633, 304, 11379, 320, 20805, 438, 458, 42924, 304, 10971, 11, 264, 19507, 304, 11379, 11, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 31227, 304, 458, 61368, 6118, 11, 323, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 568, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy (stored in an object due to its vertical position or height) and elastic potential energy (not mentioned but implied as a form of potential energy). Examples of kinetic energy include the kinetic energy of an object in motion (such as an airplane in flight, a baseball in motion, a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit).", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.262554763067643, "g_worst_claim": 0.10212781031926473, "g_content": 1.2242542188994738, "g_traj_mean": 1.0251903533935547}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10295, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 458, 42924, 304, 10971, 4152, 311, 1181, 3460, 3072, 323, 4937, 15435, 11, 323, 264, 19507, 14989, 553, 264, 40970, 4152, 311, 1181, 2613, 3072, 714, 4937, 15435, 13, 25311, 315, 4650, 4802, 525, 537, 20975, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its small mass but fast velocity. Examples of potential energy are not explicitly provided in the passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8453417023022969, "g_worst_claim": 0.10212781031926473, "g_content": 1.482536724635533, "g_traj_mean": 1.0364576578140259}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10295, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 458, 1633, 594, 2309, 476, 2608, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 11, 323, 10295, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 458, 1633, 594, 11379, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 1803, 7218, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's position or height, such as a satellite in orbit, and examples of kinetic energy include an object's motion, such as a car moving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6005978365739186, "g_worst_claim": 0.10493843754132588, "g_content": 0.9525936126708985, "g_traj_mean": 0.6251027584075928}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "297", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's gravitational potential energy due to its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy stored in objects due to their deformation. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane's kinetic energy in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, a baseball's kinetic energy due to its fast velocity despite its small mass, and the kinetic energy possessed by objects in motion such as cars, balls, rivers, athletes, amusement park rides, and satellites in orbit.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include:\n1. The energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height, such as a satellite in orbit or an athlete running.\n2. The energy stored in an object as a result of compression or stretching, such as a ball being compressed or stretched.\nExamples of kinetic energy include:\n1. The energy possessed by an object due to its motion, such as an airplane in flight or a baseball thrown by a pitcher.\n2. The energy possessed by an object due to its velocity, such as a car moving or a river flowing.\nSpecific examples provided in the passages are:\n1. An airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity.\n2. A baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its small mass and fast velocity.\n3. A satellite in orbit due to its height and gravitational potential energy.\n4. A ball in a compressed state due to its elastic potential energy.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include:\n1. The energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height, such as a satellite in orbit or an athlete running.\n2. The energy stored in an object as a result of compression or stretching, such as a ball being compressed or stretched.\nExamples of kinetic energy include:\n1. The energy possessed by an object due to its motion, such as an airplane in flight or a baseball thrown by a pitcher.\n2. The energy possessed by an object due to its velocity, such as a car moving or a river flowing.\nSpecific examples provided in the passages are:\n1. An airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity.\n2. A baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its small mass and fast velocity.\n3. A satellite in orbit due to its height and gravitational potential energy.\n4. A ball in a compressed state due to its elastic potential energy.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a satellite in orbit. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and rides in an amusement park.\", \"Based on the given passages, examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its fast velocity. Examples of potential energy include a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit. Gravitational potential energy is the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height.\", \"Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include:\\n1. The energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height, such as a satellite in orbit or an athlete running.\\n2. The energy stored in an object as a result of compression or stretching, such as a ball being compressed or stretched.\\nExamples of kinetic energy include:\\n1. The energy possessed by an object due to its motion, such as an airplane in flight or a baseball thrown by a pitcher.\\n2. The energy possessed by an object due to its velocity, such as a car moving or a river flowing.\\nSpecific examples provided in the passages are:\\n1. An airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity.\\n2. A baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its small mass and fast velocity.\\n3. A satellite in orbit due to its height and gravitational potential energy.\\n4. A ball in a compressed state due to its elastic potential energy.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\nExamples of kinetic energy include:\\n1. An airplane with large mass and fast velocity.\\n2. A baseball thrown by a pitcher with small mass and fast velocity.\\n3. An athlete running or riding in an amusement park.\\n4. A satellite in orbit.\\n\\nExamples of potential energy include:\\n1. The energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height.\\n2. The energy of a car, a ball rolling, a river flowing, and other activities seen in everyday life.\\n3. The energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height (specifically mentioned in the third passage).\"]", "time_sec": 25.257, "generation_time_seconds": 24.1589, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0834, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10295, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 25311, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 264, 2487, 49226, 553, 1181, 11379, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 323, 31227, 304, 458, 61368, 6118, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a satellite in orbit. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and rides in an amusement park.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.433571594102042, "g_worst_claim": 0.10212781031926473, "g_content": 1.6577479771205357, "g_traj_mean": 1.3287544250488281}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10295, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 458, 42924, 304, 10971, 4152, 311, 1181, 3460, 3072, 323, 4937, 15435, 11, 323, 264, 19507, 14989, 553, 264, 40970, 4152, 311, 1181, 4937, 15435, 13, 25311, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 31227, 304, 458, 61368, 6118, 11, 323, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 2825, 43110, 1663, 4650, 4802, 374, 279, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its fast velocity. Examples of potential energy include a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit. Gravitational potential energy is the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.666859395210374, "g_worst_claim": 0.10212781031926473, "g_content": 2.142703766518451, "g_traj_mean": 1.5173238515853882}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10295, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 510, 16, 13, 576, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 4152, 311, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 476, 458, 33780, 4303, 624, 17, 13, 576, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 264, 1102, 315, 25111, 476, 41849, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 4935, 1660, 30649, 476, 40298, 624, 40381, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 510, 16, 13, 576, 4802, 42790, 553, 458, 1633, 4152, 311, 1181, 11379, 11, 1741, 438, 458, 42924, 304, 10971, 476, 264, 19507, 14989, 553, 264, 40970, 624, 17, 13, 576, 4802, 42790, 553, 45