{"id": "298", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is needed. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring hot water is always available. Alternatively, recirculating pumps can be used to rapidly pull hot water from a water heater, while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. These systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor. However, it should be noted that heat loss from the pipes can occur, requiring the water heater to use more fuel.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate hot water, the following steps can be taken:\n1. Install a hot water circulation pump.\n2. Connect the pump to the water heater and the pipes in the house.\n3. Set up a continuous loop of water through the water heater as described in passage 2.\n4. Utilize the demand systems described in passage 3, such as a push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to control the circulation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate hot water, the following steps can be taken:\n1. Install a hot water circulation pump.\n2. Connect the pump to the water heater and the pipes in the house.\n3. Set up a continuous loop of water through the water heater as described in passage 2.\n4. Utilize the demand systems described in passage 3, such as a push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to control the circulation.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, use a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate hot water, the following steps can be taken:\\n1. Install a hot water circulation pump.\\n2. Connect the pump to the water heater and the pipes in the house.\\n3. Set up a continuous loop of water through the water heater as described in passage 2.\\n4. Utilize the demand systems described in passage 3, such as a push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to control the circulation.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a recirculating pump is used. This pump rapidly pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. This continuous circulation ensures that hot water is always available when needed.\"]", "time_sec": 17.763, "generation_time_seconds": 16.9231, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8288, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based 