{"id": "299", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump can be installed. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, while simultaneously pulling hot water from the heater to keep it hot. This continuous loop ensures that hot water is always available.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a pump is used to send cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This pump circulates the water through the water heater to ensure that hot water is always available. The pump works in a continuous loop, pulling hot water from the water heater and sending cool water back to be reheated and reused.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a pump is used to send cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This pump circulates the water through the water heater to ensure that hot water is always available. The pump works in a continuous loop, pulling hot water from the water heater and sending cool water back to be reheated and reused.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, one can use a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate:\\n\\n1. Install a hot water circulation pump.\\n2. Connect the pump to the water heater and the house plumbing.\\n3. Set up a return line that sends cool water back to the water heater.\\n4. Configure the demand system to either be manually controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor, or allow it to operate automatically.\\n5. Ensure the pump is powered and running continuously to maintain the circulation of water through the heater and the pipes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a pump is used to send cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This pump circulates the water through the water heater to ensure that hot water is always available. The pump works in a continuous loop, pulling hot water from the water heater and sending cool water back to be reheated and reused.\"]", "time_sec": 20.354, "generation_time_seconds": 19.1875, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1431, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3211936359831449, "g_worst_claim": 0.3176218668619792, "g_content": 1.4643227181783536, "g_traj_mean": 1.4267462491989136}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 825, 646, 990, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 504, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, one can use a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water from the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.129492001855555, "g_worst_claim": 0.3176218668619792, "g_content": 1.482333047049386, "g_traj_mean": 1.270094871520996}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 1447, 16, 13, 19242, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 624, 17, 13, 13015, 279, 13834, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 323, 279, 3753, 43188, 624, 18, 13, 2573, 705, 264, 470, 1555, 429, 21308, 7010, 3015, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 624, 19, 13, 22169, 279, 7479, 1849, 311, 2987, 387, 20083, 14071, 553, 279, 4484, 315, 264, 3137, 11, 264, 9021, 11, 476, 264, 11379, 12002, 11, 476, 2138, 432, 311, 14476, 9463, 624, 20, 13, 29279, 279, 13834, 374, 22333, 323, 4303, 30878, 311, 10306, 279, 34755, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 42238, 323, 279, 31175, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Install a hot water circulation pump.\n2. Connect the pump to 