{"id": "303", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"how to make hot water heater circulate\":\n\nA hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate water through the hot water heater and ensure that hot water is always available. The pump sends cooled water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line and circulates it through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to activate the pump and circulate the water.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, one can use a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, one can use a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"Based on the given passages, a hot water heater can circulate hot water through a recirculating pump. This pump rapidly pulls hot water from the heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.\", \"Based on the given passages, a hot water heater can circulate hot water by using a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available. Additionally, recirculating pumps can rapidly pull hot water from a water heater while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, one can use a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\"]", "time_sec": 19.017, "generation_time_seconds": 18.0696, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9365, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2586977891542812, "g_worst_claim": 0.22356408834457397, "g_content": 1.4016473351455316, "g_traj_mean": 1.394892930984497}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 646, 4225, 6334, 4017, 3015, 1526, 264, 1395, 2437, 15486, 13834, 13, 1096, 13834, 18512, 33045, 4017, 3015, 504, 279, 42238, 323, 24303, 21308, 7010, 3015, 504, 279, 4017, 3015, 5128, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 311, 387, 47206, 657, 323, 68743, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, a hot water heater can circulate hot water through a recirculating pump. This pump rapidly pulls hot water from the heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9634986801814008, "g_worst_claim": 0.22356408834457397, "g_content": 1.4745967864990235, "g_traj_mean": 1.2400416135787964}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 646, 4225, 6334, 4017, 3015, 553, 1667, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 22406, 11, 1395, 2437, 15486, 42775, 646, 18512, 6815, 4017, 3015, 504, 264, 3015, 42238, 1393, 24303, 11628, 7010, 3015, 504, 279, 4017, 3015, 5128, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 311, 387, 47206, 657, 323, 68743, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, a hot water heater can circulate hot water by using a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available. Additionally, recirculating pumps can rapidly pull hot water from a water heater while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3069282719807203, "g_worst_claim": 0.22356408834457397, "g_content": 1.7635289972478694, "g_traj_mean": 1.5675082206726074}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 825, 646, 990, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 362, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make a hot water heater circulate, one can use a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2975887352994324, "g_worst_claim": 0.22356408834457397, "g_content": 1.537372044154576, "g_traj_mean": 1.5036307573318481}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 71.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "304", "question": "what causes watermelons to explode", "gt": "Watermelons can explode due to external pressure, such as when a bunch of rubber bands are placed around the middle of the watermelon, causing potential energy to build up and eventually cause the watermelon to explode. Another cause of watermelon explosions is the buildup of gas inside the watermelon due to rotting. This increases the internal pressure and when the skin of the watermelon can no longer hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the watermelon explodes due to the increase in gas pressure as the watermelon decomposes inside. The gas will try to escape, but as it builds up slowly, the pressure increases. When the skin of the watermelon is no longer strong enough to contain the gas, it explodes, often spraying nearby surfaces with decomposed watermelon.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the watermelon explodes due to the increase in gas pressure as the watermelon decomposes inside. The gas will try to escape, but as it builds up slowly, the pressure increases. When the skin of the watermelon is no longer strong enough to contain the gas, it explodes, often spraying nearby surfaces with decomposed watermelon.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, watermelons explode due to the build-up of gas inside the watermelon as it rots. The gas pressure increases over time, eventually becoming too strong for the watermelon's skin to contain. When the skin is no longer able to withstand the pressure, the watermelon explodes, often spraying nearby surfaces with the contents of the watermelon.\", \"Based on the given passages, watermelons explode due to the build-up of internal pressure caused by the decomposition of the watermelon. As the watermelon decays, the gases produced by decomposition increase the pressure inside the watermelon. When the skin of the watermelon becomes weak enough to no longer withstand the increasing internal pressure, it bursts, often spraying nearby surfaces with the decaying contents of the watermelon.\", \"Based on the given passages, the watermelon explodes due to an increase in pressure from gas buildup inside the watermelon. As the watermelon rotting in the water leads to the production of gases, the internal pressure builds up. When the skin of the watermelon can no longer withstand this pressure, the watermelon explodes. The rubber bands mentioned in one of the passages serve as an analogy for potential energy being stored and eventually released, but they are not directly related to the cause of the watermelon explosion as described in the given passages.\", \"Based on the given passages, the watermelon explodes due to the increase in gas pressure as the watermelon decomposes inside. The gas will try to escape, but as it builds up slowly, the pressure increases. When the skin of the watermelon is no longer strong enough to contain the gas, it explodes, often spraying nearby surfaces with decomposed watermelon.\"]", "time_sec": 19.284, "generation_time_seconds": 18.5187, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7552, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3015, 27127, 2382, 15758, 4152, 311, 279, 1936, 5239, 315, 6819, 4766, 279, 3015, 71118, 438, 432, 926, 2576, 13, 576, 6819, 7262, 12703, 916, 882, 11, 9583, 10454, 2238, 3746, 369, 279, 3015, 71118, 594, 6787, 311, 6644, 13, 3197, 279, 6787, 374, 902, 5021, 2952, 311, 50471, 279, 7262, 11, 279, 3015, 71118, 93913, 11, 3545, 82536, 14046, 26431, 448, 279, 8794, 315, 279, 3015, 71118, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, watermelons explode due to the build-up of gas inside the watermelon as it rots. The gas pressure increases over time, eventually becoming too strong for the watermelon's skin to contain. When the skin is no longer able to withstand the pressure, the watermelon explodes, often spraying nearby surfaces with the contents of the watermelon.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.75795671868736, "g_worst_claim": 0.3367501497268677, "g_content": 1.4883081708635604, "g_traj_mean": 0.877232015132904}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3015, 27127, 2382, 15758, 4152, 311, 279, 1936, 5239, 315, 5306, 7262, 8881, 553, 279, 65166, 315, 279, 3015, 71118, 13, 1634, 279, 3015, 71118, 1622, 942, 11, 279, 44512, 8947, 553, 65166, 5263, 279, 7262, 4766, 279, 3015, 71118, 13, 3197, 279, 6787, 315, 279, 3015, 71118, 9044, 7469, 3322, 311, 902, 5021, 50471, 279, 7703, 5306, 7262, 11, 432, 65701, 11, 3545, 82536, 14046, 26431, 448, 279, 1622, 17270, 8794, 315, 279, 3015, 71118, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, watermelons explode due to the build-up of internal pressure caused by the decomposition of the watermelon. As the watermelon decays, the gases produced by decomposition increase the pressure inside the watermelon. When the skin of the watermelon becomes weak enough to no longer withstand the increasing internal pressure, it bursts, often spraying nearby surfaces with the decaying contents of the watermelon.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6991203392343329, "g_worst_claim": 0.11220506521371695, "g_content": 1.4596299391526442, "g_traj_mean": 0.7522148489952087}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 3015, 71118, 93913, 4152, 311, 458, 5263, 304, 7262, 504, 6819, 85665, 4766, 279, 3015, 71118, 13, 1634, 279, 3015, 71118, 5749, 1280, 304, 279, 3015, 11508, 311, 279, 5670, 315, 44512, 11, 279, 5306, 7262, 22111, 705, 13, 3197, 279, 6787, 315, 279, 3015, 71118, 646, 902, 5021, 50471, 419, 7262, 11, 279, 3015, 71118, 93913, 13, 576, 22674, 20892, 9733, 304, 825, 315, 279, 46769, 8683, 438, 458, 55103, 369, 4650, 4802, 1660, 9768, 323, 9583, 5880, 11, 714, 807, 525, 537, 59