{"id": "318", "question": "how can i check taxes were filed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, you can check the status of your tax return by:\n\n1. Using the IRS2Go app on your smartphone to check the status of your tax return online.\n2. Checking the status of your tax return over the phone by calling the IRS.\n3. Checking the status of your state tax return online or over the phone.\n\nTo check the status of your tax return, you will need your Social Security number, tax filing status, and the amount of any refund due. If you e-filed your return, you can check the status 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to check taxes were filed is:\n\nYou can check the status of your tax return online or over the phone using the methods described above.", "pred": "4. Checking state tax return: If you filed a state tax return, you can check the status of it by visiting the website of your state's tax department or using their app.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "4. Checking state tax return: If you filed a state tax return, you can check the status of it by visiting the website of your state's tax department or using their app.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, you can check taxes were filed in the following ways:\\n\\n1. Online: You can check the status of your tax return online by using the IRS2Go application for Apple users or by visiting the IRS website. If you e-filed your taxes, you should be able to get a refund status within 72 hours. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\\n\\n2. Over the Phone: You can also check the status of your tax return by phoning the IRS. It takes time for the IRS to process your taxes, so give them adequate time before checking on the status of your refund.\\n\\n3. Using Tax Software: If you e-filed your return, wait 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you provide your email address, most tax software will send you an email confirmation when the IRS accepts your tax return. Software programs also typically have an application that allows you to check the status of your return by logging into your account.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can check the status of your tax return in the following ways:\\n\\n1. **Online**: Use the IRS2Go application for Apple users. If you e-filed your taxes, you can get a refund status within 72 hours. If you mailed your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing in your taxes.\\n\\n2. **Over the Phone**: You can call the IRS to check the status of your federal tax return.\\n\\n3. **Software Application**: Use tax software that allows you to check the status of your return by logging into your account. If you provided your email address, most tax software will send you an email confirmation when the IRS accepts your tax return.\\n\\nMake sure to wait for adequate time before checking the status of your refund, especially if you mailed your taxes.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can check the status of your taxes by using the following methods:\\n\\n1. Online: You can check the status of a federal tax return online by visiting the IRS website or using the IRS2Go app. If you e-filed your taxes, you should be able to get a refund status within 72 hours. If you mailed in your taxes, you will have to wait 3 or 4 weeks after mailing.\\n\\n2. By phone: You can also check the status of your federal tax return by calling the IRS. It takes time for the IRS to process your taxes, so give them adequate time before checking on the status of your refund.\\n\\n3. Using tax software: Most tax software will send you an email confirmation when the IRS accepts your tax return. Software programs also typically have an application that allows you to check the status of your return by logging into your account.\\n\\n4. Checking state tax return: If you filed a state tax return, you can check the status of it by visiting the website of your state's tax department or using their app.\"]", "time_sec": 29.955, "generation_time_seconds": 28.5071, "selection_time_seconds": 1.4321, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 1779, 13125, 1033, 12729, 304, 279, 2701, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 8105, 25, 1446, 646, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 3742, 470, 2860, 553, 1667, 279, 33383, 17, 10850, 3766, 369, 8162, 3847, 476, 553, 16721, 279, 33383, 3910, 13, 1416, 498, 384, 14203, 67, 697, 13125, 11, 498, 1265, 387, 2952, 311, 633, 264, 20965, 2639, 2878, 220, 22, 17, 4115, 13, 1416, 498, 75210, 697, 13125, 11, 498, 686, 614, 311, 3783, 220, 18, 476, 220, 19, 5555, 1283, 32759, 304, 697, 13125, 382, 17, 13, 6065, 279, 14307, 25, 1446, 646, 1083, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 3742, 470, 553, 1319, 19744, 279, 33383, 13, 1084, 4990, 882, 369, 279, 33383, 311, 1882, 697, 13125, 11, 773, 2968, 1105, 25532, 882, 1573, 13295, 389, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 20965, 382, 18, 13, 12091, 15190, 4377, 25, 1416, 498, 384, 14203, 67, 697, 470, 11, 3783, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 1283, 279, 33383, 25498, 22567, 315, 697, 470, 13, 1416, 498, 3410, 697, 2551, 2621, 11, 1429, 3742, 3162, 686, 3624, 498, 458, 2551, 19539, 979, 279, 33383, 26344, 697, 3742, 470, 13, 4377, 7468, 1083, 11136, 614, 458, 3766, 429, 6147, 498, 311, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 470, 553, 8392, 1119, 697, 2692, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. Using Tax Software: If you e-filed your return, wait 24 hours after the IRS acknowledged receipt of your return. If you provide your email address, most tax software will send you an email confirmation when the IRS accepts your tax return. Software programs also typically have an application that allows you to check the status of your return by logging into your account.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5418295248647906, "g_worst_claim": 0.3187188704808553, "g_content": 2.1304724442331415, "g_traj_mean": 1.5529959201812744}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.40998390316963196, "g_worst_claim": -0.40998390316963196, "g_content": -0.6577897071838379, "g_traj_mean": -0.3644079566001892}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 3742, 470, 304, 279, 2701, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 19598, 95518, 5443, 279, 33383, 17, 10850, 3766, 369, 8162, 3847, 13, 1416, 498, 384, 14203, 67, 697, 13125, 11, 498, 646, 633, 264, 20965, 2639, 2878, 220, 22, 17, 4115, 13, 1416, 498, 75210, 697, 13125, 11, 498, 686, 614, 311, 3783, 220, 18, 476, 220, 19, 5555, 1283, 32759, 304, 697, 13125, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 1918, 279, 14307, 95518, 1446, 646, 1618, 279, 33383, 311, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 6775, 3742, 470, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 19250, 7323, 95518, 5443, 3742, 3162, 429, 6147, 498, 311, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 470, 553, 8392, 1119, 697, 2692, 13, 1416, 498, 3897, 697, 2551, 2621, 11, 1429, 3742, 3162, 686, 3624, 498, 458, 2551, 19539, 979, 279, 33383, 26344, 697, 3742, 470, 382, 8078, 2704, 311, 3783, 369, 25532, 882, 1573, 13295, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 20965, 11, 5310, 421, 498, 75210, 697, 13125, 13, 151645], "pred": "Make sure to wait for adequate time before checking the status of your refund, especially if you mailed your taxes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4220052986701737, "g_worst_claim": 0.3187188704808553, "g_content": 1.7305133217259456, "g_traj_mean": 1.4004110097885132}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 13125, 553, 1667, 279, 2701, 5413, 1447, 16, 13, 8105, 25, 1446, 646, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 264, 6775, 3742, 470, 2860, 553, 16721, 279, 33383, 3910, 476, 1667, 279, 33383, 17, 10850, 906, 13, 1416, 498, 384, 14203, 67, 697, 13125, 11, 498, 1265, 387, 2952, 311, 633, 264, 20965, 2639, 2878, 220, 22, 17, 4115, 13, 1416, 498, 75210, 304, 697, 13125, 11, 498, 686, 614, 311, 3783, 220, 18, 476, 220, 19, 5555, 1283, 32759, 382, 17, 13, 3216, 4540, 25, 1446, 646, 1083, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 6775, 3742, 470, 553, 8098, 279, 33383, 13, 1084, 4990, 882, 369, 279, 33383, 311, 1882, 697, 13125, 11, 773, 2968, 1105, 25532, 882, 1573, 13295, 389, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 20965, 382, 18, 13, 12091, 3742, 3162, 25, 7496, 3742, 3162, 686, 3624, 498, 458, 2551, 19539, 979, 279, 33383, 26344, 697, 3742, 470, 13, 4377, 7468, 1083, 11136, 614, 458, 3766, 429, 6147, 498, 311, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 697, 470, 553, 8392, 1119, 697, 2692, 382, 19, 13, 46093, 1584, 3742, 470, 25, 1416, 498, 12729, 264, 1584, 3742, 470, 11, 498, 646, 1779, 279, 2639, 315, 432, 553, 16721, 279, 3910, 315, 697, 1584, 594, 3742, 9292, 476, 1667, 862, 906, 13, 151645], "pred": "4. Checking state tax return: If you filed a state tax return, you can check the status of it by visiting the website of your state's tax department or using their app.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2252176321183885, "g_worst_claim": 0.12036009268327193, "g_content": 1.5211021498878403, "g_traj_mean": 1.1451560258865356}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "320", "question": "what is the effect of carbon footprint", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that the effect of a carbon footprint is a measure of the negative impact of human activities on the environment. The measurement of a carbon footprint typically indicates the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced through daily activities. Additionally, reducing one's carbon footprint can have a positive impact on the environment, even if the changes may seem small.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the effect of a carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of various human activities within a given time frame, typically measured in tons of carbon dioxide (CO2) released into the atmosphere. This measurement helps in understanding the environmental effect of activities such as heating homes with oil, coal, or gas, raising livestock, and operating restaurants.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the effect of a carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of various human activities within a given time frame, typically measured in tons of carbon dioxide (CO2) released into the atmosphere. This measurement helps in understanding the environmental effect of activities such as heating homes with oil, coal, or gas, raising livestock, and operating restaurants.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the effect of carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of human activities. It quantifies the total amount of greenhouse gases produced by various human activities within a given time frame, typically measured in tons of carbon dioxide (CO2) released into the atmosphere. This measurement helps in understanding the environmental effect of lifestyle choices, such as using energy for heating, consuming food, and driving vehicles. Reducing carbon footprint involves making changes in daily activities to decrease the amount of greenhouse gases produced, which can lead to a significant positive impact on the environment.\", \"Based on the given passages, carbon footprint measures the environmental impact of human activities on the environment. The carbon footprint is typically measured in tons of carbon dioxide (CO2) released into the atmosphere. It takes into account various activities such as heating homes with oil, coal, or gas, producing food, and driving automobiles. By tracking carbon footprint, individuals and organizations can assess the amount of greenhouse gases they are contributing to the environment and make informed decisions to reduce their impact.\", \"Based on the given passages, the concept of a carbon footprint measures the environmental impact of your lifestyle, indicating the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced as a result of your daily activities. This measurement helps in understanding the total environmental effect of various human activities within a given time frame. A carbon footprint is usually measured in tons of carbon dioxide (CO2) released into the atmosphere.\", \"Based on the given passages, the effect of a carbon footprint is to measure the environmental impact of various human activities within a given time frame, typically measured in tons of carbon dioxide (CO2) released into the atmosphere. This measurement helps in understanding the environmental effect of activities such as heating homes with oil, coal, or gas, raising livestock, and operating restaurants.\"]", "time_sec": 18.998, "generation_time_seconds": 17.9887, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9984, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2456, 315, 12499, 42872, 374, 311, 6629, 279, 12158, 5421, 315, 3738, 7488, 13, 1084, 10272, 9606, 279, 2790, 3311, 315, 36547, 44512, 8947, 553, 5257, 3738, 7488, 2878, 264, 2661, 882, 4034, 11, 11136, 16