oil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it's cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potatoes from the water and remove the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3279735163673676, "g_worst_claim": 0.0943608283996582, "g_content": 1.5975411987304688, "g_traj_mean": 1.4290977716445923}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 43690, 34167, 369, 4135, 1051, 20058, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 18115, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 624, 19, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 624, 20, 13, 4492, 812, 432, 2163, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 1101, 3322, 773, 429, 432, 748, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 697, 38734, 504, 279, 3015, 323, 4057, 279, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. Score your potatoes all the way around the center.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.458802755129293, "g_worst_claim": 0.0943608283996582, "g_content": 1.682876275510204, "g_traj_mean": 1.4948346614837646}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 43690, 34167, 369, 4135, 1051, 20058, 11, 498, 1265, 1447, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 3085, 264, 21430, 11, 5456, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 624, 19, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 624, 20, 13, 4492, 812, 432, 2163, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 1101, 3322, 773, 429, 432, 748, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to boil potatoes for easy peeling, you should:\n\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4327936705046973, "g_worst_claim": 0.3029615879058838, "g_content": 1.5269764491489954, "g_traj_mean": 1.5057549476623535}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 83.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "332", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, first, check common tick hiding places such as inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes. Once you locate a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the tick's head where it attaches to the skin. If you plan to use your fingers, wear gloves. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Regular use of tick control products can also prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Flea and tick shampoos can kill the ticks that are already on your pet.", "pred": "1. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\n2. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\n3. To prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian is also aware of diseases that are common in your area and can pose a risk to your dog.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\n2. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\n3. To prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian is also aware of diseases that are common in your area and can pose a risk to your dog.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places.\\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin.\\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to remove it.\\n4. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\\n5. If you yank the tick away too quickly, you might leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\\n\\nAdditionally, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is recommended to use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation, considering the diseases common in your area.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\\n2. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\\n3. To prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian is also aware of diseases that are common in your area and can pose a risk to your dog.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes as these are favorite tick hiding places.\\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin.\\n3. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\\n4. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to remove it. Avoid yanking it away too quickly as this could leave part of the tick's mouth behind, potentially causing an infection.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you can prevent ticks by regularly using tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. If ticks are already on your dog, you can use tick control products to kill the ticks that are already attached, but these products are not as effective for preventing new ticks from attaching.\"]", "time_sec": 24.25, "generation_time_seconds": 23.4522, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7872, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4248, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 5562, 594, 24230, 323, 2163, 1181, 6414, 11, 438, 1493, 525, 6930, 9341, 25037, 7482, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 624, 18, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 311, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 498, 379, 1180, 279, 9341, 3123, 2238, 6157, 11, 498, 2578, 5274, 949, 315, 279, 9341, 594, 10780, 4815, 11, 892, 646, 5240, 458, 18873, 382, 49574, 11, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 15502, 13, 4615, 81240, 646, 31013, 498, 911, 279, 1850, 1985, 369, 697, 5562, 323, 697, 6534, 11, 12831, 279, 18808, 4185, 304, 697, 3082, 13, 151645], "pred": "Additionally, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is recommended to use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation, considering the diseases common in your area.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3493770795750266, "g_worst_claim": 0.29778003692626953, "g_content": 1.6359272003173828, "g_traj_mean": 1.3267881870269775}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 624, 17, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 1416, 498, 379, 1180, 279, 9341, 3123, 504, 697, 5562, 2238, 6157, 11, 498, 4700, 5274, 949, 315, 279, 9341, 748, 10780, 4815, 11, 892, 646, 5240, 458, 18873, 624, 18, 13, 2014, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 11, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 15502, 13, 4615, 81240, 646, 31013, 498, 911, 279, 1850, 1985, 369, 697, 5562, 323, 697, 6534, 13, 4615, 81240, 374, 1083, 7853, 315, 18808, 429, 525, 4185, 304, 697, 3082, 323, 646, 17040, 264, 5214, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\n2. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\n3. To prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian is also aware of diseases that are common in your area and can pose a risk to your dog.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3591547571080977, "g_worst_claim": 0.3327379028002421, "g_content": 1.8804777896765508, "g_traj_mean": 1.4697108268737793}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4248, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 5562, 594, 24230, 323, 2163, 1181, 6414, 438, 1493, 525, 6930, 9341, 25037, 7482, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279,