, "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "334", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you can remove them manually or use tick control products. To remove ticks manually, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on the tick gently and steadily. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Alternatively, you can use tick control products regularly, which are advised by your veterinarian. These products are useful for killing the fleas and ticks that are already on your pet and help prevent ticks from attaching. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you can remove them manually or use tick control products. To remove ticks manually, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on the tick gently and steadily. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Alternatively, you can use tick control products regularly, which are advised by your veterinarian. These products are useful for killing the fleas and ticks that are already on your pet and help prevent ticks from attaching. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places.\\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin.\\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to remove it.\\n4. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\\n5. If you yank the tick away too quickly, you might leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\\n\\nAdditionally, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is recommended to use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation, considering the diseases common in your area.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you can remove them manually or use tick control products. To remove ticks manually, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on the tick gently and steadily. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Alternatively, you can use tick control products regularly, which are advised by your veterinarian. These products are useful for killing the fleas and ticks that are already on your pet and help prevent ticks from attaching. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should first check the dog's ears, inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes. To remove the tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on it gently and steadily. If you plan to use your fingers, it is recommended to wear gloves. It is also important to regularly use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the dog’s skin.\\n2. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.\\n3. If you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick, wear gloves.\\n4. After removing the tick, clean the area with soap and water to prevent infection.\\n5. Use tick control products as advised by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog in the future.\"]", "time_sec": 25.487, "generation_time_seconds": 24.5184, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9422, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4248, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 5562, 594, 24230, 323, 2163, 1181, 6414, 11, 438, 1493, 525, 6930, 9341, 25037, 7482, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 624, 18, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 311, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 498, 379, 1180, 279, 9341, 3123, 2238, 6157, 11, 498, 2578, 5274, 949, 315, 279, 9341, 594, 10780, 4815, 11, 892, 646, 5240, 458, 18873, 382, 49574, 11, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 15502, 13, 4615, 81240, 646, 31013, 498, 911, 279, 1850, 1985, 369, 697, 5562, 323, 697, 6534, 11, 12831, 279, 18808, 4185, 304, 697, 3082, 13, 151645], "pred": "Additionally, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is recommended to use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation, considering the diseases common in your area.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3493770795750266, "g_worst_claim": 0.29778003692626953, "g_content": 1.6359272003173828, "g_traj_mean": 1.3267881870269775}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 4057, 1105, 20083, 476, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 13, 2014, 4057, 29957, 20083, 11, 990, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 323, 6815, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 13, 38478, 11, 498, 646, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 15502, 11, 892, 525, 25104, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 525, 5390, 369, 13118, 279, 12962, 300, 323, 29957, 429, 525, 2669, 389, 697, 6753, 323, 1492, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 13, 4615, 81240, 646, 31013, 498, 911, 279, 1850, 1985, 369, 697, 5562, 323, 697, 6534, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you can remove them manually or use tick control products. To remove ticks manually, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on the tick gently and steadily. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Alternatively, you can use tick control products regularly, which are advised by your veterinarian. These products are useful for killing the fleas and ticks that are already on your pet and help prevent ticks from attaching. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1466300390894546, "g_worst_claim": 0.32793017228444415, "g_content": 1.5955023447672525, "g_traj_mean": 1.251834750175476}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 1265, 1156, 1779, 279, 5562, 594, 24230, 11, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 24230, 11, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 13, 2014, 4057, 279, 9341, 11, 990, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 323, 6815, 389, 432, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 1416, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 9850, 35416, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 2989, 311, 15502, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should first check the dog's ears, inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes. To remove the tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on it gently and steadily. If you plan to use your fingers, it is recommended to wear gloves. It is also important to regularly use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1217334889230275, "g_worst_claim": 0.32793017228444415, "g_content": 1.428663120713345, "g_traj_mean": 1.1006439924240112}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 5562, 748, 6787, 624, 17, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 11, 9850, 35416, 624, 19, 13, 4636, 17592, 279, 9341, 11, 4240, 279, 3082, 448, 26785, 323, 3015, 311, 5358, 18873, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 9341, 2524, 3871, 438, 25104, 553, 264, 81240, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 304, 279, 3853, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow these steps:\n\n1. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the dog’s skin.\n2. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.\n3. If you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick, wear gloves.\n4. After removing the tick, clean the area with soap and water to prevent infection.\n5. Use tick control products as advised by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog in the future.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8864300613898737, "g_worst_claim": -0.17585344314575196, "g_content": 1.1602752253694355, "g_traj_mean": 0.9069734811782837}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "335", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, which are common hiding places for ticks. (Passage 1)\n2. Use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to the dog. (Passage 2)\n3. Remove ticks from the dog using a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages whether there are any specific products or methods for getting rid of ticks from dogs that are already infested.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, remove the tick by following these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the dog's skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If using your fingers to remove the tick, wear gloves to avoid infection.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, remove the tick by following these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the dog's skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If using your fingers to remove the tick, wear gloves to avoid infection.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places.\\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin.\\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to remove it.\\n4. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\\n5. If you yank the tick away too quickly, you might leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\\n\\nAdditionally, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is recommended to use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation, considering the diseases common in your area.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, remove the tick by following these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the dog's skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If using your fingers to remove the tick, wear gloves to avoid infection.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products can help prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, you should check your dog's ears, behind the ears, and around the eyes as these are common tick hiding places. To remove a tick, use tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on it gently and steadily. Wearing gloves during the removal process is also recommended to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps:\\n1. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin.\\n2. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.\\n3. Ensure to check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes, as ticks have a preference for these hiding places.\\n4. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\\n5. Consider using tick control products recommended by your veterinarian, which can prevent ticks from attaching to your dog.\\n6. Regularly check your dog for ticks, as they can transmit diseases to both dogs and people.\\n7. If you find a tick that has already attached, remove it immediately following these steps to minimize the risk of infection.\"]", "time_sec": 26.154, "generation_time_seconds": 25.0672, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0696, "record_p