air of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the dog's skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If using your fingers to remove the tick, wear gloves to avoid infection.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9521617332524581, "g_worst_claim": 0.26903680960337323, "g_content": 0.8661513924598694, "g_traj_mean": 1.0349434614181519}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 646, 1492, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 1265, 1779, 697, 5562, 594, 24230, 11, 4815, 279, 24230, 11, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 438, 1493, 525, 4185, 9341, 25037, 7482, 13, 2014, 4057, 264, 9341, 11, 990, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 323, 6815, 389, 432, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 467, 13678, 35416, 2337, 279, 16652, 1882, 374, 1083, 11102, 311, 5648, 9380, 949, 315, 279, 9341, 594, 10780, 4815, 11, 892, 646, 5240, 458, 18873, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products can help prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, you should check your dog's ears, behind the ears, and around the eyes as these are common tick hiding places. To remove a tick, use tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on it gently and steadily. Wearing gloves during the removal process is also recommended to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8951662325099058, "g_worst_claim": 0.24665419260660806, "g_content": 1.180136385830966, "g_traj_mean": 0.9894842505455017}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 624, 17, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 624, 18, 13, 29279, 311, 1779, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 5562, 594, 24230, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 11, 438, 29957, 614, 264, 21933, 369, 1493, 25037, 7482, 624, 19, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 624, 20, 13, 21144, 1667, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 11, 892, 646, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 624, 21, 13, 28800, 398, 1779, 697, 5562, 369, 29957, 11, 438, 807, 646, 29282, 18808, 311, 2176, 12590, 323, 1251, 624, 22, 13, 1416, 498, 1477, 264, 9341, 429, 702, 2669, 12392, 11, 4057, 432, 7069, 2701, 1493, 7354, 311, 29337, 279, 5214, 315, 18873, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps:\n1. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin.\n2. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.\n3. Ensure to check inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes, as ticks have a preference for these hiding places.\n4. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\n5. Consider using tick control products recommended by your veterinarian, which can prevent ticks from attaching to your dog.\n6. Regularly check your dog for ticks, as they can transmit diseases to both dogs and people.\n7. If you find a tick that has already attached, remove it immediately following these steps to minimize the risk of infection.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9786634785962545, "g_worst_claim": 0.09937568008899689, "g_content": 1.2370871011312905, "g_traj_mean": 0.9600946307182312}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.25, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "337", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check your dog's body thoroughly, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, around the eyes, and other favorite tick hiding places.\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and wear gloves if needed.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily, making sure not to yank it away from your dog too quickly.\n4. Regularly use tick control products on your dog, as recommended by your veterinarian, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog in the first place.\n\nIf you have any further questions or concerns, consult your veterinarian for advice.", "pred": "1. Check your dog's fur for ticks, focusing on popular tick hiding spots such as inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes.\n2. If you find a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. If you choose to use your fingers, wear gloves.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Be careful not to yank the tick away too quickly, as this might leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\n4. Consider using tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products can help prevent ticks from attaching to your dog.\n5. Regularly check your dog for ticks, and remove them promptly to prevent potential health issues.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Check your dog's fur for ticks, focusing on popular tick hiding spots such as inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes.\n2. If you find a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. If you choose to use your fingers, wear gloves.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Be careful not to yank the tick away too quickly, as this might leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\n4. Consider using tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products can help prevent ticks from attaching to your dog.\n5. Regularly check your dog for ticks, and remove them promptly to prevent potential health issues.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places.\\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin.\\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to remove it.\\n4. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\\n5. If you yank the tick away too quickly, you might leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\\n\\nAdditionally, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is recommended to use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation, considering the diseases common in your area.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\\n1. Check the dog regularly for ticks, focusing on areas like the ears, behind the ears, around the eyes, and other common tick hiding places.\\n2. If a tick is found, remove it using tweezers by grasping the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pulling firmly and steadily.\\n3. Wear gloves when using your fingers to remove the tick to avoid direct contact with the tick.\\n4. After removing the tick, dispose of it properly to prevent the transmission of diseases.\\n5. Preventive measures include the use of tick control products recommended by a veterinarian. These products can help reduce the risk of ticks attaching to the dog in the future.\", \"Based on the given passages, to get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Check your dog's fur for ticks, focusing on popular tick hiding spots such as inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes.\\n2. If you find a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. If you choose to use your fingers, wear gloves.\\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Be careful not to yank the tick away too quickly, as this might leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\\n4. Consider using tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products can help prevent ticks from attaching to your dog.\\n5. Regularly check your dog for ticks, and remove them promptly to prevent potential health issues.\", \"The provided passages do not directly address the question of how to get rid of ticks from dogs. Therefore, the answer is:\\n\\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 25.257, "generation_time_seconds": 24.3457, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9021, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4248, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 5562, 594, 24230, 323, 2163, 1181, 6414, 11, 438, 1493, 525, 6930, 9341, 25037, 7482, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 624, 18, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 311, 4057, 432, 624, 19, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 498, 379, 1180, 279, 9341, 3123, 2238, 6157, 11, 498, 2578, 5274, 949, 315, 279, 9341, 594, 10780, 4815, 11, 892, 646, 5240, 458, 18873, 382, 49574, 11, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 15502, 13, 4615, 81240, 646, 31013, 498, 911, 279, 1850, 1985, 369, 697, 5562, 323, 697, 6534, 11, 12831, 279, 18808, 4185, 304, 697, 3082, 13, 151645], "pred": "Additionally, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is recommended to use tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation, considering the diseases common in your area.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.353447384820528, "g_worst_claim": 0.2738446394602458, "g_content": 1.6400423551860608, "g_traj_mean": 1.3338510990142822}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 510, 16, 13, 4248, 279, 5562, 15502, 369, 29957, 11, 21080, 389, 5671, 1075, 279, 24230, 11, 4815, 279, 24230, 11, 2163, 279, 6414, 11, 323, 1008, 4185, 9341, 25037, 7482, 624, 17, 13, 1416, 264, 9341, 374, 1730, 11, 4057, 432, 1667, 14545, 10125, 388, 553, 48987, 9989, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 323, 22266, 31520, 323, 41971, 624, 18, 13, 41062, 35416, 979, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 311, 5648, 2118, 3645, 448, 279, 9341, 624, 19, 13, 4636, 17592, 279, 9341, 11, 27390, 315, 432, 10277, 311, 5358, 279, 18368, 315, 18808, 624, 20, 13, 38068, 533, 10953, 2924, 279, 990, 315, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 264, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 646, 1492, 7949, 279, 5214, 315, 29957, 71808, 311, 279, 5562, 304, 279, 3853, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n1. Check the dog regularly for ticks, focusing on areas like the ears, behind the ears, around the eyes, and other common tick hiding places.\n2. If a tick is found, remove it using tweezers by grasping the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pulling firmly and steadily.\n3. Wear gloves when using your fingers to remove the tick to avoid direct contact with the tick.\n4. After removing the tick, dispose of it properly to prevent the transmission of diseases.\n5. Preventive measures include the use of tick control products recommended by a veterinarian. These products can help reduce the risk of ticks attaching to the dog in the future.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5708802786969146, "g_worst_claim": -0.2773750305175781, "g_content": 0.7456098937988281, "g_traj_mean": 0.6129084229469299}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4248, 697, 5562, 594, 18241, 369, 29957, 11, 21080, 389, 5411, 9341, 25037, 18773, 1741, 438, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 24230, 11, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 624, 17, 13, 1416, 498, 1477, 264, 9341, 11, 990, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 13, 1416, 498, 5157, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 11, 9850, 35416, 624, 18, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 2823, 16585, 537, 311, 379, 1180, 279, 9341, 3123, 2238, 6157, 11, 438, 419, 2578, 5274, 949, 315, 279, 9341, 594, 10780, 4815, 11, 892, 646, 5240, 458, 18873, 624, 19, 13, 21144, 1667, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 646, 1492, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 624, 20, 13, 28800, 398, 1779, 697, 5562, 369, 29957, 11, 323, 4057, 1105, 39422, 311, 5358, 4650, 2820, 4714, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Check your dog's fur for ticks, focusing on popular tick hiding spots such as inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes.\n2. If you find a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. If you choose to use your fingers, wear gloves.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Be careful not to yank the tick away too quickly, as this might leave part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection.\n4. Consider using tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products can help prevent ticks from attaching to your dog.\n5. Regularly check your dog for ticks, and remove them promptly to prevent potential health issues.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8079888072672976, "g_worst_claim": 0.034421107172966, "g_content": 0.8347096270825489, "g_traj_mean": 0.7534105777740479}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 3897, 46769, 653, 537, 5961, 2621, 279, 3405, 315, 1246, 311, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 13, 15277, 11, 279, 4226, 374, 1447, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.004407805084299885, "g_worst_claim": -0.0020746509544551373, "g_content": 0.1413922627766927, "g_traj_mean": -0.01801789179444313}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "338", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs with a knife. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them. Afterwards, line a baking pan with heavy duty foil. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer for heat circulation on all sides. Mix mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure it adheres to the meat. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and remove the ribs from the foil. Place them meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue this process until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs using a knife near the narrow end and pull it off in one piece.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them.\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping it to make a tent.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs using a knife near the narrow end and pull it off in one piece.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them.\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping it to make a tent.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. **Grilled Ribs:**\\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven-cooked BBQ Ribs:**\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n\\n3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. For grilling ribs:\\n   - Preheat the grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil and place them meaty-side up on the grill.\\n   - Brush the ribs with some sauce.\\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\\n   - Flip the ribs and brush them with sauce again.\\n   - Cook for another 5 minutes.\\n   - Repeat flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.\\n   - Total grilling time should be around 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. For oven-cooked BBQ ribs:\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add enough BBQ sauce to cover them.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping the foil to make a tent.\\n\\nPlease note that an additional step for oven-cooked BBQ ribs is missing in the provided passages, as the instruction specifies 3 steps but only provides 2.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs using a knife near the narrow end and pull it off in one piece.\\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them.\\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping it to make a tent.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\"]", "time_sec": 29.633, "generation_time_seconds": 28.6866, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9347, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 4374, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 46, 1037, 22471, 10823, 45277, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 256, 481, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 34860, 287, 279, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 43924, 279, 55149, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 13, 1096, 26112, 6147, 369, 8628, 4225, 7455, 389, 678, 11067, 315, 279, 55149, 624, 256, 481, 14263, 279, 55149, 25, 19219, 279, 64307, 323, 279, 14473, 16205, 11, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 624, 256, 481, 15515, 35144, 279, 55149, 448, 279, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 1281, 2704, 279, 10273, 34951, 288, 311, 279, 20131, 13041, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6792029787417937, "g_worst_claim": 0.17530266443888345, "g_content": 2.4501982421875, "g_traj_mean": 1.6135092973709106}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 1081, 9400, 55149, 510, 256, 481, 4968, 19963, 279, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 323, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 624, 256, 481, 32988, 279, 55149, 448, 1045, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 40284, 279, 55149, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 19187, 1549, 624, 256, 481, 12514, 369, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 44801, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 624, 256, 481, 10657, 1081, 9400, 882, 1265, 387, 2163, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 23387, 22471, 10823, 45277, 55149, 510, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 323, 912, 3322, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 1105, 624, 256, 481, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 54518, 46399, 11, 49817, 279, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 382, 5501, 5185, 429, 458, 5107, 3019, 369, 23387, 22471, 10823, 45277, 55149, 374, 7402, 304, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 438, 279, 7600, 29102, 220, 18, 7354, 714, 1172, 5707, 220, 17, 13, 151645], "pred": "Please note that an additional step for oven-cooked BBQ ribs is missing in the provided passages, as the instruction specifies 3 steps but only provides 2.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1342957097766642, "g_worst_claim": 0.00705178827047348, "g_content": 1.627902903455369, "g_traj_mean": 0.9811724424362183}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 1667, 264, 21430, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 323, 6815, 432, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 624, 17, 13, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 323, 912, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 1105, 624, 18, 13, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 54518, 46399, 11, 49817, 432, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs using a knife near the narrow end and pull it off in one piece.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them.\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping it to make a tent.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4835250151343857, "g_worst_claim": 0.17449198166529337, "g_content": 2.49430783589681, "g_traj_mean": 1.7180430889129639}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 624, 17, 13, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 18, 13, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9018031721430866, "g_worst_claim": 0.17449198166529337, "g_content": 2.783423447027439, "g_traj_mean": 2.051311731338501}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "339", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Then, brush both sides of the ribs with a mixture of mustard and liquid smoke. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure it sticks to the meat. Next, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and place the ribs on the grill, meaty-side up. Brush the ribs with sauce, cover the grill, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip the ribs, brush with more sauce, and cook for another 5 minutes. Repeat this process, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "3. Seasoning:\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n   - Mix mustard with liquid smoke (if using) and brush ribs on both sides.\n   - Sprinkle ribs with dry rub and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "3. Seasoning:\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n   - Mix mustard with liquid smoke (if using) and brush ribs on both sides.\n   - Sprinkle ribs with dry rub and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. **Grilled Ribs:**\\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven-cooked BBQ Ribs:**\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n\\n3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. For grilling:\\n   - Heat a grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove ribs from foil, place meaty-side up on the grill, and brush with sauce.\\n   - Cover and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce thickens, ribs are heated through, and have grill marks (20 minutes total).\\n\\n2. For oven cooking:\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n   - Put ribs in a resealable bag with BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line a baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping it to make a tent.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to make ribs:\\n\\n1. For grill method:\\n   - Preheat grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove ribs from foil, place meaty-side up on grill.\\n   - Brush ribs with sauce, cover and cook for 5 minutes.\\n   - Flip and brush, cook another 5 minutes.\\n   - Repeat flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until sauce thickens and ribs are heated through and have grill marks.\\n   - Total grilling time is 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. For oven method:\\n   - Remove membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n   - Put ribs in a resealable bag and add BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping to make a tent.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. If grilling: \\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill.\\n   - Brush them with sauce.\\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\\n   - Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.\\n   - Total grilling time: 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. If oven-cooked:\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil, overlapping foil to create a tent.\\n\\n3. Seasoning:\\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\\n   - Mix mustard with liquid smoke (if using) and brush ribs on both sides.\\n   - Sprinkle ribs with dry rub and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\"]", "time_sec": 35.92, "generation_time_seconds": 34.5388, "selection_time_seconds": 1.3738, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 4374, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 46, 1037, 22471, 10823, 45277, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 27