{"id": "340", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\nTo grill the ribs:\n\n1. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium temperature (350°F to 450°F).\n2. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n3. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\n4. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes.\n5. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n\nTo prepare the ribs before grilling:\n\n1. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n2. Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and liquid smoke (if using), and brushing the ribs on both sides.\n3. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\n\nFor oven-cooked BBQ ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag.\n3. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover the ribs.\n4. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil.\n5. Place the ribs in the baking pan and bake at 350°F for 2-3 hours, or until the ribs are tender and the meat starts to pull away from the bone.", "pred": "1. Use a gas or charcoal grill set to medium heat (350°F to 450°F for 20 minutes).\n2. Lay the ribs on the grill in a single layer to allow heat circulation.\n3. Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard, and liquid smoke if using.\n4. Brush the ribs on both sides with the sauce.\n5. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs for another 5 minutes.\n6. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Use a gas or charcoal grill set to medium heat (350°F to 450°F for 20 minutes).\n2. Lay the ribs on the grill in a single layer to allow heat circulation.\n3. Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard, and liquid smoke if using.\n4. Brush the ribs on both sides with the sauce.\n5. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs for another 5 minutes.\n6. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. **Grilled Ribs:**\\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven-cooked BBQ Ribs:**\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n\\n3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. To grill the ribs:\\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.\\n   - Total grilling time: 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. To cook ribs in the oven:\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make ribs, you can either grill them or cook them in the oven. For grilling ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Heat the grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n2. Remove the ribs from the foil and place them meaty-side up on the grill.\\n3. Brush the ribs with some sauce.\\n4. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\\n5. Flip the ribs and brush them again, then cook for another 5 minutes.\\n6. Repeat the process of flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks. The total grilling time should be 20 minutes.\\n\\nFor oven-cooked BBQ ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, using plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. Use a gas or charcoal grill set to medium heat (350°F to 450°F for 20 minutes).\\n2. Lay the ribs on the grill in a single layer to allow heat circulation.\\n3. Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard, and liquid smoke if using.\\n4. Brush the ribs on both sides with the sauce.\\n5. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs for another 5 minutes.\\n6. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.\"]", "time_sec": 33.552, "generation_time_seconds": 32.4635, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0813, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 4374, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 46, 1037, 22471, 10823, 45277, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 256, 481, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 34860, 287, 279, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 43924, 279, 55149, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 13, 1096, 26112, 6147, 369, 8628, 4225, 7455, 389, 678, 11067, 315, 279, 55149, 624, 256, 481, 14263, 279, 55149, 25, 19219, 279, 64307, 323, 279, 14473, 16205, 11, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 624, 256, 481, 15515, 35144, 279, 55149, 448, 279, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 1281, 2704, 279, 10273, 34951, 288, 311, 279, 20131, 13041, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7136452256714596, "g_worst_claim": 0.26513904333114624, "g_content": 2.473311767578125, "g_traj_mean": 1.641162395477295}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 39058, 279, 55149, 510, 256, 481, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 624, 256, 481, 10657, 1081, 9400, 882, 25, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 2014, 4296, 55149, 304, 279, 23387, 510, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 256, 481, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. To cook ribs in the oven:\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.548144652443865, "g_worst_claim": 0.08278782665729523, "g_content": 2.3108726501464845, "g_traj_mean": 1.549025297164917}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 55149, 11, 498, 646, 2987, 39058, 1105, 476, 4296, 1105, 304, 279, 23387, 13, 1752, 1081, 9400, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 26070, 279, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 323, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 624, 18, 13, 32988, 279, 55149, 448, 1045, 19187, 624, 19, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 40284, 279, 55149, 323, 15625, 1105, 1549, 11, 1221, 4296, 369, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 44801, 279, 1882, 315, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 13, 576, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 1265, 387, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 2461, 23387, 22471, 10823, 45277, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 624, 17, 13, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 323, 912, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 18, 13, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 54518, 46399, 11, 1667, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, using plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2484518886234526, "g_worst_claim": 0.0823703408241272, "g_content": 1.8716864078602893, "g_traj_mean": 1.2883561849594116}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 738, 311, 11051, 8628, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 4292, 17, 13, 43924, 279, 55149, 389, 279, 39058, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 311, 2138, 8628, 34755, 624, 18, 13, 14263, 279, 55149, 448, 264, 9058, 10273, 323, 64307, 11, 323, 14473, 16205, 421, 1667, 624, 19, 13, 32988, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 19187, 624, 20, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 1221, 18287, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 369, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Use a gas or charcoal grill set to medium heat (350°F to 450°F for 20 minutes).\n2. Lay the ribs on the grill in a single layer to allow heat circulation.\n3. Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard, and liquid smoke if using.\n4. Brush the ribs on both sides with the sauce.\n5. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs for another 5 minutes.\n6. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.242214667415639, "g_worst_claim": 0.2639867862065633, "g_content": 1.3304468008188102, "g_traj_mean": 1.023753046989441}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.72, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "341", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ribs:\n\nStep 1: Prepare the ribs\n\n* Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs (passage 3)\n* Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard mixture (passage 2)\n\nStep 2: Grill the ribs\n\n* Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium heat (passage 1)\n* Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush with some of the sauce (passage 1)\n* Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs with more sauce (passage 1)\n* Continue to cook and flip every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through (passage 1)\n\nTotal grilling time: 20 minutes\n\nNote: The passages do not mention the temperature at which to cook the ribs, but a medium heat of 350°F to 450°F is suggested.", "pred": "The oven method differs from the grill method in that it involves removing the membrane, using a resealable bag with sauce, and lining the pan with foil. The grill method involves direct grilling and brushing the ribs with sauce while cooking.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The oven method differs from the grill method in that it involves removing the membrane, using a resealable bag with sauce, and lining the pan with foil. The grill method involves direct grilling and brushing the ribs with sauce while cooking.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. **Grilled Ribs:**\\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\\n   - Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven-cooked BBQ Ribs:**\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n\\n3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\", \"Based on the given passages, here's a summary of how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. For grilling:\\n   - Preheat the grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from foil and place them meaty-side up on the grill.\\n   - Brush the ribs with sauce and cover the grill.\\n   - Cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush again.\\n   - Repeat every 5 minutes until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through.\\n   - Total grilling time should be 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. For oven-cooking:\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag with BBQ sauce.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil and cover the ribs.\\n   - Ensure the ribs are seasoned on both sides with a mixture of mustard and liquid smoke if using, and then with a dry rub.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. **Preparation**:\\n   - **Grilled Ribs**:\\n     - Use a gas or charcoal grill set to medium heat (350°F to 450°F).\\n     - Arrange the ribs on the grill in a single layer.\\n     - Season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke (if using), brushing both sides, and then sprinkling with a dry rub, patting gently to ensure the rub adheres.\\n   - **Oven-cooked BBQ Ribs**:\\n     - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n     - Place the ribs in a resealable bag with sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n     - Line a baking pan with heavy-duty foil, creating a tent.\\n\\n2. **Cooking**:\\n   - **Grilled Ribs**:\\n     - Grill the ribs for 20 minutes, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes.\\n     - Cook until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks.\\n   - **Oven-cooked BBQ Ribs**:\\n     - Bake the ribs in the prepared oven at the specified temperature for the required time (not explicitly mentioned but typically 2-3 hours at 250°F).\\n\\nBoth methods involve seasoning the ribs thoroughly and ensuring they are well-coated with sauce before cooking. The grill method involves direct heat, while the oven method uses indirect heat for a more thorough cooking process.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. For the grill method:\\n   - Heat the grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Remove the ribs from the foil and place them meaty-side up on the grill.\\n   - Brush them with some of the sauce and cover the grill.\\n   - Cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush again.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks. This will take a total of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. For the oven method:\\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag with enough BBQ sauce to cover.\\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil and make a tent.\\n   - Cook the ribs in the oven, following the specific instructions for the oven method provided in the passage.\\n\\nThe oven method differs from the grill method in that it involves removing the membrane, using a resealable bag with sauce, and lining the pan with foil. The grill method involves direct grilling and brushing the ribs with sauce while cooking.\"]", "time_sec": 40.457, "generation_time_seconds": 39.4042, "selection_time_seconds": 1.044, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 4374, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 46, 1037, 22471, 10823, 45277, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 256, 481, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 34860, 287, 279, 431, 54341, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 43924, 279, 55149, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 13, 1096, 26112, 6147, 369, 8628, 4225, 7455, 389, 678, 11067, 315, 279, 55149, 624, 256, 481, 14263, 279, 55149, 25, 19219, 279, 64307, 323, 279, 14473, 16205, 11, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 624, 256, 481, 15515, 35144, 279, 55149, 448, 279, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 1281, 2704, 279, 10273, 34951, 288, 311, 279, 20131, 13041, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. **Seasoning the Ribs:**\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7058891607091469, "g_worst_claim": 0.28160462776819867, "g_content": 2.481159423828125, "g_traj_mean": 1.6360700130462646}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 594, 264, 12126, 315, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 1081, 9400, 510, 256, 481, 4968, 19963, 279, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 46399, 323, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 624, 256, 481, 32988, 279, 55149, 448, 19187, 323, 3421, 279, 39058, 624, 256, 481, 12514, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 1221, 18287, 323, 15625, 1549, 624, 256, 481, 44801, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 3080, 279, 19187, 12045, 724, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 624, 256, 481, 10657, 1081, 9400, 882, 1265, 387, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 23387, 22471, 10746, 510, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 448, 45277, 19187, 624, 256, 481, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 54518, 46399, 323, 3421, 279, 55149, 624, 256, 481, 29279, 279, 55149, 525, 51514, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 264, 20980, 315, 64307, 323, 14473, 16205, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 1221, 448, 264, 9058, 10273, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. For oven-cooking:\n   - Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n   - Put the ribs in a resealable bag with BBQ sauce.\n   - Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil and cover the ribs.\n   - Ensure the ribs are seasoned on both sides with a mixture of mustard and liquid smoke if using, and then with a dry rub.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1330219483403403, "g_worst_claim": 0.2782551050186157, "g_content": 2.2188438839382596, "g