r body weight after a bowel movement.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2307866172082786, "g_worst_claim": 0.09790891408920288, "g_content": 1.937995365687779, "g_traj_mean": 1.2897119522094727}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3432, 264, 65258, 7203, 1558, 537, 1102, 304, 264, 42326, 4709, 315, 4680, 389, 264, 14852, 5452, 7241, 279, 5452, 374, 7548, 13382, 13, 1096, 374, 1576, 279, 4680, 4709, 429, 13666, 1283, 264, 65258, 7203, 374, 537, 4152, 311, 264, 4709, 315, 2487, 8664, 13, 12090, 11, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 3654, 7586, 315, 8664, 11, 1741, 438, 37986, 11, 646, 387, 1730, 304, 53961, 288, 13, 1096, 8664, 374, 537, 5558, 504, 279, 2487, 714, 4751, 374, 264, 4622, 949, 315, 33525, 8664, 22881, 429, 374, 537, 10277, 41001, 13, 15277, 11, 3432, 264, 65258, 7203, 1558, 537, 16792, 311, 264, 5089, 13951, 304, 2487, 4680, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, having a bowel movement does not result in a noticeable loss of weight on a bathroom scale unless the scale is highly accurate. This is because the weight loss that occurs after a bowel movement is not due to a loss of body fat. Instead, a small amount of certain forms of fat, such as cholesterol, can be found in feces. This fat is not lost from the body but rather is a normal part of dietary fat intake that is not properly absorbed. Therefore, having a bowel movement does not contribute to a significant reduction in body weight.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0221874395958566, "g_worst_claim": 0.09790891408920288, "g_content": 1.6376873896672175, "g_traj_mean": 1.0420470237731934}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 3432, 264, 65258, 7203, 1558, 537, 1102, 304, 42326, 4680, 4709, 13, 576, 4680, 4709, 374, 17339, 311, 1620, 26359, 22881, 323, 44326, 11, 537, 279, 4680, 315, 279, 53961, 288, 13, 576, 5452, 686, 4363, 537, 1473, 264, 5089, 2297, 304, 2487, 4680, 1283, 264, 65258, 7203, 7241