{"id": "351", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Company goodwill is a business asset that is created when a business provides good service or product to their customers, leading to customer trust. This trust results in repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth, which can increase a company's customer base and retain old clients. Goodwill represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation of the business possesses. It is important because it can attract investors and future buyers, and it is an advantage of the reputation and connection with customers which tends to make that connection permanent.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, including the circumstances that make the connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase the customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection a business has with its customers, which tends to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses.\\n\\nGoodwill is important in business for several reasons. Firstly, it helps increase the customer base by attracting new customers and retaining old ones. Secondly, it attracts investors, making it easier to secure funding for the business. Lastly, it can also help in attracting potential buyers when the business is up for sale.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the overall reputation and connection with customers, combined with circumstances that make this connection permanent. It is important because it can increase the customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers. Goodwill arises when a business has provided good service or product, leading customers to develop trust and become repeat customers, who then recommend the business to others. This trust and recommendation contribute to the goodwill of the business, making it a valuable asset.\"]", "time_sec": 18.955, "generation_time_seconds": 17.7935, "selection_time_seconds": 1.155, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1096, 81646, 374, 3465, 979, 264, 2562, 20699, 5707, 1661, 2473, 476, 3871, 11, 6388, 311, 13153, 6310, 323, 3409, 8668, 91039, 18564, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 12703, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 3643, 432, 8661, 311, 4559, 279, 2562, 304, 279, 3853, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5910455107257984, "g_worst_claim": 0.3678622245788574, "g_content": 1.9201647440592449, "g_traj_mean": 1.1182760000228882}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 374, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 11, 2670, 279, 13161, 429, 1281, 279, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 279, 6310, 892, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 304, 2562, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 279, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, including the circumstances that make the connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase the customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "groundi