to the overall reputation and connection with customers, combined with circumstances that make this connection permanent. It is important because it can increase the customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers. Goodwill arises when a business has provided good service or product, leading customers to develop trust and become repeat customers, who then recommend the business to others. This trust and recommendation contribute to the goodwill of the business, making it a valuable asset.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8499238500625814, "g_worst_claim": 0.10595171650250752, "g_content": 2.785056020699295, "g_traj_mean": 1.7409472465515137}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "353", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the given passages, goodwill can be understood as a business asset that comes from a positive reputation and good connections with customers. It can be increased through providing good service or products, resulting in loyal and repeat customers who also spread positive reviews about the business. This goodwill attracts new customers, investors, and future buyers, making it an important factor in business success.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed through providing good service or product. This goodwill represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill is defined as the whole advantage of the reputation and connection with customers together with the circumstances whether of habit or otherwise, which tend to make that connection permanent. It represents in connection with any business or business product the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses.\\n\\nGoodwill is important in business for several reasons. Firstly, it increases the customer base by attracting and retaining old clients. Secondly, it helps in attracting investors by creating a positive image of the business. Lastly, it also aids in attracting future buyers by maintaining a strong reputation and connection with the customers.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection with customers, along with circumstances such as habits or connections, that tend to make those connections permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\"]", "time_sec": 16.748, "generation_time_seconds": 15.7845, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9563, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1096, 81646, 374, 3465, 979, 264, 2562, 