{"id": "354", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, I can confidently answer the following questions:\n\nWhat is company goodwill?\nCompany goodwill refers to the positive image and reputation of a business that is built over time through providing quality products or services, satisfying customers, and building strong relationships with them. Goodwill is a valuable asset for any business as it helps to attract new customers, retain existing ones, and attract investors.\n\nWhy is goodwill important in business?\nGoodwill is important in business because it helps to build trust and loyalty among customers, which leads to long-term relationships and repeat business. A strong reputation and goodwill can also make a business more attractive to potential investors and buyers. Additionally, goodwill can help a business to stand out from its competitors and establish a unique identity in the marketplace.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection that a business has with its customers. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base and retains old clients, attracting investors and future buyers. This is evident as the passages mention that goodwill helps to increase customer base and retain old clients, attract investors and attract future buyers. In other words, goodwill is the advantage of the reputation and connection with customers together with the circumstances whether of habit or otherwise, which tend to make that connection permanent.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection that a business has with its customers. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base and retains old clients, attracting investors and future buyers. This is evident as the passages mention that goodwill helps to increase customer base and retain old clients, attract investors and attract future buyers. In other words, goodwill is the advantage of the reputation and connection with customers together with the circumstances whether of habit or otherwise, which tend to make that connection permanent.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection with customers that make the business attractive and permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection that a business has with its customers. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base and retains old clients, attracting investors and future buyers. This is evident as the passages mention that goodwill helps to increase customer base and retain old clients, attract investors and attract future buyers. In other words, goodwill is the advantage of the reputation and connection with customers together with the circumstances whether of habit or otherwise, which tend to make that connection permanent.\", \"Based on the provided passages, company goodwill refers to the good will of the customers toward the business. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases the customer base and retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.\"]", "time_sec": 16.141, "generation_time_seconds": 15.3801, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7529, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1096, 81646, 374, 3465, 979, 264, 2562, 20699, 5707, 1661, 2473, 476, 3871, 11, 6388, 311, 13153, 6310, 323, 3409, 8668, 91039, 18564, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 12703, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 3643, 432, 8661, 311, 4559, 279, 2562, 304, 279, 3853, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5615493751535166, "g_worst_claim": 0.4225355386734009, "g_content": 1.857861110142299, "g_traj_mean": 1.0828922986984253}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 1281, 279, 2562, 18879, 323, 15330, 13, 1084,