in old clients, attract investors and attract future buyers. In other words, goodwill is the advantage of the reputation and connection with customers together with the circumstances whether of habit or otherwise, which tend to make that connection permanent.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.02331967570146, "g_worst_claim": 0.4225355386734009, "g_content": 3.085780482138357, "g_traj_mean": 1.9876699447631836}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 1661, 686, 315, 279, 6310, 8841, 279, 2562, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 279, 6310, 892, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 304, 2562, 1576, 432, 12703, 279, 6002, 2331, 323, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 60091, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the provided passages, company goodwill refers to the good will of the customers toward the business. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases the customer base and retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.367545080440942, "g_worst_claim": 0.21092418829600015, "g_content": 3.4686097175844255, "g_traj_mean": 2.0913166999816895}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.77, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "356", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive feelings and loyalty of customers towards a business, gained through providing good services or products, building trust, and creating a strong reputation. Goodwill is important because it can increase customer retention, attract new customers, and make the business more attractive to investors and potential buyers.\n\nAccording to passage 3, goodwill is an intangible asset that represents the value of a business's reputation and customer connections, which can make the connection between the business and its customers permanent.\n\nTherefore, goodwill is important for businesses because it can lead to increased customer loyalty, positive word-of-mouth advertising, and higher sales, ultimately contributing to the long-term success and growth of the business.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill is the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business has provided good service or product to their customers, leading them to develop trust and become repeat customers. This trust and connection with the business form the goodwill asset.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill is the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business has provided good service or product to their customers, leading them to develop trust and become repeat customers. This trust and connection with the business form the goodwill asset.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection a business has with its customers. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business provides good service or product to their customers, leading to trust and repeat customers. This trust and connection with customers create the goodwill of the business.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill is the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business has provided good service or product to their customers, leading them to develop trust and become repeat customers. This trust and connection with the business form the goodwill asset.\", \"Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that tendency to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses, and it is an important asset for businesses because it helps increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\"]", "time_sec": 15.834, "generation_time_seconds": 15.0403, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7839, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1096, 81646, 374, 3465, 979, 264, 2562, 20699, 5707, 1661, 2473, 476, 3871, 11, 6388, 311, 13153, 6310, 323, 3409, 8668, 91039, 18564, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 12703, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 3643, 432, 8661, 311, 4559, 279, 2562, 304, 279, 3853, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. This goodwill is created when a business consistently provides good service or products, leading to repeat customers and word-of-mouth recommendations. Goodwill is important because it increases a company's customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and makes it easier to sell the business in the future.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5615493751535166, "g_worst_claim": 0.4225355386734009, "g_content": 1.857861110142299, "g_traj_mean": 1.0828922986984253}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 264, 2562, 702, 448, 1181, 6310, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 12703, 279, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 60091, 3853, 22630, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 3465, 979, 264, 2562, 5707, 1661, 2473, 476, 1985, 311, 862, 6310, 11, 6388, 311, 6950, 323, 13153, 6310, 13, 1096, 6950, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 1855, 279, 81646, 315, 279, 2562, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection a business has with its customers. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business provides good service or product to their customers, leading to trust and repeat customers. This trust and connection with customers create the goodwill of the business.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7371319379270878, "g_worst_claim": 0.4225355386734009, "g_content": 2.423165512084961, "g_traj_mean": 1.413275957107544}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 374, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 279, 6310, 892, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 49226, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 12703, 279, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 60091, 3853, 22630, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 3465, 979, 264, 2562, 702, 3897, 1661, 2473, 476, 1985, 311, 862, 6310, 11, 6388, 1105, 311, 2225, 6950, 323, 3635, 13153, 6310, 13, 1096, 6950, 323, 3633, 448, 279, 2562, 1352, 279, 81646, 9329, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill is the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. It is important because it increases the customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers. Goodwill is created when a business has provided good service or product to their customers, leading them to develop trust and become repeat customers. This trust and connection with the business form the goodwill asset.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0900716873209113, "g_worst_claim": 0.4225355386734009, "g_content": 3.198340837345567, "g_traj_mean": 1.9635206460952759}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 2813, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 30854, 311, 1281, 429, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 279, 6310, 892, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 49226, 11, 323, 432, 374, 458, 2989, 9329, 369, 9675, 1576, 432, 8609, 5263, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that tendency to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses, and it is an important asset for businesses because it helps increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.3304520901089907, "g_worst_claim": 0.4225355386734009, "g_content": 3.641038258870443, "g_traj_mean": 2.222977638244629}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.2, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "357", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "gt": "An ad hominem fallacy occurs when someone attacks the character, motive, or other personal attribute of the person making an argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. This is often done to invalidate their arguments by associating their character with the soundness of their argument. On the other hand, the poisoning the well fallacy, which is a type of ad hominem attack, occurs when a person's integrity or intelligence is attacked before the merits of a case can be considered, effectively redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy is that an ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument directly, while the poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. The ad hominem fallacy is typically more immediate and personal, whereas the poisoning the well fallacy is more subtle and occurs before the actual argument begins.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy is that an ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument directly, while the poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. The ad hominem fallacy is typically more immediate and personal, whereas the poisoning the well fallacy is more subtle and occurs before the actual argument begins.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument rather than attacking the argument itself. The poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. The key difference is that the ad hominem fallacy occurs during the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy happens before the argument begins.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy is that an ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument directly, while the poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. The ad hominem fallacy is typically more immediate and personal, whereas the poisoning the well fallacy is more subtle and occurs before the actual argument begins.\", \"Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of a person making an argument rather than attacking the argument itself. The poisoning the well fallacy involves attacking a person's integrity or intelligence beforehand, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one party rather than the merits of the issue at hand. The main difference lies in the timing of the attack: ad hominem attacks occur during the argument, while poisoning the well attacks happen before the discussion begins.\", \"Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument rather than attacking the argument directly. An abusive ad hominem attack is a part of this, where the traits of an opponent are attacked as a means to invalidate their arguments. Additionally, equating someone's character with the soundness of their argument is considered a logical fallacy.\\n\\nThe poisoning the well fallacy, on the other hand, is an ad hominem attack that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered. It directly targets the credibility of one of the parties involved, redirecting the discussion towards their faults, rather than addressing the actual points of the argument.\"]", "time_sec": 21.168, "generation_time_seconds": 20.4955, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6662, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 17601, 22818, 279, 3668, 11, 45994, 11, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 279, 5693, 4751, 1091, 22818, 279, 5693, 5086, 13, 576, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 374, 458, 993, 4998, 68413, 3359, 389, 264, 1697, 594, 16614, 476, 11229, 429, 4990, 1992, 1573, 279, 49832, 315, 264, 1142, 646, 387, 6509, 11, 6423, 287, 279, 10219, 311, 279, 56690, 315, 825, 315, 279, 9677, 13, 576, 1376, 6672, 374, 429, 279, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 13666, 2337, 279, 5693, 11, 1393, 279, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 8573, 1573, 279, 5693, 12033, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument rather than attacking the argument itself. The poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. The key difference is that the ad hominem fallacy occurs during the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy happens before the argument begins.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9868753417864903, "g_worst_claim": 0.05537338440