parties involved, redirecting the discussion towards their faults, rather than addressing the actual points of the argument.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3010424676664738, "g_worst_claim": 0.10845903839383807, "g_content": 2.2479940561147838, "g_traj_mean": 1.347948670387268}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "358", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the difference between ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy is that ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attribute of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. On the other hand, poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, specifically attacking a person's integrity or intelligence to redirect the discussion towards their faults.", "pred": "On the other hand, the poisoning the well fallacy is a specific type of ad hominem attack that occurs before the merits of a case can be considered. It involves attacking the faults of one of the parties, typically the person making the argument, in order to distract from the actual argument by focusing on the opponent's character or integrity. This fallacy redirects the discussion to the opponent's faults instead of addressing the argument at hand.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "On the other hand, the poisoning the well fallacy is a specific type of ad hominem attack that occurs before the merits of a case can be considered. It involves attacking the faults of one of the parties, typically the person making the argument, in order to distract from the actual argument by focusing on the opponent's character or integrity. This fallacy redirects the discussion to the opponent's faults instead of addressing the argument at hand.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument rather than attacking the argument itself. The poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. The key difference is that the ad hominem fallacy occurs during the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy happens before the argument begins.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between an ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy is as follows:\\n\\nAn ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument rather than addressing the argument itself. It is a form of indirect argument where the opponent's credibility is questioned to undermine their argument.\\n\\nOn the other hand, the poisoning the well fallacy is a specific type of ad hominem attack that occurs before the merits of a case can be considered. It involves attacking the faults of one of the parties, typically the person making the argument, in order to distract from the actual argument by focusing on the opponent's character or integrity. This fallacy redirects the discussion to the opponent's faults instead of addressing the argument at hand.\", \"Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves an attack on a person's character, motive, or other attributes rather than the argument itself, while the poisoning the well fallacy involves attacking a person's integrity or intelligence before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties.\", \"Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves attacking an argument by attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy involves attacking the integrity or intelligence of a person before the merits of a case can be considered. Both fallacies are ad hominem attacks, but the poisoning the well fallacy does so in advance of discussing the issue at hand, redirecting the discussion to personal faults rather than addressing the argument itself.\"]", "time_sec": 20.591, "generation_time_seconds": 19.8928, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6914, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 17601, 22818, 279, 3668, 11, 45994, 11, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 279, 5693, 4751, 1091, 22818, 279, 5693, 5086, 13, 576, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 374, 458, 993, 4998, 68413, 3359, 389, 264, 1697, 594, 16614, 476, 11229, 429, 4990, 1992, 1573, 279, 49832, 315, 264, 1142, 646, 387, 6509, 11, 6423, 287, 279, 10219, 311, 279, 56690, 315, 825, 315, 279, 9677, 13, 576, 1376, 6672, 374, 429, 279, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 13666, 2337, 279, 5693, 11, 1393, 279, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 8573, 1573, 279, 5693, 12033, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument rather than attacking the argument itself. The poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. The key difference is that the ad hominem fallacy occurs during the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy happens before the argument begins.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.985796021494197, "g_worst_claim": 0.05251613947061392, "g_content": 1.8240805053710938, "g_traj_mean": 1.1366997957229614}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 458, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 323, 279, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 374, 438, 11017, 1447, 2082, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 17601, 22818, 279, 3668, 11, 45994, 11, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 279, 5693, 4751, 1091, 27020, 279, 5693, 5086, 13, 1084, 374, 264, 1352, 315, 24614, 5693, 1380, 279, 14704, 59