{"g_mean_claim": 0.7822547510045539, "g_worst_claim": 0.14660021993849012, "g_content": 1.3373545662301485, "g_traj_mean": 0.8758426904678345}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 264, 6946, 323, 264, 9798, 374, 429, 264, 6946, 374, 279, 2588, 3684, 315, 279, 9393, 594, 39612, 11, 11136, 14900, 389, 279, 7329, 315, 279, 9393, 476, 7025, 16533, 279, 17171, 11, 1393, 264, 9798, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 264, 2613, 6573, 476, 1051, 59880, 429, 646, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 68031, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 323, 26210, 525, 1865, 504, 23035, 13, 22406, 11, 26210, 646, 387, 281, 3818, 291, 6707, 11, 714, 23035, 4157, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between a rock and a stone is that a rock is the hard material of the earth's crust, typically exposed on the surface of the earth or sometimes underlying the soil, while a stone can be described as a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, but rocks cannot.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8146640635142781, "g_worst_claim": 0.43244389692942303, "g_content": 2.717505626189403, "g_traj_mean": 1.7298104763031006}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.75, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "375", "question": "what is dmso used for", "gt": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used in a variety of ways both industrially and medically. Industrially, it is used as an antifreeze and a solvent for numerous chemicals. Medically, DMSO is applied to the skin as an anti-inflammatory and general pain reliever, most commonly for muscles and joints. It is also used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, and skin ulcers. DMSO has the unique ability to penetrate skin and tissue, allowing it to enter the bloodstream.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has been used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage. It has also been studied for its potential in treating skin ulcers and burns.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has been used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage. It has also been studied for its potential in treating skin ulcers and burns.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has been used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage. It has also been studied for its potential in treating skin ulcers and burns.\", \"Based on the given passages, DMSO is used for a wide range of purposes including industrial uses such as an antifreeze and a solvent for chemicals. In the medical field, DMSO is used for its ability to penetrate skin and tissue, enter the bloodstream, relieve pain, reduce swelling and inflammation, and promote healing. It is frequently used for muscles and joints pain relief and has been applied for burns, scleroderma, and other medical ailments. Several studies have documented its use in cases of soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns, indicating its effectiveness in promoting recovery.\", \"Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical applications. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial settings. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is also used to promote healing, with reported benefits for minor cuts, burns, and soft tissue damage. Some studies have documented its effectiveness in treating local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns.\", \"Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a variety of purposes, including:\\n\\n1. Industrial uses as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals.\\n2. Medical applications including:\\n   - Pain relief, reducing pain and inflammation.\\n   - Treatment for burns and other skin conditions.\\n   - General pain relief for muscles and joints.\\n   - Use in promoting healing of soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns.\\n3. It has a remarkable ability to penetrate skin and tissue and enter the bloodstream, aiding in its medical applications.\"]", "time_sec": 20.624, "generation_t