ns, and soft tissue damage. Some studies have documented its effectiveness in treating local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.258537572224935, "g_worst_claim": 0.41108159224192303, "g_content": 2.3387106115167793, "g_traj_mean": 1.2414757013320923}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 320, 12927, 41872, 25774, 15011, 577, 8, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 8045, 315, 9895, 11, 2670, 1447, 16, 13, 24545, 5711, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 68896, 369, 25266, 624, 17, 13, 12939, 8357, 2670, 510, 256, 481, 34467, 15957, 11, 17719, 6646, 323, 36040, 624, 256, 481, 30869, 369, 43054, 323, 1008, 6787, 4682, 624, 256, 481, 3251, 6646, 15957, 369, 23648, 323, 34258, 624, 256, 481, 5443, 304, 22136, 21052, 315, 8413, 19847, 5557, 11, 2205, 19847, 4545, 11, 6787, 8557, 16832, 11, 323, 43054, 624, 18, 13, 1084, 702, 264, 22804, 5726, 311, 63755, 6787, 323, 19847, 323, 3725, 279, 99116, 11, 85287, 304, 1181, 6457, 8357, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Industrial uses as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals.\n2. Medical applications including:\n   - Pain relief, reducing pain and inflammation.\n   - Treatment for burns and other skin conditions.\n   - General pain relief for muscles and joints.\n   - Use in promoting healing of soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns.\n3. It has a remarkable ability to penetrate skin and tissue and enter the bloodstream, aiding in its medical applications.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3986309865137914, "g_worst_claim": 0.06803437074025472, "g_content": 1.93106324332101, "g_traj_mean": 1.1953998804092407}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.3, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "380", "question": "what is dmso used for", "gt": "Based on the given passages, DMSO is used for various purposes, including:\n\n1. Industrial uses: As an antifreeze and solvent for a wide range of chemicals.\n2. Medical uses: To relieve pain, reduce swelling and inflammation, promote healing, and treat a variety of medical ailments such as burns, scleroderma, and soft tissue damage.\n3. Pain relief: For muscles and joints, and as a general pain reliever applied to the skin.\n4. Skin care: To penetrate skin and tissue and enter the bloodstream.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is DMSO used for?\" can be summarized as: DMSO is used for various industrial, medical, and personal care purposes, including pain relief, wound healing, and skin care.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has been used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage. It has also been studied for its potential in treating skin ulcers and burns.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has been used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage. It has also been studied for its potential in treating skin ulcers and burns.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has been used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage. It has also been studied for its potential in treating skin ulcers and burns.\", \"Based on the given passages, DMSO is used for various medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and a solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is also effective for treating burns and other soft tissue damages, and has been shown to promote healing. It has been used for conditions such as scleroderma. DMSO is generally used by applying it to the skin to penetrate and enter the bloodstream, providing a wide range of medical benefits.\", \"Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) has a wide range of uses. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent in industrial applications. In medical contexts, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and manage inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief. DMSO is also used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damages. It enters the bloodstream and is used to penetrate skin and tissue, aiding in the treatment of various medical ailments such as burns, scleroderma, and skin ulcers.\", \"Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, inflammation, and treat various medical ailments. It is particularly effective in reducing pain and inflammation in muscles and joints when applied topically. DMSO is also used to promote healing of soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns.\"]", "time_sec": 20.755, "generation_time_seconds": 19.7796, "selection_time_seconds": 0.965, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 320, 12927, 41872, 25774, 15011, 577, 8, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 6884, 2088, 315, 6457, 9895, 13, 1084, 374, 1483, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 68896, 369, 25266, 304, 12785, 8357, 13, 758, 15712, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 1483, 311, 47739, 6646, 11, 7949, 54207, 11, 323, 36040, 13, 1084, 374, 7945, 7373, 369, 15747, 323, 10284, 6646, 15957, 979, 9251, 1909, 2673, 13, 422, 4826, 46, 702, 1012, 1483, 311, 11926, 21052, 369, 8922, 15104, 11, 43054, 11, 323, 1008, 8413, 19847, 5557, 13, 1084, 702, 1083, 1012, 19476, 369, 1181, 4650, 304, 26625, 6787, 8557, 16832, 323, 43054, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has been used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage. It has also been studied for its potential in treating skin ulcers and burns.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9560490599158595, "g_worst_claim": 0.3374723196029663, "g_content": 1.7195499254309612, "g_traj_mean": 0.9950096607208252}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 1483, 369, 5257, 6457, 9895, 13, 1084, 374, 1483, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 264, 68896, 369, 25266, 304, 12785, 8357, 13, 758, 15712, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 1483, 311, 47739, 6646, 11, 7949, 54207, 11, 323, 36040, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 7373, 369, 26625, 43054, 323, 1008, 8413, 19847, 25129, 11, 323, 702, 1012, 6839, 311, 11926, 21052, 13, 1084, 702, 1012, 1483, 369, 4682, 1741, 438, 56119, 261, 4316, 1728, 13, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 8789, 1483, 553, 18950, 432, 311, 279, 6787, 311, 63755, 323, 3725, 279, 99116, 11, 8241, 264, 6884, 2088, 315, 6457, 7567, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, DMSO is used for various medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and a solvent for chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is also effective for treating burns and other soft tissue damages, and has been shown to promote healing. It has been used for conditions such as scleroderma. DMSO is generally used by applying it to the skin to penetrate and enter the bloodstream, providing a wide range of medical benefits.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7855874482173464, "g_worst_claim": 0.3374723196029663, "g_content": 1.6364368091930042, "g_traj_mean": 0.8915217518806458}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 320, 12927, 41872, 25774, 15011, 577, 8, 702, 264, 6884, 2088, 315, 5711, 13, 1084, 374, 1483, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 68896, 304, 12785, 8357, 13, 758, 6457, 37597, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 1483, 311, 47739, 6646, 11, 7949, 54207, 11, 323, 10091, 36040, 13, 1084, 374, 7945, 7373, 369, 15747, 323, 10284, 6646, 15957, 13, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 1083, 1483, 311, 11926, 21052, 369, 8922, 15104, 11, 43054, 11, 323, 1008, 8413, 19847, 25129, 13, 1084, 28833, 279, 99116, 323, 374, 1483, 311, 63755, 6787, 323, 19847, 11, 85287, 304, 279, 6380, 315, 5257, 6457, 81807, 1741, 438, 43054, 11, 56119, 261, 4316, 1728, 11, 323, 6787, 8557, 16832, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) has a wide range of uses. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent in industrial applications. In medical contexts, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and manage inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief. DMSO is also used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damages. It enters the bloodstream and is used to penetrate skin and tissue, aiding in the treatment of various medical ailments such as burns, scleroderma, and skin ulcers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0437973062593078, "g_worst_claim": 0.3374723196029663, "g_content": 1.9532365065354567, "g_traj_mean": 1.029317855834961}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 320, 12927, 41872, 25774, 15011, 577, 8, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 6884, 2088, 315, 6457, 9895, 13, 1084, 374, 1483, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 68896, 369, 5257, 25266, 304, 12785, 8357, 13, 758, 15712, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 1483, 311, 47739, 6646, 11, 7949, 54207, 11, 36040, 11, 323, 4228, 5257, 6457, 81807, 13, 1084, 374, 7945, 7373, 304, 17719, 6646, 323, 36040, 304, 23648, 323, 34258, 979, 9251, 1909, 2673, 13, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 1083, 1483, 311, 11926, 21052, 315, 8413, 19847, 5557, 11, 2205, 19847, 4545, 11, 6787, 8557, 16832, 11, 323, 43054, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, inflammation, and treat various medical ailments. It is particularly effective in reducing pain and inflammation in muscles and joints when applied topically. DMSO is also used to promote healing of soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.453029670305724, "g_worst_claim": 0.3374723196029663, "g_content": 1.9425660736706791, "g_traj_mean": 1.0940550565719604}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.12, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "381", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "pred": "1. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n2. Click on the Sort option.\n3. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n4. In the Sort By dropdown menu, choose the column you want to sort (e.g., Product column, column B).\n5. If you want to sort in alphabetical order, select the 'A to Z' option.\n6. Click on the OK button. The data in that column will now be sorted alphabetically.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n2. Click on the Sort option.\n3. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n4. In the Sort By dropdown menu, choose the column you want to sort (e.g., Product column, column B).\n5. If you want to sort in alphabetical order, select the 'A to Z' option.\n6. Click on the OK button. The data in that column will now be sorted alphabetically.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n\\nAlternatively, you can use a tool like Kutools for Excel, which includes a Sort Sheets tool that can sort all worksheets easily.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the data you want to sort by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet should highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n5. Choose the column you want to sort by.\\n6. Click on the A to Z button to sort the data in alphabetical order.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can arrange the data in an Excel sheet alphabetically.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n2. Click on the Sort option.\\n3. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n4. In the Sort By dropdown menu, choose the column you want to sort (e.g., Product column, column B).\\n5. If you want to sort in alphabetical order, select the 'A to Z' option.\\n6. Click on the OK button. The data in that column will now be sorted alphabetically.\"]", "time_sec": 26.771, "generation_time_seconds": 25.7633, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0009, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 279, 21029, 10834, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 686, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 624, 20, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 3241, 11, 3293, 279, 821, 429, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 553, 13, 758, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 8, 304, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 4292, 21, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 13, 4695, 979, 498, 470, 311, 279, 45886, 11, 279, 821, 1265, 387, 10615, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.497311783468924, "g_worst_claim": 0.10901272296905518, "g_content": 1.8118797860494473, "g_traj_mean": 1.5056190490722656}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 382, 92014, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 5392, 1075, 730, 1535, 3069, 369, 21029, 11, 892, 5646, 264, 15967, 60472, 5392, 429, 646, 3378, 678, 67525, 6707, 13, 151645], "pred": "Alternatively, you can use a tool like Kutools for Excel, which includes a Sort Sheets tool that can sort all worksheets easily.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5809577815463198, "g_worst_claim": 0.07797764539718628, "g_content": 2.4236220139723557, "g_traj_mean": 1.6748549938201904}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 821, 498, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 1265, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 624, 20, 13, 22201, 279, 3250, 498, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 624, 21, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 362, 311, 1863, 3137, 311, 3378, 279, 821, 304, 83298, 1973, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 30893, 279, 821, 304, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can arrange the data in an Excel sheet alphabetically.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0118313172862232, "g_worst_claim": 0.06977903842926025, "g_content": 1.4914356030915912, "g_traj_mean": 1.1192731857299805}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 624, 19, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 3216, 20389, 5022, 11, 5157, 279, 3250, 498, 1366, 311, 3378, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 5643, 3250, 11, 3250, 425, 4292, 20, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 3378, 304, 83298, 1973, 11, 3293, 279, 364, 32, 311, 1863, 6, 2999, 624, 21, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 13, 576, 821, 304, 429, 3250, 686, 1431, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n2. Click on the Sort option.\n3. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n4. In the Sort By dropdown menu, choose the column you want to sort (e.g., Product column, column B).\n5. If you want to sort in alphabetical order, select the 'A to Z' option.\n6. Click on the OK button. The data in that column will now be sorted alphabetically.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3009841176312007, "g_worst_claim": 0.017024051398038864, "g_content": 1.4614860424097034, "g_traj_mean": 1.014825463294983}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "382", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Passage 3 provides the necessary information to answer the question. To arrange an excel sheet alphabetically, click on the Select All button, switch to the Data tab, locate the Sort & Filter group, click on the Sort option, and then select the desired column to sort by.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can arrange your Excel sheet in alphabetical order.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can arrange your Excel sheet in alphabetical order.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the data you wish to sort in the sheet.\\n2. Go to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\\n3. Locate the Sort & Filter group and click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name.\\n5. Choose the column you want to sort by.\\n6. Click on the OK button or press Enter to perform the sort.\\n\\nThe passage does not specifically mention what column to sort by, so you would need to choose the column that corresponds to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps using Kutools for Excel:\\n\\n1. Open Kutools for Excel and select the \\\"Sort Sheets\\\" tool.\\n2. Select the data you wish to sort by, in this example, the Product column (column B).\\n3. Choose the desired sorting order (A to Z).\\n4. Click on the \\\"OK\\\" button to apply the sorting.\\n\\nAlternatively, you can use the built-in Excel functions:\\n\\n1. Select all the cells in your worksheet.\\n2. Switch to the \\\"Data\\\" tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n4. Select the column by name from the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu.\\n5. Choose the sorting order (A to Z).\\n6. Click \\\"OK\\\" to apply the sorting.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the cells in your worksheet by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells, confirming they are selected.\\n2. Navigate to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon. Within the Data tab, locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group.\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option to activate the sort function.\\n4. In the Sort By drop-down menu, select the column you wish to sort by, ensuring it corresponds to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can arrange your Excel sheet in alphabetical order.\"]", "time_sec": 27.109, "generation_time_seconds": 26.1167, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9846, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 279, 21029, 10834, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 686, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 624, 20, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 3241, 11, 3293, 279, 821, 429, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 553, 13, 758, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 8, 304, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 4292, 21, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 13, 4695, 979, 498, 470, 311, 279, 45886, 11, 279, 821, 1265, 387, 10615, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4570689049454977, "g_worst_claim": -0.006863538175821304, "g_content": 1.7939523836461508, "g_traj_mean": 1.481141448020935}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 821, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 304, 279, 10834, 624, 17, 13, 5994, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567