e \"Sort\" option.\n4. Select the column by name from the \"Sort By\" drop-down menu.\n5. Choose the sorting order (A to Z).\n6. Click \"OK\" to apply the sorting.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9007602460134081, "g_worst_claim": 0.08625642210245132, "g_content": 1.1485141802437697, "g_traj_mean": 0.7763305306434631}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 330, 3379, 2009, 1, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 1096, 686, 11167, 678, 279, 7761, 11, 48996, 807, 525, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 81739, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 13, 24236, 279, 2885, 5651, 11, 24523, 279, 330, 10231, 609, 12339, 1, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 1, 2999, 311, 20276, 279, 3378, 729, 624, 19, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 11, 3293, 279, 3250, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 553, 11, 22573, 432, 33210, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 30893, 697, 21029, 10834, 304, 83298, 1973, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can arrange your Excel sheet in alphabetical order.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7556499642220081, "g_worst_claim": 0.007146360352635384, "g_content": 1.1007552645099696, "g_traj_mean": 0.848634660243988}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 15.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "383", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an excel sheet alphabetical, one can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n5. The data should now be sorted in alphabetical order.", "pred": "After following these steps, the data in the selected column will be arranged alphabetically.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "After following these steps, the data in the selected column will be arranged alphabetically.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\\n\\n1. Click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\\n3. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by (in this example, column B).\\n4. Choose the sorting order (in this example, alphabetical order, A to Z).\\n5. Click on the OK button.\\n\\nAfter following these steps, the data in the selected column will be arranged alphabetically.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\\n\\n1. Open Microsoft Excel.\\n2. Select all the data you want to sort.\\n3. Go to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\\n4. Click on the Sort button.\\n5. Choose the column you want to sort by. In the example, the Product column (column B) was used.\\n6. Select the sort order (in this case, A to Z for alphabetical order).\\n7. Click on the OK button.\\n8. Return to the spreadsheet to see the data sorted alphabetically.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Data tab at the top of the Excel window.\\n2. In the Data tab, click on the Sort button.\\n3. In the Sort window, select the column by name that you want to sort alphabetically.\\n4. Choose whether you want to sort in ascending (A to Z) or descending (Z to A) order.\\n5. Click on the OK button to apply the sort.\\n\\nFor example, to sort the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z), you would select the \\\"Product\\\" column in the Sort window and then click on the OK button.\"]", "time_sec": 24.687, "generation_time_seconds": 23.556, "selection_time_seconds": 1.122, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 279, 21029, 10834, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 686, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 