{"id": "384", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\nPassage 1 suggests using Kutools for Excel, which provides a Sort Sheets tool to easily sort all worksheets in alphabetical order. However, if you prefer not to use macros or Kutools, Passage 2 provides an alternative method using the built-in Sort feature in Excel.\n\nTo sort an Excel sheet alphabetically using the built-in Sort feature, follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the data you wish to sort by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu and select the column you wish to sort by (e.g., Product column in alphabetical order - A to Z).\n5. Click OK.\n\nOnce you have completed these steps, the data in your Excel sheet will be sorted alphabetically.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide sufficient information to clarify how to arrange an Excel sheet numerically.", "pred": "For example, to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z), select the data that you wish to sort by, then click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "For example, to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z), select the data that you wish to sort by, then click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option.\\n3. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n4. Select the data that you wish to sort by in the Sort window.\\n5. Click on the OK button to sort the data alphabetically.\\n\\nFor example, to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z), select the data that you wish to sort by, then click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\\n\\n1. Select the data you want to sort.\\n2. Click on the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name, such as column B.\\n5. Click on the OK button.\\n6. The data should now be sorted alphabetically.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n1. Select all the cells in your worksheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option.\\n3. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n4. Choose the column you want to sort by from the drop-down menu.\\n5. Click on the A to Z option to sort the data in alphabetical order.\\n6. Click on the OK button to apply the sorting.\"]", "time_sec": 25.334, "generation_time_seconds": 24.4788, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8461, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 279, 21029, 10834, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 686, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 624, 20, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 3241, 11, 3293, 279, 821, 429, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 553, 13, 758, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 8, 304, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 4292, 21, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 13, 4695, 979, 498, 470, 311, 279, 45886, 11, 279, 821, 1265, 387, 10615, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4714087612921614, "g_worst_claim": 0.05830982327461243, "g_content": 1.7829993643411777, "g_traj_mean": 1.4868266582489014}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 624, 19, 13, 8427, 279, 821, 429, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 553, 304, 279, 15967, 3241, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 311, 3378, 279, 821, 27790, 2673, 382, 2461, 3110, 11, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 8, 304, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 701, 3293, 279, 821, 429, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 553, 11, 1221, 4205, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 13, 4695, 979, 498, 470, 311, 279, 45886, 11, 279, 821, 1265, 387, 10615, 13, 151645], "pred": "For example, to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z), select the data that you wish to sort by, then click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4170291392361518, "g_worst_claim": 0.05830982327461243, "g_content": 1.9000481893849928, "g_traj_mean": 1.4691776037216187}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 821, 498, 1366, 311, 3378, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 11, 1741, 438, 3250, 425, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 624, 21, 13, 576, 821, 1265, 1431, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\n1. Select the data you want to sort.\n2. Click on the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name, such as column B.\n5. Click on the OK button.\n6. The data should now be sorted alphabetically.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9533118152639433, "g_worst_claim": -0.05311089328357151, "g_content": 0.9978218078613281, "g_traj_mean": 0.7568164467811584}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 686, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 624, 19, 13, 22201, 279, 3250,