{"id": "385", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\nPassage 2:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. Select the data that you wish to sort by (in this case, the Product column (column B)) and choose alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings to select all the cells in the worksheet.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n\nTherefore, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can use either method described above.", "pred": "1. Select the data you want to sort by clicking on the \"Select All\" button, which highlights all the cells in the worksheet.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\n3. Locate the \"Sort & Filter\" group and click on the \"Sort\" option.\n4. Click on the \"Sort By\" drop-down menu and select the column name by which you want to sort the data; in this example, it's column B.\n5. Choose the sort order, which is \"A to Z\" for alphabetical order.\n6. Click on the \"OK\" button to sort the data according to the selected column and order.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Select the data you want to sort by clicking on the \"Select All\" button, which highlights all the cells in the worksheet.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\n3. Locate the \"Sort & Filter\" group and click on the \"Sort\" option.\n4. Click on the \"Sort By\" drop-down menu and select the column name by which you want to sort the data; in this example, it's column B.\n5. Choose the sort order, which is \"A to Z\" for alphabetical order.\n6. Click on the \"OK\" button to sort the data according to the selected column and order.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in the Excel sheet by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n5. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n6. Click on the OK button. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. Open the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\\n2. Click on the Sort option located in the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Select the column you wish to sort by from the Sort By drop-down menu.\\n4. Ensure that the sorting order is set to \\\"A to Z\\\" (alphabetical order).\\n5. Click on the OK button to sort the data.\\n\\nNow, when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be arranged alphabetically according to the selected column.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\\n\\n1. Select the data you want to sort by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button, which highlights all the cells in the worksheet.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon.\\n3. Locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group and click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n4. Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu and select the column name by which you want to sort the data; in this example, it's column B.\\n5. Choose the sort order, which is \\\"A to Z\\\" for alphabetical order.\\n6. Click on the \\\"OK\\\" button to sort the data according to the selected column and order.\", \"Based on the given passages, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the data you wish to sort by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet should highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n\\n2. Switch to the \\\"Data\\\" tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu and select the column by name that you want to sort. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n\\n4. Choose the sorting order you prefer, such as alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n\\n5. Click on the \\\"OK\\\" button.\\n\\nNow your data should be sorted alphabetically according to the selected column.\"]", "time_sec": 25.751, "generation_time_seconds": 25.019, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7237, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 279, 21029, 10834, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 8427, 2009, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 576, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 686, 11167, 311, 7683, 807, 2299, 4091, 624, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 2999, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 15967, 3216, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 624, 20, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 3241, 11, 3293, 279, 821, 429, 498, 6426,