{"id": "387", "question": "what is the normal b natriuretic peptide", "gt": "The normal B-type Natriuretic Peptide (BNP) refers to a low amount of the BNP hormone found in the blood, produced by the heart as a measure of how well it is working. The exact normal values are not stated but are suggested to be a guide and can vary based on factors like age and gender, with values tending to increase with age and being higher in women. High levels of BNP are indicative of heart failure, with higher levels at diagnosis suggesting a more severe condition. Conversely, low levels tend to exclude heart failure.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the normal levels of brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) are not explicitly stated. However, it is mentioned that only a low amount of BNP is normally found in the blood. This suggests that the normal range is one in which BNP levels are low.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the normal levels of brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) are not explicitly stated. However, it is mentioned that only a low amount of BNP is normally found in the blood. This suggests that the normal range is one in which BNP levels are low.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) levels are not explicitly stated. The passages only mention that BNP values tend to increase with age and are higher in women than men, and that low levels tend to exclude heart failure.\", \"Based on the given passages, a normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) test result is a low amount of BNP found in the blood.\", \"Based on the given passages, the normal levels of brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) are not explicitly stated. However, it is mentioned that only a low amount of BNP is normally found in the blood. This suggests that the normal range is one in which BNP levels are low.\", \"Based on the given passages, the normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) levels vary by age and gender. The passages do not provide specific normal values.\"]", "time_sec": 12.289, "generation_time_seconds": 11.4243, "selection_time_seconds": 0.854, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 4622, 8109, 308, 2361, 552, 28050, 71149, 320, 15594, 47, 8, 5866, 525, 537, 20975, 10982, 13, 576, 46769, 1172, 6286, 429, 425, 26227, 2750, 8376, 311, 5263, 448, 4231, 323, 525, 5080, 304, 3198, 1091, 2953, 11, 323, 429, 3347, 5866, 8376, 311, 21687, 4746, 7901, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) levels are not explicitly stated. The passages only mention that BNP values tend to increase with age and are higher in women than men, and that low levels tend to exclude heart failure.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0533545109487714, "g_worst_claim": 0.23438658316930136, "g_content": 1.79686850088614, "g_traj_mean": 1.0488859415054321}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 4622, 8109, 308, 2361, 552, 28050, 71149, 320, 15594, 47, 8, 1273, 1102, 374, 264, 3347, 3311, 315, 425, 26227, 1730, 304, 279, 6543, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, a normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) test result is a low amount of BNP found in the blood.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6915705257501358, "g_worst_claim": 0.22276868422826132, "g_content": 1.6100051879882813, "g_traj_mean": 0.9605612754821777}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 4622, 5866, 315, 8109, 308, 2361, 552, 28050, 71149, 320, 15594, 47, 8, 525, 537, 20975, 10982, 13, 4354, 11, 432, 374, 9733, 429, 1172, 264, 3347, 3311, 315, 425, 26227, 374, 14279, 1730, 304, 279, 6543, 13, 1096, 13230, 429, 279, 4622, 2088, 374, 825, 304, 892, 425, 26227, 5866, 525, 3347, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the normal levels of brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) are not explicitly stated. However, it is mentioned that only a low amount of BNP is normally found in the blood. This suggests that the normal range is one in which BNP levels are low.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5609855236452923, "g_worst_claim": 0.23438658316930136, "g_content": 0.9791847229003906, "g_traj_mean": 0.6467525362968445}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 4622, 8109, 308, 2361, 552, 28050, 71149, 320, 15594, 47, 8, 5866, 13289, 553, 4231, 323, 9825, 13, 576, 46769, 653, 537, 3410, 3151, 4622, 2750, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) levels vary by age and gender. The passages do not provide specific normal values.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.41467295229783535, "g_worst_claim": 0.22276868422826132, "g_content": 0.6428881813498104, "g_traj_mean": 0.37231874465942383}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.64, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
