he given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 15.67, "generation_time_seconds": 14.4619, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1997, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 4622, 8109, 308, 2361, 552, 28050, 71149, 320, 15594, 47, 8, 5866, 525, 537, 20975, 10982, 13, 576, 46769, 1172, 6286, 429, 425, 26227, 2750, 8376, 311, 5263, 448, 4231, 323, 525, 5080, 304, 3198, 1091, 2953, 11, 323, 429, 3347, 5866, 8376, 311, 21687, 4746, 7901, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) levels are not explicitly stated. The passages only mention that BNP values tend to increase with age and are higher in women than men, and that low levels tend to exclude heart failure.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0533545109487714, "g_worst_claim": 0.23438658316930136, "g_content": 1.79686850088614, "g_traj_mean": 1.0488859415054321}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 4622, 8109, 308, 2361, 552, 28050, 71149, 320, 15594, 47, 8, 2750, 10007, 525, 1101, 264, 8474, 13, 576, 5785, 2088, 369, 425, 26227, 374, 537, 20975, 10982, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) values listed are just a guide. The reference range for BNP is not explicitly stated in the given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8730369415896678, "g_worst_claim": 0.21859999497731528, "g_content": 1.4472086164686415, "g_traj_mean": 1.1039434671401978}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 4622, 425, 26227, 2188, 374, 537, 20975, 10982, 714, 646, 387, 67595, 13, 576, 46769, 6286, 429, 425, 26227, 2750, 8376, 311, 5263, 448, 4231, 323, 525, 5080, 304, 3198, 1091, 2953, 13, 22406, 11, 3347, 5866, 315, 425, 26227, 8376, 311, 21687, 4746, 7901, 11, 1393, 1550, 5866, 4190, 279, 9362, 315, 4746, 7901, 11, 448, 5080, 5866, 18860, 264, 10960, 2971, 13, 15277, 11, 279, 4622, 425, 26227, 2188, 374, 4363, 311, 387, 3347, 11, 438, 16317, 553, 279, 5785, 2088, 9733, 304, 279, 1156, 21085, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, a normal BNP level is not explicitly stated but can be inferred. The passages mention that BNP values tend to increase with age and are higher in women than men. Additionally, low levels of BNP tend to exclude heart failure, while high levels suggest the presence of heart failure, with higher levels indicating a worse condition. Therefore, the normal BNP level is likely to be low, as indicated by the reference range mentioned in the first passage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9724949104827403, "g_worst_claim": 0.23438658316930136, "g_content": 1.480137176513672, "g_traj_mean": 1.0059237480163574}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 4622, 8109, 308, 2361, 552, 28050, 71149, 320, 15594, 47, 8, 1273, 10953, 279, 3311, 315, 279, 425, 26227, 35808, 304, 279, 6543, 13, 576, 4622, 2750, 320, 269, 5785, 2088, 8, 369, 425, 26227, 525, 1101, 264, 8474, 323, 8376, 311, 5263, 448, 4231, 11, 1660, 5080, 304, 3198, 1091, 2953, 13, 576, 4734, 4622, 425, 26227, 5866, 525, 537, 5189, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the normal brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) test measures the amount of the BNP hormone in the blood. The normal values (or reference range) for BNP are just a guide and tend to increase with age, being higher in women than men. The exact normal BNP levels are not specified in the given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0209151990300134, "g_worst_claim": 0.23438658316930136, "g_content": 1.6305566267533735, "g_traj_mean": 1.1601239442825317}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.56, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "395", "question": "why should we serve others", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"Why should we serve others?\"\n\nWe should serve others because it is a way to show love and kindness to everyone, even those who may not treat us well. Serving others is an expression of our love for God and our desire to be like Him. When we truly know God, our natural response is a desire to love and serve Him in return, and serving others is a way to do so. Additionally, serving others without self-serving motives and expecting nothing in return allows us to serve out of love and build stronger character muscles.\n\nTherefore, serving others is not only a way to show love and kindness, but it is also a way to deepen our relationship with God and grow in our faith.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a fundamental part of the Christian life, which is characterized by love and service to others. We should serve others in many ways, ensuring we use every opportunity to do so, as exemplified by the Second Mile Service where we go the extra mile for our customers and employers. This service should be seen in all aspects of our work and relationships. Serving others for those reasons, such as to serve ourselves, is not proper and does not align with true Christian principles. Instead, serving others out of love with no stipulations or expectations of anything in return leads to greater rewards and strengthens our character muscles.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a fundamental part of the Christian life, which is characterized by love and service to others. We should serve others in many ways, ensuring we use every opportunity to do so, as exemplified by the Second Mile Service where we go the extra mile for our customers and employers. This service should be seen in all aspects of our work and relationships. Serving others for those reasons, such as to serve ourselves, is not proper and does not align with true Christian principles. Instead, serving others out of love with no stipulations or expectations of anything in return leads to greater rewards and strengthens our character muscles.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a fundamental aspect of the Christian life, as taught in Matthew 22:39. The spirit of service should be seen in all aspects of our work, and we should use every opportunity to serve others, even if it means going the extra mile. Serving others is not just about doing good deeds, but also about building and strengthening our character muscles. When we serve others out of love with no stipulations or expectations of anything in return, our rewards are greater than if we were to serve with self-serving motives.\", \"Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a fundamental part of the Christian life, which is characterized by love and service to others. We should serve others in many ways, ensuring we use every opportunity to do so, as exemplified by the Second Mile Service where we go the extra mile for our customers and employers. This service should be seen in all aspects of our work and relationships. Serving others for those reasons, such as to serve ourselves, is not proper and does not align with true Christian principles. Instead, serving others out of love with no stipulations or expectations of anything in return leads to greater rewards and strengthens our character muscles.\", \"Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a Christian duty as stated in Matthew 22:39, which urges us to love our neighbor as ourselves. The Christian life is characterized by serving others with kindness and using every opportunity to do so, as mentioned in the passage about the Second Mile Service. Serving others is a way to fulfill our duty to God and to strengthen our character.\", \"Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a fundamental aspect of the Christian life, as described in Matthew 22:39. Serving others demonstrates love and kindness, and it should be evident in all aspects of our work, such as providing a Second Mile Service by going the extra mile for customers and employers. Additionally, serving others is a way to build and strengthen our character muscles and can lead to greater rewards than serving with self-serving motives. It is important to serve others for the right reasons, as serving with the intention of serving oneself is not proper service or love.\"]", "time_sec": 21.276, "generation_time_seconds": 20.0117, "selection_time_seconds": 1.255, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 582, 1265, 8683, 3800, 1576, 432, 374, 264, 15811, 12893, 315, 279, 8876, 2272, 11, 438, 15599, 304, 18939, 220, 17, 17, 25, 18, 24, 13, 576, 8913, 315, 2473, 1265, 387, 3884, 304, 678, 13566, 315, 1039, 975, 11, 323, 582, 1265, 990, 1449, 6638, 311, 8683, 3800, 11, 1496, 421, 432, 3363, 2087, 279, 4960, 14587, 13, 71643, 3800, 374, 537, 1101, 911, 3730, 1661, 53711, 11, 714, 1083, 911, 4752, 323, 47413, 1039, 3668, 23648, 13, 3197, 582, 8683, 3800, 700, 315, 2948, 448, 902, 42673, 7455, 476, 16665, 315, 4113, 304, 470, 11, 1039, 21160, 525, 7046, 1091, 421, 582, 1033, 311, 8683, 448, 656, 85986, 51040, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a fundamental aspect of the Christian life, as taught in Matthew 22:39. The spirit of service should be seen in all aspects of our work, and we should use every opportunity to serve others, even if it means going the extra mile. Serving others is not just about doing good deeds, but also about building and strengthening our character muscles. When we serve others out of love with no stipulations or expectations of anything in return, our rewards are greater than if we were to serve with self-serving motives.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3653923456545, "g_worst_claim": 0.15992676019668578, "g_content": 2.113666612274793, "g_traj_mean": 1.479402780532837}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 582, 1265, 8683, 3800, 1576, 432, 374, 264, 15811, 949, 315, 279, 8876, 2272, 11, 892, 374, 31871, 553, 2948, 323, 2473, 311, 3800, 13, 1205, 1265, 8683, 3800, 304, 1657, 5510, 11, 22573, 582, 990, 1449, 6638, 311, 653, 773, 11, 438, 37939, 1870, 553, 279, 10440, 38597, 5362, 1380, 582, 728, 279, 4960, 14587, 369, 1039, 6310, 323, 22426, 13, 1096, 2473, 1265, 387, 3884, 304, 678, 13566, 315, 1039, 975, 323, 11871, 13, 71643, 3800, 369, 1846, 7966, 11, 1741, 438, 311, 8683, 13217, 11, 374, 537, 6169, 323, 1558, 537, 5285, 448, 830, 8876, 16170, 13, 12090, 11, 13480, 3800, 700, 315, 2948, 448, 902, 42673, 7455, 476, 16665, 315, 4113, 304, 470, 11508, 311, 7046, 21160, 323, 95831, 1039, 3668, 23648, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a fundamental part of the Christian life, which is characterized by love and service to others. We should serve others in many ways, ensuring we use every opportunity to do so, as exemplified by the Second Mile Service where we go the extra mile for our customers and employers. This service should be seen in all aspects of our work and relationships. Serving others for those reasons, such as to serve ourselves, is not proper and does not align with true Christian principles. Instead, serving others out of love with no stipulations or expectations of anything in return leads to greater rewards and strengthens our character muscles.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5473879326108904, "g_worst_claim": 0.2981828848520915, "g_content": 2.5825707387115995, "g_traj_mean": 1.7570452690124512}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 582, 1265, 8683, 3800, 1576, 432, 374, 264, 8876, 14189, 438, 10982, 304, 18939, 220, 17, 17, 25, 18, 24, 11, 892, 62837, 601, 311, 2948, 1039, 9565, 438, 13217, 13, 576, 8876, 2272, 374, 31871, 553, 13480, 3800, 448, 44872, 323, 1667, 1449, 6638, 311, 653, 773, 11, 438, 9733, 304, 279, 21085, 911, 279, 10440, 38597, 5362, 13, 71643, 3800, 374, 264, 1616, 311, 20423, 1039, 14189, 311, 4264, 323, 311, 19681, 1039, 3668, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a Christian duty as stated in Matthew 22:39, which urges us to love our neighbor as ourselves. The Christian life is characterized by serving others with kindness and using every opportunity to do so, as mentioned in the passage about the Second Mile Service. Serving others is a way to fulfill our duty to God and to strengthen our character.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0150859349192467, "g_worst_claim": 0.21265819072723388, "g_content": 1.897234598795573, "g_traj_mean": 1.0207629203796387}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 582, 1265, 8683, 3800, 1576, 432, 374, 264, 15811, 12893, 315, 279, 8876, 2272, 11, 438, 7481, 304, 18939, 220, 17, 17, 25, 18, 24, 13, 71643, 3800, 31116, 2948, 323, 44872, 11, 323, 432, 1265, 387, 29476, 304, 678, 13566, 315, 1039, 975, 11, 1741, 438, 8241, 264, 10440, 38597, 5362, 553, 2087, 279, 4960, 14587, 369, 6310, 323, 22426, 13, 22406, 11, 13480, 3800, 374, 264, 1616, 311, 1936, 323, 19681, 1039, 3668, 23648, 323, 646, 2990, 311, 7046, 21160, 1091, 13480, 448, 656, 85986, 51040, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 311, 8683, 3800, 369, 279, 1290, 7966, 11, 438, 13480, 448, 279, 14602, 315, 13480, 56569, 374, 537, 6169, 2473, 476, 2948, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, we should serve others because it is a fundamental aspect of the Christian life, as described in Matthew 22:39. Serving others demonstrates love and kindness, and it should be evident in all aspects of our work, such as providing a Second Mile Service by going the extra mile for customers and employers. Additionally, serving others is a way to build and strengthen our character muscles and can lead to greater rewards than serving with self-serving motives. It is important to serve others for the right reasons, as serving with the intention of serving oneself is not proper service or love.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3340322623246137, "g_worst_claim": 0.2981828848520915, "g_content": 2.2476013728550504, "g_traj_mean": 1.5723140239715576}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.47, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "399", "question": "temperature bucharest", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the current temperature in Bucharest, Romania is:\n\nPassage 1 does not provide real-time weather data, so I cannot find the current temperature in Bucharest.\n\nPassage 2 provides a map of UK weather warnings and flood warnings, but it does not provide information on the temperature in Bucharest.\n\nPassage 3 provides general information about the climate in Bucharest, including the average monthly weather patterns, but it does not provide the current temperature. Therefore, I am unable to answer your question based on these passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, Bucharest, Romania has a humid continental climate. Winters can get windy and temperatures often dip below 0 °Celsius (32 °Fahrenheit), sometimes even dropping to minus 20 °C (4 °F). In summer (July and August), the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F). Temperatures often reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, Bucharest, Romania has a humid continental climate. Winters can get windy and temperatures often dip below 0 °Celsius (32 °Fahrenheit), sometimes even dropping to minus 20 °C (4 °F). In summer (July and August), the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F). Temperatures often reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, Bucharest, Romania has a humid continental climate. Winters can get windy and temperatures often dip below 0 °Celsius (32 °Fahrenheit), sometimes even dropping to minus 20 °C (4 °F). In summer (July and August), the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F). Temperatures often reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.\", \"Based on the given passages, the temperature in Bucharest, Romania can vary significantly throughout the year. In winter, 