{"id": "401", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "To remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, first remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle. Additionally, there's a pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place which needs to be removed. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off. Ensure to remove all screws and clips in the door panel and gently pull the panel away from the frame. Finally, remove any wiring connections and the panel will come off the frame.", "pred": "To remove the rear door panel in your 2006 Chevy HHR, follow these steps:\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\n4. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel using a screwdriver.\n5. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n6. Remove any wiring connections.\n7. The panel will come off the frame.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To remove the rear door panel in your 2006 Chevy HHR, follow these steps:\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\n4. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel using a screwdriver.\n5. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n6. Remove any wiring connections.\n7. The panel will come off the frame.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\\n8. The panel will come off the frame.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in your 2006 Chevy HHR, follow these steps:\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\\n4. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel using a screwdriver.\\n5. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n6. Remove any wiring connections.\\n7. The panel will come off the frame.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel of a 2006 Chevrolet Impala, follow these steps:\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the door.\\n5. Remove any screws and clips in the door panel using a screwdriver.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Disconnect any wiring connections.\\n8. The door panel will come off the frame.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in your 2006 Chevy HHR, follow these steps:\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\\n4. Use a screwdriver to remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n5. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n6. If there are any wiring connections, remove them.\\n7. The door panel will come off the frame.\\nAn instructional video is also available that shows the entire process and where everything is located.\"]", "time_sec": 22.452, "generation_time_seconds": 21.5956, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8453, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 6945, 504, 264, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 57298, 14390, 6053, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 1378, 44922, 7407, 4766, 279, 6006, 6815, 10525, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 21966, 304, 279, 6149, 315, 279, 4766, 6006, 3705, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 279, 8983, 389, 279, 15955, 6821, 315, 279, 6006, 429, 9982, 279, 6945, 304, 1992, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 264, 6006, 6945, 16652, 5392, 311, 81279, 279, 6006, 6945, 1007, 279, 14639, 6006, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 678, 44922, 323, 26111, 304, 279, 6006, 6945, 624, 21, 13, 479, 4402, 6815, 279, 6945, 3123, 504, 279, 4034, 624, 22, 13, 10783, 894, 18827, 13234, 624, 23, 13, 576, 6945, 686, 2525, 1007, 279, 4034, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\n8. The panel will come off the frame.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6392606279273116, "g_worst_claim": -0.04344696303208669, "g_content": 2.010586866691931, "g_traj_mean": 1.4197711944580078}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 279, 14639, 6006, 6945, 304, 697, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 57298, 472, 17088, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 1378, 44922, 7407, 4766, 279, 6006, 6815, 10525, 323, 279, 21966, 304, 279, 6149, 315, 279,