{"id": "403", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "To remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle. You will also need to remove a pin on the outer edge of the door. Once these are removed, you can use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel from a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove two screws located inside the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle. Additionally, there's a pin on the outer edge of the door that needs to be removed. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel from a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove two screws located inside the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle. Additionally, there's a pin on the outer edge of the door that needs to be removed. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\\n8. The panel will come off the frame.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the rear door.\\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\\nThe video by 1A Auto is also helpful for this process and shows where everything is located.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevrolet HHR, you will need to:\\n1. Remove two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove one screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove a pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\\n5. Remove any wiring connections.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n\\nThe process involves multiple steps, and an instructional video has been enclosed below to show where everything is located.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel from a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove two screws located inside the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle. Additionally, there's a pin on the outer edge of the door that needs to be removed. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off.\"]", "time_sec": 19.445, "generation_time_seconds": 18.486, "selection_time_seconds": 0.95, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 6945, 504, 264, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 57298, 14390, 6053, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 1378, 44922, 7407, 4766, 279, 6006, 6815, 10525, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 21966, 304, 279, 6149, 315, 279, 4766, 6006, 3705, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 279, 8983, 389, 279, 15955, 6821, 315, 279, 6006, 429, 9982, 279, 6945, 304, 1992, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 264, 6006, 6945, 16652, 5392, 