{"id": "404", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "The passage provides step-by-step instructions for removing the rear door panel on a 2006 Chevy HHR. To perform this task, the passenger must locate and remove the two screws inside the door pull cup and the middle of the inside door handle. A pin on the outside edge of the door must also be removed using a door panel removal tool. Once all these steps are completed, the door panel can be carefully pulled away from the frame, taking care not to damage any wiring connections.\n\nAccordingly, the answer to the question is:\n\nRemoving the rear door panel on a 2006 Chevy HHR involves locating and removing the screws inside the door pull cup and the middle of the inside door handle, as well as removing the pin on the outside edge of the door using a door panel removal tool.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the two screws inside the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle.\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\n4. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\n5. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n6. Disconnect any wiring connections.\n7. The panel will come off the frame.\nAn instructional video is also provided that shows the entire process and where everything is located.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the two screws inside the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle.\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\n4. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\n5. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n6. Disconnect any wiring connections.\n7. The panel will come off the frame.\nAn instructional video is also provided that shows the entire process and where everything is located.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\\n8. The panel will come off the frame.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door, there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, which you will need to remove. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy Impala, you will need to follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the one screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, follow these steps:\\n1. Locate the two screws inside the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\\n4. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n5. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n6. Disconnect any wiring connections.\\n7. The panel will come off the frame.\\nAn instructional video is also provided that shows the entire process and where everything is located.\"]", "time_sec": 21.886, "generation_time_seconds": 20.6161, "selection_time_seconds": 1.2595, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 6945, 504, 264, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 57298, 14390, 6053, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 1378, 44922, 7407, 4766, 279, 6006, 6815, 10525, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 21966, 304, 279, 6149, 315, 279, 4766, 6006, 3705, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 279, 8983, 389, 279, 15955, 6821, 315, 279, 6006, 429, 9982, 279, 6945, 304, 1992, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 264, 6006, 6945, 16652, 5392, 311, 81279, 279, 6006, 6945, 1007, 279, 14639, 6006, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 678, 44922, 323, 26111, 304, 279, 6006, 6945, 624, 21, 13, 479, 4402, 6815, 279, 6945, 3123, 504, 279, 4034, 624, 22, 13, 10783, 894, 18827, 13234, 624, 23, 13, 576, 6945, 686, 2525, 1007, 279, 4034, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\n8. The panel will come off the frame.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6418607747313951, "g_worst_claim": -0.07119227449099223, "g_content": 2.0185020788392025, "g_traj_mean": 1.4118452072143555}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4057, 279, 14639, 6006, 6945, 304, 264, 22