{"id": "405", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you should follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\n\nIt is important to note that an instructional video is also available that shows the entire process and location of the screws and pin.", "pred": "Based on the given passages:\n\nTo remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\n1. Use a screwdriver to remove two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove another screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove a pin located on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages:\n\nTo remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\n1. Use a screwdriver to remove two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove another screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove a pin located on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\\n8. The panel will come off the frame.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel of a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\\n4. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n5. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n6. Remove any wiring connections.\\n7. The panel will come off the frame.\\nThe instructional video included below shows where everything is located and the entire process.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel from a 2006 Chevrolet HHR, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Disconnect any wiring connections.\\n\\nThese steps will allow you to successfully remove the rear door panel from your 2006 Chevrolet HHR.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\nTo remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\\n1. Use a screwdriver to remove two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove another screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove a pin located on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\"]", "time_sec": 20.348, "generation_time_seconds": 19.4