{"id": "406", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, you will need to:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin that holds the panel in place on the outer edge of the door.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\n5. Remove any wiring connections.\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\n\nAfter removing the screws and clips, you will be able to remove the door panel. It is recommended to watch an instructional video to see the process and locate the parts mentioned.", "pred": "This process is detailed in the video provided by 1A Auto, which also covers removing or replacing the interior door panel trim for various repairs on the Chevy Impala, model years 06, 07, 08, 09, 10, 11, and 12.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "This process is detailed in the video provided by 1A Auto, which also covers removing or replacing the interior door panel trim for various repairs on the Chevy Impala, model years 06, 07, 08, 09, 10, 11, and 12.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\\n8. The panel will come off the frame.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy Impala, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the rear door.\\n5. Remove any wiring connections.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\", \"To remove the door panel from a 2006 Chevy, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup.\\n2. Remove the screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n3. On the outer edge of the door, remove the pin that holds the panel in place.\\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the rear door.\\n5. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel using a screwdriver.\\n6. Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n7. Remove any wiring connections.\\n8. The panel should now come off the frame.\\n\\nIf you need further assistance, an instructional video is available below that shows this entire process and where everything is located.\", \"Based on the given passages, to remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup and the one in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n2. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n3. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off the HHR rear door.\\n4. Remove all screws and clips in the door panel and gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n5. Disconnect any wiring connections if present.\\n\\nThis process is detailed in the video provided by 1A Auto, which also covers removing or replacing the interior door panel trim for various repairs on the Chevy Impala, model years 06, 07, 08, 09, 10, 11, and 12.\"]", "time_sec": 24.105, "generation_time_seconds": 23.139, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9553, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715,