9, 61795, 1803, 5645, 11, 3421, 11, 323, 27235, 3080, 49247, 96577, 1352, 11, 911, 220, 17, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 220, 17, 4279, 10834, 63783, 624, 24, 13, 52074, 3080, 279, 96577, 1101, 3161, 311, 13876, 323, 525, 41854, 11, 911, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 16, 15, 13, 23931, 279, 96577, 389, 279, 63783, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 16, 16, 13, 23200, 279, 64310, 96577, 311, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 3553, 1105, 518, 3054, 9315, 369, 705, 311, 220, 17, 5555, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. If using a food processor, push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow it to cool completely before transferring the crumbs to an airtight container.\n7. If using a blender, place all ingredients into the blender carafe, cover, and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes.\n8. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans.\n9. Bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes.\n10. Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes.\n11. Transfer the cooled crumbs to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2343609637514705, "g_worst_claim": 0.1656281054019928, "g_content": 1.326408736202695, "g_traj_mean": 1.0289714336395264}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "410", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Torn pieces of bread are pushed through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n3. The crumbs are spread on a baking sheet.\n4. The sheet is baked in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. The sheet is shaken twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. After baking, the crumbs are removed from the oven and allowed to cool completely.\n\nAlternatively, according to passage 2, you can also make panko crumbs by:\n\n1. Pushing chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n2. Spreading the crumbs on a baking sheet and baking at 300 degrees F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n3. Shaking the sheet twice during baking.\n4. Being careful not to let the crumbs brown.\n\nFinally, passage 3 provides a third method for making panko crumbs, which involves blending the ingredients in a blender carafe and baking them on half sheet pans until they are crisp and lightly browned.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and let the crumbs cool completely.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and let the crumbs cool completely.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and cool the crumbs completely.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, which should take about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and cool the crumbs completely before using them.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (300 degrees C).\\n2. Using a food processor, push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, which should take about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown while baking.\\n7. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely before transferring them to an airtight container.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and let the crumbs cool completely.\"]", "time_sec": 19.823, "generation_time_seconds": 19.0296, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7875, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 624, 17, 13, 22950, 26757, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 72323, 279, 27815, 10834, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 279, 27815, 10834, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 7010, 279, 96577, 6587, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and cool the crumbs completely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9678765812404733, "g_worst_claim": 0.178227961063385, "g_content": 1.4301237979177701, "g_traj_mean": 1.011435627937317}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 624, 17, 13, 22950, 26757, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 279, 96577, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 892, 1265, 1896, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 72323, 279, 27815, 10834, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 279, 27815, 10834, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 7010, 279, 96577, 6587, 1573, 1667, 1105, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, which should take about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and cool the crumbs completely before using them.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9003238120326241, "g_worst_claim": 0.1639479696750641, "g_content": 1.3577959654761143, "g_traj_mean": 0.9240514039993286}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 12091, 264, 3607, 17654, 11, 4484, 21145, 9666, 315, 16002, 476, 26757, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 892, 1265, 1896, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 72323, 279, 27815, 10834, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 624, 21, 13, 2823, 16585, 537, 311, 1077, 279, 96577, 13876, 1393, 27815, 624, 22, 13, 10783, 279, 27815, 10834, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 96577, 311, 7010, 6587, 1573, 49951, 1105, 311, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (300 degrees C).\n2. Using a food processor, push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, which should take about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. Be careful not to let the crumbs brown while baking.\n7. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely before transferring them to an airtight container.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9088250832363246, "g_worst_claim": 0.1639479696750641, "g_content": 1.4157190694437398, "g_traj_mean": 0.904684841632843}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 624, 17, 13, 22950, 26757, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 279, 96577, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 72323, 279, 27815, 10834, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 41047, 9058, 279, 96577, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 279, 27815, 10834, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 1077, 279, 96577, 7010, 6587, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and let the crumbs cool completely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9584867663136991, "g_worst_claim": 0.258937018258231, "g_content": 1.4194680575666756, "g_traj_mean": 0.9519113898277283}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "411", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted, 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n\nIf you want to store the panko crumbs for later use, you can transfer them to an airtight container and keep them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. Once baked, remove the crumbs from the oven and allow them to cool completely.\n7. Transfer the cooled crumbs to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. Once baked, remove the crumbs from the oven and allow them to cool completely.\n7. Transfer the cooled crumbs to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and cool the crumbs completely.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove the crumbs from the oven and cool them completely.\\n7. Transfer the cooled crumbs to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to make panko crumbs:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\\n2. Choose white bread and push chunks through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, which takes about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove the panko crumbs from the oven and cool them completely.\\n7. Store the cooled panko crumbs in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Once baked, remove the crumbs from the oven and allow them to cool completely.\\n7. Transfer the cooled crumbs to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\"]", "time_sec": 20.527, "generation_time_seconds": 19.7021, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8165, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 624, 17, 13, 22950, 26757, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 72323, 279, 27815, 10834, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 279, 27815, 10834, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 7010, 279, 96577, 6587, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and cool the crumbs completely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9829885755967771, "g_worst_claim": 0.3157624800999959, "g_content": 1.4517010187698622, "g_traj_mean": 1.017619013786316}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "toke