{"id": "422", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, a barcode symbology used extensively in multiple countries including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and in Europe. It is used for tracking trade items in stores. UPC consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. It is primarily used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in countries like the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and Europe for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that uniquely identify each trade item.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in countries like the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and Europe for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that uniquely identify each trade item.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.\", \"A Universal Product Code (UPC) is a 12-digit barcode symbology used widely in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Europe, and other countries for tracking trade items in stores.\", \"Based on the given passages, a Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, uniquely assigned to each trade it