{"id": "425", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, an UPDescription is:\n\n1. A barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores, consisting of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. (Passage 1)\n2. A process involving receiving a specimen bottle from a member, ensuring it contains a minimum of 30 milliliters of urine, initialing the label in the member's presence, and verifying the information on the label and DD Form 2624 (a military form). (Passage 2)\n3. A barcode partner that provides GS1 Originated UPC and EAN codes, as well as a toll-free number and positive customer reviews. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, a Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used for tracking trade items in various countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, a Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used for tracking trade items in various countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.\", \"Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, each assigned uniquely to each trade item. The UPC is part of the GS1 specifications and is the main barcode used for scanning trade items at the point of sale.\", \"Based on the given passages, a Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology widely used for tracking trade items in various countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.\", \"Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used for tracking trade items in stores in various countries, including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and Europe. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.\"]", "time_sec": 14.006, "generation_time_seconds": 13.2687, "selection_time_seconds": 0.732, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 95129, 320, 58278, 5643, 6119, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 13570, 1483, 304, 5257, 5837, 369, 14849, 6559, 3589, 304, 10533, 13, 1084, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 576, 95129, 374, 15503, 1483, 369, 35101, 6559, 3589, 518, 279, 1459, 315, 6278, 11, 438, 817, 35270, 16, 28703, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mea