{"id": "427", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "Based on the given passages, I am unable to answer the question \"What is a UPC description?\" as none of the passages provide a clear definition or explanation of what a UPC description is.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.\", \"Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a 12 numeric digit barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It was originated by GS1 and widely used in various countries including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and Europe. The barcode is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications. Additionally, it is mentioned that the UPC is also involved in the process of specimen bottle collection for urine samples, ensuring the bottle contains a minimum of 30 milliliters of urine, is not reopened, and verifying the data on DD 2624 before completing the collection process.\", \"Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.\", \"Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used for tracking trade items in various countries including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and Europe. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.\"]", "time_sec": 15.934, "generation_time_seconds": 15.1613, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7684, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 95129, 320, 58278, 5643, 6119, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 13570, 1483, 304, 5257, 5837, 369, 14849, 6559, 3589, 304, 10533, 13, 1084, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 576, 95129, 374, 15503, 1483, 369, 35101, 6559, 3589, 518, 279, 1459, 315, 6278, 11, 438, 817, 35270, 16, 28703, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6702726798431549, "g_worst_claim": 0.314641813437144, "g_content": 2.0425292121039496, "g_traj_mean": 1.411910