04, 10533, 13, 1084, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 576, 95129, 374, 15503, 1483, 369, 35101, 6559, 3589, 518, 279, 1459, 315, 6278, 11, 438, 817, 35270, 16, 28703, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4236098266561334, "g_worst_claim": 0.314641813437144, "g_content": 1.7142620086669922, "g_traj_mean": 1.3125427961349487}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 264, 95129, 320, 58278, 5643, 6119, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 13570, 1483, 369, 14849, 6559, 3589, 304, 5257, 5837, 2670, 279, 3639, 4180, 11, 6864, 11, 3639, 15072, 11, 8330, 11, 1532, 16911, 11, 323, 4505, 13, 1084, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 576, 95129, 374, 15503, 1483, 369, 35101, 6559, 3589, 518, 279, 1459, 315, 6278, 4092, 311, 35270, 16, 28703, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, a UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used for tracking trade items in various countries including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and Europe. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.086794337538872, "g_worst_claim": 0.314641813437144, "g_content": 1.9617382473415799, "g_traj_mean": 1.2721474170684814}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "428", "question": "how do twins happen", "gt": "Twins are two offspring produced by the same pregnancy. They can be either monozygotic (identical), meaning they develop from one zygote that splits and forms two embryos, or dizygotic (fraternal), meaning they develop from two different eggs with each being fertilized by its own sperm cell. Monoamniotic twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization. Dizygotic twin pregnancies are more likely in women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, aged between 30 and 40 years, of above average height and weight, and who have had several previous pregnancies.", "pred": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two main ways:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic twins (identical twins): This occurs when a single fertilized egg (zygote) splits into two embryos. This happens after the ninth day after fertilization. An example of this is conjoined twins, where the division of the developing zygote into two embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization, resulting in shared organs and a high mortality rate.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.\", \"Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two ways: as monozygotic twins or dizygotic twins. Monozygotic twins develop from a single egg that splits into two embryos within a short period after fertilization, usually within 8 days. This results in two genetically identical twins. Dizygotic twins develop from two separate eggs fertilized by two different sperm cells, leading to two genetically different twins. The likelihood of dizygotic twins occurring is slightly higher for women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.\", \"Based on the given passages, twins can happen in several ways:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic twins: This occurs when the division of the fertilized egg into two embryos happens after the ninth day. An example of this is conjoined twins, which occur 99% of the time within 8 days of fertilization and have a high mortality rate due to shared organs.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic twins: These twins develop from two different eggs, each fertilized by its own sperm cell. The likelihood of dizygotic twins is slightly higher in women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, between the ages of 30 and 40, who are greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.\", \"Based on the given passages, twins happen in the following ways:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic twins (identical twins) occur when the zygote splits into two embryos after the ninth day after fertilization, resulting in two genetically identical embryos.\\n2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins) develop when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells, leading to two genetically different embryos.\"]", "time_sec": 20.624, "generation_time_seconds": 19.8888, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7304, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 646, 3537, 304, 1378, 1887, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 320, 1713, 938, 43636, 1648, 1096, 13666, 979, 264, 3175, 35114, 1506, 18636, 320, 4246, 70, 1272, 8, 40467, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13, 1096, 8573, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 1283, 35114, 2022, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 390, 71154, 43636, 11, 1380, 279, 12804, 315, 279, 11220, 1147, 48765, 1272, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13666, 2878, 220, 23, 2849, 315, 35114, 2022, 11, 12942, 304, 6094, 35753, 323, 264, 1550, 28428, 4379, 382, 17, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 320, 1626, 266, 2978, 43636, 1648, 1096, 8573, 979, 1378, 8651, 18805, 525, 35114, 1506, 553, 1378, 2155, 39599, 7761, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 27061, 553, 9363, 1741, 438, 279, 5220, 594, 56878, 11, 4231, 11, 2608, 11, 4680, 11, 323, 3681, 81208, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 42286, 48765, 14212, 43636, 11, 892, 525, 10078, 803, 4363, 311, 12170, 304, 3198, 315, 4312, 11643, 36952, 11, 7945, 809, 269, 30429, 11, 879, 525, 1948, 279, 16639, 315, 220, 18, 15, 323, 220, 19, 15, 1635, 11, 7046, 1091, 5461, 2608, 323, 4680, 11, 323, 614, 1030, 3807, 3681, 81208, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1118992792623628, "g_worst_claim": 0.041259435506967396, "g_content": 1.5620854409892908, "g_traj_mean": 0.9982826113700867}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 646, 3537, 304, 1378, 5510, 25, 438, 39674, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 476, 42286, 48765, 14212, 43636, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 2225, 504, 264, 3175, 18636, 429, 40467, 1119, 1378, 88773, 2878, 264, 2805, 4168, 1283, 35114, 2022, 11, 5990, 2878, 220, 23, 2849, 13, 1096, 3059, 304, 1378, 50933, 19516, 43636, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 2225, 504, 1378, 8651, 18805, 35114, 1506, 553, 1378, 2155, 39599, 7761, 11, 6388, 311, 1378, 50933, 2155, 43636, 13, 576, 28636, 315, 42286, 48765, 14212, 43636, 30865, 374, 10078, 5080, 369, 3198, 315, 4312, 11643, 36952, 11, 5310, 809, 269, 30429, 11, 879, 525, 1948, 279, 16639, 315, 220, 18, 15, 323, 220, 19, 15, 1635, 11, 7046, 1091, 5461, 2608, 323, 4680, 11, 323, 614, 1030, 3807, 3681, 81208, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two ways: as monozygotic twins or dizygotic twins. Monozygotic twins develop from a single egg that splits into two embryos within a short period after fertilization, usually within 8 days. This results in two genetically identical twins. Dizygotic twins develop from two separate eggs fertilized by two different sperm cells, leading to two genetically different twins. The likelihood of dizygotic twins occurring is slightly higher for women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8638535073538921, "g_worst_claim": -0.04896731674671173, "g_content": 0.9802441804305367, "g_traj_mean": 0.7557777166366577}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 646, 3537, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 25, 1096, 13666, 979, 279, 12804, 315, 279, 35114, 1506, 18636, 1119, 1378, 88773, 8573, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 390, 71154, 43636, 11, 892, 12170, 220, 24, 24, 4, 315, 279, 882, 2878, 220, 23, 2849, 315, 35114, 2022, 323, 614, 264, 1550, 28428, 4379, 4152, 311, 6094, 35753, 382, 17, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 25, 4220, 43636, 2225, 504, 1378, 2155, 18805, 11, 1817, 35114, 1506, 553, 1181, 1828, 39599, 2779, 13, 576, 28636, 315, 42286, 48765, 14212, 43636, 374, 10078, 5080, 304, 3198, 315, 4312, 11643, 36952, 11, 5310, 809, 269, 30429, 11, 1948, 279, 16639, 315, 220, 18, 15, 323, 220, 19, 15, 11, 879, 525, 7046, 1091, 5461, 2608, 323, 4680, 11, 323, 614, 1030, 3807, 3681, 81208, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. Dizygotic twins: These twins develop from two different eggs, each fertilized by its own sperm cell. The likelihood of dizygotic twins is slightly higher in women of West African descent, especially Yoruba, between the ages of 30 and 40, who are greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1520636032255689, "g_worst_claim": 0.30414408445358276, "g_content": 1.6754461435171275, "g_traj_mean": 1.2400606870651245}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 3537, 304, 279, 2701, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 320, 1713, 938, 43636, 8, 12170, 979, 279, 1147, 48765, 1272, 40467, 1119, 1378, 88773, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 1283, 35114, 2022, 11, 12942, 304, 1378, 50933, 19516, 88773, 624, 17, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 320, 1626, 266, 2978, 43636, 8, 2225, 979, 1378, 8651, 18805, 525, 35114, 1506, 553, 1378, 2155, 39599, 7761, 11, 6388, 311, 1378, 50933, 2155, 88773, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, twins happen in the following ways:\n\n1. Monozygotic twins (identical twins) occur when the zygote splits into two embryos after the ninth day after fertilization, resulting in two genetically identical embryos.\n2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins) develop when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells, leading to two genetically different embryos.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.37349722262885837, "g_worst_claim": -0.05752138793468475, "g_content": 0.6269891871962436, "g_traj_mean": 0.44402623176574707}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.41, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "429", "question": "how do twins happen", "gt": "Twins can happen in two ways: monozygotic (identical) twins occur when one zygote splits into two embryos, while dizygotic (fraternal) twins happen when two different eggs are fertilized by two separate sperm cells. The likelihood of dizygotic twins is influenced by factors such as West African descent, being between 30 and 40 years old, being taller and heavier than average, and having had several previous pregnancies. Conjoined twins occur when the division of the zygote happens within 8 days of fertilization and can result in complications due to shared organs.", "pred": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. Each twin has their own unique set of genetic material, so dizygotic twins are not genetically identical but can look similar due to shared environmental factors. This type of pregnancy occurs more frequently in certain populations and among women who meet specific criteria, such as being of West African descent, between the ages of 30 and 40 years, having a greater than average height and weight, and having had several previous pregnancies.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. Each twin has their own unique set of genetic material, so dizygotic twins are not genetically identical but can look similar due to shared environmental factors. This type of pregnancy occurs more frequently in certain populations and among women who meet specific criteria, such as being of West African descent, between the ages of 30 and 40 years, having a greater than average height and weight, and having had several previous pregnancies.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two main ways:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic twins (identical twins): This occurs when a single fertilized egg (zygote) splits into two embryos. This happens after the ninth day after fertilization. An example of this is conjoined twins, where the division of the developing zygote into two embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization, resulting in shared organs and a high mortality rate.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.\", \"Based on the given passages, twins happen in two main ways based on the information provided:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic Twins: These twins are also known as identical twins. They develop from a single fertilized egg (zygote) that splits into two embryos. This splitting occurs after the ninth day after fertilization. This type of twin formation is rare, occurring in approximately 1% of all human births. An example mentioned is that for conjoined twins, which are a type of monozygotic twins, the division of the developing zygote into two embryos typically occurs within 8 days of fertilization.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic Twins: These are also known as fraternal twins. Unlike identical twins, they develop from two separate eggs that are each fertilized by a different sperm cell. This type of twin formation is more common, occurring in about 30% of all twin births. Factors that can increase the likelihood of dizygotic twin pregnancies include the woman being of West African descent (especially Yoruba), being between the ages of 30 and 40 years, being greater than average height and weight, and having had several previous pregnancies.\", \"Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two main ways:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic (identical) twins occur when the zygote splits into two embryos after the ninth day after fertilization. This results in conjoined twins, where 99% of the time the division occurs within 8 days of fertilization.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic (fraternal) twins develop when two different eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This process can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity (especially Yoruba), age, height, weight, and the number of previous pregnancies.\", \"Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two main ways:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic twins (identical twins): This occurs when a single fertilized egg (zygote) splits into two embryos before implantation. This type of division typically happens within the first 8 days after fertilization. As a result, monozygotic twins share almost all of their DNA and have identical genetic makeup.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. Each twin has their own unique set of genetic material, so dizygotic twins are not genetically identical but can look similar due to shared environmental factors. This type of pregnancy occurs more frequently in certain populations and among women who meet specific criteria, such as being of West African descent, between the ages of 30 and 40 years, having a greater than average height and weight, and having had several previous pregnancies.\"]", "time_sec": 26.205, "generation_time_seconds": 25.4212, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7787, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 646, 3537, 304, 1378, 1887, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 320, 1713, 938, 43636, 1648, 1096, 13666, 979, 264, 3175, 35114, 1506, 18636, 320, 4246, 70, 1272, 8, 40467, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13, 1096, 8573, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 1283, 35114, 2022, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 390, 71154, 43636, 11, 1380, 279, 12804, 315, 279, 11220, 1147, 48765, 1272, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13666, 2878, 220, 23, 2849, 315, 35114, 2022, 11, 12942, 304, 6094, 35753, 323, 264, 1550, 28428, 4379, 382, 17, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 320, 1626, 266, 2978, 43636, 1648, 1096, 8573, 979, 1378, 8651, 18805, 525, 35114, 1506, 553, 1378, 2155, 39599, 7761, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 27061, 553, 9363, 1741, 438, 279, 5220, 594, 56878, 11, 4231, 11, 2608, 11, 4680, 11, 323, 3681, 81208, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 42286, 48765, 14212, 43636, 11, 892, 525, 10078, 803, 4363, 311, 12170, 304, 3198, 315, 4312, 11643, 36952, 11, 7945, 809, 269, 30429, 11, 879, 525, 1948, 279, 16639, 315, 220, 18, 15, 323, 220, 19, 15, 1635, 11, 7046, 1091, 5461, 2608, 323, 4680, 11, 323, 614, 1030, 3807, 3681, 81208, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0996826915843827, "g_worst_claim": 0.04166950629307674, "g_content": 1.559881317481566, "g_traj_mean": 0.993072509765625}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 3537, 304, 1378, 1887, 5510, 3118, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 1447, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 65268, 25, 4220, 43636, 525, 1083, 3881, 438, 19516, 43636, 13, 2379, 2225, 504, 264, 3175, 35114, 1506, 18636, 320, 4246, 70, 1272, 8, 429, 40467, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13, 1096, 44373, 13666, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 1283, 35114, 2022, 13, 1096, 943, 315, 27397, 18003, 374, 8848, 11, 30865, 304, 13187, 220,