208, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. Each twin has their own unique set of genetic material, so dizygotic twins are not genetically identical but can look similar due to shared environmental factors. This type of pregnancy occurs more frequently in certain populations and among women who meet specific criteria, such as being of West African descent, between the ages of 30 and 40 years, having a greater than average height and weight, and having had several previous pregnancies.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6339558597607707, "g_worst_claim": 0.012381766851131733, "g_content": 0.7168330530966481, "g_traj_mean": 0.4632366895675659}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.09, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "430", "question": "how do twins happen", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how twins happen:\n\n* Monoamniotic twins: These twins occur when the split takes place after the ninth day after fertilization.\n* Conjoined twins: When the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs, it happens within 8 days of fertilization, and mortality is highest for conjoined twins due to the many complications resulting from shared organs.\n* Dizygotic twin pregnancies: These twins are slightly more likely to occur in women who are of West African descent (especially Yoruba), between the ages of 30 and 40, are taller and heavier than average, and have had several previous pregnancies.\n* Identical twins (monozygotic): These twins develop from one zygote, which splits and forms two embryos.\n* Fraternal twins (dizygotic): These twins develop from two different eggs, and each twin is fertilized by its own sperm cell.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages: The passage does not provide information on the exact timing or mechanism of twinning beyond what is mentioned above.", "pred": "These are the main types of twins explained in the given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These are the main types of twins explained in the given passages.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two main ways:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic twins (identical twins): This occurs when a single fertilized egg (zygote) splits into two embryos. This happens after the ninth day after fertilization. An example of this is conjoined twins, where the division of the developing zygote into two embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization, resulting in shared organs and a high mortality rate.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.\", \"Based on the given passages, twins can happen in two main ways: monozygotic (identical) and dizygotic (fraternal).\\n\\n1. Monozygotic twins: These twins develop from one zygote, which splits and forms two embryos. This process typically happens after the ninth day after fertilization.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic twins: These twins develop from two different eggs, each fertilized by its own sperm cell. Dizygotic twins are slightly more likely to occur when the following factors are present in the woman:\\n   - She is of West African descent, especially Yoruba.\\n   - She is between the age of 30 and 40 years.\\n   - She is greater than average height and weight.\\n   - She has had several previous pregnancies.\", \"Based on the given passages, twins can occur through two main types: monozygotic (identical) and dizygotic (fraternal).\\n\\n1. Monozygotic twins: This occurs when a single fertilized egg separates into two embryos early in the development process. This happens after the ninth day after fertilization. The passage mentions that 99% of the time, the division of the developing zygote into 2 embryos occurs within 8 days of fertilization, which is relatively early in the pregnancy.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic twins: This type of twin pregnancy is more likely when specific factors are present in the woman such as being of West African descent (especially Yoruba), being between the age of 30 and 40 years, being greater than average height and weight, and having had several previous pregnancies. The passage indicates that dizygotic twins develop from two different eggs, each fertilized by its own sperm cell. This means that each twin has its own genetic makeup, which is why they are often referred to as fraternal twins or non-identical twins.\", \"Based on the given passages, twins can happen in several ways:\\n\\n1. Monozygotic twins (identical): This occurs when a single fertilized egg splits into two embryos. The split typically happens within 8 days of fertilization, and both twins share the same genetic makeup.\\n\\n2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. Each twin has its own unique set of genes and can be of different genders.\\n\\n3. Conjoined twins: This is a rare occurrence where the division of the developing zygote into two embryos happens very early in the pregnancy, usually within 8 days of fertilization, and the twins share common organs and tissues.\\n\\n4. Monoamniotic twins: These twins develop in the same amniotic sac and share the same amniotic fluid. This happens when the split to form two embryos occurs after the ninth day after fertilization.\\n\\nThese are the main types of twins explained in the given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 26.625, "generation_time_seconds": 25.7603, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8601, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 646, 3537, 304, 1378, 1887, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 320, 1713, 938, 43636, 1648, 1096, 13666, 979, 264, 3175, 35114, 1506, 18636, 320, 4246, 70, 1272, 8, 40467, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13, 1096, 8573, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 1283, 35114, 2022, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 390, 71154, 43636, 11, 1380, 279, 12804, 315, 279, 11220, 1147, 48765, 1272, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13666, 2878, 220, 23, 2849, 315, 35114, 2022, 11, 12942, 304, 6094, 35753, 323, 264, 1550, 28428, 4379, 382, 17, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 320, 1626, 266, 2978, 43636, 1648, 1096, 8573, 979, 1378, 8651, 18805, 525, 35114, 1506, 553, 1378, 2155, 39599, 7761, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 27061, 553, 9363, 1741, 438, 279, 5220, 594, 56878, 11, 4231, 11, 2608, 11, 4680, 11, 323, 3681, 81208, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 42286, 48765, 14212, 43636, 11, 892, 525, 10078, 803, 4363, 311, 12170, 304, 3198, 315, 4312, 11643, 36952, 11, 7945, 809, 269, 30429, 11, 879, 525, 1948, 279, 16639, 315, 220, 18, 15, 323, 220, 19, 15, 1635, 11, 7046, 1091, 5461, 2608, 323, 4680, 11, 323, 614, 1030, 3807, 3681, 81208, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. Dizygotic twins (fraternal twins): This happens when two separate eggs are fertilized by two different sperm cells. This can be influenced by factors such as the woman's ethnicity, age, height, weight, and previous pregnancies. An example of this is dizygotic twins, which are slightly more likely to occur in women of West African descent, particularly Yoruba, who are between the ages of 30 and 40 years, greater than average height and weight, and have had several previous pregnancies.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0996826915843827, "g_worst_claim": 0.04166950629307674, "g_content": 1.559881317481566, "g_traj_mean": 0.993072509765625}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 646, 3537, 304, 1378, 1887, 5510, 25, 39674, 4246, 70, 14212, 320, 1713, 938, 8, 323, 42286, 48765, 14212, 320, 1626, 266, 2978, 3593, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 25, 4220, 43636, 2225, 504, 825, 1147, 48765, 1272, 11, 892, 40467, 323, 7586, 1378, 88773, 13, 1096, 1882, 11136, 8573, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 1283, 35114, 2022, 382, 17, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 25, 4220, 43636, 2225, 504, 1378, 2155, 18805, 11, 1817, 35114, 1506, 553, 1181, 1828, 39599, 2779, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 525, 10078, 803, 4363, 311, 12170, 979, 279, 2701, 9363, 525, 3042, 304, 279, 5220, 510, 256, 481, 2932, 374, 315, 4312, 11643, 36952, 11, 5310, 809, 269, 30429, 624, 256, 481, 2932, 374, 1948, 279, 4231, 315, 220, 18, 15, 323, 220, 19, 15, 1635, 624, 256, 481, 2932, 374, 7046, 1091, 5461, 2608, 323, 4680, 624, 256, 48