 twins: This type of twin pregnancy is more likely when specific factors are present in the woman such as being of West African descent (especially Yoruba), being between the age of 30 and 40 years, being greater than average height and weight, and having had several previous pregnancies. The passage indicates that dizygotic twins develop from two different eggs, each fertilized by its own sperm cell. This means that each twin has its own genetic makeup, which is why they are often referred to as fraternal twins or non-identical twins.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0050021290754443, "g_worst_claim": -0.026941455900669098, "g_content": 1.4650450675718245, "g_traj_mean": 0.9626666903495789}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 43636, 646, 3537, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 12691, 4246, 70, 14212, 43636, 320, 1713, 938, 1648, 1096, 13666, 979, 264, 3175, 35114, 1506, 18636, 40467, 1119, 1378, 88773, 13, 576, 6718, 11136, 8573, 2878, 220, 23, 2849, 315, 35114, 2022, 11, 323, 2176, 43636, 4332, 279, 1852, 18929, 26551, 382, 17, 13, 422, 449, 48765, 14212, 43636, 320, 1626, 266, 2978, 1648, 1096, 8573, 979, 1378, 8651, 18805, 525, 35114, 1506, 553, 1378, 2155, 39599, 7761, 13, 8886, 27397, 702, 1181, 1828, 4911, 738, 315, 20727, 323, 646, 387, 315, 2155, 81328, 382, 18, 13, 1200, 71154, 43636, 25, 1096, 374, 264, 8848, 31559, 1380, 279, 12804, 315, 279, 11220, 1147, 48765, 1272, 1119, 1378, 88773, 8573, 1602, 4124, 304, 279, 19636, 11, 5990, 2878, 220, 23, 2849, 315, 35114, 2022, 11, 323, 279, 43636, 4332, 4185, 35753, 323, 38781, 382, 19, 13, 12691, 309, 7751, 14212, 43636, 25, 4220, 43636, 2225, 304, 279, 1852, 1079, 7751, 14212, 11100, 323, 4332, 279, 1852, 1079, 7751, 14212, 15590, 13, 1096, 8573, 979, 279, 6718, 311, 1352, 1378, 88773, 13666, 1283, 279, 42541, 1899, 1283, 35114, 2022, 382, 9485, 525, 279, 1887, 4494, 315, 43636, 11247, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "These are the main types of twins explained in the given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.500508449772796, "g_worst_claim": -0.26243531703948975, "g_content": 0.744172507838199, "g_traj_mean": 0.4987652003765106}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "431", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first determine the extent of the tarnish. If the jewelry is slightly dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth into the solution. Rub the jewelry with the cloth, rinse in cool water, and buff with a cloth until dry. If the tarnish is heavier, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the jewelry and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth. If your silver jewelry is lightly tarnished, you can also try submerging it in a hot saltwater bath. Ensure that if your jewelry has gemstones, they won't be affected by the saltwater. For diamonds, clean with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush, and pat dry with a soft cloth.", "pred": "Additionally, you can use a saltwater solution by pouring two cups of hot water into a bowl. Ensure the jewelry is submerged in the solution, and check if the stones will be affected by the process. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without damaging the silver. Adjust the amount of water based on the quantity of jewelry being cleaned.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Additionally, you can use a saltwater solution by pouring two cups of hot water into a bowl. Ensure the jewelry is submerged in the solution, and check if the stones will be affected by the process. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without damaging the silver. Adjust the amount of water based on the quantity of jewelry being cleaned.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use a few different methods:\\n\\n1. For items that are merely dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip the jewelry in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\\n\\n2. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth (not paper towels, which can scratch).\\n\\n3. For diamonds, the best way to clean them is with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush. Pat it dry with a soft cloth.\\n\\n4. For silver jewelry, you can pour two cups of hot water into a bowl. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without abrading the silver. If your silver is lightly tarnished, the salt bath should take the tarnish right off. If you're cleaning a lot of jewelry at once, you can use more water. For just one piece of jewelry, use less water. If your jewelry has gemstones, make sure they won't be affected by being submerged in a saltwater solution.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to clean tarnished jewelry at home:\\n\\n1. For items that are merely dull, filmy or starting to discolor: Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry. \\n2. For heavier tarnish: Mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth (not paper towels, which can scratch). \\n3. For diamonds: The best way to clean a diamond is with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush. Pat it dry with a soft cloth. \\n4. For silver with gemstones: Pour two cups of hot water into a bowl. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without abrading the silver. If your silver is lightly tarnished, the salt bath should take the tarnish right off. If you're cleaning a lot of jewelry at once, you can use more water. For just one piece of jewelry, use less water.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the methods to clean tarnished jewelry at home:\\n\\n1. Mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip the jewelry in a soft cloth to clean items that are merely dull, filmy, or starting to discolor. Rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry. This method is suitable for items that have light tarnish.\\n2. For heavier tarnish, create a paste by mixing three parts baking soda with one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth. Avoid paper towels as they can scratch the jewelry.\\n3. For diamonds, use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush. Pat it dry with a soft cloth to clean the jewelry.\\n\\nAdditionally, you can use a saltwater solution by pouring two cups of hot water into a bowl. Ensure the jewelry is submerged in the solution, and check if the stones will be affected by the process. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without damaging the silver. Adjust the amount of water based on the quantity of jewelry being cleaned.\", \"Based on the given passages, to clean tarnished jewelry at home, you can use a mild dish soap solution for items that are merely dull, filmy, or starting to discolor. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water and apply it with a soft, lint-free cloth. Alternatively, you can use warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds. If your silver jewelry is lightly tarnished, you can submerge it in a bowl of hot water mixed with two cups of hot water, which acts as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without abrading the silver.\"]", "time_sec": 28.911, "generation_time_seconds": 28.1187, "selection_time_seconds": 0.786, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4240, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 2421, 2155, 5413, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 3589, 429, 525, 16234, 40530, 11, 89394, 11, 476, 5916, 311, 2560, 789, 11, 6514, 264, 2421, 210