f your jewelry has gemstones, make sure they won't be affected by being submerged in a saltwater solution.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8055967403452817, "g_worst_claim": -0.057477474212646484, "g_content": 2.2472876187028556, "g_traj_mean": 1.7983282804489136}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 4240, 86480, 3304, 30717, 518, 2114, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 3589, 429, 525, 16234, 40530, 476, 5916, 311, 2560, 789, 11, 6514, 264, 2421, 21025, 315, 23034, 12000, 26785, 448, 8205, 3015, 323, 23604, 304, 264, 8413, 27292, 13, 12839, 279, 30717, 11, 1221, 73241, 304, 7010, 3015, 323, 11522, 448, 264, 27292, 3080, 9058, 624, 17, 13, 1752, 43822, 86480, 812, 11, 6514, 264, 24937, 315, 2326, 5479, 27815, 38862, 311, 825, 949, 3015, 13, 44856, 279, 14961, 323, 3796, 279, 31881, 448, 264, 8413, 11, 57920, 12577, 27292, 624, 18, 13, 1752, 48051, 11, 279, 1850, 1616, 311, 4240, 1105, 374, 448, 8205, 773, 9667, 3015, 323, 264, 8413, 30117, 28300, 15625, 476, 2310, 25507, 36061, 13, 7135, 9058, 448, 264, 8413, 27292, 624, 19, 13, 25968, 1378, 25374, 315, 4017, 3015, 1119, 264, 19212, 323, 1186, 19052, 279, 30717, 13, 1096, 1714, 4278, 438, 264, 21700, 34194, 261, 429, 28160, 86480, 812, 2041, 668, 81, 2228, 279, 14961, 13, 27196, 279, 3311, 315, 3015, 3118, 389, 279, 1372, 315, 9666, 315, 30717, 498, 2299, 15826, 13, 1416, 697, 30717, 702, 18747, 32510, 11, 1281, 2704, 807, 2765, 944, 387, 11495, 553, 1660, 84077, 304, 264, 12021, 12987, 6291, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. For items that are merely dull or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip in a soft cloth. Rub the jewelry, then rinse in cool water and buff with a cloth until dry.\n2. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the silver and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth.\n3. For diamonds, the best way to clean them is with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush. Pat dry with a soft cloth.\n4. Pour two cups of hot water into a bowl and submerge the jewelry. This method works as a gentle cleanser that removes tarnish without abrading the silver. Adjust the amount of water based on the number of pieces of jewelry you're cleaning. If your jewelry has gemstones, make sure they won't be affected by being submerged in a saltwater solution.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.494709283070483, "g_worst_claim": -0.04870950678984324, "g_content": 2.0905912810680913, "g_traj_mean": 1.5798077583312988}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "435", "question": "how to find someone in france", "gt": "To find someone in France, you can use a website for people search in France. Sending an email or letter to the Town Hall in the person's city of birth can also be helpful, especially if you have lost relatives or friends. Try to find out the person's middle name, it could make the search easier. You can also use the French white pages, available in English at www.pagesjaunes.fr. Enter the person's last name in the 'Nom' field and first name in the 'Prenom' field, enter address information if known, and then click 'Trouver' to search. For searching in Paris and its suburbs, instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field. Posting a missed connection on Paris Craigslist might also be helpful.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can effectively search for someone in France, whether you're looking for a family member, a friend, or any other person.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can effectively search for someone in France, whether you're looking for a family member, a friend, or any other person.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. When searching, instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field. This will search for the person in Paris and its suburbs. Additionally, you can try posting an MC (missed connection) on Paris Craigslist (http://paris.craigslist.org/cgi-bin/pers...\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to find someone in France:\\n\\n1. Use the French white pages (in English) at www.pagesjaunes.fr.\\n2. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field.\\n3. Optionally, enter a first name in the Prenom field.\\n4. If you know the address, enter it in the Ou section; otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country.\\n5. Click Trouver to search for the name.\\n6. The search results will display the name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.\\n\\nThis method will help you find someone in France using their last name, and if possible, their first name and address.\", \"Based on the given passages, to find someone in France, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Visit www.pagesjaunes.fr, the Pages Blanches, which is the French version of the white pages.\\n2. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field.\\n3. Optionally, enter a first name in the Prenom field.\\n4. Enter address information, if known, in the Ou section.\\n5. Leave it blank to search the entire country.\\n6. Click Trouver to search for the name.\\n7. The search results will display name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.\", \"To find someone in France, you can try the following steps:\\n\\n1. **Use the French White Pages**: Visit www.pagesjaunes.fr, the French version of the white pages. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field. You can enter a first name in the Prenom field. Enter address information, if known, in the Ou section. Otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country.\\n\\n2. **Utilize Online Search Engines**: Try the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. To narrow down your search to Paris and its suburbs, instead of typing \\\"Paris\\\" in the City field, write \\\"IDF\\\" (or \\\"Ile de France\\\") in the Department district or region field.\\n\\n3. **Post on Craigslist**: You can also try posting a Missed Connection (MC) on Paris Craigslist (http://paris.craigslist.org/cgi-bin/pers... to see if your query is relevant to the search criteria.\\n\\n4. **Visit Town Halls**: If you have lost relatives in specific French cities or towns, you can send an email or letter to the Town Hall in their city of birth. This can be helpful if you have not seen the person for over ten or twenty years and pictures will not be much help.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively search for someone in France, whether you're looking for a family member, a friend, or any other person.\"]", "time_sec": 27.257, "generation_time_seconds": 26.4333, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8151, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1477, 4325, 304, 9625, 11, 498, 646, 990, 279, 8585, 4158, 6816, 320, 258, 6364, 8, 518, 1758, 1110, 2136, 37980, 5580, 8531, 18798, 4322, 65, 59014, 30, 5205, 61757, 13, 3197, 15039, 11, 4518, 315, 19496, 12095, 304, 279, 4311, 2070, 11, 3270, 71555, 320, 269, 358, 273, 409, 9625, 8, 304, 279, 50221, 9290, 476, 5537, 2070, 13, 1096, 686, 2711, 369, 279, 1697, 304, 12095, 323, 1181, 46913, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 17004, 458, 20869, 320, 1831, 291, 3633, 8, 389, 12095, 72292, 320, 1254, 1110, 1732, 285, 520, 956, 48922, 2659, 70416, 49125, 4322, 388, 1112, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. When searching, instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field. This will search for the person in Paris and its suburbs. Additionally, you can try posting an MC (missed connection) on Paris Craigslist (http://paris.craigslist.org/cgi-bin/pers...", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2144224880306234, "g_worst_claim": 0.25325151284535724, "g_content": 3.5888444853992, "g_traj_mean": 2.652642250061035}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1477, 4325, 304, 9625, 1447, 16, 13, 5443, 279, 8585, 4158, 6816, 320, 258, 