he 'Ou' section blank to search the entire country.\n6. Click 'Trouver' to search for the name.\n7. The search results will display the name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3199349133974652, "g_worst_claim": 0.20894575119018555, "g_content": 1.6039937337239583, "g_traj_mean": 1.1980582475662231}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "440", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "gt": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they help in the regeneration of the forest. Fires consume dead and decaying vegetation, clearing the way for new growth. Jack pines rely on fire to spread their seeds. They produce seratonous (resin-filled) cones that remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin, causing the cones to open and the seeds to fall or blow out. Furthermore, fires can disrupt the growth of other trees like spruce, providing an advantage to the more fire-tolerant jack pines and allowing them to proliferate.", "pred": "1. Fire consumes dead, decaying vegetation on the forest floor, clearing the way for new growth.\n2. Some species, such as the jack pine, rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.\n3. In the Canadian boreal forest, aspen and jack pine are the most important 'pioneer species'. These species can regenerate after a fire, as they are more fire-tolerant and can begin to proliferate again after another fire comes and disturbs the cycle.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Fire consumes dead, decaying vegetation on the forest floor, clearing the way for new growth.\n2. Some species, such as the jack pine, rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.\n3. In the Canadian boreal forest, aspen and jack pine are the most important 'pioneer species'. These species can regenerate after a fire, as they are more fire-tolerant and can begin to proliferate again after another fire comes and disturbs the cycle.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines in several ways:\\n\\n1. Fire consumes dead, decaying vegetation on the forest floor, clearing the way for new growth.\\n2. Some species, such as the jack pine, rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.\\n3. In the Canadian boreal forest, aspen and jack pine are the most important 'pioneer species'. These species can regenerate after a fire, as they are more fire-tolerant and can begin to proliferate again after another fire comes and disturbs the cycle.\", \"Based on the given passages, forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines in several ways:\\n\\n1. Fire consumes dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, clearing the way for new growth, as mentioned in passage 2.\\n\\n2. Fire can help some species, such as the jack pine, spread their seeds, as described in passage 2. The jack pine produces resin-filled cones that remain dormant until a fire melts the resin, causing the cones to pop open and release seeds.\\n\\n3. In regions where spruce trees are plentiful, spruce have better access to sunlight and shade out other trees like jack pine and aspen. However, when a fire comes and disturb this cycle, the more fire-tolerant jack pine and aspen regain the advantage and proliferate, as stated in passage 3.\\n\\nThese actions by forest fires help conifers like jack pines by creating favorable conditions for new growth and seed dispersal while also counteracting the dominance of other tree species.\", \"Based on the given passages, forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines in the following ways:\\n\\n1. Fires consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. This allows the ground to be prepared for fresh plantings.\\n\\n2. Some species, such as the jack pine, rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.\\n\\n3. In the Canadian boreal forest, aspen and jack pine are the most important 'pioneer species'. These species are able to take advantage of the cleared area after a fire.\\n\\n4. When another fire comes and disturbs the cycle, the more fire-tolerant jack pine and aspen regain the advantage and again proliferate.\\n\\nThese points show that forest fires can help conifers like jack pines by clearing out old growth and promoting new growth, as well as by aiding in seed dispersal for species that rely on fire for this process.\", \"Based on the given passages, forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. Additionally, the jack pine produces seratonous cones that are very durable. These cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin, then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out. This mechanism allows the jack pine to spread its seeds and regrow after a fire.\"]", "time_sec": 24.421, "generation_time_seconds": 23.5915, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8216, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 13638, 26084, 525, 23699, 311, 390, 98813, 1075, 25072, 281, 1543, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 6647, 59506, 5593, 11, 1622, 17270, 53732, 389, 279, 13638, 6422, 11, 32750, 279, 1616, 369, 501, 6513, 624, 17, 13, 4329, 9419, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 25072, 33597, 11, 17188, 389, 3940, 311, 8865, 862, 19056, 13, 576, 25072, 33597, 18644, 1420, 23535, 782, 320, 416, 258, 43418, 8,