{"id": "471", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, has no discernible taste or smell, and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in several aspects:\\n\\n1. **Aroma and Flavor**:\\n   - Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor.\\n   - Refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in the loss of its signature coconut flavor and smell.\\n\\n2. **Smoke Point**:\\n   - Refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\\n   - Unrefined coconut oil has a lower smoke point of 350 degrees F.\\n\\n3. **Taste**:\\n   - Unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\\n   - Refined coconut oil has no discernible taste or smell due to the deodorization process.\", \"Based on the given passages, the key differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are:\\n\\n1. Taste and smell:\\n   - Refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its coconut flavor and aroma.\\n   - Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\\n\\n2. Smoking point:\\n   - Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F.\\n   - Unrefined coconut oil has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F.\\n\\n3. Production process:\\n   - Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit.\\n   - Unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. It is deodorized and loses its signature coconut flavor and has no discernible taste or smell. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F. It has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Despite this, unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\"]", "time_sec": 21.802, "generation_time_seconds": 20.9906, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8061, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 18037, 11, 12656, 11, 323, 8628, 24098, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 31620, 33457, 13779, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 429, 374, 5558, 2337, 73185, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 7707, 311, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 594, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 3259, 432, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1075, 86096, 13, 22406, 11, 37191, 33457, 5590, 374, 409, 48917, 1506, 11, 12942, 304, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 11, 19853, 650, 1097, 1589, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0285581564325574, "g_worst_claim": 0.37431152661641437, "g_content": 1.4318995475769043, "g_traj_mean": 1.0223636627197266}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 3807, 13566, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 32, 56984, 323, 64999, 334, 510, 256, 481, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 624, 256, 481, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 409, 48917, 1506, 11, 12942, 304, 279, 4709, 315, 1181, 11957, 33457, 17172, 323, 22068, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 76880, 5126, 334, 510, 256, 481, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 16205, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 3259, 432, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1075, 86096, 624, 256, 481, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 4722, 16205, 1459, 315, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 51, 5525, 334, 510, 256, 481, 1230, 1097, 1589, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 624, 256, 481, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 4152, 311, 279, 409, 48917, 2022, 1882, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. **Taste**:\n   - Unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\n   - Refined coconut oil has no discernible taste or smell due to the