865, 504, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 323, 702, 264, 4722, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 13, 1084, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 429, 374, 5558, 2337, 73185, 13, 17715, 419, 11, 650, 1097, 1589, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. It is deodorized and loses its signature coconut flavor and has no discernible taste or smell. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F. It has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Despite this, unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0142872366157325, "g_worst_claim": 0.18020879654657274, "g_content": 1.6617462370130751, "g_traj_mean": 1.056556224822998}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "473", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is the process used to extract it. Refined coconut oil is extracted from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is extracted from the flesh of the fresh coconut. Another difference is that refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point and is therefore better suited for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no taste or smell, while unrefined oil retains its distinctive coconut flavor and aroma.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is in their taste, aroma, smoking point, and flavor. Refined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining, but it has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to 350 degrees F for unrefined coconut oil. The taste of refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is in their taste, aroma, smoking point, and flavor. Refined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining, but it has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to 350 degrees F for unrefined coconut oil. The taste of refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their processing, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. Unrefined coconut oil, on the other hand, is made from fresh coconuts and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F. It retains its distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has no discernible taste or smell, while unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is in their taste, aroma, smoking point, and flavor. Refined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining, but it has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to 350 degrees F for unrefined coconut oil. The taste of refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is primarily in their taste and aroma, as well as their smoking point. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct coconut flavor and aroma, whereas refined coconut oil has lost its signature taste and smell due to deodorization. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying.\"]", "time_sec": 19.128, "generation_time_seconds": 18.393, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7308, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 18037, 11, 12656, 11, 323, 8628, 24098, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 31620, 33457, 13779, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 429, 374, 5558, 2337, 73185, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 7707, 311, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 594, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 3259, 432, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1075, 86096, 13, 22406, 11, 37191, 33457, 5590, 374, 409, 48917, 1506, 11, 12942, 304, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 11, 19853, 650, 1097, 1589, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor an