avor and aroma, whereas refined coconut oil has lost its signature taste and smell due to deodorization. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.66939823139655, "g_worst_claim": 0.1920621578509991, "g_content": 1.066568445276331, "g_traj_mean": 0.6752755045890808}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "474", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil retains its distinct aroma and flavor, while refined coconut oil loses these qualities during the refining process.\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) than unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\nTherefore, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their source, aroma, flavor, and smoking point.", "pred": "4. **Taste**: Refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its coconut flavor, resulting in no discernible taste or smell. Unrefined coconut oil, on the other hand, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "4. **Taste**: Refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its coconut flavor, resulting in no discernible taste or smell. Unrefined coconut oil, on the other hand, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in several key aspects:\\n\\n1. Aroma and Flavor: Unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, has a distinct aroma and flavor from fresh coconuts. This flavor is lost during the refining process, making refined coconut oil tasteless and odorless.\\n\\n2. Smoking Point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees Fahrenheit, which makes it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\\n\\n3. Taste: Refined coconut oil loses its signature coconut flavor, resulting in no discernible taste or smell. In contrast, unrefined coconut oil retains a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\\n\\n4. Production Method: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil is produced from the fresh coconuts, preserving the natural aroma and flavor.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil can be summarized as follows:\\n\\n1. **Production Process**: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconuts.\\n\\n2. **Aroma and Flavor**: Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process for refined coconut oil.\\n\\n3. **Heat Tolerance**: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees Fahrenheit compared to 350 degrees Fahrenheit for unrefined coconut oil. This makes refined coconut oil a better option for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\\n\\n4. **Taste**: Refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its coconut flavor, resulting in no discernible taste or smell. Unrefined coconut oil, on the other hand, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil include:\\n1. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconuts.\\n2. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining.\\n3. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F).\\n4. Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, while refined coconut oil loses its signature coconut flavor and has no discernible taste or smell.\"]", "time_sec": 23.468, "generation_time_seconds": 22.7314, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7322, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 18037, 11, 12656, 11, 323, 8628, 24098, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 31620, 33457, 13779, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 429, 374, 5558, 2337, 73185, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 7707, 311, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 594, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 3259, 432, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1075, 86096, 13, 22406, 11, 37191, 33457, 5590, 374, 409, 48917, 1506, 11, 12942, 304, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 11, 19853, 650, 1097, 1589, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their composition, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.019958317372411, "g_worst_claim": 0.298076073328654, "g_content": 1.4092729568481446, "g_traj_mean": 1.0070542097091675}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 3807, 1376, 13566, 1447, 16, 13, 362, 56984, 323, 64999, 25, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 504, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1096, 17172, 374, 5558, 2337, 279, 73185, 1882, 11, 3259, 37191, 33457, 5590, 12656, 1717, 323, 52997, 1717, 382, 17, 13, 72599, 5126, 25, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 892, 3643, 432, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1741, 438, 86096, 13, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 4722, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 382, 18, 13, 57981, 25, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 32191, 1181, 11957, 33457, 17172, 11, 12942, 304, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 51844, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 382, 19, 13, 24039, 6730, 25, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 31620, 1062, 443, 6128, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 374, 8947, 504, 279, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 11, 46895, 279, 5810, 54179, 323, 17172, 13, 151645], "pred": "4. Production Method: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil is produced from the fr