{"id": "479", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "To change your US postal address, you can visit the official website of the U.S. Postal Service, fill out an online form, or contact their call center. The process is fast and versatile, allowing you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the USPS. It's important to note that you can also use this feature to have your business mail forwarded to a new address due to a permanent move or temporary relocation. The process involves submitting either an online form or filling out and submitting a physical form at any U.S. Post Office.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, changing your address with the U.S. Postal Service can be done in as little as 1 minute or completed online. There are three ways to change your address:\n\n1. Visit the website moversguide.usps.com and safeguard your personal information with a $1 charge to your credit or debit card.\n2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).\n3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, which can be mailed or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, changing your address with the U.S. Postal Service can be done in as little as 1 minute or completed online. There are three ways to change your address:\n\n1. Visit the website moversguide.usps.com and safeguard your personal information with a $1 charge to your credit or debit card.\n2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).\n3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, which can be mailed or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers a fast and versatile change of address service that can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The service is secure, using the latest encryption technologies to ensure data safety. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.\", \"Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers a fast change of address service that can be completed in as little as 1 minute. The service is versatile, allowing users to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and safeguard your personal information with identity validation by a simple $1 charge to your credit or debit card. Alternatively, you can call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777) or fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be obtained at any U.S. Post Office.\", \"Based on the given passages, changing your address with the U.S. Postal Service can be done in as little as 1 minute or completed online. There are three ways to change your address:\\n\\n1. Visit the website moversguide.usps.com and safeguard your personal information with a $1 charge to your credit or debit card.\\n2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).\\n3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, which can be mailed or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers a Change of Address service that can be completed quickly and securely. The service allows users to notify up to 100 organizations besides the Postal Service, and it is designed to safeguard personal information through encryption technologies. To change your address, you can visit the official website moversguide.usps.com, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS, or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.\"]", "time_sec": 19.442, "generation_time_seconds": 18.6964, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7394, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rol