o your credit or debit card.\n2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).\n3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office, which can be mailed or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.348415772761068, "g_worst_claim": 0.32279396057128906, "g_content": 2.0820751847891974, "g_traj_mean": 1.4177191257476807}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 547, 808, 13, 54217, 5362, 6081, 264, 10388, 315, 9177, 2473, 429, 646, 387, 8145, 6157, 323, 51023, 13, 576, 2473, 6147, 3847, 311, 15456, 705, 311, 220, 16, 15, 15, 11104, 27758, 279, 54217, 5362, 11, 323, 432, 374, 6188, 311, 47971, 4345, 1995, 1526, 25463, 14310, 13, 2014, 2297, 697, 2621, 11, 498, 646, 3947, 279, 3946, 3910, 95354, 48370, 21916, 1690, 905, 11, 1618, 279, 84876, 7143, 5832, 518, 220, 16, 12, 23, 15, 15, 12, 7384, 32340, 5012, 11, 476, 5155, 700, 323, 9318, 11405, 3377, 220, 18, 20, 22, 20, 518, 894, 547, 808, 13, 3877, 8246, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers a Change of Address service that can be completed quickly and securely. The service allows users to notify up to 100 organizations besides the Postal Service, and it is designed to safeguard personal information through encryption technologies. To change your address, you can visit the official website moversguide.usps.com, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS, or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2499774876070266, "g_worst_claim": 0.395400603612264, "g_content": 2.216574401855469, "g_traj_mean": 1.425641417503357}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.76, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "480", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"change of address u.s. postal service\":\n\nTo change your address with the U.S. Postal Service, you can visit the USPS website (moversguide.usps.com), call the USPS Call Center (1-800-ASK-USPS), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. You can also use the USPS change of address feature to notify up to 100 organizations, including the Postal Service, with secure encryption technology to protect your data.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers a fast and versatile change of address service that can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The service is secure, using the latest encryption technologies to ensure data safety. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers a fast and versatile change of address service that can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The service is secure, using the latest encryption technologies to ensure data safety. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers a fast and versatile change of address service that can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The service is secure, using the latest encryption technologies to ensure data safety. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.\", \"Based on the given passages, changing an address with the U.S. Postal Service can be done through several methods:\\n\\n1. Visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ and safeguard your personal information with identity validation by a simple $1 charge to your credit or debit card.\\n\\n2. Call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).\\n\\n3. Fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be picked up at any U.S. Post Office, and submit it at the Post Office. The form may be submitted at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.\\n\\nThe process is fast and secure, ensuring that your data is protected with the latest encryption technologies. Additionally, you can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service (USPS), making the service versatile.\", \"Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers several methods to change an address:\\n\\n1. **Online Form:** You can complete the U.S. Postal Service Official Change of Address form online. This form can be accessed through the provided website link: https://moversguide.usps.com/. To safeguard your personal information, a simple $1 charge for identity validation can be made using a credit or debit card.\\n\\n2. **Call Center:** You can call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777) to change your address.\\n\\n3. **Form Submission:** You can fill out and submit PS Form 3575. This form can be picked up at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier. The form can be submitted at any U.S. Post Office, mailed to any Post Office, or provided to any Postal Mail Carrier.\", \"Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers a fast and versatile change of address service. You can change your address online using the Official Change of Address form. Alternatively, you can call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777) or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. The process ensures that your data is secure with the latest encryption technologies.\"]", "time_sec": 22.873, "generation_time_seconds": 22.0831, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7853, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 547, 808, 13, 54217, 5362, 6081, 264, 4937, 323, 31945, 2297, 315, 2621, 2473, 429, 646, 15456, 705, 311, 220, 16, 15, 15, 11104, 304, 5256, 311, 279, 54217, 5362, 13, 576, 2473, 374, 9767, 11, 1667, 279, 5535, 25463, 14310, 311, 5978, 821, 7149, 13, 2014, 2297, 697, 2621, 11, 498, 646, 3947, 3703, 1110, 76, 8969, 48370, 21916, 1690, 905, 34545, 1618, 279, 84876, 7143, 5832, 518, 220, 16, 12, 23, 15, 15, 12, 7384, 32340, 5012, 320, 16, 12, 23, 15, 15, 12, 17, 22, 20, 12, 23, 22, 22, 22, 701, 476, 5155, 700, 323, 9318, 11405, 3377, 220, 18, 20, 22, 20, 518, 894, 547, 808, 13, 3877, 8246, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the U.S. Postal Service offers a fast and versatile change of address service that can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The service is secure, using the latest encryption technologies to ensure data safety. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.381282622310331, "g_worst_claim": 0.3544132709503174, "g_content": 2.3077296447753906, "g_traj_mean": 1.4484033584594727}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10018, 458, 2621, 448, 279, 547, 808, 13, 54217, 5362, 646, 387, 2814, 1526, 3807, 5413, 1447, 16, 13, 19008, 3703, 1110, 76, 8969, 48370, 21916, 1690, 905, 14, 323, 47971, 697, 4345, 1995, 448, 9569, 10519, 553, 264, 4285, 400, 16,