{"id": "489", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can see who liked your tweets by using tracking websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These sites can give you an idea of who is favouriting your tweets. Alternatively, you can also set up notifications on Twitter itself. By going to your account settings and clicking on the notifications link, you can arrange to be notified via email whenever someone likes one of your tweets.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites that track favorited tweets. Two examples mentioned are Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to see who is favoriting your tweets or the same tweets as you. This information can help you find other Twitter users to follow or see what tweets people like. Additionally, you can set up notifications on Twitter to be informed when someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites that track favorited tweets. Two examples mentioned are Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to see who is favoriting your tweets or the same tweets as you. This information can help you find other Twitter users to follow or see what tweets people like. Additionally, you can set up notifications on Twitter to be informed when someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites that track favorited tweets. Two examples mentioned are Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to see who is favoriting your tweets or the same tweets as you. This information can help you find other Twitter users to follow or see what tweets people like. Additionally, you can set up notifications on Twitter to be informed when someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite.\", \"Based on the provided passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets, such as Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to see who has favorited your tweets and which tweets you and others have also favored. Additionally, you can set up notifications in your Twitter account to receive alerts whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite.\", \"Based on the given passages, there are two main ways to tell who liked your tweet:\\n\\n1. Using websites: You can use websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, which allow you to track who is favoriting your tweets and which tweets you and others are also favoriting. This can help you find other Twitter users to follow or see what tweets people like of yours.\\n\\n2. Setting up notifications: You can set up your Twitter account to receive notifications via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites. This requires logging in to Twitter, clicking on your Twitter name, selecting the Settings option, and then selecting the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. Keep in mind, if you're very popular on Twitter, you might receive a lot of email notifications.\"]", "time_sec": 18.124, "generation_time_seconds": 17.3221, "selection_time_seconds": 0.797, "