{"id": "490", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, you can track who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone marks one of your tweets as their favorite.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website such as Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track and see who has favorited your tweets, providing insights into which tweets people like and helping you find other Twitter users to follow. Alternatively, you can set up your Twitter account to receive notifications via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. This way, you will be alerted when someone has liked your tweet.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that checks Twitterers who favorite tweets. One such website is mentioned in the passages: Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. By using these websites, you can identify the Twitter users who have favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you. This can help you find other Twitter users to follow or see what tweets people like of yours.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a web-based tool. Here are the steps:\\n1. Go to Twitter.com and log in with your Twitter username and password.\\n2. Click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right-hand corner of your account's Home page.\\n3. Click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu.\\n4. Click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen.\\n5. You can set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.\"]", "time_sec": 17.468, "generation_time_seconds": 16.745, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7181, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 1667, 264, 3910, 429, 13918, 4694, 1608, 23150, 13, 3776, 1741, 3910, 9733, 374, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 13, 2014, 990, 419, 3910, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 728, 311, 6271, 905, 11, 1487, 304, 448, 697, 6271, 5934, 323, 3552, 11, 4205, 389, 697, 6271, 829, 7407, 389, 279, 8416, 1290, 1424, 9131, 315, 697, 2692, 594, 5379, 2150, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 11296, 2999, 429, 7952, 304, 279, 5943, 14875, 5022, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 389, 279, 6303, 52938, 2656, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 279, 4171, 13, 1096, 686, 2138, 498, 311, 738, 705, 697, 2692, 773, 429, 498, 2299, 29216, 4566, 2551, 15356, 4325, 15423, 825, 315, 697, 23150, 438, 825, 315, 862, 26574, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4775597133226444, "g_worst_claim": 0.26339858770370483, "g_content": 2.456865692138672, "g_traj_mean": 1.6066372394561768}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 1667, 264, 3910, 1741, 438, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 476, 80941, 11870, 70485, 13, 4220, 13037, 2138, 498, 311, 3754, 323, 1490, 879, 702, 4694, 1608, 697, 23150, 11, 8241, 25709, 1119, 892, 23150, 1251, 1075, 323, 10476, 498, 1477, 1008, 6271, 3847, 311, 1795, 13, 38478, 11, 498, 646, 738, 705, 697, 6271, 2692, 311, 5258, 21969, 4566, 2551, 15356, 4325, 15423, 825, 315, 697, 23150, 438, 264, 6930, 13, 1096, 1616, 11, 498, 686, 387, 66669, 979, 4325, 702, 14915, 697, 11809, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website such as Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track and see who has favorited your tweets, providing insights into which tweets people like and helping you find other Twitter users to follow. Alternatively, you can set up your Twitter account to receive notifications via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. This way, you will be alerted when someone has liked your tweet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2275141087180497, "g_worst_claim": 0.24736642837524414, "g_content": 1.9431543764860735, "g_traj_mean": 1.4554731845855713}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 1667, 264, 3910, 429, 12341, 6271, 388, 879, 6930, 23150, 13, 3776, 1741, 3910, 374, 9733, 304, 279, 46769, 25, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 323, 80941, 11870, 70485, 13, 3216, 1667, 1493, 13037, 11, 498, 646, 10542, 279, 6271, 3847, 879, 614, 4694, 1608, 697, 23150, 476, 279, 1852, 23150, 438, 498, 13, 1096, 646, 1492, 498, 1477, 1008, 6271, 3847, 311, 1795, 476, 1490, 1128, 23150, 1251, 1075, 315, 18316, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that checks Twitterers who favorite tweets. One such website is mentioned in the passages: Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. By using these websites, you can identify the Twitter users who have favorited your tweets or the same tweets as you. This can help you find other Twitter users to follow or see what tweets people like of yours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5586785783544619, "g_worst_claim": 0.24736642837524414, "g_content": 2.0972222464425223, "g_traj_mean": 1.8849278688430786}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 1667, 264, 3482, 5980, 5392, 13, 5692, 525, 279, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 5994, 311, 6271, 905, 323, 1487, 304, 448, 697, 6271, 5934, 323, 3552, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 697, 6271, 829, 11, 7407, 389, 279, 8416, 1290, 24413, 9131, 315, 697, 2692, 594, 5379, 2150, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 11296, 2999, 429, 7952, 304, 279, 5943, 14875, 5022, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 6303, 52938, 2656, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 279, 4171, 624, 20, 13, 1446, 646, 738, 705, 697, 2692, 773, 429, 498, 2299, 29216, 4566, 2551, 15356, 4325, 15423, 825, 315, 697, 23150, 438, 825, 315, 862, 26574, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a web-based tool. Here are the steps:\n1. Go to Twitter.com and log in with your Twitter username and password.\n2. Click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right-hand corner of your account's Home page.\n3. Click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu.\n4. Click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen.\n5. You can set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.472950085151545, "g_worst_claim": 0.26339858770370483, "g_content": 1.987999794699929, "g_traj_mean": 1.3233941793441772}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "491", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by going to Twitter.com and logging in with your Twitter username and password. Once logged in, click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, then click on Settings and finally Blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. By setting this feature, you will receive an email notification whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.\", \"Based on the given passages, to tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These sites allow you to track who has favorited your tweets. Additionally, you can set up notifications on your Twitter account via email when someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. This can be done by logging into Twitter.com, accessing your account settings, and enabling email notifications for favorites.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website such as Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track which tweets you and your followers have favorited, helping you see who is favoriting your tweets or the same tweets as you. This can also help you find other Twitter users to follow or understand what tweets people are liking from you.\\n\\nSpecifically, to track who favorited your tweets using these websites, you would need to access the website, enter your Twitter handle, and then search for your tweets. The website will show you a list of users who favorited your tweets, and you can also see additional information such as the date and time the tweet was favorited, and the number of times the tweet was favorited.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track who is favoriting your tweets and which tweets you and others are also favoriting. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone favorites one of your tweets.\"]", "time_sec": 17.564, "generation_time_seconds": 16.7765, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7819, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 1667, 264, 3910, 429, 13918, 4694, 1608, 23150, 13, 3776, 1741, 3910, 9733, 374, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 13, 2014, 990, 419, 3910, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 728, 311, 6271, 905, 11, 1487, 304, 448, 697, 6271, 5934, 323, 3552, 11, 4205, 389, 697, 6271, 829, 7407, 389, 279, 8416, 1290, 1424, 9131, 315, 697, 2692, 594, 5379, 2150, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 11296, 2999, 429, 7952, 304, 279, 5943, 14875, 5022, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 389, 279, 6303, 52938, 2656, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 279, 4171, 13, 1096, 686, 2138, 498, 311, 738, 705, 697, 2692, 773, 429, 498, 2299, 29216, 4566, 2551, 15356, 4325, 15423, 825, 315, 697, 23150, 438, 825, 315, 862, 26574, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.470625691900969, "g_worst_claim": 0.16970843076705933, "g_content": 2.4701332092285155, "g_traj_mean": 1.6093237400054932}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 11, 498, 646, 990, 13037, 1075, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 476, 80941, 11870, 70485, 13, 4220, 6594, 2138, 498, 311, 3754, 879, 702, 4694, 1608, 697, 23150, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 646, 738, 705, 21969, 389, 697, 6271, 2692, 4566, 2551, 979, 4325, 15423, 825, 315, 697, 23150, 438, 264, 6930, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 2814, 553, 8392, 1119, 6271, 905, 11, 31788, 697, 2692, 5003, 11, 323, 27362, 2551, 21969, 369, 26574, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to tell who liked your tweet, you can use websites like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These sites allow you to track who has favorited your tweets. Additionally, you can set up notifications on your Twitter account via email when someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. This can be done by logging into Twitter.com, accessing your account settings, and enabling email notifications for favorites.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.097461702835647, "g_worst_claim": 0.0662217651094709, "g_content": 1.6850981461374384, "g_traj_mean": 1.347243070602417}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 1667, 264, 3910, 1741, 438, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 476, 80941, 11870, 70485, 13, 4220, 13037, 2138, 498, 311, 3754, 892, 23150, 498, 323, 697, 20119, 614, 4694, 1608, 11, 10476, 498, 1490, 879, 374, 4694, 5853, 697, 23150, 476, 279, 1852, 23150, 438, 498, 13, 1096, 646, 1083, 1492, 498, 1477, 1008, 6271, 3847, 311, 1795, 476, 3535, 1128, 23150, 1251, 525, 48737, 504, 498, 382, 47514, 745, 11, 311, 3754, 879, 4694, 1608, 697, 23150, 1667, 1493, 13037, 11, 498, 1035, 1184, 311, 2615, 279, 3910, 11, 3725, 697, 6271, 3705, 11, 323, 1221, 2711, 369, 697, 23150, 13, 576, 3910, 686, 1473, 498, 264, 1140, 315, 3847, 879, 4694, 1608, 697, 23150, 11, 323, 498, 646, 1083, 1490, 5107, 1995, 1741, 438, 279, 2400, 323, 882, 279, 11809, 572, 4694, 1608, 11, 323, 279, 1372, 315, 3039, 279, 11809, 572, 4694, 1608, 13, 151645], "pred": "Specifically, to track who favorited your tweets using these websites, you would need to access the website, enter your Twitter handle, and then search for your tweets. The website will show you a list of users who favorited your tweets, and you can also see additional information such as the date and time the tweet was favorited, and the number of times the tweet was favorited.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6832945715369215, "g_worst_claim": -0.27088238511766705, "g_content": 1.1747983088258838, "g_traj_mean": 0.9554763436317444}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 553, 1667, 13037, 1075, 80941, 354, 465, 5071, 323, 80941, 11870, 70485, 13, 4220, 13037, 2138, 498, 311, 3754, 879, 374, 4694, 5853, 697, 23150, 323, 892, 23150, 498, 323, 3800, 525, 1083, 4694, 5853, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 646, 738, 705, 697, 6271, 2692, 311, 5258, 2551, 21969, 15356, 4325, 26574, 825, 315, 697, 23150, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track who is favoriting your tweets and which tweets you and others are also favoriting. Additionally, you can set up your Twitter account to receive email notifications whenever someone favorites one of your tweets.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4295548504985887, "g_worst_claim": 0.16970843076705933, "g_content": 1.69902712504069, "g_traj_mean": 1.651115894317627}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "492", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, there are several ways to track who likes your tweets:\n\n1. Favotter.net and Favstar.fm - These websites allow you to track who has favorited your tweets and which tweets have been favorited by multiple users. (Passage 1)\n2. Using a web-based website - There are websites that allow you to check Twitter users who favorite tweets. (Passage 2)\n3. On Twitter - You can set up your account settings to receive notifications via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is: You can use Favotter.net, Favstar.fm, or a web-based website to track who likes your tweets, or you can set up your Twitter account settings to receive email notifications.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track which tweets you and others have favorited, giving you insight into who is interested in your content and helping you find other users to follow.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track which tweets you and others have favorited, giving you insight into who is interested in your content and helping you find other users to follow.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using a website that tracks favorited tweets. One such website mentioned is Favotter.net. To use this website, you need to go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and then click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. This will allow you to set up your account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by following these steps:\\n\\n1. Use a website like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm to track who is favoriting your tweets.\\n2. These two sites allow you to see who is favoriting your tweets and which tweets that you and others are also favoriting.\\n3. You can also set up your Twitter account so that you're notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites. To do this, go to Twitter.com, log in with your Twitter username and password, click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, click on the Settings option that appears in the drop-down menu, and click on the blue Notifications link at the top of the screen.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net and Favstar.fm. These sites allow you to track who is favoriting your tweets or preferred the same tweets as you. Additionally, you can set up email notifications on Twitter so that you are notified via email whenever someone marks one of your tweets as a favorite. Keep in mind that if you're very popular on Twitter, you might receive a lot of email notifications.\", \"Based on the given passages, you can tell who liked your tweet by using websites like Favotter.net or Favstar.fm. These websites allow you to track which tweets you and others have favorited, giving you insight into who is interested in your content and helping you find other users to follow.\"]", "time_sec": 17.951, "generation_time_seconds": 17.0608, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8856, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 498, 646, 3291, 879, 14915, 697, 11809,