The employer pays lower NICs as a result of paying their employees a reduced salary. Employers pay a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme as a non-cash benefit. For example, for members of USS, the regular contribution is 7.5% of the pay, and for members of USPAS, it is 9%.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.5186449999565252, "g_worst_claim": 1.3626838191863029, "g_content": 3.0674031575520835, "g_traj_mean": 2.0760607719421387}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "496", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "gt": "Salary exchange pension contributions allow employees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment made by their employer. This arrangement benefits both employers and employees as employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to the reduced salary, and employees can save money by making pension contributions through this method. The amount of salary waived under the salary exchange is equivalent to the regular pension contribution, and the employer pays a corresponding amount into the pension scheme. The specific details of the contributions may vary depending on the pension scheme being used.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money. Employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) as a result of paying their employees a reduced salary. The value of the salary waived under the Salary Exchange is equal to the value of the employee's regular pension contribution to USS, USPAS, or SGSS, excluding additional contributions. For example, for members of USS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 October 2011 is 7.5% of their pay, and for members of USPAS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 August 2011 is 9%.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money. Employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) as a result of paying their employees a reduced salary. The value of the salary waived under the Salary Exchange is equal to the value of the employee's regular pension contribution to USS, USPAS, or SGSS, excluding additional contributions. For example, for members of USS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 October 2011 is 7.5% of their pay, and for members of USPAS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 August 2011 is 9%.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee agreeing to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to save money. Employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) as a result of paying their employees a reduced salary. The value of the salary waived under the Salary Exchange is equal to the value of the employee's regular pension contribution to USS, USPAS, or SGSS, excluding additional contributions. For example, for members of USS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 October 2011 is 7.5% of their pay, and for members of USPAS, the regular contribution with effect from 1 August 2011 is 9%.\", \"Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions refer to a method where an individual agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment made by their employer. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to benefit from reduced National Insurance Contributions (NICs) for the employer and potentially increased pension savings for the employee.\\n\\nSpecifically, in the context provided, the University offers a salary exchange program where the individual waives a portion of their regular pension contribution, and in return, the University pays an equivalent amount into the relevant pension scheme. For example, for members of USS, the regular contribution is 7.5% of pay, while for members of USPAS, it is 9%. This exchange helps in setting up pension payments and can lead to savings for both parties involved.\", \"Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions refer to a way in which an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. This arrangement offers both employers and employees the opportunity to make savings, as employers pay lower National Insurance Contributions (NICs) due to paying their employees a reduced salary. The specific examples provided include the University of Bath where, for members of USS, the regular contribution is 7.5% of pay, and for USPAS, it is 9%. The University would then pay a corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme as part of the salary exchange agreement.\", \"Based on the given passages, salary exchange pension contributions involve an arrangement where an employee agrees to give up part of their salary or bonus in exchange for a pension payment by their employer. This arrangement benefits both parties: employers save on National Insurance Contributions (NICs), and employees contribute to a pension plan. For example, for members of USS, the regular contribution from 1 October 2011 is 7.5% of pay, and for USPAS, it is 9% from 1 August 2011.\"]", "time_sec": 20.894, "generation_time_seconds": 20.04, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8482, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 16107, 9289, 27681, 19026, 21058, 458, 9364, 38327, 311, 2968, 705, 949, 315, 862, 16107, 476, 12037, 304, 9289, 369, 264, 27681, 8160, 7171, 553, 862, 19136, 13, 1096, 26112, 6147, 2176, 22426, 323, 8256, 311, 3581, 3220, 13, 20782, 388, 2291, 4722, 5055, 21674, 96004, 320, 44947, 82, 8, 438, 264, 1102, 315, 12515, 862, 8256, 264, 11046, 16107, 13, 576, 897, 315, 279, 16107, 81482, 1212, 279, 41758, 18705, 374, 6144, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 9364, 594, 5792, 27681, 18527, 311, 38508, 11, 2274, 47, 1911, 11, 476, 29626, 1220, 11, 