11, 11, 697, 5792, 18527, 448, 2456, 504, 220, 16, 6156, 220, 17, 15, 16, 16, 374, 220, 24, 14360, 1096, 9289, 6147, 2176, 22426, 323, 8256, 311, 1281, 18986, 13, 20782, 388, 2291, 4722, 64215, 82, 438, 264, 1102, 315, 12515, 862, 8256, 264, 11046, 16107, 13, 151645], "pred": "Salary exchange pension contributions involve an employee giving up part of their salary in exchange for a pension payment paid by their employer. For example, for members of USS, your regular contribution with effect from 1 October 2011 will be 7.5% of your pay; for members of USPAS, your regular contribution with effect from 1 August 2011 is 9%. This exchange allows both employers and employees to make savings. Employers pay lower NICs as a result of paying their employees a reduced salary.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.309775549593471, "g_worst_claim": 0.9189872741699219, "g_content": 2.5100262451171873, "g_traj_mean": 1.962144136428833}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.06, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "501", "question": "factors that cause oily skin", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the factors that cause oily skin are primarily genetic/hereditary factors and hormonal shifts in the body. Diet and poor hygiene/topical applications have a limited effect on the oiliness of the skin. Combination skin, which is a mix of oily and dry/normal areas, can also contribute to oily skin in certain areas such as the T-zone.", "pred": "1. Genetic inheritance: If your parents have oily skin, there is a higher chance that you will also have oily skin.\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics.\n3. Combination skin: Some people have a combination of skin types, which can include oily areas like the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This type of skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.\n4. Poor hygiene and topical applications: It is important to identify if the oiliness is due to natural phenomena or poor hygiene and topical applications.\n5. Diet: Although diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Genetic inheritance: If your parents have oily skin, there is a higher chance that you will also have oily skin.\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics.\n3. Combination skin: Some people have a combination of skin types, which can include oily areas like the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This type of skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.\n4. Poor hygiene and topical applications: It is important to identify if the oiliness is due to natural phenomena or poor hygiene and topical applications.\n5. Diet: Although diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. Genetic inheritance: If your parents have oily skin, there is a higher chance that you will also have oily skin.\\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics.\\n3. Combination skin: Some people have a combination of skin types, which can include oily areas like the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This type of skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.\\n4. Poor hygiene and topical applications: It is important to identify if the oiliness is due to natural phenomena or poor hygiene and topical applications.\\n5. Diet: Although diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin.\", \"Based on the given passages, factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. Genetic factors: Oily skin is often hereditary, meaning if your parents have oily skin, there is a high chance you will as well. This is highlighted in passage 1 which states, \\\"Oily skin is hereditary -- you can change your diet or change your lifestyle, but if your mom or dad has oily skin, chances are you will, too.\\\"\\n\\n2. Hormonal shifts: If oily skin comes and goes, it may be due to hormonal changes in the body rather than genetics. This is mentioned in the second paragraph of passage 1.\\n\\n3. Diet: Although the passages clarify that diet does not directly cause oily skin, they suggest that certain foods, such as greasy pizza, can exacerbate the condition. Passage 1 mentions, \\\"Diet can aggravate acne, but it doesn't cause oily skin.\\\"\\n\\n4. Topical applications: Improper hygiene or use of certain topical products can lead to oily skin. This is indicated in passage 2 which emphasizes, \\\"Before investigating the cause of your oily skin, it is important to first identify if this 'oiliness' is a natural phenomenon or due to poor hygiene and topical applications.\\\"\\n\\n5. Skin type changes: The passage suggests that skin type can vary over time, and some areas might have different skin types, like a combination of oily and dry skin in the T-zone. This information is derived from the third passage.\\n\\n6. Combination skin: Some people have a combination of skin types in different areas of their skin. This is mentioned in the third passage, noting that certain individuals might have areas with oily skin and others with dry skin, particularly in the T-zone.\\n\\n7. Overly dilated pores: Combination skin can produce overly dilated pores, which is a characteristic of oily skin. This is described in the third passage.\\n\\n8. Blackheads: People with oily skin are more prone to blackheads. This is also mentioned in the third passage.\\n\\n9. Shiny skin: Oily skin tends to appear shiny. This is stated in the third passage.\\n\\nThese factors collectively contribute to the development of oily skin, as outlined in the passages provided.\", \"Oily skin is primarily caused by genetics, with a strong predisposition if one's parents have oily skin. It can also be influenced by hormonal shifts in the body, which may cause it to come and go. While diet does not directly cause oily skin, it can aggravate acne. However, the myth that oily foods like chocolates and peanut butter cause oiliness is not supported by the given passages.\", \"Based on the given passages, oily skin is primarily caused by hereditary factors. The passages suggest that if a person's parents have oily skin, there is a higher likelihood that the individual will also have oily skin. Additionally, hormonal shifts can influence the condition of oily skin, making it come and go. The passages also mention that diet has a limited effect on oily skin, emphasizing that common myths about greasy foods causing oily skin are not accurate.\"]", "time_sec": 26.675, "generation_time_seconds": 25.6253, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0436, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 9363, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 74126, 41822, 25, 1416, 697, 6562, 614, 77471, 6787, 11, 1052, 374, 264, 5080, 6012, 429, 498, 686, 1083, 614, 77471, 6787, 624, 17, 13, 91108, 24202, 28635, 25, 1416, 697, 77471, 6787, 4041, 323, 5780, 11, 432, 1231, 387, 803, 5435, 311, 73118, 4344, 304, 697, 2487, 4751, 1091, 55004, 624, 18, 13, 85856, 6787, 25, 4329, 1251, 614, 264, 10601, 315, 6787, 4494, 11, 892, 646, 2924, 77471, 5671, 1075, 279, 350, 77763, 320, 77, 960, 11, 51254, 11, 323, 45075, 568, 1096, 943, 315, 6787, 646, 8193, 38432, 18840, 657, 70928, 11, 3691, 35810, 11, 323, 41199, 6787, 624, 19, 13, 44673, 51956, 323, 65276, 8357, 25, 1084, 374, 2989, 311, 10542, 421, 279, 5590, 1880, 374, 4152, 311, 5810, 43147, 476, 7852, 51956, 323, 65276, 8357, 624, 20, 13, 26212, 25, 10328, 9968, 646, 44941, 349, 45805, 11, 432, 1558, 537, 5961, 5240, 77471, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Genetic inheritance: If your parents have oily skin, there is a higher chance that you will also have oily skin.\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics.\n3. Combination skin: Some people have a combination of skin types, which can include oily areas like the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This type of skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.\n4. Poor hygiene and topical applications: It is important to identify if the oiliness is due to natural phenomena or poor hygiene and topical applications.\n5. Diet: Although diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.476939574769578, "g_worst_claim": 0.0583328902721405, "g_content": 2.1678096771240236, "g_traj_mean": 1.3937560319900513}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 9363, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 74126, 9363, 25, 506, 1541, 6787, 374, 35