, 35810, 25, 8853, 448, 77471, 6787, 525, 803, 36997, 311, 3691, 35810, 13, 1096, 374, 1083, 9733, 304, 279, 4843, 21085, 382, 24, 13, 1417, 6441, 6787, 25, 506, 1541, 6787, 27236, 311, 4994, 41199, 13, 1096, 374, 10982, 304, 279, 4843, 21085, 382, 9485, 9363, 44825, 16792, 311, 279, 4401, 315, 77471, 6787, 11, 438, 32640, 304, 279, 46769, 3897, 13, 151645], "pred": "These factors collectively contribute to the development of oily skin, as outlined in the passages provided.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8871575770471549, "g_worst_claim": -0.08697479963302612, "g_content": 1.3344668579101562, "g_traj_mean": 0.9582449793815613}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [46, 1541, 6787, 374, 15503, 8881, 553, 55004, 11, 448, 264, 3746, 79532, 3487, 421, 825, 594, 6562, 614, 77471, 6787, 13, 1084, 646, 1083, 387, 27061, 553, 73118, 28635, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 892, 1231, 5240, 432, 311, 2525, 323, 728, 13, 5976, 9968, 1558, 537, 5961, 5240, 77471, 6787, 11, 432, 646, 44941, 349, 45805, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 21163, 429, 77471, 15298, 1075, 98949, 323, 49833, 14100, 5240, 5590, 1880, 374, 537, 7248, 553, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Oily skin is primarily caused by genetics, with a strong predisposition if one's parents have oily skin. It can also be influenced by hormonal shifts in the body, which may cause it to come and go. While diet does not directly cause oily skin, it can aggravate acne. However, the myth that oily foods like chocolates and peanut butter cause oiliness is not supported by the given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4351634601312135, "g_worst_claim": 0.5805081587571365, "g_content": 1.7718122327649914, "g_traj_mean": 1.365700602531433}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 77471, 6787, 374, 15503, 8881, 553, 1059, 94354, 9363, 13, 576, 46769, 4190, 429, 421, 264, 1697, 594, 6562, 614, 77471, 6787, 11, 1052, 374, 264, 5080, 28636, 429, 279, 3842, 686, 1083, 614, 77471, 6787, 13, 22406, 11, 73118, 28635, 646, 10173, 279, 2971, 315, 77471, 6787, 11, 3259, 432, 2525, 323, 728, 13, 576, 46769, 1083, 6286, 429, 9968, 702, 264, 7199, 2456, 389, 77471, 6787, 11, 80903, 429, 4185, 50186, 911, 2816, 6405, 15298, 14381, 77471, 6787, 525, 537, 13382, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, oily skin is primarily caused by hereditary factors. The passages suggest that if a person's parents have oily skin, there is a higher likelihood that the individual will also have oily skin. Additionally, hormonal shifts can influence the condition of oily skin, making it come and go. The passages also mention that diet has a limited effect on oily skin, emphasizing that common myths about greasy foods causing oily skin are not accurate.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9004940520671807, "g_worst_claim": 0.0126505047082901, "g_content": 1.1606799905950373, "g_traj_mean": 0.8540274500846863}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "503", "question": "factors that cause oily skin", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main factors that contribute to oily skin are:\n\n1. Genetics: According to passage 1, oily skin is hereditary, meaning that if one's parents have oily skin, they are more likely to experience it themselves.\n2. Hormonal shifts: Passage 1 suggests that hormonal changes in the body can cause oily skin to come and go.\n3. Diet: While diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin, according to passage 1.\n4. Poor hygiene: Passage 2 mentions that poor hygiene and topical applications can contribute to oily skin.\n5. Combination skin: Passage 3 defines different skin types, including combination skin, which can be prone to oily skin in certain areas, such as the T-zone.\n\nThere is no additional information provided in the passages to suggest other factors that might contribute to oily skin. Therefore, the answer to the question is based on the information provided in the passages.", "pred": "3. Combination skin: Some people have combination skin, which can be dry or normal in some areas and oily in others, such as the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). The passages suggest that combination skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "3. Combination skin: Some people have combination skin, which can be dry or normal in some areas and oily in others, such as the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). The passages suggest that combination skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. Genetic inheritance: If your parents have oily skin, there is a higher chance that you will also have oily skin.\\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics.\\n3. Combination skin: Some people have a combination of skin types, which can include oily areas like the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This type of skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.\\n4. Poor hygiene and topical applications: It is important to identify if the oiliness is due to natural phenomena or poor hygiene and topical applications.\\n5. Diet: Although diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin.\", \"Based on the given passages, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. Heredity: Oily skin is hereditary, meaning if your parents have oily skin, there is a high chance you will too. This is mentioned in passages 1 and 2.\\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may have less to do with genes and more to do with hormonal shifts in your body. This is mentioned in passage 1.\\n3. No significant effect from diet: While diet can aggravate acne, it doesn't cause oily skin. This is mentioned in both passages 1 and 2.\\n4. No significant effect from topical applications: Contrary to popular belief, your diet has a limited effect on the oiliness of the skin. This is mentioned in passage 2.\\n5. Different skin types: Some people have a combination of skin types in different areas of their skin, which can include oily skin. This is mentioned in passage 3.\\n6. Aging: Your skin type can change over time, with younger people more likely to have a normal skin type than older people. This is mentioned in passage 3.\\n7. Combination skin type: Combination skin can be dry or normal in some areas and oily in others, such as the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This is mentioned in passage 3.\", \"Based on the given passages, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. Genetic inheritance: If your mother or father has oily skin, you are likely to have it as well. This is due to the hereditary nature of oily skin. The passages suggest that the truth is people should blame their genes for oily skin rather than blaming it on diet or lifestyle changes.\\n\\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may have less to do with genetics and more to do with hormonal changes in your body. The passages also suggest that diet has a limited effect on the oiliness of the skin.\\n\\n3. Combination skin: Some people have combination skin, which can be dry or normal in some areas and oily in others, such as the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). The passages suggest that combination skin can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin.\", \"Based on the given passages, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. Genetics: Oily skin is hereditary. If your parents have oily skin, there is a higher likelihood that you will have oily skin as well.\\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be due to hormonal changes in your body.\\n3. Poor hygiene and topical applications: Oily skin can be caused by poor cleanliness or the use of certain topical products.\\n4. Diet: Although diet does not directly cause oily skin, it can exacerbate acne, which may be linked to oily skin.\\n5. Combination skin type: Some people have a combination of skin types, including oily areas like the T-zone, which can contribute to oily skin.\\n\\nThese factors can affect the oiliness of the skin and are important to consider when trying to manage oily skin.\"]", "time_sec": 27.312, "generation_time_seconds": 26.4911, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8159, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 9363, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 74126, 41822, 25, 1416, 697, 6562, 614, 77471, 6787, 11, 1052, 374, 264, 5080, 6012, 429, 498, 686, 1083, 614, 77471, 6787, 624, 17, 13, 91108, 24202, 28635, 25, 1416, 697, 77471, 6787, 4041, 323, 5780, 11, 432, 1231, 387, 803, 5435, 311, 73118, 4344, 304, 697, 2487, 4751, 1091, 55004, 624, 18, 13, 858