{"id": "504", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "gt": "The floor of a tropical rainforest biome is characterized by a fast rate of decay due to the heat and moisture. This decay provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow. Various types of fruits, nuts, herbs, and mushrooms grow on the rainforest floor. Additionally, vines and ferns grow all over the rainforest, including the floor, helping to connect the various layers of the biome.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines. These plants help to connect the different layers of the biome. Additionally, the floor of the tropical rainforest is characterized by high humidity and frequent rainfall, which contribute to the rapid decomposition of dead plant material and animals, providing rich nutrients for the growth of other plants.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines. These plants help to connect the different layers of the biome. Additionally, the floor of the tropical rainforest is characterized by high humidity and frequent rainfall, which contribute to the rapid decomposition of dead plant material and animals, providing rich nutrients for the growth of other plants.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\\n\\n1. The floor is home to various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines.\\n2. It supports a diverse range of flora, including bananas which grow on vines.\\n3. The floor is characterized by high humidity due to the heavy rainfall typical of tropical rainforests.\\n4. The rapid decomposition of organic matter on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.\", \"Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\\n\\n1. The floor of the tropical rainforest is home to a variety of plants and animals.\\n2. It is characterized by high humidity due to the abundant rainfall.\\n3. There are several types of plants, including herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\\n4. Various types of fruits and nuts grow on the plants and in the trees.\\n5. The floor supports diverse ecosystems, with different species occupying various levels and niches.\\n6. The decay of plants and animals provides rich nutrients for the growth of other plants on the floor.\", \"Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines. These plants help to connect the different layers of the biome. Additionally, the floor of the tropical rainforest is characterized by high humidity and frequent rainfall, which contribute to the rapid decomposition of dead plant material and animals, providing rich nutrients for the growth of other plants.\", \"Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include various types of plants such as vines and ferns that grow all over the biome. Examples of floor vegetation include herbs, mushrooms, and fruits like bananas. The floor of the tropical rainforest is characterized by a high level of humidity due to the heavy rainfall, which averages 50 to 260 inches (125 to 660 cm.) per year. The decaying matter from plants and animals that die on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.\"]", "time_sec": 17.185, "generation_time_seconds": 16.3351, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8447, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 2114, 311, 5257, 4494, 315, 10779, 1741, 438, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 85429, 624, 17, 13, 1084, 11554, 264, 16807, 2088, 315, 80988, 11, 2670, 67342, 892, 3063, 389, 85429, 624, 18, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 31871, 553, 1550, 37093, 4152, 311, 279, 8811, 52858, 14260, 315, 34048, 11174, 1324, 36279, 624, 19, 13, 576, 11048, 65166, 315, 17356, 4925, 389, 279, 6422, 5707, 9080, 36393, 369, 1008, 10779, 311, 3063, 504, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\n\n1. The floor is home to various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines.\n2. It supports a diverse range of flora, including bananas which grow on vines.\n3. The floor is characterized by high humidity due to the heavy rainfall typical of tropical rainforests.\n4. The rapid decomposition of organic matter on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.13795330828041, "g_worst_claim": 0.27518698904249406, "g_content": 1.318163235982259, "g_traj_mean": 0.931755542755127}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 6422, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 374, 2114, 311, 264, 8045, 315, 10779, 323, 9898, 624, 17, 13, 1084, 374, 31871, 553, 1550, 37093, 4152, 311, 279, 43511, 52858, 624, 18, 13, 2619, 525, 3807, 4494, 315, 10779, 11, 2670, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 25322, 11, 323, 29949, 624, 19, 13, 39641, 4494, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 3063, 389, 279, 10779, 323, 304, 279, 12408, 624, 20, 13, 576, 6422, 11554, 16807, 60851, 11, 448, 2155, 9419, 71180, 5257, 5866, 323, 57871, 288, 624, 21, 13, 576, 30715, 315, 10779, 323, 9898, 5707, 9080, 36393, 369, 279, 6513, 315, 1008, 10779, 389, 279, 6422, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. The floor of the tropical rainforest is home to a variety of plants and animals.\n2. It is characterized by high humidity due to the abundant rainfall.\n3. There are several types of plants, including herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\n4. Various types of fruits and nuts grow on the plants and in the trees.\n5. The floor supports diverse ecosystems, with different species occupying various levels and niches.\n6. The decay of plants and animals provides rich nutrients for the growth of other plants on the floor.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6996062356785416, "g_worst_claim": 0.17118728160858154, "g_content": 1.3431785458424053, "g_traj_mean": 0.7705157399177551}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 279, 9362, 315, 5257, 4494, 315, 10779, 1741, 438, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 85429, 13, 4220, 10779, 1492, 311, 4564, 279, 2155, 13617, 315, 279, 83610, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 6422, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 374, 31871, 553, 1550, 37093, 323, 20757, 52858, 11, 892, 16792, 311, 279, 11048, 65166, 315, 5593, 6008, 3684, 323, 9898, 11, 8241, 9080, 36393, 369, 279, 6513, 315, 1008, 10779, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines. These plants help to connect the different layers of the biome. Additionally, the floor of the tropical rainforest is characterized by high humidity and frequent rainfall, which contribute to the rapid decomposition of dead plant material and animals, providing rich nutrients for the growth of other plants.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8619964715252575, "g_worst_claim": 0.2780144214630127, "g_content": 1.6531907988757621, "g_traj_mean": 0.901555597782135}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 5257, 4494, 315, 10779, 1741, 438, 85429, 323, 87024, 82, 429, 3063, 678, 916, 279, 83610, 13, 25311, 315, 6422, 53732, 2924, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 25322, 1075, 67342, 13, 576, 6422, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 374, 31871, 553, 264, 1550, 2188, 315, 37093, 4152, 311, 279, 8811, 52858, 11, 892, 48820, 220, 20, 15, 311, 220, 17, 21, 15, 14924, 320, 16, 17, 20, 311, 220, 21, 21, 15, 9961, 6138, 817, 1042, 13, 576, 1622, 17270, 4925, 504, 10779, 323, 9898, 429, 2746, 389, 279, 6422, 5707, 9080, 36393, 369, 1008, 10779, 311, 3063, 504, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include various types of plants such as vines and ferns that grow all over the biome. Examples of floor vegetation include herbs, mushrooms, and fruits like bananas. The floor of the tropical rainforest is characterized by a high level of humidity due to the heavy rainfall, which averages 50 to 260 inches (125 to 660 cm.) per year. The decaying matter from plants and animals that die on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3693416264699247, "g_worst_claim": 0.2884033719698588, "g_content": 1.8583138077347368, "g_traj_mean": 1.292994737625122}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "507", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor are:\n\n1. High levels of rainfall, with some areas receiving up to 400 inches of rain annually.\n2. High humidity due to the large amount of rainfall.\n3. Abundant vegetation, including tall trees, vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\n4. Quick decay of plant and animal matter due to the heat and moisture, which provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow.\n5. Presence of bananas growing on vines.\n\nTherefore, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by high rainfall, humidity, and lush vegetation, with a diverse array of plant species and a rapid rate of decay and nutrient cycling.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\n\n1. Presence of various plants such as vines, ferns, herbs, and mushrooms.\n2. Growth of fruits and nuts on plants and in trees.\n3. Support for the connections between the different layers of the tropical rainforest biome.\n4. Dense vegetation due to the abundant sunlight and rain.\n5. Rich nutrients available from the decaying organic matter of plants and animals, which supports the growth of other plants.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\n\n1. Presence of various plants such as vines, ferns, herbs, and mushrooms.\n2. Growth of fruits and nuts on plants and in trees.\n3. Support for the connections between the different layers of the tropical rainforest biome.\n4. Dense vegetation due to the abundant sunlight and rain.\n5. Rich nutrients available from the decaying organic matter of plants and animals, which supports the growth of other plants.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\\n\\n1. The floor is home to various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines.\\n2. It supports a diverse range of flora, including bananas which grow on vines.\\n3. The floor is characterized by high humidity due to the heavy rainfall typical of tropical rainforests.\\n4. The rapid decomposition of organic matter on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.\", \"Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include being wet, humid, and having a high number of vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, and various types of fruits and nuts growing on the plants and in the trees. This layer is vital for the overall structure of the tropical rainforest biome.\", \"Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of various types of plants such as vines, ferns, herbs, and mushrooms. These plants help to connect the different layers found in the biome. Examples of plants found on the floor include herbs and mushrooms that grow on the floor, as well as various types of fruits and nuts that grow on the plants and in the trees. Bananas are also mentioned as growing on vines in this particular biome. The decay of plants and animals that die in the location provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.\", \"Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\\n\\n1. Presence of various plants such as vines, ferns, herbs, and mushrooms.\\n2. Growth of fruits and nuts on plants and in trees.\\n3. Support for the connections between the different layers of the tropical rainforest biome.\\n4. Dense vegetation due to the abundant sunlight and rain.\\n5. Rich nutrients available from the decaying organic matter of plants and animals, which supports the growth of other plants.\"]", "time_sec": 16.142, "generation_time_seconds": 15.3967, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7407, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 2114, 311, 5257, 4494, 315, 10779, 1741, 438, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 85429, 624, 17, 13, 1084, 11554, 264, 16807, 2088, 315, 80988, 11, 2670, 67342, 892, 3063, 389, 85429, 624, 18, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 31871, 553, 1550, 37093, 4152, 311, 279, 8811, 52858, 14260, 315, 34048, 11174, 1324, 36279, 624, 19, 13, 576, 11048, 65166, 315, 17356, 4925, 389, 279, 6422, 5707, 9080, 36393, 369, 1008, 10779, 311, 3063, 504, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\n\n1. The floor is home to various types of plants such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines.\n2. It supports a diverse range of flora, including bananas which grow on vines.\n3. The floor is characterized by high humidity due to the heavy rainfall typical of tropical rainforests.\n4. The rapid decomposition of organic matter on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.136683303790751, "g_worst_claim": 0.24438450733820596, "g_content": 1.3214041392008464, "g_traj_mean": 0.9325355887413025}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 1660, 14401, 11, 65938, 11, 323, 3432, 264, 1550, 1372, 315, 85429, 11, 87024, 82, 11, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 5257, 4494, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 7826, 389, 279, 10779, 323, 304, 279, 12408, 13, 1096, 6193, 374, 16198, 369, 279, 8084, 5944, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 83610, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include being wet, humid, and having a high number of vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, and various types of fruits and nuts growing on the plants and in the trees. This layer is vital for the overall structure of the tropical rainforest biome.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7775158015886943, "g_worst_claim": 0.19292869170506796, "g_content": 2.148382910366716, "g_traj_mean": 1.0229759216308594}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 279, 9362, 315, 5257, 4494, 315, 10779, 1741, 438, 85429, 11, 87024, 82, 11, 41293, 11, 323, 47151, 13, 4220, 10779, 1492, 311, 4564, 279, 2155, 13617, 1730, 304, 279, 83610, 13, 25311, 315, 10779, 1730, 389, 279, 6422, 2924, 41293, 323, 47151, 429, 3063, 389, 279, 6422, 11, 438, 1632, 438, 5257, 4494, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 429, 3063, 389, 279, 10779, 323, 304, 279, 12408, 13, 22730, 25908, 525, 1083, 9733, 438, 7826, 389, 85429, 304, 419, 3953, 83610, 13, 576, 30715, 315, 10779, 323, 9898, 429, 2746, 304, 279, 3728, 5707, 9080, 36393, 369, 1008, 10779, 311, 3063, 504, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of various types of plants such as vines, ferns, herbs, and mushrooms. These plants help to connect the different layers found in the biome. Examples of plants found on the floor include herbs and mushrooms that grow on the floor, as well as various types of fruits and nuts that grow on the plants and in the trees. Bananas are also mentioned as growing on vines in this particular biome. The decay of plants and animals that die in the location provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6574639692279027, "g_worst_claim": 0.24438450733820596, "g_content": 2.8364759172712053, "g_traj_mean": 1.6994210481643677}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 78623, 315, 5257, 10779, 1741, 438, 85429, 11, 87024, 82, 11, 41293, 11, 323, 47151, 624, 17, 13, 33771, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 389, 10779, 323, 304, 12408, 624, 18, 13, 9186, 369, 279, 13234, 1948, 279, 2155, 13617, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 83610, 624, 19, 13, 42522, 53732, 4152, 311, 279, 43511, 39020, 323, 11174, 624, 20, 13, 8107, 36393, 2500, 504, 279, 1622, 17270, 17356, 4925, 315, 10779, 323, 9898, 11, 892, 11554, 279, 6513, 315, 1008, 10779, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\n\n1. Presence of various plants such as vines, ferns, herbs, and mushrooms.\n2. Growth of fruits and nuts on plants and in trees.\n3. Support for the connections between the different layers of the tropical rainforest biome.\n4. Dense vegetation due to the abundant sunlight and rain.\n5. Rich nutrients available from the decaying organic matter of plants and animals, which supports the growth of other plants.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0148517413981377, "g_worst_claim": 0.05846114953358968, "g_content": 1.4863739013671875, "g_traj_mean": 0.9844049215316772}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.06, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "508", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and contain more of the tenderloin or fillet than sirloin steaks. They are essentially a larger version of the T-Bone steak, carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin. On the other hand, the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, continuing off the short loin from which T-bone, porterhouse, and club steaks are cut. The sirloin is divided into several different types of steak.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the two is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks, with a corresponding price difference. Both steaks are cut from the short loin area of the beef, and a Porterhouse is just a larger version of the T-Bone because it is carved from the larger portion of the tenderloin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between the two is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks, with a corresponding price difference. Both steaks are cut from the short loin area of the beef, and a Porterhouse is just a larger version of the T-Bone because it is carved from the larger portion of the tenderloin.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, while the porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that the sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, while the porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin. Additionally, the porterhouse steak contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than the T-Bone steak.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between the two is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks, with a corresponding price difference. Both steaks are cut from the short loin area of the beef, and a Porterhouse is just a larger version of the T-Bone because it is carved from the larger portion of the tenderloin.\"]", "time_sec": 13.427, "generation_time_seconds": 12.6728, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7495, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 429, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 374, 264, 48959, 3931, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 9864, 11, 1393, 279, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 8916, 5610, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, while the porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9812746618899348, "g_worst_claim": 0.40438878536224365, "g_content": 1.9805267997409985, "g_traj_mean": 1.1725373268127441}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 4