, 3349, 714, 3010, 279, 6012, 311, 3164, 400, 16, 15, 11, 15, 15, 15, 13, 51778, 614, 279, 6638, 311, 15759, 304, 1493, 8350, 11552, 4479, 435, 80535, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. **Cash Tip Board Raffles**: These raffles are not included in the ticket price but offer the chance to win $10,000. Participants have the opportunity to participate in these cash tip board raffles.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.70193184282335, "g_worst_claim": 0.41670819123586017, "g_content": 2.790999256480824, "g_traj_mean": 1.6728394031524658}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 16.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "520", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's how raffles work:\n\nA reverse raffle works by having participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, usually between 1 and 55. Each ticket costs $50, and a table consists of 20 individuals who pool their money together to form a complete ticket worth $1000. There are also two $500 prizes, one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled.\n\nThe 50-50 draw is a raffle that takes place during a single event, where tickets are sold to patrons throughout the event by roaming staff. 50% of the gross proceeds go into a prize pool, and the winner of the random draw at the end of the event receives 50% of the prize pool. The remaining 50% goes to a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\n\nFinally, some events may include cash tip board raffles, where participants can pay to play and have the chance to win $10,000. These raffles are not included in the ticket price.", "pred": "3. Cash tip board raffles: Participants have the opportunity to win a $10,000 prize by participating in these raffles, which are not included in the ticket price. Drinks and dinner are included with the ticket price.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "3. Cash tip board raffles: Participants have the opportunity to win a $10,000 prize by participating in these raffles, which are not included in the ticket price. Drinks and dinner are included with the ticket price.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, raffles work as follows:\\n\\n1. **Reverse Raffle**: In a reverse raffle, participants buy tickets with numbers from 1 to approximately 55. Each ticket costs $50, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket worth $1000. There are two $500 prizes: one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled.\\n\\n2. **50-50 Draw**: The 50-50 draw is a raffle held during a single day at a particular event. Tickets are sold to patrons throughout the stadium during the event by roaming staff equipped with handheld electronic mobile devices. The gross proceeds of 50-50 tickets sold at the event go into a prize pool. 50% of the prize pool will go to the winner of the random draw which occurs towards the end of the event. The remaining 50% will be set aside for a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\\n\\n3. **Cash Tip Board Raffles**: These are included with the ticket price and offer the chance to win $10,000.\", \"Based on the given passages, raffles work as follows:\\n\\n1. In a reverse raffle: Participants buy tickets with numbers ranging from 1 to approximately 55. Each ticket costs $50, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket at $1000. There are two $500 prizes, one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled.\\n\\n2. In a 50-50 draw: This is a raffle held during a single day at a particular event. Tickets are sold to patrons throughout the stadium by roaming staff using handheld electronic mobile devices. Proceeds from the tickets go into a prize pool. At the end of the event, a random draw occurs, and 50% of the prize pool is given to the winner. The remaining 50% is set aside for a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\\n\\n3. Cash tip board raffles: Participants have the opportunity to win a $10,000 prize by participating in these raffles, which are not included in the ticket price. Drinks and dinner are included with the ticket price.\", \"Based on the given passages, raffles work as follows:\\n\\n1. In a reverse raffle, participants buy tickets with a number, and the highest-numbered ticket wins. The prizes are distributed among the top two tickets drawn.\\n2. The 50-50 draw is a raffle where proceeds are split between the winner and a charity. The draw occurs at the end of the event.\\n3. Cash tip board raffles are separate events where participants can win additional prizes, such as $10,000, after paying for their tickets.\\n\\nThese details show different ways raffles operate, including ticket purchases, prize distribution, and additional opportunities for winnings.\", \"Based on the given passages, raffles typically involve selling tickets for a chance to win a prize. The prize pool is created by the money collected from ticket sales. In a reverse raffle, participants buy tickets with numbers from 1 to approximately 55, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket at $1000. Two $500 prizes are drawn, one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled. The exact number of participants is not specified but is around 55. In a 50-50 draw, held during a single day at a particular event, the gross proceeds of tickets sold go into a prize pool. 50% of the prize pool goes to the winner, and 50% is set aside for a charitable purpose. The specifics of how other types of raffles might work are not provided in the given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 26.563, "generation_time_seconds": 25.6449, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9136, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 435, 80535, 975, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 45695, 431, 44090, 95518, 758, 264, 9931, 435, 44090, 11, 13026, 3695, 14403, 448, 5109, 504, 220, 16, 311, 13187, 220, 20, 20, 13, 8886, 11727, 7049, 400, 20, 15, 11, 323, 264, 1965, 315, 220, 17, 15, 7775, 41575, 825, 4583, 11727, 5802, 400, 16, 15, 15, 15, 13, 2619, 525, 1378, 400, 20, 15, 15, 37408, 25, 825, 369, 279, 4124, 11958, 13330, 323, 825, 369, 279, 1156, 11727, 13238, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 20, 15, 12, 20, 15, 11992, 95518, 576, 220, 20, 15, 12, 20, 15, 4038, 374, 264, 435, 44090, 5644, 2337, 264, 3175, 1899, 518, 264, 3953, 1538, 13, 35615, 525, 6088, 311, 51760, 6814, 279, 23889, 2337, 279, 1538, 553, 68253, 5570, 18650, 448, 64949, 14346, 6371, 7611, 13, 576, 19952, 33455, 315, 220, 20, 1