 an overall average high of 79 degrees Fahrenheit and an average low of 56 degrees Fahrenheit.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.975186232364539, "g_worst_claim": 0.5773682594299316, "g_content": 1.0745543311623966, "g_traj_mean": 1.0099645853042603}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 5461, 1550, 9315, 304, 41102, 91966, 4060, 11, 9589, 374, 220, 22, 24, 12348, 68723, 11, 323, 279, 5461, 3347, 374, 220, 20, 21, 12348, 68723, 13, 576, 5461, 9104, 369, 41102, 91966, 4060, 646, 387, 1730, 304, 279, 220, 18, 17, 18, 16, 15, 10308, 2038, 11, 323, 432, 374, 14260, 369, 279, 9315, 311, 5943, 311, 220, 17, 15, 12348, 68723, 10293, 23, 12348, 61347, 8, 476, 4722, 60916, 329, 2673, 504, 6702, 311, 5470, 11, 448, 458, 5461, 315, 1378, 476, 2326, 21461, 24084, 1741, 19879, 13, 22406, 11, 1052, 525, 2849, 979, 279, 8028, 9315, 21025, 311, 220, 19, 15, 11, 220, 18, 17, 11, 476, 220, 17, 15, 12348, 68723, 476, 4722, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the average high temperature in Tallahassee, Florida is 79 degrees Fahrenheit, and the average low is 56 degrees Fahrenheit. The average weather for Tallahassee can be found in the 32310 zip code, and it is typical for the temperature to drop to 20 degrees Fahrenheit (-8 degrees Celsius) or lower sporadically from November to March, with an average of two or three nights experiencing such temperatures. Additionally, there are days when the minimum temperature drops to 40, 32, or 20 degrees Fahrenheit or lower.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.184105333445526, "g_worst_claim": 0.3911294070157138, "g_content": 1.5686957881135761, "g_traj_mean": 1.3342586755752563}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 41102, 91966, 4060, 11, 9589, 702, 458, 8084, 5461, 1550, 9315, 315, 220, 22, 24, 12348, 323, 458, 5461, 3347, 315, 220, 20, 21, 12348, 13, 576, 5461, 9315, 369, 41102, 91966, 4060, 21283, 504, 13187, 220, 18, 17, 311, 220, 22, 24, 12348, 68723, 11, 448, 27861, 19879, 25100, 311, 438, 3347, 438, 220, 17, 15, 12348, 68723, 476, 4722, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, Tallahassee, Florida has an overall average high temperature of 79 degrees and an average low of 56 degrees. The average temperature for Tallahassee ranges from approximately 32 to 79 degrees Fahrenheit, with occasional temperatures dropping to as low as 20 degrees Fahrenheit or lower.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9469655174197572, "g_worst_claim": 0.5777309338251749, "g_content": 1.3594303746377268, "g_traj_mean": 1.051312804222107}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "530", "question": "how does ez pass charges work", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here is how E-ZPass charging works:\n\nWhen you sign up for E-ZPass, a certain amount is charged to your credit card to establish a balance (specifically, $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag). This balance is used to pay for tolls as you drive through toll lanes. When you drive through a toll booth, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by the antennae, and your E-ZPass account is charged the appropriate amount. The amount is deducted from your balance. If your balance falls below a certain threshold ($10 for the TX-Tag), E-ZPass will charge your credit card an additional $100 or $25 to top up your balance.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows: As your vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on your vehicle's windshield is read by antennae. Your E-ZPass® account is charged the proper amount as your vehicle passes through the toll lane. Feedback is provided on an electronic display. If your vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies you as a violator, and cameras take photos of your license plate for processing. The toll tag is used to charge the account based on the distance traveled.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows: As your vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on your vehicle's windshield is read by antennae. Your E-ZPass® account is charged the proper amount as your vehicle passes through the toll lane. Feedback is provided on an electronic display. If your vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies you as a violator, and cameras take photos of your license plate for processing. The toll tag is used to charge the account based on the distance traveled.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows:\\n\\n1. When a vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on the windshield is read by the antennae.\\n2. The E-ZPass account is charged the proper amount as the vehicle passes through the toll lane.\\n3. Feedback is provided to the driver on an electronic display.\\n4. If the vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies it as a violator, and cameras take photos of the license plate for processing.\", \"Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows: As your vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on your vehicle's windshield is read by antennae. Your E-ZPass® account is charged the proper amount as your vehicle passes through the toll lane. Feedback is provided on an electronic display. If your vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies you as a violator, and cameras take photos of your license plate for processing. The toll tag is used to charge the account based on the distance traveled.\", \"Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows:\\n\\n1. When entering a toll lane, the E-ZPass tag on the windshield is read by the antennae.\\n2. Your E-ZPass account is automatically charged the appropriate toll amount.\\n3. Feedback is displayed on an electronic display to confirm the charge.\\n4. If the vehicle does not have an E-ZPass tag, the system identifies it as a violator.\\n\\nThis process ensures seamless toll payment and monitoring for E-ZPass users.\", \"Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work by reading the toll tag mounted on the vehicle's windshield as it enters the toll lane. The system then charges the proper amount to the E-ZPass account. If the vehicle does not have a toll tag, it is classified as a violator, and cameras take photos of the license plate for processing.\"]", "time_sec": 16.007, "generation_time_seconds": 15.3076, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6934, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 468, 11171, 12187, 10195, 975, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 3197, 264, 7310, 28833, 264, 25851, 21272, 11, 279, 25851, 4772, 21810, 389, 279, 73939, 374, 1349, 553, 279, 71477, 5918, 624, 17, 13, 576, 468, 11171, 12187, 2692, 374, 11430, 279, 6169, 3311, 438, 279, 7310, 16211, 1526, 279, 25851, 21272, 624, 18, 13, 36857, 374, 3897, 311, 279, 5579, 389, 458, 14346, 3037, 624, 19, 13, 1416, 279, 7310, 1558, 537, 614, 264, 25851, 4772, 11, 279, 1849, 536, 9606, 432, 438, 264, 4634, 850, 11, 323, 18139, 1896, 7249, 315, 279, 5723, 11968, 369, 8692, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows:\n\n1. When a vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on the windshield is read by the antennae.\n2. The E-ZPass account is charged the proper amount as the vehicle passes through the toll lane.\n3. Feedback is provided to the driver on an electronic display.\n4. If the vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies it as a violator, and cameras take photos of the license plate for processing.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.542869667315968, "g_worst_claim": 0.4287347396214803, "g_content": 2.306482842627992, "g_traj_mean": 1.4509427547454834}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 468, 11171, 12187, 10195, 975, 438, 11017, 25, 1634, 697, 7310, 28833, 264, 25851, 21272, 11, 279, 25851, 4772, 21810, 389, 697, 7310, 594, 73939, 374, 1349, 553, 71477, 5918, 13, 4615, 468, 11171, 12187, 11909, 2692, 374, 11430, 279, 6169, 3311, 438, 697, 7310, 16211, 1526, 279, 25851, 21272, 13, 36857, 374, 3897, 389, 458, 14346, 3037, 13, 1416, 697, 7310, 1558, 537, 614, 264, 25851, 4772, 11, 279, 1849, 536, 9606, 498, 438, 264, 4634, 850, 11, 323, 18139, 1896, 7249, 315, 697, 5723, 11968, 369, 8692, 13, 576, 25851, 4772, 374, 1483, 311, 6757, 279, 2692, 3118, 389, 279, 6010, 30696, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows: As your vehicle enters a toll lane, the toll tag mounted on your vehicle's windshield is read by antennae. Your E-ZPass® account is charged the proper amount as your vehicle passes through the toll lane. Feedback is provided on an electronic display. If your vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system classifies you as a violator, and cameras take photos of your license plate for processing. The toll tag is used to charge the account based on the distance traveled.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6029371464693989, "g_worst_claim": 0.3979872385660807, "g_content": 2.082278382544424, "g_traj_mean": 1.5502113103866577}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 468, 11171, 12187, 10195, 975, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 3197, 16262, 264, 25851, 21272, 11, 279, 468, 11171, 12187, 4772, 389, 279, 73939, 374, 1349, 553, 279, 71477, 5918, 624, 17, 13, 4615, 468, 11171, 12187, 2692, 374, 9463, 11430, 279, 8311, 25851, 3311, 624, 18, 13, 36857, 374, 12596, 389, 458, 14346, 3037, 311, 7683, 279, 6757, 624, 19, 13, 1416, 279, 7310, 1558, 537, 614, 458, 468, 11171, 12187, 4772, 11, 279, 1849, 35511, 432, 438, 264, 4634, 850, 382, 1986, 1882, 25351, 46870, 25851, 8160, 323, 16558, 369, 468, 11171, 12187, 3847, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work as follows:\n\n1. When entering a toll lane, the E-ZPass tag on the windshield is read by the antennae.\n2. Your E-ZPass account is automatically charged the appropriate toll amount.\n3. Feedback is displayed on an electronic display to confirm the charge.\n4. If the vehicle does not have an E-ZPass tag, the system identifies it as a violator.\n\nThis process ensures seamless toll payment and monitoring for E-ZPass users.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2782289827598179, "g_worst_claim": 0.4287347396214803, "g_content": 1.6532315793244734, "g_traj_mean": 1.0524169206619263}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 468, 11171, 12187, 10195, 975, 553, 5290, 279, 25851, 4772, 21810, 389, 279, 7310, 594, 73939, 438, 432, 28833, 279, 25851, 21272, 13, 576, 1849, 1221, 10195, 279, 6169, 3311, 311, 279, 468, 11171, 12187, 2692, 13, 1416, 279, 7310, 1558, 537, 614, 264, 25851, 4772, 11, 432, 374, 21091, 438, 264, 4634, 850, 11, 323, 18139, 1896, 7249, 315, 279, 5723, 11968, 369, 8692, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, E-ZPass charges work by reading the toll tag mounted on the vehicle's windshield as it enters the toll lane. The system then charges the proper amount to the E-ZPass account. If the vehicle does not have a toll tag, it is classified as a violator, and cameras take photos of the license plate for processing.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4542154417596505, "g_worst_claim": 0.40930767854054767, "g_content": 2.540907859802246, "g_traj_mean": 1.4656341075897217}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "532", "question": "what are safety pins in a first aid box used for", "gt": "Safety pins in a first aid box are used for various purposes such as immobilizing an arm by creating a makeshift sling, securing a bandana over a wounded arm or leg, closing severe wounds in emergency situations, and removing splinters.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for multiple purposes in first aid. They can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling. Safety pins can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg. They can even be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. Additionally, safety pins are used to remove splinters in the wilderness.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for multiple purposes in first aid. They can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling. Safety pins can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg. They can even be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. Additionally, safety pins are used to remove splinters in the wilderness.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for several purposes:\\n\\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\\n3. Keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\\n4. Removing splinters in the wilderness.\", \"Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for multiple purposes in first aid. They can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling. Safety pins can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg. They can even be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. Additionally, safety pins are used to remove splinters in the wilderness.\", \"Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for various purposes: immobilizing an arm by attaching a long sleeve shirt cuff to the chest to form a makeshift arm sling, securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg, and keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. Additionally, safety pins are used to remove splinters in the wilderness.\", \"Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for immobilizing limbs, securing bandages, and closing severe wounds in place of stitches. They are versatile and can even be used to remove splinters in the wilderness.\"]", "time_sec": 14.364, "generation_time_seconds": 13.623, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7353, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 7149, 26944, 304, 264, 1156, 12296, 3745, 525, 1483, 369, 3807, 9895, 1447, 16, 13, 15335, 27929, 4849, 458, 6773, 553, 8983, 1229, 279, 74423, 315, 264, 1293, 36153, 15478, 311, 1181, 15138, 311, 11153, 264, 86080, 6773, 87633, 624, 17, 13, 4520, 1677, 264, 7055, 3362, 916, 264, 27493, 323, 34663, 6773, 476, 2472, 624, 18, 13, 55378, 264, 15386, 26555, 7877, 304, 1992, 315, 61936, 304, 13207, 13161, 624, 19, 13, 66703, 12503, 49940, 304, 279, 48262, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for several purposes:\n\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\n3. Keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\n4. Removing splinters in the wilderness.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.256683109880804, "g_worst_claim": 0.4198872248331706, "g_content": 2.6218253048983486, "g_traj_mean": 2.079662561416626}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 7149, 26944, 304, 264, 1156, 12296, 3745, 525, 1483, 369, 5248, 9895, 304, 1156, 12296, 13, 2379, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 76341, 551, 458, 6773, 553, 8983, 1229, 279, 74423, 315, 264, 1293, 36153, 15478, 311, 1181, 15138, 311, 11153, 264, 86080, 6773, 87633, 13, 18702, 26944, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 9767, 264, 7055, 3362, 916, 264, 27493, 323, 34663, 6773, 476, 2472, 13, 2379, 646, 1496, 387, 1483, 311, 1492, 2506, 264, 15386, 26555, 7877, 304, 1992, 315, 61936, 304, 13207, 13161, 13, 22406, 11, 7149, 26944, 525, 1483, 311, 4057, 12503, 49940, 304, 279, 48262, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for multiple purposes in first aid. They can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling. Safety pins can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg. They can even be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. Additionally, safety pins are used to remove splinters in the wilderness.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6600564708603394, "g_worst_claim": 0.43643760681152344, "g_content": 2.295094021883878, "g_traj_mean": 1.886486291885376}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 7149, 26944, 304, 264, 1156, 12296, 3745, 525, 1483, 369, 5257, 9895, 25, 76341, 4849, 458, 6773, 553, 71808, 264, 1293, 36153, 15478, 74423, 311, 279, 15138, 311, 1352, 264, 86080, 6773, 87633, 11, 40477, 264, 7055, 3362, 916, 264, 27493, 323, 34663, 6773, 476, 2472, 11, 323, 10282, 264, 15386, 26555, 7877, 304, 1992, 315, 61936, 304, 13207, 13