-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "534", "question": "what are safety pins in a first aid box used for", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for the following purposes:\n\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to create a makeshift arm sling (Passage 2).\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg (Passage 2).\n3. Helping to keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances (Passage 2).\n4. Removing splinters (Passage 3).\n\nThe passages mention these specific uses for safety pins in a first aid context, but do not provide any additional information regarding their use in a survival kit.", "pred": "1. Immobilizing an arm: A safety pin can be used to pin the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to the chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\n2. Securing a bandana: They can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\n3. Keeping wounds closed: Safety pins can be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\n4. Removing splinters: They are mentioned as a trusted tool for removing splinters in the wilderness.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Immobilizing an arm: A safety pin can be used to pin the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to the chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\n2. Securing a bandana: They can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\n3. Keeping wounds closed: Safety pins can be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\n4. Removing splinters: They are mentioned as a trusted tool for removing splinters in the wilderness.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for several purposes:\\n\\n1. Immobilizing an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\\n2. Securing a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\\n3. Keeping a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\\n4. Removing splinters in the wilderness.\", \"Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for a variety of purposes. They can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling. Safety pins can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg. They can also be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. Additionally, safety pins can be used to remove splinters in the wilderness.\", \"Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for several purposes:\\n\\n1. Immobilizing an arm: A safety pin can be used to pin the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to the chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling.\\n2. Securing a bandana: They can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg.\\n3. Keeping wounds closed: Safety pins can be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances.\\n4. Removing splinters: They are mentioned as a trusted tool for removing splinters in the wilderness.\", \"Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for various purposes. They can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling. Safety pins can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg. They can even be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. Additionally, safety pins are used to remove splinters in the wilderness. Safety pins are considered a valuable item in a survival kit due to their versatility and usefulness in first aid situations.\"]", "time_sec": 17.461, "generation_time_seconds": 16.5238, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9317, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0