 76341, 551, 458, 6773, 553, 8983, 1229, 279, 74423, 315, 264, 1293, 36153, 15478, 311, 1181, 15138, 311, 11153, 264, 86080, 6773, 87633, 13, 18702, 26944, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 9767, 264, 7055, 3362, 916, 264, 27493, 323, 34663, 6773, 476, 2472, 13, 2379, 646, 1496, 387, 1483, 311, 1492, 2506, 264, 15386, 26555, 7877, 304, 1992, 315, 61936, 304, 13207, 13161, 13, 22406, 11, 7149, 26944, 525, 1483, 311, 4057, 12503, 49940, 304, 279, 48262, 13, 18702, 26944, 525, 6509, 264, 15172, 1509, 304, 264, 19661, 16138, 4152, 311, 862, 59012, 323, 75864, 304, 1156, 12296, 14740, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, safety pins in a first aid box are used for various purposes. They can be used to immobilize an arm by pinning the cuff of a long sleeve shirt to its chest to fashion a makeshift arm sling. Safety pins can be used to secure a bandana over a wounded and bleeding arm or leg. They can even be used to help keep a severe wound closed in place of stitches in dire circumstances. Additionally, safety pins are used to remove splinters in the wilderness. Safety pins are considered a valuable item in a survival kit due to their versatility and usefulness in first aid situations.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5102889209141617, "g_worst_claim": 0.20804885717538688, "g_content": 2.109239520448627, "g_traj_mean": 1.719138741493225}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "539", "question": "lyrics he was a friend of mine", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the lyrics \"he was a friend of mine\" are mentioned in the following passages:\n\n* Passage 1: In the context of the Greenbriar Boys recording the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" with singer Dian James in 1963.\n* Passage 2: As part of a fragmented repetition of the line \"He was a friend of mine\" in the passage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is:\n\nPassage 1 and Passage 2", "pred": "Based on the given passages, lyrics to the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" include:\n- \"He was a friend of mine, he was a friend of mine.\"\n- \"He died without a penny, he didn't have a dime.\"\n- \"He was a friend of mine, he died neath the midnight sun.\"\n- \"He was a friend of mine, he never done no wrong.\"\n- \"He never harmed no one.\"\n- \"He was a friend of mine, every time I hear his name, Lord, I just can't keep from crying.\"\n- \"Cause he was a friend of mine.\"\nThe song is attributed to songwriter Dylan Bob.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, lyrics to the song \"He Was a Friend of Mine\" include:\n- \"He was a friend of mine, he was a friend of mine.\"\n- \"He died without a penny, he didn't have a dime.\"\n- \"He was a friend of mine, he died neath the midnight sun.\"\n- \"He was a friend of mine, he never done no wrong.\"\n- \"He never harmed no one.\"\n- \"He was a friend of mine, every time I hear his name, Lord, I just can't keep from crying.\"\n- \"Cause he was a friend of mine.\"\nThe song is attributed to songwriter Dylan Bob.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\" are part of a song that was recorded by various artists including the Greenbriar Boys, the Briarwood Singers, Bobby Bare, and Petula Clark. The song was released in 1963 and 1964. The lyrics are repeated multiple times in the song, emphasizing the bond between the singer and the person being referred to as a friend. The song also mentions the friend's death and the singer's sadness over it.\", \"Based on the given passages, the lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\" are sung in the song \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine\\\" by Bob Dylan. The song was released in 1963 on their Elektra Records album \\\"Dian & the Greenbriar Boys.\\\" The lyrics describe a friend who died without any money, under the midnight sun, and were never wronged. The songwriters are listed as Bobby Bare, with the song being published by Bob Dylan.\", \"Based on the given passages, lyrics to the song \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine\\\" include:\\n- \\\"He was a friend of mine, he was a friend of mine.\\\"\\n- \\\"He died without a penny, he didn't have a dime.\\\"\\n- \\\"He was a friend of mine, he died neath the midnight sun.\\\"\\n- \\\"He was a friend of mine, he never done no wrong.\\\"\\n- \\\"He never harmed no one.\\\"\\n- \\\"He was a friend of mine, every time I hear his name, Lord, I just can't keep from crying.\\\"\\n- \\\"Cause he was a friend of mine.\\\"\\nThe song is attributed to songwriter Dylan Bob.\", \"Based on the given passages, the lyrics \\\"He was a friend of mine\\\" appear in the song \\\"He Was a Friend of Mine,\\\" which has been recorded by several artists including the Greenbriar Boys, the Briarwood Singers, Bobby Bare, and Petula Clark. The song's lyrics express deep sorrow and longing for a friend who has died, including phrases such as \\\"He died without a penny,\\\" \\\"He was a friend of mine,\\\" and \\\"Lord, I just can't keep from cryin'.\\\"\"]", "time_sec": 17.7, "generation_time_seconds": 16.9808, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7146, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 23261, 330, 1519, 572, 264, 4238, 315, 10485, 1, 525, 949, 315, 264, 5492, 429, 572, 12433, 553, 5257, 13511, 2670, 279, 78