laim": 1.8543190294569667, "g_worst_claim": 0.3044215242067973, "g_content": 2.737670644124349, "g_traj_mean": 1.9364761114120483}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.94, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 2.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "608", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To do employee schedules, you need to first understand work laws related to overtime and age restrictions, and you may need to consult a lawyer for this. After that, make a list of all your employees and their duties. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create a chart of work days and hours for each day. Once the schedule is complete, it can be distributed to employees through printing physical copies or sending digital copies to employee email accounts. It's advisable to keep a master schedule in case changes need to be made. Tools like Microsoft Excel can be used to create these schedules, especially as your business grows.", "pred": "1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use software like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing for continued use of the schedule template as the business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use software like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing for continued use of the schedule template as the business grows.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.\", \"Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use software like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing for continued use of the schedule template as the business grows.\", \"Based on the given passages, to create an employee schedule, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n\\nThis information is provided in Passage 2.\", \"Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing for continued use of the schedule template as the business grows.\"]", "time_sec": 17.34, "generation_time_seconds": 16.629, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7019, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 62