{"id": "609", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create employee schedules, start by making a list of all employees and the tasks they can perform. Then, create a chart with the work days and hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to do this. Afterward, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts. It's also important to maintain a master schedule for making any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be modified as your business expands.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n\nThese steps are outlined in passage 2, which provides a straightforward method for organizing and creating a work schedule.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n\nThese steps are outlined in passage 2, which provides a straightforward method for organizing and creating a work schedule.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.\", \"Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n\\nThese steps are outlined in passage 2, which provides a straightforward method for organizing and creating a work schedule.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to do employee schedules:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to make the schedule.\\n4. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n5. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n6. Use tools like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to use the same schedule template as your business grows.\", \"Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue to use the schedule template as your business grows.\"]", "time_sec": 15.202, "generation_time_seconds": 14.5366, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6563, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 624, 18, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 9364, 2551, 9618, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 3259, 