Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create the schedules.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0256798411754753, "g_worst_claim": 0.3219614028930664, "g_content": 2.319772139839504, "g_traj_mean": 1.7508840560913086}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "611", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to create an employee schedule:\n\n1. Talk to a lawyer about work laws: It is important to understand the legal requirements for creating an employee schedule, including paying overtime for hours worked beyond 40 per week. Additionally, there may be other laws to consider, such as restrictions for employees under the age of 18.\n2. Use scheduling software or a simple word processing program: You can create an employee schedule using scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or even a sheet of paper. Make a list of all employees and their duties, and create a chart of work days and hours for each day.\n3. Print or send schedules to employees: Once you have created the schedule, print out copies for each employee or send them to their email accounts. Keep a master schedule for making any changes. If you are using a digital tool, you can easily edit and share the schedule with employees.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to create an employee schedule, such as setting up the schedule format, determining pay rates, or communicating the schedule to employees.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.\", \"Based on the given passages, to do employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule to make any changes.\\nMicrosoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, making it easier to manage as the business grows.\", \"Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\"]", "time_sec": 13.997, "generation_time_seconds": 13.072, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9205, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 624, 18, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 9364, 2551, 9618, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 3259, 894, 4344, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 5100, 21029, 311, 1855, 264, 975, 9700, 369, 5248, 8256, 11, 10693, 498, 311, 3060, 1667, 279, 9700, 3811, 438, 697, 2562, 27715, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9541975283894446, "g_worst_claim": 0.32088702917099, "g_content": 2.469009986290565, "g_traj_mean": 1.903611183166504}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 653, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 624, 18, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 9364, 2551, 9618, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 3259, 894, 4344, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to do employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7865131113264294, "g_worst_claim": 0.3414204915364583, "g_content": 2.3300098964146208, "g_traj_mean": 1.7602580785751343}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 624, 18, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 9364, 2551, 9618, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 311, 1281, 894, 4344, 624, 12778, 21029, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 1855, 264, 975, 9700, 369, 5248, 8256, 11, 3259, 432, 8661, 311, 10091, 438, 279, 2562, 27715, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule to make any changes.\nMicrosoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, making it easier to manage as the business grows.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7454137747929162, "g_worst_claim": 0.32088702917099, "g_content": 2.1395382690429687, "g_traj_mean": 1.754324197769165}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to create employee schedules, follow these steps:\n\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3697461906108228, "g_worst_claim": 0.3220782478650411, "g_content": 1.6455679393949962, "g_traj_mean": 1.6402263641357422}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.22, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "614", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Based on the information given in the passages, to force remove a printer in devices and printers, you need to go to Control Panel, then click on Hardware and Sound, and then on Printers. Right-click the printer that you want to remove, and click Delete. If it doesn't delete, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete. If your printer is connected to your computer via a USB, disconnect the cable, turn the printer on and off again, and ensure it is in a ready state. If you used Print Manager or Printers folder to remove a printer or printer port, close these applications and stop and restart the Spooler Service.", "pred": "1. To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, start by stopping and restarting the Spooler Service.\n2. In Control Panel, navigate to Hardware and Sound, then click on Printers.\n3. Right-click on the printer you want to remove and select Delete if you can do so.\n4. If deletion is unavailable, right-click the printer again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n5. Depending on the printer's connection method, if it's connected with a USB cable, disconnect the cable before proceeding.\n6. Turn the printer off and on again to ensure it is in a ready state before removing it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, start by stopping and restarting the Spooler Service.\n2. In Control Panel, navigate to Hardware and Sound, then click on Printers.\n3. Right-click on the printer you want to remove and select Delete if you can do so.\n4. If deletion is unavailable, right-click the printer again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n5. Depending on the printer's connection method, if it's connected with a USB cable, disconnect the cable before proceeding.\n6. Turn the printer off and on again to ensure it is in a ready state before removing it.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Control Panel.\\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n3. Click on Printers.\\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\\n5. Click Delete.\\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again.\\n7. Click Run as administrator.\\n8. Click Delete.\", \"Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the printer from the devices list.\\n2. Disconnect the USB cable from the printer if it connects to the computer with one.\\n3. Turn the printer off and on again.\\n4. Ensure the printer is in a ready state.\\n\\nThese steps should help in removing the printer forcefully from the Devices and Printers list.\", \"Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers follow these steps:\\nStep 1: Remove the printer from the devices list.\\nStep 2: In Windows Devices and Printers, remove printers and uninstall any Windows print drivers.\\nStep 3: If your printer connects to the computer with a USB cable, disconnect the cable from the printer.\\nStep 4: Turn the printer off and on again.\\nStep 5: Make sure that the printer is in a ready state.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, start by stopping and restarting the Spooler Service.\\n2. In Control Panel, navigate to Hardware and Sound, then click on Printers.\\n3. Right-click on the printer you want to remove and select Delete if you can do so.\\n4. If deletion is unavailable, right-click the printer again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\\n5. Depending on the printer's connection method, if it's connected with a USB cable, disconnect the cable before proceeding.\\n6. Turn the printer off and on again to ensure it is in a ready state before removing it.\"]", "time_sec": 18.475, "generation_time_seconds": 17.7576, "selection_time_seconds": 0.708, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 19, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 10428, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 498, 4157, 3698, 279, 22380, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 624, 22, 13, 9189, 6452, 438, 28093, 624, 23, 13, 9189, 10428, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\n5. Click Delete.\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again.\n7. Click Run as administrator.\n8. Click Delete.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9608221788427013, "g_worst_claim": 0.16229331493377686, "g_content": 0.7999954223632812, "g_traj_mean": 0.6279183626174927}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 22380, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 624, 17, 13, 69090, 279, 11348, 14652, 504, 279, 22380, 421, 432, 33061, 311, 279, 6366, 448, 825, 624, 18, 13, 11999, 279, 22380, 1007, 323, 389, 1549, 624, 19, 13, 29279, 279, 22380, 374, 304, 264, 5527, 1584, 382, 9485, 7354, 1265, 1492, 304, 17592, 279, 22380, 85978, 504, 279, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 1140, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the printer from the devices list.\n2. Disconnect the USB cable from the printer if it connects to the computer with one.\n3. Turn the printer off and on again.\n4. Ensure the printer is in a ready state.\n\nThese steps should help in removing the printer forcefully from the Devices and Printers list.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0456568430201347, "g_worst_claim": 0.23543183008829752, "g_content": 1.0086479187011719, "g_traj_mean": 0.8970094323158264}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 8304, 220, 16, 25, 10783, 279, 22380, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 758, 5515, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 4057, 55953, 323, 53635, 894, 5515, 1173, 11788, 624, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 1416, 697, 22380, 33061, 311, 279, 6366, 448, 264, 11348, 14652, 11, 28969, 279, 14652, 504, 279, 22380, 624, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 11999, 279, 22380, 1007, 323, 389, 1549, 624, 8304, 220, 20, 25, 7405, 2704, 429, 279, 22380, 374, 304, 264, 5527, 1584, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers follow these steps:\nStep 1: Remove the printer from the devices list.\nStep 2: In Windows Devices and Printers, remove printers and uninstall any Windows print drivers.\nStep 3: If your printer connects to the computer with a USB cable, disconnect the cable from the printer.\nStep 4: Turn the printer off and on again.\nStep 5: Make sure that the printer is in a ready state.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2920083670847804, "g_worst_claim": 0.2926245133082072, "g_content": 1.4610309600830078, "g_traj_mean": 1.219245195388794}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1191, 553, 22535, 323, 92524, 279, 3089, 1749, 261, 5362, 624, 17, 13, 758, 7779, 18946, 11, 20876, 311, 36765, 323, 14594, 11, 1221, 4205, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 18, 13, 10083, 28118, 389, 279, 22380, 49