{"id": "615", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Passage 2 provides the necessary information to force removal of a printer in devices and printers. You can do this by first clicking on Control Panel, then selecting Hardware and Sound, followed by clicking on Printers. Right-click on the printer you want to remove and click Delete. If you are unable to delete the printer, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, perform the following steps:\n\n1. Open the Devices and Printers window.\n2. Right-click on the printer you want to remove.\n3. Select \"Delete\" from the context menu.\n4. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click on it again.\n5. Select \"Run as administrator.\"\n6. Confirm the deletion of the printer.\n\nThese steps ensure that the printer is completely removed from the devices list in Devices and Printers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, perform the following steps:\n\n1. Open the Devices and Printers window.\n2. Right-click on the printer you want to remove.\n3. Select \"Delete\" from the context menu.\n4. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click on it again.\n5. Select \"Run as administrator.\"\n6. Confirm the deletion of the printer.\n\nThese steps ensure that the printer is completely removed from the devices list in Devices and Printers.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Control Panel.\\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n3. Click on Printers.\\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\\n5. Click Delete.\\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again.\\n7. Click Run as administrator.\\n8. Click Delete.\", \"Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n1. Open the Control Panel.\\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n3. Select Printers.\\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove.\\n5. Click Delete.\\nIf the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\", \"Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n1. Go to Control Panel and select Hardware and Sound.\\n2. Click on Printers.\\n3. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\\n4. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again and select Run as administrator, then click Delete.\\n5. Disconnect any USB cable connecting the printer to the computer if it is connected.\\n6. Turn the printer off and on again.\\n7. Ensure the printer is in a ready state after重启ing it.\", \"Based on the given passages, to force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, perform the following steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Devices and Printers window.\\n2. Right-click on the printer you want to remove.\\n3. Select \\\"Delete\\\" from the context menu.\\n4. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click on it again.\\n5. Select \\\"Run as administrator.\\\"\\n6. Confirm the deletion of the printer.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the printer is completely removed from the devices list in Devices and Printers.\"]", "time_sec": 18.603, "generation_time_seconds": 17.7283, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8677, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 19, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 10428, 624, 21, 13, 1416