{"id": "631", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to guard a tall person in basketball\":\n\nTo guard a tall person in basketball, it's important to stay as close as possible to them when they're near the three-point line. Slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against them effectively.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them while actively sliding your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize their shot opportunities.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them while actively sliding your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize their shot opportunities.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should:\\n\\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall player, especially near the three-point line.\\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\\n3. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\\n4. Use tips from an experienced basketball player to improve your defense.\", \"Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should:\\n\\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall player near the three-point line.\\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near the opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\\n3. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\\n4. Use tips from an experienced basketball player to improve your defensive skills.\", \"Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball:\\n\\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall player, especially near the three-point line.\\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\\n3. Maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against tall players.\", \"Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them while actively sliding your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize their shot opportunities.\"]", "time_sec": 14.576, "generation_time_seconds": 13.752, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8186, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 498, 1265, 1447, 16, 13, 28737, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 279, 16217, 2781, 11, 5310, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 624, 17, 13, 3218, 3132, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488, 624, 18, 13, 13655, 264, 63685, 1948, 279, 14024, 323, 279, 15183, 2781, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 10414, 504, 458, 10321, 19240, 2781, 311, 7269, 697, 9055, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall player, especially near the three-point line.\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\n3. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\n4. Use tips from an experienced basketball player to improve your defense.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7908963882733906, "g_worst_claim": 0.2763168215751648, "g_content": 2.2051302887672604, "g_traj_mean": 1.7418153285980225}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 498, 1265, 1447, 16, 13, 28737, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 279, 16217, 2781, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 624, 17, 13, 3218, 3132, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 279, 14704, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488, 624, 18, 13, 13655, 264, 63685, 1948, 279, 14024, 323, 279, 15183, 2781, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 10414, 504, 458, 10321, 19240, 2781, 311, 7269, 697, 16016, 7361, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall player near the three-point line.\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near the opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\n3. Keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player.\n4. Use tips from an experienced basketball player to improve your defensive skills.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7778818045416447, "g_worst_claim": 0.2763168215751648, "g_content": 2.2370263033134994, "g_traj_mean": 1.6917574405670166}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 1447, 16, 13, 28737, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 279, 16217, 2781, 11, 5310, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 624, 17, 13, 3218, 3132, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488, 624, 18, 13, 86377, 264, 63685, 1948, 279, 14024, 323, 279, 15183, 2781, 311, 13444, 10505, 2348, 16217, 4217, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball:\n\n1. Stay as close as possible to the tall player, especially near the three-point line.\n2. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\n3. Maintain a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to effectively defend against tall players.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6576505624372342, "g_worst_claim": 0.2763168215751648, "g_content": 2.3188243768154044, "g_traj_mean": 1.757272720336914}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 498, 1265, 4717, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 1105, 1393, 22040, 33832, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 323, 29337, 862, 6552, 10488, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them while actively sliding your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize their shot opportunities.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1396243738945417, "g_worst_claim": 0.27286360661188763, "g_content": 1.9139849344889324, "g_traj_mean": 1.6016230583190918}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.23, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "632", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system are both critical to maintaining homeostasis in the body by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. They both use chemical messengers, although their method of transmission and release differs. The nervous system is made of interconnected neuron cells and uses electrochemical pulses for signal transmission. In contrast, the endocrine system is made of discrete glands that use hormones for signal transmission and utilizes the circulatory system to carry these signals.", "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is performed by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, in contrast to the discrete organs of the endocrine system.\n4. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system for signal transmission.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is performed by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, in contrast to the discrete organs of the endocrine system.\n4. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system for signal transmission.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\\n\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nThe differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\\n\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Based on the given passages, similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\\n\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\\n\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, while the organs of the endocrine system are discrete.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, whereas the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Based on the given passages, the nervous system and the endocrine system share similarities and differences in various aspects. Firstly, both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. Secondly, both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms, which ensures equilibrium and consistency in function. Additionally, chemical messengers are crucial in both systems for their respective functions.\\n\\nIn terms of differences, the nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is comprised of glands. Transmission in the nervous system is accomplished through electrochemical pulses, whereas the endocrine system relies on hormones for signal transmission.\\n\\nFurthermore, the nervous system is a continuous structure with interconnected cells, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, but the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\\n\\nIn conclusion, while both systems are necessary for maintaining homeostasis and utilize chemical messengers, their composition, structure, and methods of signal transmission differ significantly.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\nSimilarities:\\n1. Both the nervous system and the endocrine system are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells while the endocrine system is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is performed by chemicals known as hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, in contrast to the discrete organs of the endocrine system.\\n4. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system for signal transmission.\"]", "time_sec": 28.821, "generation_time_seconds": 28.1059, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7097, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 42774, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 785, 11799, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 25266, 3881, 438, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.231249453940288, "g_worst_claim": 0.04852795600891113, "g_content": 1.6601497350114116, "g_traj_mean": 1.08947551250