 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 11, 432, 374, 10660, 553, 25266, 3881, 438, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 304, 12872, 311, 279, 43179, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 5711, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 369, 8286, 18368, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is performed by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, in contrast to the discrete organs of the endocrine system.\n4. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system for signal transmission.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.253539684664239, "g_worst_claim": 0.24563877582550048, "g_content": 1.54844134366965, "g_traj_mean": 1.0752149820327759}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "633", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system have both similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n1. Both systems are dedicated to maintaining homeostasis and coordinating the activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n3. Chemical messengers play a crucial role in both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n1. The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system occurs through electrochemical pulses, while chemical hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n3. The nervous system utilizes interconnected cells to transmit signals, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals through neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "pred": "1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\\n\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nThe differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\\n\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Based on the given passages, the similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs.\\n\\nThe differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system include:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, the signals are transmitted by chemicals known as hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous and interconnected, in contrast to the discrete organs of the Endocrine System.\\n4. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System utilizes the circulatory system for signal transmission.\", \"Based on the given passages, the nervous system and the endocrine system have several differences and at least one similarity.\\n\\nDifference 1: Composition - The nervous system is made of neuron cells, whereas the endocrine system consists of endocrine glands.\\n\\nDifference 2: Transmission - The nervous system transmits signals via electrochemical pulses, while the endocrine system uses hormones as chemical messengers.\\n\\nDifference 3: Physical Connection - The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, but the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected; they are discrete.\\n\\nSimilarity: Both systems are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\", \"Based on the given passages, the similarities between the nervous system and the endocrine system are that both are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nThe differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system are as follows:\\n\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission is performed by the electrochemical pulses in the nervous system, whereas hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the Endocrine System.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, while the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, whereas the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\"]", "time_sec": 29.093, "generation_time_seconds": 28.2541, "selection_time_seconds": 0.832, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 42774, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 785, 11799, 1948, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 25266, 3881, 438, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.24629796781704, "g_worst_claim": 0.08639606833457947, "g_content": 1.