{"id": "641", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "gt": "Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are found in the blood and are part of the circulatory system. They are both formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow and contain cell membranes and cytoplasm. The main difference is their functions. RBCs are responsible for delivering oxygen from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases, viruses, etc.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\n2. Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\n3. Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\nThe differences between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n2. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n3. Red blood cells are found in the circulatory system, while white blood cells are found in the circulatory system and can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\n2. Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\n3. Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\nThe differences between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n2. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n3. Red blood cells are found in the circulatory system, while white blood cells are found in the circulatory system and can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells are:\\n1. Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\\n2. Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n3. Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\\nThe differences between red and white blood cells are:\\n1. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n2. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n3. Red blood cells are found in the circulatory system, while white blood cells are found in the circulatory system and can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are as follows:\\n\\n1. Function: RBCs are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n2. Cell type: RBCs are red and carry oxygen, whereas WBCs are white and are part of the immune system.\\n\\nSimilarities:\\n1. Both are formed elements of blood.\\n2. Both are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\\n3. Both have cell membrane and cytoplasm.\", \"Based on the given passages, the differences between red and white blood cells are:\\n\\n1. Function: Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n2. Composition: Red blood cells are primarily composed of hemoglobin, which carries oxygen, while white blood cells are not primarily composed of hemoglobin but contain a nucleus and other organelles.\\n\\nThe similarities between red and white blood cells are:\\n\\n1. Both are formed elements of blood.\\n2. Both are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\\n3. Both have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\\n4. Both are found in the circulatory system.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\nSimilarities:\\n- Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\\n- Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n- Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body.\\n- White blood cells are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\"]", "time_sec": 26.201, "generation_time_seconds": 24.9225, "selection_time_seconds": 1.271, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 42774, 1948, 2518, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 2518, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 279, 2518, 17240, 82648, 624, 18, 13, 11733, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 614, 2779, 78248, 323, 9503, 98605, 10530, 624, 785, 11799, 1948, 2518, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 510, 16, 13, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 8480, 369, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 624, 17, 13, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 949, 315, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 323, 6777, 2513, 1741, 438, 23552, 6814, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 624, 18, 13, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 1730, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 1730, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 323, 646, 387, 11691, 553, 6543, 504, 825, 949, 311, 2441, 949, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\n2. Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\n3. Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\nThe differences between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n2. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n3. Red blood cells are found in the circulatory system, while white blood cells are found in the circulatory system and can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8731317574285443, "g_worst_claim": 0.06413334257462446, "g_content": 1.4429542327595648, "g_traj_mean": 0.9263081550598145}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 2518, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 5712, 25, 431, 4897, 82, 525, 8480, 369, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 624, 17, 13, 13972, 943, 25, 431, 4897, 82, 525, 2518, 323, 6777, 23552, 11, 19853, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 4158, 323, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 382, 34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 2518, 17240, 82648, 624, 18, 13, 11733, 614, 2779, 38554, 323, 9503, 98605, 10530, 13, 151645], "pred": "Similarities:\n1. Both are formed elements of blood.\n2. Both are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\n3. Both have cell membrane and cytoplasm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1322054548502338, "g_worst_claim": 0.32690032323201496, "g_content": 1.6056310592159149, "g_traj_mean": 0.9441890716552734}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 11799, 1948, 2518, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 1447, 16, 13, 5712, 25, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 8480, 369, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 264, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 624, 17, 13, 67106, 25, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 15503, 23415, 315, 17280, 93755, 11, 892, 23377, 23552, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 537, 15503, 23415, 315, 17280, 93755, 714, 6644, 264, 61507, 323, 1008, 1240, 2387, 642, 382, 785, 42774, 1948, 2518, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 1447, 16, 13, 11733, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 2518, 17240, 82648, 624, 18, 13, 11733, 614, 2779, 78248, 323, 9503, 98605, 10530, 624, 19, 13, 11733, 525, 1730, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Both are formed elements of blood.\n2. Both are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\n3. Both have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\n4. Both are found in the circulatory system.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8712041158356473, "g_worst_claim": 0.026341197391351063, "g_content": 1.177750752766927, "g_traj_mean": 0.7909579873085022}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 34402, 1361, 510, 12, 11733, 2518, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 624, 12, 11733, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 2518, 17240, 82648, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 12, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 8480, 369, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 624, 12, 5807, 6543, 7761, 525, 264, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages:\n\nSimilarities:\n- Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\n- Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\n\nDifferences:\n- Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body.\n- White blood cells are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.048140903049045, "g_worst_claim": 0.4175884246826172, "g_content": 1.8438129001193577, "g_traj_mean": 1.117358922958374}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.08, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "643", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the primary difference between red and white blood cells is their respective functions within the body. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery to tissues, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help combat diseases and viruses. However, both types of cells share some common features, such as being formed elements of blood, being formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow, having a cell membrane and cytoplasm, and circulating in the fluids in blood vessels, which is pumped by the heart.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\n2. Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\n3. Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\nThe differences between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n2. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n3. Red blood cells are found in the circulatory system, while white blood cells are found in the circulatory system and can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\n2. Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\n3. Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\nThe differences between red and white blood cells are:\n1. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n2. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n3. Red blood cells are found in the circulatory system, while white blood cells are found in the circulatory system and can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells are:\\n1. Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\\n2. Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n3. Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\\nThe differences between red and white blood cells are:\\n1. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n2. Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n3. Red blood cells are found in the circulatory system, while white blood cells are found in the circulatory system and can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.\", \"Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells include:\\n- Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\\n- Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\\n- Both types of cells have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\\nThe differences between red and white blood cells include:\\n- Red blood cells are part of the circulatory system and carry oxygen, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n- Red blood cells are responsible for delivering oxygen to the body's tissues, whereas white blood cells protect the body against pathogens.\\n- The red blood cells and white blood cells can be carried by blood from one part to another part of the body.\", \"Based on the given passages, the similarities between red and white blood cells include:\\n\\n- Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood.\\n- Both RBCs and WBCs can be carried by blood from one part of the body to another.\\n- Both RBCs and WBCs are found in the circulatory system.\\n- Both RBCs and WBCs have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\\n- Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n\\nHowever, the passage does not provide specific differences between red and white blood cells.\", \"Based on the given passages, the red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) share several similarities:\\n- Both are formed elements of blood.\\n- Both are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n\\nTheir differences include:\\n- RBCs are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body and carry things such as oxygen throughout the body.\\n- WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n- RBCs are part of the circulatory system, while WBCs are part of the immune system.\\n- RBCs are found in the circulatory system, while WBCs are found in the circulatory system.\\n- RBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow, while WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\"]", "time_sec": 29.691, "generation_ti