78, 264, 17423, 323, 21700, 15826, 1882, 429, 8609, 10306, 279, 2820, 323, 13143, 315, 697, 6869, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps ensure a thorough and gentle cleaning process that helps maintain the health and beauty of your hair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2562240317485376, "g_worst_claim": 0.3563303550084432, "g_content": 1.3750557277513586, "g_traj_mean": 1.110592246055603}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.65, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "656", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Rinse your hair completely with water.\n2. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n3. Apply a conditioner and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n4. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n5. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles.\n\nAdditionally, it is recommended to use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair after washing, and to be gentle when handling wet hair to prevent damage.", "pred": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly.\\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\", \"Based on the given passages, to properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n1. Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. While in the shower, make sure your water is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down just a bit so you're not splashing all over the place.\\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\\n4. Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand, approximately a nickel-sized amount, and work it through the hair. If your hair is longer, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo.\\n8. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes.\\n9. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n10. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Never rub the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to avoid causing damage.\\n11. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, handling your hair with proper care to make them beautiful.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n1) Rinse the hair completely.\\n2) Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\\n3) Apply a conditioner and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n4) Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n5) Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion instead of rubbing.\\n6) Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n7) Wet the hair thoroughly.\\n8) Apply a bit of shampoo and work it through the hair.\\n9) Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\\n10) Handle your hair with proper care to avoid damage while drying.\", \"Based on the given passages, to properly clean your hair:\\n\\n1. Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Thoroughly wet the hair while ensuring the water is warm but not too hot.\\n3. Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand (a nickel sized amount) and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n4. Rinse the hair completely.\\n5. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo.\\n6. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes.\\n7. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n8. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel.\"]", "time_sec": 31.537, "generation_time_seconds": 30.4661, "selection_time_seconds": 1.058, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 2704, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 11, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 2484, 279, 6396, 1495, 10078, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 279, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 8, 311, 279, 32452, 315, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 279, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 5358, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.489398590019202, "g_worst_claim": 0.35274724165598553, "g_content": 1.6490308783027563, "g_traj_mean": 1.331782341003418}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 7405, 2704, 311, 3293, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 5976, 304, 279, 17196, 11, 1281, 2704, 697, 3015, 374, 8205, 11, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 2484, 279, 6396, 1495, 1101, 264, 2699, 773, 498, 2299, 537, 12503, 19049, 678, 916, 279, 1992, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 279, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2699, 315, 61932, 1119, 279, 32452, 315, 697, 1424, 11, 13187, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 11, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 279, 6869, 13, 1416, 697, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 3614, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 624, 23, 13, 26530, 279, 64324, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 16, 15, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 13, 14695, 10273, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 5648, 14381, 5557, 624, 16, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 11589, 697, 6869, 448, 6169, 2453, 311, 1281, 1105, 6233, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\n1. Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. While in the shower, make sure your water is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down just a bit so you're not splashing all over the place.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand, approximately a nickel-sized amount, and work it through the hair. If your hair is longer, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo.\n8. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes.\n9. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n10. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Never rub the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to avoid causing damage.\n11. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, handling your hair with proper care to make them beautiful.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5180104399239573, "g_worst_claim": 0.35640811920166016, "g_content": 1.813633411854237, "g_traj_mean": 1.417365550994873}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 510, 16, 8, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 17, 8, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 624, 18, 8, 20552, 264, 64324, 323, 2138, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 19, 8, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 20, 8, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 4518, 315, 55935, 624, 21, 8, 7405, 2704, 311, 3293, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 22, 8, 44856, 279, 6869, 26364, 624, 23, 8, 20552, 264, 2699, 315, 61932, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 279, 6869, 624, 24, 8, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 624, 16, 15, 8, 13760, 697, 6869, 448, 6169, 2453, 311, 5648, 5557, 1393, 45379, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages:\n1) Rinse the hair completely.\n2) Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n3) Apply a conditioner and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n4) Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n5) Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion instead of rubbing.\n6) Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n7) Wet the hair thoroughly.\n8) Apply a bit of shampoo and work it through the hair.\n9) Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\n10) Handle your hair with proper care to avoid damage while drying.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4916821531935698, "g_worst_claim": 0.5756918907165527, "g_content": 1.9902807871500652, "g_traj_mean": 1.414249062538147}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 2704, 311, 3293, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 279, 6869, 1393, 22573, 279, 3015, 374, 8205, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 264, 2699, 315, 61932, 1119, 279, 32452, 315, 697, 1424, 320, 64, 51249, 29287, 3311, 8, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 279, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 19, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 20, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 624, 21, 13, 26530, 279, 64324, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 23, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Thoroughly wet the hair while ensuring the water is warm but not too hot.\n3. Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand (a nickel sized amount) and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n4. Rinse the hair completely.\n5. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo.\n6. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes.\n7. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n8. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5248759866501809, "g_worst_claim": 0.4545350869496663, "g_content": 1.6782462661330764, "g_traj_mean": 1.3720109462738037}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.73, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "657", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Wet your hair thoroughly.\n3. Apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through your hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is longer.\n4. Rinse the hair completely and use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n5. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n6. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n7. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles.\n8. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\n\nTherefore, the steps to properly clean your hair are:\n\n1. Choose the right products.\n2. Wet your hair.\n3. Shampoo your hair.\n4. Rinse and detangle.\n5. Condition your hair.\n6. Rinse and comb.\n7. Dry your hair with a towel.\n8. Use a hair dryer.", "pred": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly.\\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\n1. Ensure the water temperature is warm but not too hot.\\n2. Use a nickel-sized amount of shampoo and work it through your hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n3. Apply conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n4. Rinse the hair completely, and if your hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\\n5. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n6. Wrap a towel or pat gently to soak the water from your hair. Avoid rubbing it with a towel to dry it as wet hair is weak and such frictions can lead to damage.\\n7. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, using a patting or stroking motion rather than rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel.\", \"Based on the given passages, to properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Ensure you have the right shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make the water warm and adjust the flow slightly to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\\n4. Apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo to your hand and work it through your hair, combing with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is long.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair for longer hair.\\n7. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\", \"Based on the given passages, the proper way to clean your hair is as follows:\\n\\n1. Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Wet your hair thoroughly with warm, but not too hot, water.\\n3. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) to your palm and work it through your hair.\\n4. If your hair is longer, comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse your hair completely with your hands or a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\\n6. Apply a conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo and leave it on for a few minutes.\\n7. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n8. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles to prevent damage.\\n\\nThese steps ensure your hair is thoroughly cleaned and treated properly, leaving it looking and feeling its best.\"]", "time_sec": 31.907, "generation_time_seconds": 30.7814, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1171, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 2704, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 11, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 2484, 279, 6396, 1495, 10078, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 279, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 8, 311, 279, 32452, 315, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 279, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 5358, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4696734726200662, "g_worst_claim": 0.2679348985354106, "g_content": 1.6514556541871488, "g_traj_mean": 1.3245590925216675}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 29279, 279, 3015, 9315, 374, 8205, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 315, 61932, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 11, 323, 421, 697, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 990, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 21, 13, 42187, 264, 42613, 476, 3272, 29273, 311, 60692, 279, 3015, 504, 697, 6869, 13, 34006, 55935, 432, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 9058, 432, 438, 14401, 6869, 374, 7469, 323, 1741, 1422, 21439, 646, 2990, 311, 5557, 624, 22, 13, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 4751, 1091, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Ensure the water temperature is warm but not too hot.\n2. Use a nickel-sized amount of shampoo and work it through your hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n3. Apply conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n4. Rinse the hair completely, and if your hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n5. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n6. Wrap a towel or pat gently to soak the water from your hair. Avoid rubbing it with a towel to dry it as wet hair is weak and such frictions can lead to damage.\n7. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, using a patting or stroking motion rather than rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5600373022765057, "g_worst_claim": 0.3957432985305786, "g_content": 2.2040302322571534, "g_traj_mean": 1.571645975112915}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 29279, 498, 614, 279, 1290, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 279, 3015, 8205, 323, 7500, 279, 6396, 10078, 311, 5648, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 697, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 315, 61932, 311, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 421, 697, 6869, 374, 1293, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 369, 5021, 6869, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 438, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 432, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 5358, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Ensure you have the right shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make the water warm and adjust the flow slightly to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\n4. Apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo to your hand and work it through your hair, combing with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is long.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair for longer hair.\n7. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4025452136636083, "g_worst_claim": 0.26437536875406903, "g_content": 1.778439992881683, "g_traj_mean": 1.33846116065979}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 4240, 697, 6869, 374, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 2704, 311, 3293, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 44856, 697, 6869, 26364, 448, 8205, 11, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 3015, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 8, 311, 697, 32452, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 1416, 697, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 3614, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 697, 6869, 6587, 448, 697, 6078, 476, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 624, 21, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 438, 279, 61932, 323, 5274, 432, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 23, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 432, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 311, 5358, 5557, 382, 9485, 7354, 5978, 697, 6869, 374, 26364, 27722, 323, 11758, 10277, 11, 9380, 432, 3330, 323, 8266, 1181, 1850, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps ensure your hair is thoroughly cleaned and treated properly, leaving it looking and feeling its best.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1189955161278735, "g_worst_claim": -0.30940714478492737, "g_content": 1.2943261040581597, "g_traj_mean": 1.0324082374572754}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.86, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "659", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "gt": "Vinegar can be used to improve a dog's skin and coat, clean out their ears, repel fleas, and soothe itchy ears.", "pred": "4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\\n\\n1. To improve the skin and coat: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance the dog's skin pH levels. This mixture can also be sprayed full-strength on the dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin.\\n\\n2. To clean ears: Diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water provides a solution for itchy ears. Use a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the diluted vinegar to soothe the itchy ears. If the itchy ears persist, it may indicate an allergic reaction to something in the dog's diet.\\n\\n3. To repel fleas: Spray the dog's coat with vinegar to repel fleas. Additionally, a flea comb can be used to remove fleas after spraying the coat.\\n\\n4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.\", \"Based on the given passages, vinegar is used for dogs in several ways:\\n\\n1. Improve skin and coat health: Vinegar can be mixed with water (1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water) and used as a final rinse for a shiny, healthy coat and to help balance your dog's skin pH levels.\\n\\n2. Clean ears: Vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears by diluting it with 50 percent water and applying it with a cotton swab or gauze pad.\\n\\n3. Repel fleas: Vinegar can be sprayed on the dog's coat to repel fleas.\\n\\n4. Fight fleas: A bath with an ACV-soap mixture is suggested to fight fleas.\\n\\n5. Normalizing pH balance: Full-strength vinegar can be sprayed on the dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin.\", \"Based on the given passages, vinegar has multiple uses for dogs. It can be used to improve a dog's skin and coat health by normalizing skin pH levels. Vinegar can be mixed with water to create a rinse that can be used after washing a dog to help maintain a healthy coat. Additionally, vinegar can be used to repel fleas when sprayed on a dog's coat. To address itchy ears, vinegar can be diluted with water and used to soothe the issue. The passages suggest mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water for rinses and using a 50% dilution for ear issues.\", \"Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\\n\\n1. To improve the skin and coat of dogs, a mixture of 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water can be used as a final rinse after bathing. This helps balance the dog's skin pH levels and rejuvenates the coat.\\n\\n2. To normalize the pH balance of a dog's skin, vinegar can be sprayed full-strength on the dog's coat.\\n\\n3. To repel fleas, vinegar can be sprayed on the dog's coat.\\n\\n4. To soothe itchy ears, apple cider vinegar diluted with 50% water can be used. A cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in this solution can be applied to the dog's ear to alleviate itching. If the itching persists, it may indicate a dietary allergy.\"]", "time_sec": 28.05, "generation_time_seconds": 27.2193, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8214, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 369, 12590, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 7269, 279, 6787, 323, 22875, 25, 19219, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 25374, 315, 3015, 323, 990, 438, 264, 1590, 73241, 311, 72384, 349, 279, 22875, 323, 1492, 8172, 279, 5562, 594, 6787, 36043, 5866, 13, 1096, 20980, 646, 1083, 387, 77621, 2480, 5477, 17842, 389, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 311, 21694, 279, 36043, 8172, 315, 1181, 6787, 3