5, 311, 21694, 279, 36043, 8172, 315, 1181, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "5. Normalizing pH balance: Full-strength vinegar can be sprayed on the dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1984533583411991, "g_worst_claim": 0.39023367563883465, "g_content": 1.6769089809683866, "g_traj_mean": 1.1999069452285767}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 46105, 702, 5248, 5711, 369, 12590, 13, 1084, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 7269, 264, 5562, 594, 6787, 323, 22875, 2820, 553, 4622, 4849, 6787, 36043, 5866, 13, 49695, 12164, 646, 387, 9519, 448, 3015, 311, 1855, 264, 73241, 429, 646, 387, 1483, 1283, 27686, 264, 5562, 311, 1492, 10306, 264, 9314, 22875, 13, 22406, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 979, 77621, 389, 264, 5562, 594, 22875, 13, 2014, 2621, 432, 57964, 24230, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 79603, 448, 3015, 323, 1483, 311, 43176, 1782, 279, 4265, 13, 576, 46769, 4190, 26792, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 25374, 315, 3015, 369, 96039, 288, 323, 1667, 264, 220, 20, 15, 4, 18840, 1488, 369, 2430, 4714, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, vinegar has multiple uses for dogs. It can be used to improve a dog's skin and coat health by normalizing skin pH levels. Vinegar can be mixed with water to create a rinse that can be used after washing a dog to help maintain a healthy coat. Additionally, vinegar can be used to repel fleas when sprayed on a dog's coat. To address itchy ears, vinegar can be diluted with water and used to soothe the issue. The passages suggest mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water for rinses and using a 50% dilution for ear issues.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0202360291747152, "g_worst_claim": 0.38843464851379395, "g_content": 1.2898152278019832, "g_traj_mean": 0.8981044888496399}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 369, 12590, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 7269, 279, 6787, 323, 22875, 315, 12590, 11, 264, 20980, 315, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 25374, 315, 3015, 646, 387, 1483, 438, 264, 1590, 73241, 1283, 72409, 13, 1096, 8609, 8172, 279, 5562, 594, 6787, 36043, 5866, 323, 72384, 973, 279, 22875, 382, 17, 13, 2014, 21694, 279, 36043, 8172, 315, 264, 5562, 594, 6787, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 77621, 2480, 5477, 17842, 389, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 382, 18, 13, 2014, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 77621, 389, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 382, 19, 13, 2014, 43176, 1782, 432, 57964, 24230, 11, 23268, 65055, 46105, 79603, 448, 220, 20, 15, 4, 3015, 646, 387, 1483, 13, 362, 23522, 2021, 370, 476, 342, 2863, 2986, 11016, 68875, 304, 419, 6291, 646, 387, 9251, 311, 279, 5562, 594, 2430, 311, 60605, 84975, 13, 1416, 279, 84975, 66045, 11, 432, 1231, 13216, 264, 33525, 59654, 13, 151645], "pred": "4. To soothe itchy ears, apple cider vinegar diluted with 50% water can be used. A cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in this solution can be applied to the dog's ear to alleviate itching. If the itching persists, it may indicate a dietary allergy.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2702011576215744, "g_worst_claim": 0.38843464851379395, "g_content": 1.6652451480727597, "g_traj_mean": 1.1538689136505127}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "662", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "gt": "Sure, I can answer your question based on the given passages. Here are some uses for vinegar for dogs:\n\n1. Coat and skin health: Mixing vinegar with water and using it as a final rinse can help to rejuvenate your dog's coat and balance their skin pH levels, according to Passage 1.\n2. Flea control: Vinegar can be used to repel fleas and remove them from your dog's coat, as mentioned in Passage 2.\n3. Itchy ears: Diluted vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears, as stated in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions or if there's anything else I can assist you with.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in the following ways:\n\n1. Improving skin and coat health: Vinegar can be mixed with water to serve as a final rinse for a shiny, healthy coat and to help balance a dog's skin pH levels.\n\n2. Repelling fleas: Spraying vinegar on a dog's coat can repel fleas.\n\n3. Soothing itchy ears: Diluted apple cider vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears in dogs.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in the following ways:\n\n1. Improving skin and coat health: Vinegar can be mixed with water to serve as a final rinse for a shiny, healthy coat and to help balance a dog's skin pH levels.\n\n2. Repelling fleas: Spraying vinegar on a dog's coat can repel fleas.\n\n3. Soothing itchy ears: Diluted apple cider vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears in dogs.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\\n\\n1. To improve the skin and coat: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance the dog's skin pH levels. This mixture can also be sprayed full-strength on the dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin.\\n\\n2. To clean ears: Diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water provides a solution for itchy ears. Use a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the diluted vinegar to soothe the itchy ears. If the itchy ears persist, it may indicate an allergic reaction to something in the dog's diet.\\n\\n3. To repel fleas: Spray the dog's coat with vinegar to repel fleas. Additionally, a flea comb can be used to remove fleas after spraying the coat.\\n\\n4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.\", \"Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\\n\\n1. To improve the skin and coat of dogs, by mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and using it as a final rinse.\\n2. To normalize the pH balance of a dog's skin by spraying vinegar full-strength on the coat.\\n3. To soothe itchy ears by diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water and using a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the solution.\\n4. To repel fleas by spraying the coat.\\n5. As part of a flea combing process, where dogs are bathed in an ACV-soap mixture.\", \"Based on the given passages, vinegar has multiple uses for dogs:\\n\\n1. Improve coat health: A 1:2 to 1:4 ratio of vinegar to water can be used as a final rinse to refresh and balance a dog’s skin pH levels, resulting in a shiny, healthy coat.\\n2. Ear care: Diluting apple cider vinegar with water (50%) can soothe itchy ears in dogs. A cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in this diluted vinegar can be used to alleviate the discomfort. If the problem persists, it may indicate an allergy to something in the dog's diet.\\n3. Flea control: Vinegar can be sprayed directly onto a dog's coat to help repel fleas. Additionally, using an ACV-soap mixture during a bath can help fight fleas.\\n4. Ear cleaning: Vinegar can also be used to clean a dog's ears, although it is important to follow the correct dilution ratio and use it carefully to avoid irritation.\", \"Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in the following ways:\\n\\n1. Improving skin and coat health: Vinegar can be mixed with water to serve as a final rinse for a shiny, healthy coat and to help balance a dog's skin pH levels.\\n\\n2. Repelling fleas: Spraying vinegar on a dog's coat can repel fleas.\\n\\n3. Soothing itchy ears: Diluted apple cider vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears in dogs.\"]", "time_sec": 28.405, "generation_time_seconds": 27.3805, "selection_time_seconds": 1.015, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 369, 12590, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 7269, 279, 6787, 323, 22875, 25, 19219, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 25374, 315, 3015, 323, 990, 438, 264, 1590, 73241, 311, 72384, 349, 279, 22875, 323, 1492, 8172, 279, 5562, 594, 6787, 36043, 5866, 13, 1096, 20980, 646, 1083, 387, 77621, 2480, 5477, 17842, 389, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 311, 21694, 279, 36043, 8172, 315, 1181, 6787, 382, 17, 13, 2014, 4240, 24230, 25, 52767, 10607, 23268, 65055, 46105, 448, 220, 20, 15, 3266, 3015, 5707, 264, 6291, 369, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 5443, 264, 23522, 2021, 370, 476, 342, 2863, 2986, 11016, 68875, 304, 279, 79603, 46105, 311, 43176, 1782, 279, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 1416, 279, 432, 57964, 24230, 22334, 11, 432, 1231, 13216, 458, 56496, 12720, 311, 2494, 304, 279, 5562, 594, 9968, 382, 18, 13, 2014, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 25, 60561, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 448, 46105, 311, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 13, 22406, 11, 264, 95855, 3614, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 4057, 12962, 300, 1283, 82536, 279, 22875, 382, 19, 13, 2014, 4367, 12962, 300, 25, 16098, 383, 279, 5562, 304, 264, 20980, 315, 10584, 53, 33019, 391, 311, 4367, 12962, 300, 13, 151645], "pred": "4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4022866605078383, "g_worst_claim": 0.4244676431020101, "g_content": 2.12557382