1199, 11, 9314, 22875, 323, 311, 1492, 8172, 264, 5562, 594, 6787, 36043, 5866, 382, 17, 13, 3321, 6293, 12962, 300, 25, 15515, 17270, 46105, 389, 264, 5562, 594, 22875, 646, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 382, 18, 13, 2055, 78, 1596, 432, 57964, 24230, 25, 52767, 2774, 23268, 65055, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 43176, 1782, 432, 57964, 24230, 304, 12590, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in the following ways:\n\n1. Improving skin and coat health: Vinegar can be mixed with water to serve as a final rinse for a shiny, healthy coat and to help balance a dog's skin pH levels.\n\n2. Repelling fleas: Spraying vinegar on a dog's coat can repel fleas.\n\n3. Soothing itchy ears: Diluted apple cider vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears in dogs.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8983868144176625, "g_worst_claim": 0.31770858764648435, "g_content": 1.506092529296875, "g_traj_mean": 0.9330582022666931}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.93, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "663", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "gt": "Sure, here are some possible answers based on the given passages:\n\nQ: What are some uses for vinegar when it comes to dogs?\n\nA: Vinegar can be used to:\n\n* Improve a dog's skin and coat by mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and using it as a final rinse.\n* Normalize the pH balance of a dog's skin by spraying full-strength vinegar on its coat.\n* Repel fleas by spraying a dog's coat with apple cider vinegar.\n* Soothe itchy ears by using a diluted solution of apple cider vinegar (50% water, 50% vinegar) on a cotton swab or gauze pad.\n* Clean a dog's ears by using apple cider vinegar.\n* Fight fleas by bathing a dog in a soap mixture that includes apple cider vinegar.\n* Remove fleas using a flea comb after bathing a dog in an apple cider vinegar soap mixture.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "5. Rinse: After using ACV-soap mixture or vinegar to bathe your dog, rinse them thoroughly to remove any residue.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "5. Rinse: After using ACV-soap mixture or vinegar to bathe your dog, rinse them thoroughly to remove any residue.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\\n\\n1. To improve the skin and coat: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance the dog's skin pH levels. This mixture can also be sprayed full-strength on the dog's coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin.\\n\\n2. To clean ears: Diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water provides a solution for itchy ears. Use a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the diluted vinegar to soothe the itchy ears. If the itchy ears persist, it may indicate an allergic reaction to something in the dog's diet.\\n\\n3. To repel fleas: Spray the dog's coat with vinegar to repel fleas. Additionally, a flea comb can be used to remove fleas after spraying the coat.\\n\\n4. To fight fleas: Bathe the dog in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.\", \"Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in the following ways:\\n\\n1. To improve the skin and coat health: By mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and using it as a final rinse, the vinegar helps rejuvenate the coat and balance the dog's skin pH levels. This mixture is recommended for achieving a shiny and healthy coat.\\n\\n2. To normalize the pH balance of the skin: Spraying vinegar full-strength on the dog's coat can normalize the pH balance of its skin.\\n\\n3. To repel fleas: Spraying your dog's coat with vinegar can help repel fleas.\\n\\n4. To soothe itchy ears: Diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water can be used to provide a solution for itchy ears in dogs. A cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the diluted vinegar can be used, and if itchy ears continue, it may indicate an allergy to something in the dog's diet.\", \"Based on the given passages, vinegar has several uses for dogs:\\n\\n1. Improve coat and skin health: Vinegar can be used as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance a dog's skin pH levels. For a shiny, healthy coat, mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse.\\n\\n2. Wash and rinse: Vinegar can be used to wash and rinse dogs. It can be used to clean out a dog's ears by spraying it on and then rinsing thoroughly. \\n\\n3. Flooding and repelling fleas: Vinegar can be sprayed on a dog's coat to repel fleas. Alternatively, a dog can be bathed in a mixture of ACV-soap to fight fleas.\\n\\n4. Soothing itchy ears: Diluted apple cider vinegar can soothe itchy ears in dogs. A cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in diluted vinegar can be used. If the itching continues, it may indicate a diet allergy.\", \"Based on the given passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\\n\\n1. Improve skin and coat health: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance the dog's skin pH levels. Spray vinegar full-strength on your dog’s coat to normalize the pH balance of its skin.\\n\\n2. Ear cleaning: Diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water provides a solution for a common dog problem: itchy ears. Use a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the diluted vinegar to soothe itchy ears. If itchy ears continue, your dog may be allergic to something in his diet.\\n\\n3. Repel fleas: Spray vinegar's coat to repel fleas.\\n\\n4. Fight fleas: Bathe your dog in an ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas.\\n\\n5. Rinse: After using ACV-soap mixture or vinegar to bathe your dog, rinse them thoroughly to remove any residue.\"]", "time_sec": 33.787, "generation_time_seconds": 33.0097, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7719, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 369, 12590, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 2014, 7269, 279, 6787, 323, 22875, 25, 19219, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 25374, 315, 3015, 323, 990, 438, 264, 1590, 73241, 311, 72384, 349, 279, 22875, 323, 1492, 8172, 279, 5562, 594, 6787, 36043, 5866, 13, 1096, 20980, 646, 1083, 387, 77621, 2480, 5477, 17842, 389, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 311, 21694, 279, 36043, 8172, 315, 1181, 6787, 382, 17, 13, 2014, 4240, 24230, 25, 52767, 10607, 23268, 65055, 46105, 448, 220, 20, 15, 3266, 3015, 5707, 264, 6291, 369, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 5443, 264, 23522, 2021, 370, 476, 342, 2863, 2986, 11016, 68875, 304, 279, 79603, 46105, 311, 43176, 1782, 279, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 1416, 279, 432, 57964, 24230, 22334, 11, 432, 1231, 13216, 458, 56496, 12720, 311, 2494, 304, 279, 5562, 594, 9968, 382, 18, 13, 2014, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 25, 60561, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 448, 46105, 311, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 13, 22406, 11, 264, 95855, 3614, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 4057, 1296