, 73241, 311, 72384, 349, 279, 22875, 323, 1492, 8172, 279, 5562, 594, 6787, 36043, 5866, 13, 60561, 46105, 2480, 5477, 17842, 389, 697, 5562, 748, 22875, 311, 21694, 279, 36043, 8172, 315, 1181, 6787, 382, 17, 13, 6809, 15826, 25, 52767, 10607, 23268, 65055, 46105, 448, 220, 20, 15, 3266, 3015, 5707, 264, 6291, 369, 264, 4185, 5562, 3491, 25, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 5443, 264, 23522, 2021, 370, 476, 342, 2863, 2986, 11016, 68875, 304, 279, 79603, 46105, 311, 43176, 1782, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 1416, 432, 57964, 24230, 3060, 11, 697, 5562, 1231, 387, 56496, 311, 2494, 304, 806, 9968, 382, 18, 13, 3321, 301, 12962, 300, 25, 60561, 46105, 594, 22875, 311, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 382, 19, 13, 18629, 12962, 300, 25, 16098, 383, 697, 5562, 304, 458, 10584, 53, 33019, 391, 20980, 311, 4367, 12962, 300, 382, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 25, 4636, 1667, 10584, 53, 33019, 391, 20980, 476, 46105, 311, 15743, 383, 697, 5562, 11, 73241, 1105, 26364, 311, 4057, 894, 48132, 13, 151645], "pred": "5. Rinse: After using ACV-soap mixture or vinegar to bathe your dog, rinse them thoroughly to remove any residue.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5441957030953661, "g_worst_claim": 0.407781720161438, "g_content": 2.097855934729943, "g_traj_mean": 1.5863724946975708}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.8, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "664", "question": "what happens when you breath in and out", "gt": "When you breathe in, or inhale, the intercostal muscles contract and expand the ribcage while the diaphragm contracts and pulls downward to increase the volume of the chest. This lowers the pressure inside the chest and allows air to be sucked into the lungs through the windpipe. When you breathe out, or exhale, the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, and the intercostal muscles also relax. This reduces the space in the chest cavity and forces out air that is rich in carbon dioxide out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "pred": "When you breathe out (expiration):\n1. The diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity.\n2. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity.\n3. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "When you breathe out (expiration):\n1. The diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity.\n2. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity.\n3. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, when you breathe in (inspiration), the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. Pressure inside the chest is lowered, and air is sucked into the lungs.\\n\\nWhen you breathe out (expiration), the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.\", \"Based on the given passages, when you inhale, the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage, and the diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. This causes the pressure inside the chest to be lowered, and air is sucked into the lungs.\\n\\nWhen you exhale, your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity, and the intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\nWhen you breathe in (inspiration):\\n1. The intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage.\\n2. The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest.\\n3. Pressure inside the chest is lowered, and air is sucked into the lungs.\\n\\nWhen you breathe out (expiration):\\n1. The diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity.\\n2. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity.\\n3. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.\", \"Based on the given passages, when you breathe in (inhale), the intercostal muscles contract, expanding the ribcage. The diaphragm contracts, pulling downwards to increase the volume of the chest. As a result, pressure inside the chest is lowered, and air is sucked into the lungs.\\n\\nWhen you breathe out (exhale), your diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax, reducing the space in the chest cavity. As the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.\"]", "time_sec": 23.878, "generation_time_seconds": 22.9498, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9231, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 498, 36297, 304, 320, 1330, 28479, 701, 279, 946, 16440, 278, 23648, 5116, 11, 23175, 279, 20131, 66, 424, 13, 576, 1853, 94796, 76, 17080, 11, 22266, 91270, 311, 5263, 279, 8123, 315, 279, 15138, 13, 38990, 4766, 279, 15138, 374, 38820, 11, 323, 3720, 374, 52212, 1119, 279, 44174, 382, 4498, 498, 36297, 700, 320, 63643, 701, 279, 1853, 94796, 76, 11967, 288, 323, 10797, 39772, 1119, 279, 15138, 55329, 13, 576, 946, 16440, 278, 23648, 1948, 279, 55149, 1083, 11967, 311, 7949, 279, 3550, 304, 279, 15138, 55329, 13, 1634, 279, 3550, 304, 279, 15138, 55329, 5221, 9155, 11, 3720, 9080, 304, 12499, 39489, 374, 9575, 700, 315, 697, 44174, 323, 9956, 13768, 11, 323, 1221, 700, 315, 697, 19142, 476, 10780, 13, 151645], "pred": "When you breathe out (expiration), the diaphragm relaxes and moves upward into the chest cavity. The intercostal muscles between the ribs also relax to reduce the space in the chest cavity. As the space in the chest cavity gets smaller, air rich in carbon dioxide is forced out of your lungs and windpipe, and then out of your nose or mouth.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1998396835669918, "g_worst_claim": -0.007557312292712075, "g_content": 1.77412838406033, "g_traj_mean": 1.2931404113769531}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 979, 498, 59437, 1574, 11, 279, 946, 16440, 278, 23648, 5116, 11, 23175, 279, 20131, 66, 424, 11, 323, 279, 1853, 94796, 76, 17080, 11, 22266, 91270, 311, 5263, 279, 8123, 315, 279, 15138, 13, 1096, 11137, 279, 7262, 4766, 279, 15138, 311, 387, 38820, 11, 323, 3720, 374, 52212, 1119, 279, 44174, 382, 4498, 498, 56659, 1574, 11, 697, 1853, 94796, 76, 11967, 288, 323, 10797, 39772, 1119, 279, 15138, 55329, 11, 323, 279, 946, 16