o an individual unit, or when the accounting system is not sophisticated enough to track FIFO or LIFO inventory layers. This method results in the recorded amount of inventory on hand representing a value somewhere between the oldest and newest units purchased into stock.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5680735853139576, "g_worst_claim": 0.3896525700887044, "g_content": 2.1008443059148014, "g_traj_mean": 1.572701096534729}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 36824, 5461, 1714, 315, 15444, 53724, 49912, 458, 5461, 2783, 311, 1817, 6573, 315, 15444, 979, 432, 374, 6088, 13, 1096, 1714, 17601, 4633, 279, 5461, 2783, 315, 678, 17023, 2433, 5023, 2500, 979, 264, 4982, 374, 6088, 13, 576, 5461, 3349, 12607, 311, 279, 1509, 6088, 25963, 279, 38288, 53543, 15444, 7576, 11, 892, 51294, 4344, 279, 36824, 5461, 2783, 13, 1096, 1714, 374, 16626, 1483, 304, 14740, 1380, 15444, 3589, 525, 773, 946, 5311, 832, 429, 432, 374, 11997, 311, 9793, 264, 3151, 2783, 311, 458, 3842, 4982, 11, 476, 979, 279, 23168, 1849, 374, 537, 38944, 26779, 311, 3754, 47007, 476, 444, 25997, 15444, 13617, 13, 576, 4179, 1102, 315, 1667, 279, 36824, 5461, 53724, 1714, 374, 429, 279, 12433, 3311, 315, 15444, 389, 1424, 10868, 264, 897, 14696, 1948, 279, 23513, 323, 23601, 8153, 14733, 1119, 5591, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the weighted average method of inventory costing assigns an average cost to each piece of inventory when it is sold. This method involves taking the average cost of all inventories currently available when a unit is sold. The average price assigned to the item sold reflects the fluctuating inventory prices, which consequently changes the weighted average cost. This method is commonly used in situations where inventory items are so intermingled that it is impossible to assign a specific cost to an individual unit, or when the accounting system is not sufficiently sophisticated to track FIFO or LIFO inven