{"id": "686", "question": "michigan-how much to replace sewer lines", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the cost of replacing sewer lines in Michigan can vary significantly depending on the extent of the damage and the specific needs of the sewer line. According to the passage, the cost of pipe replacement may range from $3,000 to around $12,000. The cost can be influenced by factors such as the location of the pipe, its accessibility, and whether only a damaged section or the entire sewer line needs to be replaced.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the cost of replacing sewer lines in Michigan can vary significantly depending on the extent of the damage and the specific needs of the sewer line. According to the passage, the cost of pipe replacement may range from $3,000 to around $12,000. The cost can be influenced by factors such as the location of the pipe, its accessibility, and whether only a damaged section or the entire sewer line needs to be replaced.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the cost of replacing sewer lines in Michigan can vary significantly depending on the extent of the damage and the location of the pipe. If a section of the pipe is beyond repair, it may require pipe replacement, which could cost from $3,000 to around $12,000. If the entire sewer line needs to be replaced, the cost could be even higher. The cost of a sewer line repair or replacement could break the bank.\", \"Based on the given passages, the cost of replacing sewer lines in Michigan can vary significantly depending on the extent of the damage and the specific circumstances. A pipe camera inspection to assess the damage could cost anywhere from $250 to $500. For minor repairs, the cost might be around $50 per foot for sewer line repair, while more extensive work, such as pipe replacement, could range from $3,000 to around $12,000, depending on whether only the damaged section or the entire sewer line needs to be replaced.\", \"Based on the given passages, the cost of replacing sewer lines in Michigan can vary significantly depending on the extent of the damage and the specific needs of the sewer line. According to the passage, the cost of pipe replacement may range from $3,000 to around $12,000. The cost can be influenced by factors such as the location of the pipe, its accessibility, and whether only a damaged section or the entire sewer line needs to be replaced.\", \"Based on the given passages, the cost of replacing sewer lines can vary significantly. It depends on the extent of the damage and the location of the pipe. If only a damaged section needs replacement, the cost could be from $50 per foot, which would be quite affordable. However, if the entire sewer line needs to be replaced, the cost could range from $3,000 to around $12,000, which would be a substantial financial burden.\"]", "time_sec": 20.03, "generation_time_seconds": 19.17, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8534, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2783, 315, 24891, 61920, 5128, 304, 14630, 646, 13289, 11941, 11649, 389, 279, 12818, 315, 279, 5557, 323, 279, 3728, 315, 279, 13647, 13, 1416, 264, 3772, 315, 279, 13647, 374, 7797, 12733, 11, 432, 1231, 1373, 13647, 13723, 11, 892, 1410, 2783, 504, 400, 18, 11, 15, 15, 15, 311, 2163, 400, 16, 17, 11, 15, 15, 15, 13, 1416, 279, 4453, 61920, 1555, 3880, 311, 387, 12575, 11, 279, 2783, 1410, 387, 1496, 5080, 13, 576, 2783, 315, 264, 61920, 1555, 12733, 476, 13723, 1410, 1438, 279, 6073, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the cost of replacing sewer lines in Michigan can vary significantly depending on the extent of the damage and the location of the pipe. If a section of the pipe is beyond repair, it may require pipe replacement, which coul