{"id": "694", "question": "does watching snapchat stories increase score", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that watching Snapchat stories does not directly increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is increased by sending and receiving more snaps, and by interacting with friends on the platform. Watching stories is not mentioned as a factor that contributes to increasing one's score. Therefore, the answer to the question is: No, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The score is calculated based on the number of snaps you send and receive, not on the number of stories you watch.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The score is calculated based on the number of snaps you send and receive, not on the number of stories you watch.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is a sum of the number of snaps sent and snaps received, and there is no indication that watching stories contributes to this score.\", \"Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score. The passage mentions that Snapchat scores are a sum of the number of snaps sent and received, and simply watching stories does not contribute to this total.\", \"Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The score is calculated based on the number of snaps you send and receive, not on the number of stories you watch.\", \"Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase score.\"]", "time_sec": 11.051, "generation_time_seconds": 10.0296, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0153, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10099, 55179, 7343, 1558, 537, 5263, 697, 55179, 5456, 13, 576, 46769, 6286, 429, 279, 5456, 374, 264, 2629, 315, 279, 1372, 315, 51304, 3208, 323, 51304, 3949, 11, 323, 1052, 374, 902, 27039, 429, 10099, 7343, 42972, 311, 419, 5456, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The passages mention that the score is a sum of the number of snaps sent and snaps received, and there is no indication that watching stories contributes to this score.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.792534532141589, "g_worst_claim": 0.24828160726107085, "g_content": 1.2983593318773352, "g_traj_mean": 0.9598943591117859}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10099, 55179, 7343, 1558, 537, 5263, 697, 5456, 13, 576, 21085, 33845, 429, 55179, 12205, 525, 264, 2629, 315, 279, 1372, 315, 51304, 3208, 323, 3949, 11, 323, 4936, 10099, 7343, 1558, 537, 16792, 311, 419, 2790, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your score. The passage mentions that Snapchat scores are a sum of the number of snaps sent and received, and simply watching stories does not contribute to this total.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6623777099932083, "g_worst_claim": 0.14352682503786954, "g_content": 1.1049959876320579, "g_traj_mean": 0.851208508014679}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10099, 55179, 7343, 1558, 537, 5263, 697, 55179, 5456, 13, 576, 5456, 374, 16588, 3118, 389, 279, 1372, 315, 51304, 498, 3624, 323, 5258, 11, 537, 389, 279, 1372, 315, 7343, 498, 3736, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase your Snapchat score. The score is calculated based on the number of snaps you send and receive, not on the number of stories you watch.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5052755177021027, "g_worst_claim": 0.16595176855723062, "g_content": 0.8526725769042969, "g_traj_mean": 0.5416989326477051}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 10099, 55179, 7343, 1558, 537, 5263, 5456, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, watching Snapchat stories does not increase score.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.2148149535059929, "g_worst_claim": 0.09431777894496918, "g_content": 0.32522958517074585, "g_traj_mean": 0.12131530791521072}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.07, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "695", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, you start by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Next, transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mix thoroughly, for at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "pred": "Once the base is ready, you can pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker as described in Passage 1. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. Passage 1 also mentions that when the ice cream is softly frozen, it can be served immediately or placed in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Once the base is ready, you can pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker as described in Passage 1. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. Passage 1 also mentions that when the ice cream is softly frozen, it can be served immediately or placed in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Start by making the ice cream base. This can be a vanilla ice cream base or a cream-based ice cream, which is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. The recipe provided makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double the recipe if you want more.\\n\\n2. In a saucepan, stir together sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n\\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n\\n4. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine. Churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"Based on the given passages, making ice cream involves two main methods:\\n\\n1. **Churn Method**: \\n   - Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker.\\n   - Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions.\\n   - This process typically takes 20 to 25 minutes.\\n   - Once the ice cream is softly frozen, it can be served immediately or placed in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\n2. **Dissolve and Chill Method**:\\n   - Stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\\n   - Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n   - Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup.\\n   - Stir in vanilla extract and chill the mix thoroughly, taking at least 2 hours.\\n   - This method results in a cream-based ice cream, which is described as being a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\nBoth methods produce ice cream, with the churn method being simpler and yielding a lighter texture, while the dissolve and chill method allows for customization and a thicker texture.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make ice cream, start by mixing your base. Passage 3 suggests a good vanilla ice cream base can be used to make a wide variety of ice cream flavors. Cream-based ice cream is described as being a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\nThe instructions provided in Passage 3 indicate that the recipe will make one quart of ice cream. If you want more, you should double the recipe.\\n\\nPassage 1 then describes the process of making the ice cream mixture. It instructs to stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. After heating, transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup. Finally, stir in vanilla extract and chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n\\nOnce the base is ready, you can pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker as described in Passage 1. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. Passage 1 also mentions that when the ice cream is softly frozen, it can be served immediately or placed in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n2. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\"]", "time_sec": 31.362, "generation_time_seconds": 30.3515, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0035, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 5145, 553, 3259, 279, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 476, 264, 12644, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 892, 374, 264, 2699, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 13, 576, 11116, 3897, 3643, 825, 40276, 315, 9853, 12644, 11, 773, 498, 646, 1990, 279, 11116, 421, 498, 1366, 803, 382, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19187, 848, 11, 23065, 3786, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14