{"id": "696", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for about 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours to ripen.", "pred": "1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (20 to 25 minutes).\n2. Alternatively, you can mix the base by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup.\n4. Chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n5. Stir in vanilla extract.\n6. Serve the ice cream immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (20 to 25 minutes).\n2. Alternatively, you can mix the base by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup.\n4. Chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n5. Stir in vanilla extract.\n6. Serve the ice cream immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Start by making the ice cream base. This can be a vanilla ice cream base or a cream-based ice cream, which is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. The recipe provided makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double the recipe if you want more.\\n\\n2. In a saucepan, stir together sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n\\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n\\n4. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine. Churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"To make ice cream:\\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved.\\n2. Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n3. Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup.\\n4. Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n5. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make ice cream, you need to:\\n\\n1. Mix your base: Combine ingredients to create a vanilla ice cream base. This base serves as the foundation for various ice cream flavors.\\n2. Prepare the ice cream mix: Pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker.\\n3. Churn the mix according to the manufacturer's instructions: This typically takes 20 to 25 minutes.\\n4. If the ice cream is not fully frozen, cover it with plastic wrap and freeze it for 2 to 3 hours to ripen.\\n\\nPlease note that the passages do not provide a complete recipe or all the details needed to make ice cream from scratch.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make ice cream, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (20 to 25 minutes).\\n2. Alternatively, you can mix the base by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup.\\n4. Chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n5. Stir in vanilla extract.\\n6. Serve the ice cream immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\"]", "time_sec": 27.604, "generation_time_seconds": 26.429, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1647, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 5145, 553, 3259, 279, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 476, 264, 12644, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 892, 374, 264, 2699, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 13, 576, 11116, 3897, 3643, 825, 40276, 315, 9853, 12644, 11, 773, 498, 646, 1990, 279, 11116, 421, 498, 1366, 803, 382, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19187, 848, 11, 23065, 3786, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 382, 18, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 13, 86489, 279, 20980, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 382, 19, 13, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 2484, 389, 279, 5662, 13, 910, 399, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 20, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2803358984618196, "g_worst_claim": 0.35541550318400067, "g_content": 1.847961708351418, "g_traj_mean": 1.2669719457626343}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 510, 16, 13, 64192, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 13163, 702, 55667, 624, 17, 13, 26070, 1101, 3080, 6514, 374, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 624, 18, 13, 23200, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 624, 19, 13, 64192, 304, 32065, 8649, 323, 36301, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 624, 20, 13, 25968, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 11, 2484, 389, 279, 5662, 11, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 13963, 594, 17961, 11, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ice cream:\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n3. Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup.\n4. Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n5. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7585316103540862, "g_worst_claim": 0.5095026016235351, "g_content": 1.8971349080403646, "g_traj_mean": 1.5387965440750122}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 1447, 16, 13, 19219, 697, 2331, 25, 46812, 13966, 311, 1855, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1096, 2331, 17045, 438, 279, 16266, 369, 5257, 9853, 12644, 31423, 624, 17, 13, 31166, 279, 9853, 12644, 6514, 25, 25968, 279, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 624, 18, 13, 910, 399, 279, 6514, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 11221, 25, 1096, 11136, 4990, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 1416, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 537, 7225, 19690, 11, 3421, 432, 448, 12188, 15061, 323, 29930, 432, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 311, 23288, 268, 382, 5501, 5185, 429, 279, 46769, 653, 537, 3410, 264, 4583, 11116, 476, 678, 279, 3565, 4362, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 504, 18778, 13, 151645], "pred": "Please note that the passages do not provide a complete recipe or all the details needed to make ice cream from scratch.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.001702525159392, "g_worst_claim": 0.15016410661780316, "g_content": 1.0516855945325878, "g_traj_mean": 0.8465014696121216}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 25968, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 320, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 4292, 17, 13, 38478, 11, 498, 646, 6514, 279, 2331, 553, 53954, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 624, 18, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 624, 19, 13, 86489, 279, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 624, 20, 13, 64192, 304, 32065, 8649, 624, 21, 13, 52932, 279, 9853, 12644, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (20 to 25 minutes).\n2. Alternatively, you can mix the base by stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup.\n4. Chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n5. Stir in vanilla extract.\n6. Serve the ice cream immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4157727718148496, "g_worst_claim": 0.14882596731185913, "g_content": 1.904383403498952, "g_traj_mean": 1.378183364868164}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 80.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "697", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to manufacturer's instructions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. For a creamy and flavorful base, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly before using it as a base for your desired ice cream flavor.", "pred": "1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes, as described in passage 1.\n2. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved, as outlined in passage 2.\n3. Heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n4. Transfer the hot cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup.\n5. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours, as mentioned in passage 2.\n6. Add vanilla extract to the chilled mixture.\n7. Use the chilled vanilla ice cream base as a starting point and add various flavorings to create different ice cream flavors, as suggested in passage 3.\n8. Serve the ice cream immediately as it is softly frozen, or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on it and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours, as detailed in passage 1.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes, as described in passage 1.\n2. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved, as outlined in passage 2.\n3. Heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n4. Transfer the hot cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup.\n5. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours, as mentioned in passage 2.\n6. Add vanilla extract to the chilled mixture.\n7. Use the chilled vanilla ice cream base as a starting point and add various flavorings to create different ice cream flavors, as suggested in passage 3.\n8. Serve the ice cream immediately as it is softly frozen, or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on it and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours, as detailed in passage 1.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Start by making the ice cream base. This can be a vanilla ice cream base or a cream-based ice cream, which is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. The recipe provided makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double the recipe if you want more.\\n\\n2. In a saucepan, stir together sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n\\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n\\n4. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine. Churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine, following the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n2. When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\nThis process focuses on the final steps of making ice cream, assuming that the base has already been prepared according to the instructions provided in the earlier passages.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Prepare the base: Add cream and milk to a saucepan over low heat until the mixture is hot and a small ring of foam appears. Remove from heat and add vanilla extract, then chill thoroughly for at least 2 hours.\\n\\n2. Activate the ice cream maker: Pour the chilled ice cream mix into the ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions for about 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n3. Check the consistency: Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place it in the freezer. If you want to ripen it, cover it with a piece of plastic wrap and freeze for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\n4. Customize flavors: If you want to make different flavors, you can start with a vanilla ice cream base and adjust it with various ingredients to create unique tastes.\", \"Based on the given passages, the steps to make ice cream are as follows:\\n\\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes, as described in passage 1.\\n2. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved, as outlined in passage 2.\\n3. Heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n4. Transfer the hot cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup.\\n5. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours, as mentioned in passage 2.\\n6. Add vanilla extract to the chilled mixture.\\n7. Use the chilled vanilla ice cream base as a starting point and add various flavorings to create different ice cream flavors, as suggested in passage 3.\\n8. Serve the ice cream immediately as it is softly frozen, or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on it and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours, as detailed in passage 1.\"]", "time_sec": 33.225, "generation_time_seconds": 32.1442, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0741, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 5145, 553, 3259, 279, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 476, 264, 12644, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 892, 374, 264, 2699, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 13, 576, 11116, 3897, 3643, 825, 40276, 315, 9853, 12644, 11, 773, 498, 646, 1990, 279, 11116, 421, 498, 1366, 803, 382, 17, 13, 758, 264, 19187, 848, 11, 23065, 3786, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 382, 18, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 13, 86489, 279, 20980, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 382, 19, 13, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 2484, 389, 279, 5662, 13, 910, 399, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 20, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3111994260914328, "g_worst_claim": 0.40811340014139813, "g_content": 1.8563351101345487, "g_traj_mean": 1.2891771793365479}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 25968, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 2484, 389, 279, 5662, 11, 2701, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 624, 17, 13, 3197, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 3421, 432, 448, 12188, 15061, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 382, 1986, 1882, 23497, 389, 279, 1590, 7354, 315, 3259, 9853, 12644, 11, 25538, 429, 279, 2331, 702, 2669, 1012, 10030, 4092, 311, 279, 11221, 3897, 304, 279, 6788, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "This process focuses on the final steps of making ice cream, assuming that the base has already been prepared according to the instructions provided in the earlier passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0401519151434067, "g_worst_claim": 0.39193495114644367, "g_content": 1.3178486217151988, "g_traj_mean": 1.0222766399383545}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2331, 25, 2691, 12644, 323, 14074, 311, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 20980, 374, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 13, 10783, 504, 8628, 323, 912, 32065, 8649, 11, 1221, 36301, 26364, 369, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 382, 17, 13, 51714, 279, 9853, 12644, 24232, 25, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 279, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 11221, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 18, 13, 4248, 279, 28137, 25, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 23288, 268, 432, 11, 3421, 432, 448, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 323, 29930, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 382, 19, 13, 46334, 31423, 25, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 1281, 2155, 31423, 11, 498, 646, 1191, 448, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 323, 7500, 432, 448, 5257, 13966, 311, 1855, 4911, 35163, 13, 151645], "pred": "4. Customize flavors: If you want to make different flavors, you can start with a vanilla ice cream base and adjust it with various ingredients to create unique tastes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9723060919234089, "g_worst_claim": -0.17296960949897766, "g_content": 1.224832492404514, "g_traj_mean": 0.9081722497940063}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 7354, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 525, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 25968, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 11, 438, 7481, 304, 21085, 220, 16, 624, 17, 13, 38478, 11, 23065, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 11, 438, 32640, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 624, 18, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 432, 374, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 624, 19, 13, 23200, 279, 4017, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 624, 20, 13, 86489, 279, 20980, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 11, 438, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 624, 21, 13, 2691, 32065, 8649, 311, 279, 83942, 20980, 624, 22, 13, 5443, 279, 83942, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 438, 264, 5916, 1459, 323, 912, 5257, 17172, 819, 311, 1855, 2155, 9853, 12644, 31423, 11, 438, 11827, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 624, 23, 13, 52932, 279, 9853, 12644, 7069, 438, 432, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 432, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 11, 438, 11682, 304, 21085, 220, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes, as described in passage 1.\n2. Alternatively, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved, as outlined in passage 2.\n3. Heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n4. Transfer the hot cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup.\n5. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours, as mentioned in passage 2.\n6. Add vanilla extract to the chilled mixture.\n7. Use the chilled vanilla ice cream base as a starting point and add various flavorings to create different ice cream flavors, as suggested in passage 3.\n8. Serve the ice cream immediately as it is softly frozen, or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on it and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours, as detailed in passage 1.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1773828084066995, "g_worst_claim": 0.18186000982920328, "g_content": 1.4215624534477622, "g_traj_mean": 1.085106611251831}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "698", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\nPassage 1 provides instructions for making ice cream using an ice cream maker. To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes). Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nPassage 2 provides a recipe for making ice cream from scratch. To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Then, heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n\nPassage 3 provides general instructions for making ice cream bases. To make ice cream, you will need to start with a good vanilla ice cream base. This type of base is made with cream rather than custard, and it results in a lighter and less icy texture. To make one quart of ice cream, you will need to double the recipe.\n\nTherefore, to summarize:\n\nTo make ice cream using an ice cream maker:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker and turn on the machine.\n2. Churn the ice cream according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes).\n3. Serve the ice cream immediately or place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nTo make ice cream from scratch:\n\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges.\n3. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract.\n4. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n", "pred": "5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Start by making the ice cream base. This can be a vanilla ice cream base or a cream-based ice cream, which is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. The recipe provided makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double the recipe if you want more.\\n\\n2. In a saucepan, stir together sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n\\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n\\n4. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine. Churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n1. Start by mixing your base. A good vanilla ice cream base is recommended. For a cream-based ice cream, the texture will be icier and lighter compared to a custard-based ice cream. \\n2. Prepare the mix. This involves stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge of the pan.\\n3. Chill the mix thoroughly. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup, and chill it for at least 2 hours.\\n4. Pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, which should take about 20 to 25 minutes.\\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Prepare the ice cream base by combining cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churning according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n2. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and let it ripen in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\nNote: These steps are based on the information provided in passage 1, and do not include the additional steps from passage 2 or passage 3.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved. Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup.\\n2. Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n3. Pour the chilled mixture into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes.\\n4. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\\n5. To create a specific flavor, start with a good vanilla ice cream base and adjust as needed to your desired flavor profile.\"]", "time_sec": 29.859, "generation_time_seconds": 29.0567, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7931, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids":