, 1096, 17601, 53954, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 7215, 624, 18, 13, 86489, 279, 6514, 26364, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 11, 323, 36301, 432, 369, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 624, 19, 13, 25968, 279, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 13, 11999, 389, 279, 5662, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 11, 892, 1265, 1896, 911, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to make ice cream, follow these steps:\n1. Start by mixing your base. A good vanilla ice cream base is recommended. For a cream-based ice cream, the texture will be icier and lighter compared to a custard-based ice cream. \n2. Prepare the mix. This involves stirring sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge of the pan.\n3. Chill the mix thoroughly. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup, and chill it for at least 2 hours.\n4. Pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, which should take about 20 to 25 minutes.\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3366324538423149, "g_worst_claim": 0.19185749689737955, "g_content": 1.9110710575895489, "g_traj_mean": 1.2993587255477905}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 7354, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 9853, 12644, 2331, 553, 34171, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 521, 53344, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 624, 17, 13, 3197, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1077, 432, 23288, 268, 304, 279, 49585, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 382, 9112, 25, 4220, 7354, 525, 3118, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 21085, 220, 16, 11, 323, 653, 537, 2924, 279, 5107, 7354, 504, 21085, 220, 17, 476, 21085, 220, 18, 13, 151645], "pred": "Note: These steps are based on the information provided in passage 1, and do not include the additional steps from passage 2 or passage 3.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8558912208267285, "g_worst_claim": 0.2840963900089264, "g_content": 1.25227668637135, "g_traj_mean": 0.9714558720588684}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 64192, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 1101, 3080, 6514, 374, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 13, 23200, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 624, 17, 13, 64192, 304, 32065, 8649, 323, 36301, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 624, 18, 13, 25968, 279, 83942, 20980, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 11, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 3197, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 624, 20, 13, 2014, 1855, 264, 3151, 17172, 11, 1191, 448, 264, 1661, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 323, 7500, 438, 4362, 311, 697, 12685, 17172, 5526, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved. Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup.\n2. Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n3. Pour the chilled mixture into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions, 20 to 25 minutes.\n4. When ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\n5. To create a specific flavor, start with a good vanilla ice cream base and adjust as needed to your desired flavor profile.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5988105685274518, "g_worst_claim": 0.3217313090960185, "g_content": 1.9121339217476223, "g_traj_mean": 1.4437981843948364}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 15.09, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "699", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine, following the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n2. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved, then heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2).\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract before chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2).\n4. Once the ice cream base is ready, pour it into the ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n5. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1).\n\nNote that the passages do not provide a specific recipe for making ice cream, but rather provide general steps and tips for making ice cream using an ice cream maker.", "pred": "5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. Start by making the ice cream base. This can be a vanilla ice cream base or a cream-based ice cream, which is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. The recipe provided makes one quart of ice cream, so you can double the recipe if you want more.\\n\\n2. In a saucepan, stir together sugar, cream, and milk over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n\\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. Chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n\\n4. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine. Churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Start by creating a base for your ice cream. This can be a vanilla ice cream base or a mixture of sugar, cream, and milk heated to a specific consistency. The passage mentions that a vanilla ice cream base is easy to work with and that cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\n2. Prepare the ice cream mix. If using a homemade base, chill the mixture thoroughly. If using store-bought ice cream, pour the mix into an ice cream maker.\\n\\n3. Churn the ice cream mix according to the manufacturer's directions, which typically takes about 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n4. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.\", \"Based on the given passages, here is how to make ice cream:\\n\\n1. For the base:\\n   - Mix your base. This involves combining ingredients to create a creamy base. You can start with a good vanilla ice cream base.\\n   - The base can be either cream-based or custard-based. Cream-based ice cream is described as being a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\n2. For the mix:\\n   - Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\\n   - Heat the mix just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n   - Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container.\\n   - Stir in vanilla extract and chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n\\n3. For the ice cream:\\n   - Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker.\\n   - Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions.\\n   - The churning process should take approximately 20 to 25 minutes.\\n   - Once the ice cream is softly frozen, it can be served immediately or placed in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.\", \"Based on the given passages, to make ice cream, start by mixing your base. A good vanilla ice cream base is recommended as it is easy to make. Cream-based ice cream is a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. \\n\\nFor a specific method, follow these steps:\\n1. If using a base, mix it well. \\n2. If starting from scratch, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. \\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. \\n4. Stir in vanilla extract and chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. \\n\\nAfter chilling, pour the mixture into an ice cream maker, turn it on, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. \\n\\nOnce the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.\"]", "time_sec": 33.857, "generation_time_seconds": 32.6274, "selection_time_seconds": 1.2202, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 9853, 12644, 1447, 16, 13, 5145, 553, 3259, 279, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 476, 264, 12644, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 892, 374, 264, 2699, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 13, 576, 11116, 3897, 3643, 825, 40