l_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 84.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "720", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "Sure! Here's how to poach an egg using a PoachPod® based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil. (Passage 1)\n2. Carefully crack an egg into the PoachPod®, being careful not to break the yolk. (Passage 2)\n3. Gently slide the PoachPod® into the boiling water, making sure it floats upright and no water enters the pod. (Passage 2)\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and cook for 6 minutes. (Passage 2)\n5. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully remove the PoachPod® from the water and flip it upside down over a plate. (Passage 2)\n6. Press gently on the bottom of the PoachPod® to release the poached egg onto the plate. (Passage 2)\n\nThat's it! According to the passages, the PoachPod® makes it easy to poach eggs by allowing you to float them in boiling water without breaking the yolk. Just make sure to lightly oil the pod before adding the egg to prevent sticking.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\", \"Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to poach an egg using a PoachPod:\\n\\n1. Lightly oil the PoachPod.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the PoachPod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Float the PoachPod in a saucepan of simmering water.\\n4. Cover the pan with a tight-fitting lid.\\n5. Cook the egg for about 4-6 minutes.\\n6. After cooking, flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate.\\n7. Gently press on the bottom of the PoachPod to release the poached egg onto the plate.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\", \"Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod:\\n\\n1. Lightly oil the PoachPod.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod.\\n3. Float the poaching pod in a saucepan of simmering water.\\n4. Cover the pan with a tight-fitting lid.\\n5. Cook for about 4-6 minutes.\\n6. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n7. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\"]", "time_sec": 25.043, "generation_time_seconds": 23.9031, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1287, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3460, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 54945, 458, 18636, 323, 29273, 14983, 432, 1119, 279, 52925, 3193, 11829, 7509, 11, 1660, 16585, 537, 311, 1438, 279, 18636, 594, 379, 22604, 624, 18, 13, 13001, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 304, 279, 49837, 3015, 11, 22573, 279, 7509, 26558, 48585, 323, 902, 3015, 5221, 1119, 279, 7509, 624, 19, 13, 17757, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 26334, 323, 1077, 279, 18636, 4296, 369, 4743, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 279, 26334, 323, 990, 264, 3460, 1739, 15521, 45505, 476, 259, 13181, 311, 11893, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 700, 315, 279, 4017, 3015, 624, 21, 13, 40284, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 35841, 1495, 916, 264, 11968, 323, 29273, 3493, 389, 279, 5622, 311, 4879, 279, 3193, 3854, 18636, 8630, 279, 11968, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2457058743280107, "g_worst_claim": 0.21814817190170288, "g_content": 1.7275450422957137, "g_traj_mean": 1.2339739799499512}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 279, 7354, 311, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 1447, 16, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 624, 17, 13, 54945, 458, 18636, 323, 29273, 14983, 432, 1119, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 1660, 16585, 537, 311, 1438, 279, 18636, 594, 379, 22604, 624, 18, 13, 13001, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 304, 264, 19187, 848, 315, 61815, 287, 3015, 624, 19, 13, 17757, 279, 7215, 448, 264, 10296, 2220, 14810, 26334, 624, 20, 13, 12514, 279, 18636, 369, 911, 220, 19, 12, 21, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 4636, 17233, 11, 18287, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 35841, 1495, 916, 264, 11968, 624, 22, 13, 479, 4402, 3493, 389, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 311, 4879, 279, 3193, 3854, 18636, 8630, 279, 11968, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Lightly oil the PoachPod.\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the PoachPod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the PoachPod in a saucepan of simmering water.\n4. Cover the pan with a tight-fitting lid.\n5. Cook the egg for about 4-6 minutes.\n6. After cooking, flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate.\n7. Gently press on the bottom of the PoachPod to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1360722284177283, "g_worst_claim": 0.3