{"id": "722", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to poach an egg using a PoachPod®:\n\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the yolk.\n3. Gently slide the pod into the boiling water, making sure it stays upright and no water gets in.\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and press the bottom to release the poached egg.\n\nSo, to summarize, the steps to poach an egg using a PoachPod® are:\n\n1. Bring water to a boil.\n2. Crack egg into pod.\n3. Float pod in boiling water.\n4. Cook for 6 minutes.\n5. Remove pod from water.\n6. Release egg onto plate.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod:\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod:\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\", \"Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod®:\\n\\n1. Fill a large pot with water.\\n2. Bring the water to a boil.\\n3. Crack an egg into the silicone poaching pod, ensuring not to break the yolk.\\n4. Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, keeping it upright.\\n5. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n6. Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n7. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\", \"Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod:\\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\", \"Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod:\\n\\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\"]", "time_sec": 26.326, "generation_time_seconds": 25.2123, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1061, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 311, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3460, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 54945, 458, 18636, 323, 29273, 14983, 432, 1119, 279, 52925, 3193, 11829, 7509, 11, 1660, 16585, 537, 311, 1438, 279, 18636, 594, 379, 22604, 624, 18, 13, 13001, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 304, 279, 49837, 3015, 11, 22573, 279, 7509, 26558, 48585, 323, 902, 3015, 5221, 1119, 279, 7509, 624, 19, 13, 17757, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 26334, 323, 1077, 279, 18636, 4296, 369, 4743, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 279, 26334, 323, 990, 264, 3460, 1739, 15521, 45505, 476, 259, 13181, 311, 11893, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 700, 315, 279, 4017, 3015, 624, 21, 13, 40284, 279, 3193, 11829, 7509, 35841, 1495, 916, 264, 11968, 323, 29273, 3493, 389, 279, 5622, 311, 4879, 279, 3193, 3854, 18636, 8630, 279, 11968, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, to poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a 