{"id": "731", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that the breathing process involves the contraction and relaxation of various muscles, including the diaphragm muscle, to move air in and out of the lungs. This process involves an exchange of gases between the body and the external environment, specifically oxygen and carbon dioxide. Increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity by contracting the muscles involved in breathing draws air into the lungs, causing them to expand and decreasing air pressure below atmospheric pressure. Therefore, the passage does not mention any specific step involved in processing air before it reaches the lungs.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.\", \"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells of your body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, or the movement of oxygen into, and carbon dioxide out of, your lungs, and circulation, or transporting the oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. In all, breathing enhances your therapeutic back exercise program or your successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy. The ventilation component takes center stage.\", \"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air.\", \"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. The passages explain that there are two components to breathing: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen from the lungs to the body. The ventilation component is the focus of enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.\"]", "time_sec": 17.996, "generation_time_seconds": 17.3153, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6754, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 11, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 1096, 9289, 8573, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 576, 1882, 315, 25938, 702, 1378, 6813, 25, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7557, 315, 23552, 4429,