on, or the movement of oxygen into, and carbon dioxide out of, your lungs, and circulation, or transporting the oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. In all, breathing enhances your therapeutic back exercise program or your successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy. The ventilation component takes center stage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.807750200514652, "g_worst_claim": -0.2745589017868042, "g_content": 3.4167877773068986, "g_traj_mean": 2.2715766429901123}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 11, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 429, 13666, 1948, 498, 11, 304, 3953, 11, 279, 7761, 315, 697, 2487, 11, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 11, 892, 374, 279, 3720, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3913239738676286, "g_worst_claim": 0.12147835890452068, "g_content": 1.7400984513132196, "g_traj_mean": 1.8442736864089966}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 576, 46769, 10339, 429, 1052, 525, 1378, 6813, 311, 25938, 25, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7557, 315, 23552, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 55134, 3692, 374, 279, 5244, 315, 46494, 36371, 1182, 10158, 7468, 476, 6849, 20239, 304, 264, 462, 31244, 60776, 15069, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. The passages explain that there are two components to breathing: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen from the lungs to the body. The ventilation component is the focus of enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3019492853215802, "g_worst_claim": 0.12147835890452068, "g_content": 3.27267802845348, "g_traj_mean": 1.8057441711425781}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.48, "GAVIE-Rel": 4.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "732", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the process of processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs involves the following steps:\n\n1. The diaphragm muscle contracts to take air into the lungs, moving down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region. (Passage 1)\n2. The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment, occurring in the lungs. (Passage 2)\n3. Increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity, including the lungs, decreases the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, forcing air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing us to inhale. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the main steps in processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs are:\n\n1. Contraction of the diaphragm muscle to draw air into the lungs.\n2. Exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment in the lungs.\n3. Expansion of the thoracic cavity to decrease air pressure in the lungs and facilitate inhalation.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, specifically oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells of the body and the external environment, which is the air. This exchange occurs in the lungs and consists of two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing, contracts to take air into the lungs and relaxes to let air out again. The process of breathing also involves the movement of air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation, by decreasing the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, specifically oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells of the body and the external environment, which is the air. This exchange occurs in the lungs and consists of two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing, contracts to take air into the lungs and relaxes to let air out again. The process of breathing also involves the movement of air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation, by decreasing the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.\", \"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells in your body and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. The ventilation component of breathing takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercises and participating in a pro-active holistic therapy.\", \"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, specifically oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells of the body and the external environment, which is the air. This exchange occurs in the lungs and consists of two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing, contracts to take air into the lungs and relaxes to let air out again. The process of breathing also involves the movement of air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation, by decreasing the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure.\", \"Based on the given passages, the air you breathe is processed before it reaches your lungs through the following steps:\\n1. The air travels through the respiratory tract, starting from the nostrils or mouth.\\n2. The air moves down the pharynx, larynx, and trachea, which act as a passageway for the air.\\n3. The air then enters the bronchi, which are branches of the trachea, and further divide into smaller bronchioles.\\n4. The air continues to travel through the bronchioles, which are lined with cilia and mucus, trapping dust, bacteria, and other particles.\\n5. The air reaches the alveoli, which are tiny air sacs in the lungs, where gas exchange occurs between the air and blood.\"]", "time_sec": 22.543, "generation_time_seconds": 21.4947, "selection_time_seconds": 1.041, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 11, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 1096, 9289, 8573, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 576, 1882, 315, 25938, 702, 1378, 6813, 25, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7557, 315, 23552, 4429, 1119, 279, 2487, 2337, 55134, 311, 1380, 432, 374, 4362, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 55134, 3692, 4990, 4126, 6430, 304, 46494, 36371, 1182, 10158, 7468, 476, 6849, 20239, 304, 264, 462, 31244, 60776, 15069, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5469879058962435, "g_worst_claim": 0.07074856758117676, "g_content": 3.484621534160539, "g_traj_mean": 2.181560754776001}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 7761, 304, 697, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 1096, 9289, 13666, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 576, 55134, 3692, 315, 25938, 4990, 4126, 6430, 304, 46494, 36371, 1182, 22932, 323, 23528, 304, 264, 462, 31244, 60776, 15069, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells in your body and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. The ventilation component of breathing takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercises and participating in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.510102287377802, "g_worst_claim": 0.07074856758117676, "g_content": 3.7837124448834043, "g_traj_mean": 2.267425775527954}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 11689, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 7761, 315, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 9250, 4573, 11, 892, 374, 279, 3720, 13, 1096, 9289, 13666, 304, 279, 44174, 323, 17167, 315, 1378, 6813, 25, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7557, 315, 23552, 4429, 1119, 279, 2487, 2337, 55134, 311, 1380, 432, 374, 4362, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 1853, 94796, 76, 15747, 11, 892, 374, 279, 12435, 15747, 315, 25938, 11, 17080, 311, 1896, 3720, 1119, 279, 44174, 323, 11967, 288, 311, 1077, 3720, 700, 1549, 13, 576, 1882, 315, 25938, 1083, 17601, 279, 7203, 315, 3720, 504, 279, 16566, 1119, 279, 44174, 11, 14381, 76673, 367, 11, 553, 43549, 279, 3720, 7262, 304, 279, 44174, 3685, 279, 44375, 7262, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, specifically oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells of the body and the external environment, which is the air. This exchange occurs in the lungs and consists of two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing, contracts to take air into the lungs and relaxes to let air out again. The process of breathing also involves the movement of air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation, by decreasing the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.292396559690688, "g_worst_claim": -0.001930306355158488, "g_content": 2.026430130004883, "g_traj_mean": 1.2597711086273193}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 3720, 498, 36297, 374, 15233, 1573, 432, 24491, 697, 44174, 1526, 279, 2701, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 576, 3720, 34192, 1526, 279, 41531, 41829, 11, 5916, 504, 279, 56326, 8669, 476, 10780, 624, 17, 13, 576, 3720, 10797, 1495, 279, 1319, 658, 23357, 11, 326, 658, 23357, 11, 323, 489, 1777, 64, 11, 892, 1160, 438, 264, 1494, 351, 24723, 369, 279, 3720, 624, 18, 13, 576, 3720, 1221, 28833, 279, 29971, 14604, 11, 892, 525, 23091, 315, 279, 489, 1777, 64, 11, 323, 4623, 21749, 1119, 9155, 29971, 52401, 642, 624, 19, 13, 576, 3720, 9539, 311, 5821, 1526, 279, 29971, 52401, 642, 11, 892, 525, 31293, 448, 272, 24078, 323, 296, 37501, 11, 92569, 15797, 11, 23157, 11, 323, 1008, 18730, 624, 20, 13, 576, 3720, 24491, 279, 452, 586, 14225, 11, 892, 525, 13673, 3720, 11100, 82, 304, 279, 44174, 11, 1380, 6819, 9289, 13666, 1948, 279, 3720, 323, 6543, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the air you breathe is processed before it reaches your lungs through the following steps:\n1. The air travels through the respiratory tract, starting from the nostrils or mouth.\n2. The air moves down the pharynx, larynx, and trachea, which act as a passageway for the air.\n3. The air then enters the bronchi, which are branches of the trachea, and further divide into smaller bronchioles.\n4. The air continues to travel through the bronchioles, which are lined with cilia and mucus, trapping dust, bacteria, and other particles.\n5. The air reaches the alveoli, which are tiny air sacs in the lungs, where gas exchange occurs between the air and blood.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.01775074592821959, "g_worst_claim": -0.22378261089324952, "g_content": 0.04849232832590739, "g_traj_mean": 0.01665157824754715}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.39, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "733", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how the air you breathe is processed before it reaches your lungs:\n\nWhen you inhale, the diaphragm muscle contracts, moving down from the bottom of your rib cage towards your abdominal region, which causes the thoracic cavity to increase in volume. This decrease in air pressure in the lungs below atmospheric pressure forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing you to inhale.\n\nTherefore, the air you breathe is processed by the diaphragm muscle before it reaches your lungs, which contracts to take air into the lungs and relax to let it out again. Additionally, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, such as oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment, which occurs in the lungs.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment through the lungs. This exchange is facilitated by the contraction and relaxation of the diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing. The diaphragm contracts to move down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region, creating a decrease in air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, which forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment through the lungs. This exchange is facilitated by the contraction and relaxation of the diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing. The diaphragm contracts to move down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region, creating a decrease in air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, which forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment through the lungs. This exchange is facilitated by the contraction and relaxation of the diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing. The diaphragm contracts to move down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region, creating a decrease in air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, which forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation.\", \"Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. Breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transportation of oxygen to where it is needed in the body. Therefore, the air you breathe is processed through the lungs, where the gases are exchanged, primarily through the ventilation component.\"]", "time_sec": 16.659, "generation_time_seconds": 15.6812, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9723, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 11, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 1096, 9289, 8573, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 576, 1882, 315, 25938, 702, 1378, 6813, 25, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7557, 315, 23552, 4429, 1119, 279, 2487, 2337, 55134, 311, 1380, 432, 374, 4362, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 55134, 3692, 4990, 4126, 6430, 304, 46494, 36371, 1182, 10158, 7468, 476, 6849, 20239, 304, 264, 462, 31244, 60776, 15069, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange happens in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5290333701504601, "g_worst_claim": 0.1343105137348175, "g_content": 3.4577352486404718, "g_traj_mean": 2.158809185028076}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.2630153000354767, "g_worst_claim": -0.2630153000354767, "g_content": -0.4261442184448242, "g_traj_mean": -0.23372668027877808}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 1526, 279, 44174, 13, 1096, 9289, 374, 71749, 553, 279, 70795, 323, 42585, 315, 279, 1853, 94796, 76, 15747, 11, 892, 374, 279, 12435, 15747, 315, 25938, 13, 576, 1853, 94796, 76, 17080, 311, 3271, 1495, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 20131, 35360, 6974, 279, 55956, 5537, 11, 6825, 264, 18472, 304, 3720, 7262, 304, 279, 44174, 3685, 279, 44375, 7262, 11, 892, 8437, 3720, 504, 279, 16566, 1119, 279, 44174, 11, 14381, 76673, 367, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment through the lungs. This exchange is facilitated by the contraction and relaxation of the diaphragm muscle, which is the principal muscle of breathing. The diaphragm contracts to move down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region, creating a decrease in air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, which forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing inhalation.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0738375561448918, "g_worst_claim": 0.1343105137348175, "g_content": 1.7400241608315326, "g_traj_mean": 1.2253135442733765}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 1096, 9289, 13666, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 11427, 43561, 702, 1378, 6813, 25, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 374, 279, 17903, 315, 23552, 311, 1380, 432, 374, 4362, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 15277, 11, 279, 3720, 498, 36297, 374, 15233, 1526, 279, 44174, 11, 1380, 279, 44512, 525, 47401, 11, 15503, 1526, 279, 55134, 3692, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. Breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transportation of oxygen to where it is needed in the body. Therefore, the air you breathe is processed through the lungs, where the gases are exchanged, primarily through the ventilation component.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0153105566769967, "g_worst_claim": 0.1343105137348175, "g_content": 1.6476563244331173, "g_traj_mean": 1.0300685167312622}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.87, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "735", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "SMS stands for Short Message Service, commonly referred to as a text message, and allows you to send a text message of up to 160 characters to another device. MMS, which stands for Multimedia Messaging Service, is an evolution of SMS. It allows you to send messages that include pictures, video, or audio content to another device. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB. SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS allows a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.", "pred": "3. Functionality: SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS offers a more comprehensive messaging experience including multimedia content.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "3. Functionality: SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS offers a more comprehensive messaging experience including multimedia content.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS (Short Message Service) only allows you to send text, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four.\", \"Based on the given passages:\\n\\nThe main differences between SMS and MMS are:\\n\\n1. Format: SMS sends plain text messages, while MMS can send multiple types of media such as pictures, sounds, videos, or any combination of these.\\n\\n2. Size: SMS messages are limited to 160 characters per message, while MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.\\n\\n3. Functionality: SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS offers a more comprehensive messaging experience including multimedia content.\", \"Based on the given passages, the key differences between SMS and MMS are:\\n\\n1. Purpose: SMS is primarily for sending text messages, while MMS is designed for sending multimedia content like pictures, videos, or audio files.\\n\\n2. Content: SMS is limited to text-only messages, whereas MMS can include text, pictures, sounds, videos, or any combination of these.\\n\\n3. Size: MMS messages can carry a larger size of content, up to 300KB in extensions of formats like WAV, JPEG, or GIF, compared to SMS.\\n\\n4. Evolution: MMS is an evolution of SMS, offering additional capabilities for sending multimedia content.\\n\\n5. Support: Most cell phones support SMS, which is a standard feature, whereas MMS might require an additional service offered by the mobile company.\"]", "time_sec": 20.495, "generation_time_seconds": 19.6874, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8004, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 1172, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 279, 3040, 13, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 479, 333, 11, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2343613864772238, "g_worst_claim": 0.3521428638034397, "g_content": 2.6425282614571706, "g_traj_mean": 1.602094292640686}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 1172, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 320, 40404, 26936, 73170, 5362, 8, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 279, 3040, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS (Short Message Service) only allows you to send text, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7505276281338233, "g_worst_claim": 0.22056503295898439, "g_content": 1.0159125120743462, "g_traj_mean": 0.7617610692977905}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 1447, 785, 1887, 11799, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 525, 1447, 16, 13, 15042, 25, 29909, 21308, 14396, 1467, 6605, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 646, 3624, 5248, 4494, 315, 3687, 1741, 438, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 1493, 382, 17, 13, 8478, 25, 29909, 6605, 525, 7199, 311, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 817, 1943, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 479, 333, 11, 4992, 382, 18, 13, 5712, 2719, 25, 29909, 374, 21739, 311, 11628, 1467, 15382, 6605, 11, 19853, 386, 4826, 6081, 264, 803, 15817, 29522, 3139, 2670, 56513, 2213, 13, 151645], "pred": "3. Functionality: SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS offers a more comprehensive messaging experience including multimedia content.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5640257545892566, "g_worst_claim": -0.5910040140151978, "g_content": 1.2143094199044364, "g_traj_mean": 0.8079740405082703}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1376, 11799, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 525, 1447, 16, 13, 29045, 25, 29909, 374, 15503, 369, 11628, 1467, 6605, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 374, 6188, 369, 11628, 56513, 2213, 1075, 9185, 11, 6803, 11, 476, 7699, 3542, 382, 17, 13, 8883, 25, 29909, 374, 7199, 311, 1467, 15382, 6605, 11, 19853, 386, 4826, 646, 2924, 1467, 11, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 1493, 382, 18, 13, 8478, 25, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 11, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 19856, 1075, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 476, 46766, 11, 7707, 311, 29909, 382, 19, 13, 37221, 25, 386, 4826, 374, 458, 15379, 315, 29909, 11, 10004, 5107, 16928, 369, 11628, 56513, 2213, 382, 20, 13, 9186, 25, 7496, 2779, 17619, 1824, 29909, 11, 892, 374, 264, 5297, 4565, 11, 19853, 386, 4826, 2578, 1373, 458, 5107, 2473, 8900, 553, 279, 6371, 2813, 13, 151645], "pred": "5. Support: Most cell phones support SMS, which is a standard feature, whereas MMS might require an additional service offered by the mobile company.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7802721273176157, "g_worst_claim": -0.4865575631459554, "g_content": 1.437540054321289, "g_traj_mean": 0.8941354155540466}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "736", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text-only messages of up to 160 characters, while MMS allows you to send messages with pictures, sounds, videos, and text, with a larger content size of up to 300KB.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS, or Short Message Service, is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS, or Multimedia Messaging Service, allows for sending a variety of content such as pictures, sounds, videos, and text.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS, or Short Message Service, is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS, or Multimedia Messaging Service, allows for sending a variety of content such as pictures, sounds, videos, and text.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS stands for Short Message Service and is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service and allows sending a wider range of content including pictures, sounds, videos, and text. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS, or Short Message Service, is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS, or Multimedia Messaging Service, allows for sending a variety of content such as pictures, sounds, videos, and text.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four.\"]", "time_sec": 14.902, "generation_time_seconds": 14.0019, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8945, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 1172, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 279, 3040, 13, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 479, 333, 11, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.273591785895967, "g_worst_claim": 0.3547211488087972, "g_content": 2.695955276489258, "g_traj_mean": 1.6419330835342407}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 13352, 369, 10698, 4856, 5362, 323, 374, 21739, 311, 11628, 1467, 15382, 6605, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 13352, 369, 82222, 73170, 5362, 323, 6147, 11628, 264, 21864, 2088, 315, 2213, 2670, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 323, 1467, 13, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 46766, 11, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS stands for Short Message Service and is restricted to sending text-only messages, while MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service and allows sending a wider range of content including pictures, sounds, videos, and text. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.185046877064393, "g_worst_claim": 0.5741860469182333, "g_content": 1.919462155073117, "g_traj_mean": 1.2797906398773193}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 11, 476, 10698, 4856, 5362, 11, 374, 7199, 311, 11628, 1467, 15382, 6605, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 11, 476, 82222, 73170, 5362, 11, 6147, 369, 11628, 264, 8045, 315, 2213, 1741, 438, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 323, 1467, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS, or Short Message Service, is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS, or Multimedia Messaging Service, allows for sending a variety of content such as pictures, sounds, videos, and text.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5493201327745361, "g_worst_claim": 0.012693315744400024, "g_content": 1.1149907112121582, "g_traj_mean": 0.6277613639831543}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 1172, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 279, 3040, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8327858342565632, "g_worst_claim": 0.36792776319715714, "g_content": 1.464190539191751, "g_traj_mean": 0.9295870661735535}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "737", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Based on the given passages, SMS stands for Short Message Service and allows you to send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. In contrast, MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send a message including pictures, videos, sounds, text, or any combination of the four. The content of an MMS message has a maximum size of 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif etc.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif etc.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS (Short Message Service) allows you to send text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content, up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif etc.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif etc.\", \"Based on the given passages, the main difference between SMS and MMS is the type of content that can be sent.\\n\\nSMS (Short Message Service) allows for text-only messages to be sent between mobile devices. It has a character limit of up to 160 characters for each message. Longer messages are automatically split into multiple parts.\\n\\nMMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is an evolution of SMS and allows for the sending of multimedia content such as pictures, audio, video, and extended text messages. It has a larger content allowance of up to 300KB, enabling the transmission of various file types including WAV, JPEG, and GIF.\\n\\nIn summary, SMS is restricted to text-only messages, whereas MMS expands the types of messages that can be sent to include multimedia content.\"]", "time_sec": 19.479, "generation_time_seconds": 18.7103, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7639, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 1172, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 279, 3040, 13, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 479, 333, 11, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2421564798769569, "g_worst_claim": 0.3447388278113471, "g_content": 2.6873261587960378, "g_traj_mean": 1.6326955556869507}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 15382, 6605, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 320, 40404, 26936, 73170, 5362, 8, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 279, 3040, 13, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 11, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 479, 333, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS (Short Message Service) allows you to send text-only messages, while MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content, up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6178957853867038, "g_worst_claim": 0.28626537322998047, "g_content": 2.236299351283482, "g_traj_mean": 1.3587337732315063}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 1172, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 279, 3040, 13, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 479, 333, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5953516348548409, "g_worst_claim": 0.3447388278113471, "g_content": 2.77626827784947, "g_traj_mean": 1.6947941780090332}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1887, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 279, 943, 315, 2213, 429, 646, 387, 3208, 382, 65565, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 6147, 369, 1467, 15382, 6605, 311, 387, 3208, 1948, 6371, 7611, 13, 1084, 702, 264, 3668, 3930, 315, 705, 311, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 369, 1817, 1943, 13, 93326, 6605, 525, 9463, 6718, 1119, 5248, 5479, 382, 44, 4826, 320, 40404, 26936, 73170, 5362, 8, 374, 458, 15379, 315, 29909, 323, 6147, 369, 279, 11628, 315, 56513, 2213, 1741, 438, 9185, 11, 7699, 11, 2766, 11, 323, 11577, 1467, 6605, 13, 1084, 702, 264, 8131, 2213, 40358, 315, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 11, 27362, 279, 18368, 315, 5257, 1034, 4494, 2670, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 323, 46766, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 29909, 374, 21739, 311, 1467, 15382, 6605, 11, 19853, 386, 4826, 51856, 279, 4494, 315, 6605, 429, 646, 387, 3208, 311, 2924, 56513, 2213, 13, 151645], "pred": "In summary, SMS is restricted to text-only messages, whereas MMS expands the types of messages that can be sent to include multimedia content.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.707982946867328, "g_worst_claim": -0.12173393037584093, "g_content": 0.9573297242860537, "g_traj_mean": 0.5816238522529602}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "739", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the given passages:\n\nThe main difference between SMS (Short Message Service) and MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is that SMS is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS allows for sending multimedia content such as images, videos, and audio files, in addition to text.\n\nAccording to passage 1, SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts if they are longer. MMS messages, on the other hand, can carry a larger size of content, including pictures, videos, and audio files, with a maximum size of 300KB.\n\nPassage 2 explains that SMS is a premium service offered by mobile companies, while passage 3 highlights the differences between SMS and MMS, stating that SMS only allows for text, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between SMS and MMS are:\n\n* SMS is limited to text-only messages, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n* SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts, while MMS messages can carry a larger size of content.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS can only send text messages, while MMS allows the transmission of pictures, sounds, videos, and text, or any combination of these four types of content. Additionally, MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of formats like WAV, JPEG, and Gif.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS can only send text messages, while MMS allows the transmission of pictures, sounds, videos, and text, or any combination of these four types of content. Additionally, MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of formats like WAV, JPEG, and Gif.", "cot": "[\"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is primarily in the type of content they can transmit. SMS is limited to text-only messages, while MMS allows for the transmission of various types of content including pictures, sounds, and videos. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content compared to SMS, with extensions of up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. Additionally, SMS has a character limit of up to 160 characters, and longer messages are automatically split, whereas MMS messages are not subject to this restriction.\", \"Based on the given passages, the key differences between SMS and MMS are:\\n\\n1. Functionality:\\n   - SMS (Short Message Service) allows sending text-only messages.\\n   - MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) allows sending a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.\\n\\n2. Content:\\n   - SMS can carry messages up to 160 characters.\\n   - MMS can carry messages up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, GIF, etc.\\n\\n3. Support:\\n   - Most cell phones support SMS.\\n   - MMS is an evolution of SMS, supporting multimedia content.\\n\\n4. Usage:\\n   - SMS is used for text-only communication.\\n   - MMS is commonly used to send photos taken with a camera phone to another phone.\\n\\n5. Service:\\n   - SMS is a premium service offered by mobile companies apart from making phone calls.\\n   - MMS is a step further in the evolution of SMS, offering multimedia support.\", \"Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS can only send text messages, while MMS allows the transmission of pictures, sounds, videos, and text, or any combination of these four types of content. Additionally, MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of formats like WAV, JPEG, and Gif.\"]", "time_sec": 22.08, "generation_time_seconds": 21.1126, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9626, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 1172, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 279, 3040, 13, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 479, 333, 11, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of WAV, JPEG, Gif, etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2483761910458857, "g_worst_claim": 0.3305894798702664, "g_content": 2.659306117466518, "g_traj_mean": 1.6291064023971558}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 15503, 304, 279, 943, 315, 2213, 807, 646, 29282, 13, 29909, 374, 7199, 311, 1467, 15382, 6605, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147, 369, 279, 18368, 315, 5257, 4494, 315, 2213, 2670, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 323, 6803, 13, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 7707, 311, 29909, 11, 448, 19721, 315, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19856, 1075, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 323, 46766, 13, 22406, 11, 29909, 702, 264, 3668, 3930, 315, 705, 311, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 11, 323, 5021, 6605, 525, 9463, 6718, 11, 19853, 386, 4826, 6605, 525, 537, 3832, 311, 419, 19455, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is primarily in the type of content they can transmit. SMS is limited to text-only messages, while MMS allows for the transmission of various types of content including pictures, sounds, and videos. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content compared to SMS, with extensions of up to 300KB in formats like WAV, JPEG, and GIF. Additionally, SMS has a character limit of up to 160 characters, and longer messages are automatically split, whereas MMS messages are not subject to this restriction.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0324175332283312, "g_worst_claim": 0.1592743613503196, "g_content": 1.6758843246771364, "g_traj_mean": 0.956932544708252}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 1376, 11799, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 525, 1447, 16, 13, 5712, 2719, 510, 256, 481, 29909, 320, 12472, 4856, 5362, 8, 6147, 11628, 1467, 15382, 6605, 624, 256, 481, 386, 4826, 320, 40404, 26936, 73170, 5362, 8, 6147, 11628, 264, 10601, 315, 1467, 11, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 323, 6803, 382, 17, 13, 8883, 510, 256, 481, 29909, 646, 6777, 6605, 705, 311, 220, 16, 21, 15, 5766, 624, 256, 481, 386, 4826, 646, 6777, 6605, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 46766, 11, 4992, 382, 18, 13, 9186, 510, 256, 481, 7496, 2779, 17619, 1824, 29909, 624, 256, 481, 386, 4826, 374, 458, 15379, 315, 29909, 11, 12613, 56513, 2213, 382, 19, 13, 24567, 510, 256, 481, 29909, 374, 1483, 369, 1467, 15382, 10535, 624, 256, 481, 386, 4826, 374, 16626, 1483, 311, 3624, 7249, 4429, 448, 264, 6249, 4540, 311, 2441, 4540, 382, 20, 13, 5362, 510, 256, 481, 29909, 374, 264, 14848, 2473, 8900, 553, 6371, 5110, 10747, 504, 3259, 4540, 6738, 624, 256, 481, 386, 4826, 374, 264, 3019, 4623, 304, 279, 15379, 315, 29909, 11, 10004, 56513, 1824, 13, 151645], "pred": "5. Service:\n   - SMS is a premium service offered by mobile companies apart from making phone calls.\n   - MMS is a step further in the evolution of SMS, offering multimedia support.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.842632193775445, "g_worst_claim": -0.036587503221299916, "g_content": 1.6385062081473214, "g_traj_mean": 0.8986965417861938}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 374, 429, 29909, 646, 1172, 3624, 1467, 6605, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147, 279, 18368, 315, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 323, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 1493, 3040, 4494, 315, 2213, 13, 22406, 11, 386, 4826, 6605, 646, 6777, 264, 8131, 1379, 315, 2213, 705, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 29862, 304, 19721, 315, 19856, 1075, 88330, 11, 54562, 11, 323, 479, 333, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS can only send text messages, while MMS allows the transmission of pictures, sounds, videos, and text, or any combination of these four types of content. Additionally, MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB in extensions of formats like WAV, JPEG, and Gif.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.088978730837504, "g_worst_claim": 0.454234520594279, "g_content": 2.367883005449849, "g_traj_mean": 1.432347297668457}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.68, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
